 Pahalgam.                      ',15),(130,13,'PAHALGAM ','After breakfast one can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.   ',15),(131,14,'CHECK-OUT AT PAHALGAM HOTEL','After breakfast check-out from Pahalgam hotel and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.   ',15),(132,1,'Arrival SIN Airport','Transfer from Changi International Airport to the BOOKED Hotel [with Private transport]. Check-in and relax. You can explore nearby places on your own.',16),(133,2,'City Orientation Drive-MBS Skypark Non-Peak Hours-Gardens By The Bay','â€¢ Transfer from  the Booked Hotel to City Orientation Drive - Drop off Little India (3Hrs) [with PVT transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from  the Booked Hotel to MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay [with PVT transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay to the Booked Hotel [with PVT transport]\r\n',16),(134,3,'Full Day Sentosa Island Tour','â€¢ Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Full Day Sentosa Island Tour [with PVT transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Full Day Sentosa Island Tour to the Booked Hotel [with PVT transport]\r\n',16),(135,4,'Universal Studios Tour','â€¢ Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Universal Studios Tour [with PVT transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Universal Studios Tour to the Booked Hotel [with PVT transport]\r\n',16),(136,5,'Evening Mandai','â€¢ Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Evening Mandai [with PVT transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Evening Mandai to the Booked Hotel [with PVT transport]',16),(137,6,'Departure','* Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Changi International Airport [with PVT transport]',16),(138,1,' Cochin - Munnar (Arrival)','Meet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Throughout the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.',17),(139,2,'Munnar Sightseeing','Morning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nl ',17),(140,3,'Munnar - Thekkady','Morning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady. Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit Elephant junction, spice plantations. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.',17),(141,4,' Thekkady to Alleppey','Morning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort.',17),(142,5,'Alleppey to Kovalam','Morning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.',17),(143,6,'Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam','Morning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum. Overnight stay at Kovalam.',17),(144,7,'Kovalam to Kanyakumari','Morning after breakfast drive to Kanyakumari. Upon arrival check into the hotel. . Kanyakumari is located at the southern tip of the Indian subcontinent. With an area of 1672 sq.km. Kanyakumari occupies 1.29% of the total extent of Tamil Nadu. Visit Kanyakumari Devi Temple, Vivekananda Rock and Gandhi Mandap. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.',17),(145,8,'Kanyakumari to Rameshwaram','After breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram. Ramanathaswamy, this magnificent temple is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas situated in different parts of India. Ramanathaswamy Temple also has its name in history books as it has the largest hallway anywhere in India. The construction of Ramanathaswamy Temple which was started in the 12th century was contributed to by many rulers. During its construction period, many dynasties came and fell and each of them put their input into the temple. The list of unique features in its construction seems to be endless. There is this huge hallway that is of approximately 1220 meters in length. Throughout the length of the hall, there are brilliantly carved pillars, the alignment of which will leave you totally mesmerized. The 54 meter tall Gopuram has become the symbol of divinity in the heart of many pilgrims; such is the beauty and presence of it. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.',17),(146,9,' Rameshwaram','After breakfast sightseeing of Rameshwaram- Visit Sri Ramanatha Swamy temple, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Museum, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman temple, Villoondi Theertham etc. Overnight at the Resort/hotel',17),(147,10,'Rameswaram to Kodaikanal','After breakfast checkout from hotel and proceed to Kodaikanal Today proceed on a sightseeing trip around Kodaikanal that include Green Valley View, Pillar Rocks, Dolphinâ€™s Nose, Murugan temple and Pillar Rocks. Kodaikanal is a city in the hills and referred as Princess of Hill stations and listed as popular romantic destination for newlyweds. Overnight at Hotel',17),(148,11,' Kodaikanal Sightseeing','After munching some healthy breakfast in the morning, step out for a sightseeing tour of Kodaikanal. Spend the day amid the beauty and tranquility of the place. Visit attractions like Pillar Rocks and Bear-Shola falls which are known to offer breathtaking sights to the visitors. Later, you can visit places like Bryant Park and Kodai Lake. While the Bryant Park is a visited for its beautiful greenery, the Kodai Lake is known for its serenity and boat rides. After this long sightseeing tour, return back to the hotel for dinner. Enjoy a comfortable stay at night in the hotel.',17),(149,12,'Departure','Check-out from the hotel and proceed towards for onward journey',17),(150,1,'Arrival at  Amritsar and stay at Amritsar ','Arrival at airport of Amritsar and then transfer to booked hotel . After check-in, the remainder of the day is free for leisure. You can explore nearby local attractions, markets, and eateries at your own pace or relax at the hotel. Overnight stay in Amritsar.',18),(151,2,'Early morning Golden temple visit and transfer to Dharmshala','Start your day early and visit the beautiful and peaceful Golden Temple. Spend some time exploring the temple complex, enjoying the calm surroundings, and taking in the spiritual atmosphere. You can also visit the Langar Hall, where free meals are served to all visitors.\r\n\r\nAfter the visit, return to the hotel for breakfast and check out.\r\n\r\nLater, begin your journey to Dharamshala by road. Enjoy the drive as the scenery changes from city roads to green hills and mountain views.\r\n\r\nOn reaching Dharamshala, check in to your booked hotel and relax. The rest of the evening is free for you to rest or explore nearby places at your own pace.',18),(152,3,'Dharamshala â†’ McLeodganj sightseeing','Visit Tsuglagkhang Complex (Dalai Lama Temple area)\r\nWalk around McLeodganj market\r\nExplore Bhagsu Waterfall\r\nStop at Bhagsunag Temple\r\nSunset at Naddi View Point\r\nOptional evening cafÃ©s in McLeodganj',18),(153,4,'Dharmshala to Dalhousie sightseeing and stay at dharmshala ','Start from Dharamshala and drive through the hills to Dalhousie. On arrival, visit St. John\'s Church, known for its peaceful colonial-era setting. Continue to Subhash Baoli to enjoy the quiet surroundings and scenic views. Later, explore Panchpula, a popular spot with streams and small waterfalls. If time permits and you want more panoramic mountain views, head up to Dainkund Peak before ending the day.',18),(154,5,'Khajjiar day trip ','Visit Khajjiar and spend time exploring its beautiful meadow and lake area, often called the â€œMini Switzerland of Indiaâ€ for its open green landscapes and surrounding deodar forests. Continue to Khajji Nag Temple, an ancient temple known for its traditional wooden architecture and local significance. If you have extra time, enjoy optional activities such as horse riding across the meadows, zorbing for a fun outdoor experience, or take a short forest walk to enjoy the peaceful mountain scenery and fresh air.',18),(155,6,'Dharamshala â†’ Amritsar drop','Walk to Jallianwala Bagh Massacre memorial at Jallianwala Bagh\r\nEvening option: Attariâ€“Wagah Border ceremony',18),(234,1,'Arrive into Paris - the City of Romance, Lights and Glamour. ','Welcome! Today board our flight to one of the most beautiful and elegant city of Paris- known for its haute couture, renowned museums, breath-taking beautiful monuments and sensational cabarets. On arrival collect your baggage and proceed outside where you will be met by your professional tour manager, who will later escort you to your hotel. Check in and relax in the comforts of your hotel. \r\n(Dinner)',22),(235,2,'Guided city tour of Paris. Visit to Eiffel tower 3rd (Top) Level. Visit the Palace of Versailles, a testament to the pinnacle of French 17th-century artistry and achievement. Enjoy a romantic cruise on the River Seine. Paris by Night Tour.','Today proceed for a guided city tour of Paris. Marvel at the finest Parisian tourist attractions, Place VendÃ´me, Place de lâ€™OpÃ©ra Garnier, MusÃ©e dâ€™Orsay, Place de la Concorde, Champs ElysÃ©es, one of the most recognized fashionable avenues in the world, Arc de Triomphe, Alexander Bridge, Les Invalides and several others. Next visit the iconic Eiffel Tower â€“ 3rd Level, and get a stunning view of the city from the top. With its famous tapering cast iron tip, the Eiffel Tower is not just the symbol of Paris but of all of France Our adventure continues with a visit to the Palace of Versailles, an internationally acclaimed masterpiece located in Versailles, approximately 12 miles (19 km) west of Paris, France. This magnificent palace is the property of the French Republic and has been under the stewardship of the Public Establishment of the Palace, Museum, and National Estate of Versailles, overseen by the French Ministry of Culture since 1995. Later take a romantic cruise down the river Seine, one of the worldâ€™s most scenic cruise, flanked by exquisite monuments like Notre Dame, Eiffel Tower, Orsay Museum and many more. Gliding under one bridge to one another with a view of the finest monuments in the heart of bustling Paris. After the cruise, we proceed for a captivating and enchanting experience to witness the City of Light in all its night time splendour. Paris, often referred to as the \"City of Light\". See some of Paris\'s most famous landmarks, all bathed in a soft, golden glow. These might include the Eiffel Tower, Notre-Dame Cathedral, Place de la Concorde, Champs-Ã‰lysÃ©es, and the Arc de Triomphe.',22),(236,3,'Enjoy your fun filled day at DisneylandÂ® Paris choice of DisneyÂ® Park or Walt Disney StudiosÂ® Park.','Get ready for a day full of excitement at Disneyland Paris- a popular amusement park. Enjoy different kind of thrill rides and studio movies with your loved ones. You may choose between Disney Park, where fairy tales take flight across five incredible lands filled with classic attractions, shows and street parades with Disney Characters OR you may visit the Walt Disney Studios Park Studios and be astounded by the outstanding stunt shows, watch a film being made and see real-life sets used for creating blockbuster movies. ',22),(237,4,'Orientation tour of Geneva. ','Check out from your hotel and proceed to Switzerland, a mountainous Central European country, home to numerous lakes, villages and the high peaks of the Alps. On arrival proceed for orientation tour of Geneva. See The Jet d\'Eau, a large fountain in Geneva, Switzerland and is one of the city\'s most famous landmarks, UN Buildings - The United Nations Office and the Flower Clock, located just in front of the famous Lake Geneva. Later proceed to your hotel and check-in and relax in the comforts of your hotel.',22),(238,5,'Enjoy a magical alpine excursion to the top of Europe - the amazing Jungfraujoch which is included in your tour and scenic Interlaken.','Get set for a memorable magical alpine excursion to Jungfraujoch â€“ The Top of Europe, a highâ€“point of your tour. First proceed to Grindelwald Terminal. The new 3S-Bahn Eiger Express takes you from the Grindelwald Terminal to the Eigergletscher station in just 15 minutes. There you board a cogwheel train to reach the highest railway station in Europe at 11,333 feet â€“ a world of eternal ice and snow. Visit the Ice Palace where artistes create their work of art in ice. Visit the Sphinx observatory deck to experience a breath-taking panoramic view of the longest glacier in the Alps - Aletsch Glacier.',22),(239,6,'Visit Mt. Titlis- enjoy Cable car rides including the worldâ€™s first rotating cable car, the Rotair â€“ to the top of Mt. Titlis at 3,020 metres. Enjoy a scenic cruise on Lake Lucerne.','Today enjoy amazing scenery, a once in a lifetime experience with an exhilarating tip to the top of Mt Titlis at 3020 metres on various cable cars including Rotair, the worldâ€™s first revolving cable car. Get a breath taking unrestricted 360 degrees stunning view of the dazzling snow caped peak, deep crevasses and pristine white snow fields, dotted with massive ice boulders from every angle. Do not forget to visit the â€œCliff Walkâ€ the highest suspension bridge in Europe along the cliff of Mt.Titlis. Later proceed on an orientation tour of Lucerne one of most beautiful cities in Switzerland. Visit the Lion Monument, Kapell Brucke with some free time to shop for famous Swiss watches, knives and chocolates. Later enjoy a scenic and relaxing cruise on Lake Lucerne',22),(240,7,'Visit the magnificent Rhine Falls','Today after breakfast, sit back and enjoy the scenic drive towards Schaffhausen, where you see the magnificent Rhine Falls â€“ Europeâ€™s biggest and most spectacular falls. Explore the Rhine Falls with a boat ride which offers a thrilling close-up experience of the powerful cascading waters where you can behold the breathtaking Rhine Falls, the largest and most stunning waterfall in Europe. The cascading waters of the Rhine River create a mesmerizing spectacle, drawing visitors to its scenic surroundings and boat excursions for a closer encounter with this natural wonder. Enroute to Innsbruck visit Vaduz, the capital of Liechtenstein, a tiny principality nestled between Switzerland and Austria. It lies entirely within the Alps and covering an area of just sixty-two square miles. Liechtenstein is the sixth smallest independent nation in the world. It follows a policy of neutrality and is one of the few countries in the world that maintains no military. The Vaduz train ride offers a serene and immersive way to appreciate the natural beauty and idyllic surroundings that make Liechtenstein so special. Next we proceed to Wattens, where you\'ll have the opportunity to explore the Swarovski World of Crystals and be enchanted by the exquisite crystalline artworks on display.\r\nFollowing this captivating visit, we\'ll continue on to Innsbruck, a city of extraordinary beauty. During our orientation tour, you\'ll have the chance to admire the iconic Golden Roof, known for its fire-gilded copper tiles, which serves as a defining landmark of Innsbruck. Stroll along the charming cobblestone paths of Maria Theresien Strasse, where you can choose to relax at one of the many outdoor cafes. As you do so, you\'ll be treated to magnificent baroque architecture and the chance to immerse yourself in the rich culture of medieval Europe. With the splendid Alps as a backdrop, the setting is nothing short of a picture-postcard perfect. \r\n\r\n',22),(241,8,'Welcome to Venice - the floating city of Italy. Enjoy Gondola ride.','Check out of your hotel and proceed towards Venice â€“ Italy. City of Beautiful Monuments, Serpentine Canals, city that inspired poetry and passion through the ages. Arrive at the pier in Venice, where we board a private boat to arrive at St. Markâ€™s Square â€“ the main square of Venice. View St Markâ€™s Basilica - one of the best examples of Byzantine architecture, Witness the famed Bell Tower and Clock Tower with the dominant sign of the Zodiac and current phase of the moon. See the Bridge of Sighs, made of white limestone, that passes over the Rio di Palazzo, connecting the old prisons with interrogations rooms at the Dogeâ€™s Palace. Treasure a romantic Gondola ride in a flat-bottomed Venetian rowing boat, amidst the stunning backdrop of baroque buildings. This truly is the best way to enjoy this enchanting city. We return to the pier and later check in to your hotel. ',22),(242,9,' Guided walking city tour of Florence. View the remarkable and famous Leaning Tower of Pisa.','This morning check out and drive to Florence â€“ the cradle of the Renaissance. Along with your English-speaking local guide, walk and absorb into the culture of the historic city. View the Duomo â€“ the cityâ€™s most iconic landmark, the Campanile and the Baptistery with its Gates to Paradise. Also see the Piazza Della Signoria â€“ an open-air museum crammed with Renaissance sculptures, edged by historic cafes and presided over by the magnificent Palazzo Vecchio and the famed Ponte Vecchio (bridge) across the River Arno. Later proceed towards Pisa. On arrival see the Square of Miracles with the stupendous Leaning Tower of Pisa.',22),(243,10,'All roads lead to Rome â€“ the eternal city. Visit the worldâ€™s smallest country â€“ the Vatican City and see the St. Peterâ€™s Basilica.','Today, we drive to the eternal city of Rome. Our first destination is the Vatican City, the world\'s smallest independent country. Here, you\'ll have the opportunity to explore the exquisitely beautiful St. Peter\'s Basilica, where you can marvel at the magnificent works of art created by masters such as Michelangelo and Bernini.\r\nOur exploration of Rome continues to see the awe-inspiring Colosseum, an immense amphitheater that has endured the passage of centuries, retaining its grandeur and historical significance. Our next stop on the itinerary is the enchanting Trevi Fountain. According to legend, tossing a coin over your shoulder into the fountain guarantees your return to Rome, making it a cherished tradition among visitors. Check in to your hotel\r\n',22),(244,11,'Fly back home','Your memorable holiday ends, today itâ€™s time to fly back home. Say goodbye to the wonderful new friends you have made on the tour. Check out and depart for the Airport with pleasant memories of your European trip which you will cherish for a lifetime.\r\n(Breakfast)',22),(245,1,'ARRIVAL IN SRINAGAR & LOCAL SIGHTSEEING ','Upon arrival at Srinagar Airport, guests will be warmly welcomed by our representative and transferred to the hotel. After check-in and some relaxation, begin your exploration of Srinagar, the summer capital of Jammu & Kashmir. Visit the world-famous Mughal Gardens including Nishat Garden, known for its terraced lawns and stunning views of Dal Lake. Continue to Shalimar Garden, built by Mughal Emperor Jahangir for Noor Jahan. Later visit Chashme Shahi, famous for its natural spring and beautiful landscape. Proceed to the sacred Shankaracharya Temple situated atop a hill overlooking Srinagar city. From here guests can enjoy breathtaking panoramic views of Dal Lake, Zabarwan Mountains and the city below. Spend the evening exploring local markets or enjoying leisure time around Srinagar. And enjoy 1 hour shikara ride complementary. Return to the hotel for dinner and overnight stay. ',23),(246,2,'SRINAGAR TO SONAMARG TO SRINAGAR  ','After breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed towards Sonamarg, popularly known as the Meadow of Gold. The drive takes guests through picturesque villages, green valleys and alongside the beautiful Sindh River. En route enjoy magnificent mountain views, lush meadows and glacier-fed streams. Sonamarg serves as the gateway to Ladakh and is surrounded by towering snow-clad peaks. After arrival, enjoy sightseeing around Sonamarg and spend time admiring the untouched beauty of the valley. Guests may opt for pony rides and local excursions at their own expense. Lunch break during the journey. Evening free to relax and enjoy the serene surroundings. Return to Srinagar Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar . ',23),(247,3,'SRINAGAR TO GULMARG TO SRINAGAR  ','Following breakfast, proceed towards Gulmarg, one of Indiaâ€™s most famous hill resorts and ski destinations. The scenic drive passes through beautiful countryside landscapes and traditional Kashmiri villages. Upon arrival in Gulmarg, explore the vast meadows surrounded by pine forests and snowcovered mountains. Visit the famous Gulmarg Golf Course, one of the highest golf courses in the world. Guests can enjoy optional Gondola rides, snow activities and pony rides (at additional cost). The Gulmarg Gondola offers spectacular views of the Himalayas and is among the highest cable car systems in the world. Lunch break during sightseeing. Spend the evening at leisure amidst the stunning alpine scenery. Return to Srinagar. Dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar  ',23),(248,4,'SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM ','After breakfast, depart for Pahalgam, known as the Valley of Shepherds. The journey passes through saffron fields, apple orchards and charming villages that showcase the traditional lifestyle of Kashmir. Upon arrival, explore the beautiful Lidder River flowing through the valley. Visit local markets and enjoy the peaceful atmosphere created by pine forests and surrounding mountains. Pahalgam is one of the most picturesque destinations in Kashmir and serves as the base camp for the annual Amarnath Yatra. Guests can enjoy riverside walks, photography and shopping for local handicrafts. Lunch break en route. Dinner and overnight stay in Pahalgam. ',23),(249,5,'PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT DEPARTURE','After breakfast, check out from the hotel and proceed towards Srinagar Airport. Enjoy the final views of Kashmirâ€™s valleys, rivers and mountains as you travel back. Arrive at the airport for your onward journey carrying unforgettable memories of the paradise called Kashmir. ',23),(250,1,'1st Day (Mon 7th September) : Nairobi to Nakuru - Transfer & Sightseeing','â€¢	Early breakfast & depart for Lake Nakuru National Park\r\nâ€¢	Drive through the scenic Great Rift Valley with a brief stop at the viewpoint\r\nâ€¢	Arrive in Nakuru in time for lunch at a lodge\r\nâ€¢	Afternoon game drive in Lake Nakuru National Park â€“ search for rhinos, giraffes, flamingos, and more\r\nâ€¢	Overnight & Meals: Nakuru\r\n\r\n: Lake Nakuru National Park - Park Fees In Nakuru National Park\r\nLake Nakuru National Park, renowned for its diverse wildlife and birdlife, including the famous flamingo populations, is located in the central Rift Valley of Kenya. The park is accessible from Nairobi via the A104 road, approximately 156 km northwest of the city.\r\n',24),(251,2,'2nd Day (Tue 8th September) : Nakuru to Maasai Mara - Transfer & Sightseeing','â€¢	Early breakfast & depart for Masai Mara National Reserve\r\nâ€¢	Drive through the scenic Great Rift Valley\r\nâ€¢	Arrive for lunch at lodge\r\nâ€¢	Afternoon game drive\r\nâ€¢	Overnight & Meals: Maasai Mara (Full Board)\r\n\r\n: Maasai Mara National Reserve - Park Fees Maasai Mara\r\n',24),(252,3,'3rd Day (Wed 9th September) : Maasai Mara - Full Day Sightseeing','â€¢	Full day game drive with picnic lunch OR morning & afternoon game drives\r\nâ€¢	Explore wildlife: lions, leopards, elephants, giraffes, and more\r\nâ€¢	Optional: Maasai village visit (extra cost)\r\nâ€¢	Overnight & Meals: Maasai Mara (Full Board)\r\n\r\n: Maasai Mara National Reserve - Park Fees Maasai Mara\r\n\r\n: Maasai Mara National Reserve - Visit Maasai Village\r\nVisiting a Maasai village near the Masai Mara offers a unique cultural experience, providing insight into the traditions and daily life of the Maasai people.\r\n\r\n',24),(253,4,' 4th Day (Thu 10th September) : Maasai Mara - Full Day Sightseeing','â€¢	Full day game drive with picnic lunch OR morning & afternoon game drives\r\nâ€¢	Explore wildlife: lions, leopards, elephants, giraffes, and more\r\nâ€¢	Optional: Maasai village visit (extra cost)\r\nâ€¢	Overnight & Meals: Maasai Mara (Full Board)\r\n\r\n: Maasai Mara National Reserve - Park Fees Maasai Mara\r\n',24),(254,5,'5th Day (Fri 11th September) : Maasai Mara to Nairobi - Transfer & Sightseeing','â€¢	Breakfast and check-out.\r\nâ€¢	Drive to Nairobi (7-8hrs).\r\nâ€¢	Enjoy lunch in Nairobi before your transfer to Jomo Kenyatta International Airport for your onward flight.\r\n',24),(273,1,' Arrival in Moscow','As soon as you are ready to kick-start your vacation in Russia, our representative awaits you at Moscow Airport. Transfer to Hotel, Overnight in Moscow',25),(274,2,'Moscow City Tour ','â¤ Metro Tour\r\nâ¤ Moscow Kremlin, Red Square, Park Zaryade\r\nâ¤ Alexandrosky Sad / St Basil,s Cathedral, Lenin Mausoleum\r\nâ¤ Nikolskya Street/Gum Mall/KGB Bldg\r\n',25),(275,3,'Moscow City Tour ','â¤ Christ the Saviour Cathedral\r\nâ¤ Moscow state University, Sparrow Hills, Cable Car at Luzhniki Stadium\r\nâ¤ Arbat Street\r\nâ¤ Moscow Radisson River Cruise',25),(276,4,'Moscow City Tour','â¤ VDNKH Park\r\nâ¤ Pavallions of ex Soviet states\r\nâ¤ Cosmonautic Arena\r\nâ¤ Cable Car Ride\r\nâ¤Visit the tallest tower in Europe at 337 floor.',25),(277,5,'Moscow to St Petersburg.','Moscow to St Petersburg. Checkout and transfer to train station. Arrive St Petersburg and transfer to hotel. Drop to Hotel â€“ Free time. Overnight in St Petersburg\r\n',25),(278,6,'St Petersburg Pvt City Tour with Evening Neva Cruise','â¤SPB City tour with visit to Hermitage (entrance included)\r\nâ¤ Admirality, Bronje Horseman, Kazan Cathedral\r\nâ¤ Church of the spilled Blood\r\nâ¤ Shopping at art Galleria\r\nâ¤ Evening Neva Cruise\r\n\r\nOvernight in St Petersburg\r\n',25),(279,7,'Kronstadt Tour','Kronstadt is a town and naval base on Kotlin Island, just west of St. Petersburg, Russia. Anchor Square is dotted with military memorials. On the square, the 20th-century Byzantine-style Naval Cathedral has an ornate interior. Tree-lined Petrovskiy Park is home to the 19th-century Monument to Peter the Great. Kronstadt History Museum displays regional artifacts. Offshore is the man-made island of Fort Alexander . Peter and Paul Fortress ',25),(280,8,'Departure from St Petesburg to Moscow . (07:00 â€“ 10:00)','Breakfast at Hotel, Checkout and Transfer to the Railway Station and Board the Train for St Petesburg to Moscow . After reaching Moscow Railway station transfer to the Airport for International flight.',25),(323,1,' Hyderabad to Srisailam - Transfer To Srisailam & Stay','Approx Distance: 250 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out of the hotel and proceed to Srisailam. It Is Situated In The Nallamala Hills Of Kurnool District And Is Famous For Its Bramaramba Millikan Juna Swamy Temple, Which Is One Of The 12 Jyotirlingas Hotels and Welcome To Check In To The Hotel.  Overnight Stay at Hotel. Srisailam',27),(324,2,'Srisailam to Hyderabad - Srisailam Local Sightseeing Hyderabad',' Est. Travel Time: 5 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out of the hotel & proceed to Srisailam. Local Sightseeing: Sakshi Ganapathi Temple, Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple, Bhramaramba Devi Temple, Pathalaganga, Shikhareshwara Temple, Srisailam Dam, Srisailam And Afternoon Lunch after Drive to And After Evening Back To The Hotel .Overnight Stay At The Hotel. Hyderabad',27),(325,3,'Hyderabad - Ramoji Film City Day Tour',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Ramoji Film City Tour Day Tour From 9.00 Am To 5.30 Pm. Guided Tour Of Ramoji Film City In a Non-A/C Vintage Bus (10am To 5pm). Visit To Bahubali Set (Last Bus At 4pm). Visit To Eco Zone â€“ Butterfly Park, Exotic Bird Park â€“ Wings &Amp; Bonsai Garden. Fundustan (Child Play Area), Borasura, Toyland &Amp; Rain Dance. Ramoji Movie Magic â€” Action Theater &Amp; Space Yatra Entertainment Shows At Eureka â€” Spirit Of Ramoji, Fort Frontier Wild West Stunt Show, Dada Jinnâ€™s Live Tv Show &Amp; Lights Camera Action (Hollywood Black Light Spectacular Show). Complimentary Rides â€” Ranger, Break Dance, Twister, Super Jet, Carousel, Frisbee Coaster. Shooting Locations & Gardens. Live Entertainment Stage Shows In Eureka. Spectacular Carnival Parade. Experience Ramoji Film City In Dazzling Lights. DSLR Cameras Above 18-55mm Is Not Permitted And Evening Back To The Hotel . Overnight Stay At The Hotel. Hyderabad',27),(326,4,' Hyderabad - Hyderabad Local Sightseeing',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Hyderabad Local Sightseeing: Charminar, Macca Masjid, Chowmahala Palace, & After Lunch Proceed Salarjung Museum, Free Time Shopping Special Karachi Biscuits, Pearls, Bangles, Sarees At Abids And Evening Back To Hotel . Overnight Stay At Hotel. Hyderabad',27),(327,5,'Hyderabad - Hyderabad Local Sightseeing',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Hyderabad Local Sightseeing: Golkonda Fort Afternoon Lunch Proceed To Lumbini Park, Ntr Garden, Necklace Road, Gautama Buddha Statue In Hussain Sager Lake Boating, Birla Temple, Evening Back To Hotel . Overnight Stay At Hotel. Hyderabad',27),(328,6,'Hyderabad - The Statue Of Equality & Arrival to Tirupati ','â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning after Breakfast Check Out From the Hotel & Proceed To THE STATUE OF EQUALITY, Also Referred To As The Ramanuja Statue, Is A Statue Of The 11th-Century Vaishnavaite Ramanuja, Located On The Premises Of The Chinna Jeeyar Trust At Muchintal, Hyderabad. It Is The Second-Tallest Sitting Statue In The World Drop To Hyderabad Airport. Enjoy Your Unforgettable Holiday Experience.',27),(361,1,' Hyderabad to Srisailam - Transfer To Srisailam & Stay','Approx Distance: 250 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out of the hotel and proceed to Srisailam. It Is Situated In The Nallamala Hills Of Kurnool District And Is Famous For Its Bramaramba Millikan Juna Swamy Temple, Which Is One Of The 12 Jyotirlingas Hotels and Welcome To Check In To The Hotel.  Overnight Stay at Hotel. Srisailam',26),(362,2,'Srisailam to Hyderabad - Srisailam Local Sightseeing Hyderabad',' Est. Travel Time: 5 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out of the hotel & proceed to Srisailam. Local Sightseeing: Sakshi Ganapathi Temple, Mallikarjuna Swamy Temple, Bhramaramba Devi Temple, Pathalaganga, Shikhareshwara Temple, Srisailam Dam, Srisailam And Afternoon Lunch after Drive to And After Evening Back To The Hotel. Overnight Stay At The Hotel. Hyderabad',26),(363,3,'Hyderabad - Ramoji Film City Day Tour',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Ramoji Film City Tour Day Tour From 9.00 Am To 5.30 Pm. Guided Tour Of Ramoji Film City In a Non-A/C Vintage Bus (10am To 5pm). Visit To Bahubali Set (Last Bus At 4pm). Visit To Eco Zone â€“ Butterfly Park, Exotic Bird Park â€“ Wings &Amp; Bonsai Garden. Fundustan (Child Play Area), Borasura, Toyland &Amp; Rain Dance. Ramoji Movie Magic â€” Action Theater &Amp; Space Yatra Entertainment Shows At Eureka â€” Spirit Of Ramoji, Fort Frontier Wild West Stunt Show, Dada Jinnâ€™s Live Tv Show &Amp; Lights Camera Action (Hollywood Black Light Spectacular Show). Complimentary Rides â€” Ranger, Break Dance, Twister, Super Jet, Carousel, Frisbee Coaster. Shooting Locations & Gardens. Live Entertainment Stage Shows In Eureka. Spectacular Carnival Parade. Experience Ramoji Film City In Dazzling Lights. DSLR Cameras Above 18-55mm Is Not Permitted And Evening Back To The Hotel . Overnight Stay At The Hotel. Hyderabad',26),(364,4,' Hyderabad - Hyderabad Local Sightseeing',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Hyderabad Local Sightseeing: Charminar, Macca Masjid, Chowmahala Palace, & After Lunch Proceed Salarjung Museum, Free Time Shopping Special Karachi Biscuits, Pearls, Bangles, Sarees At Abids And Evening Back To Hotel . Overnight Stay At Hotel. Hyderabad',26),(365,5,'Hyderabad - Hyderabad Local Sightseeing',' Est. Travel Time: 1-2 hrs\r\n\r\nMorning After Breakfast Proceed To Hyderabad Local Sightseeing: Golkonda Fort Afternoon Lunch Proceed To Lumbini Park, Ntr Garden, Necklace Road, Gautama Buddha Statue In Hussain Sager Lake Boating, Birla Temple, Evening Back To Hotel. Overnight Stay At Hotel. Hyderabad',26),(366,6,'Departure from Hyderabad & Arrival to Chennai ','Morning after Breakfast Check Out From the Hotel Drop To Hyderabad Airport. On arrival at the Chennai airport, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Tirupati. Tirupati is a city in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. Its Sri Venkateswara Temple sits atop one of the the 7 peaks of Tirumala Hills, attracting scores of Hindu pilgrims. Sri Venkateswara National Park, home to the temple. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. During your free time, you can walk out to explore the surroundings, interact with locals, visit local markets or stay back in hotel to take pleasure of its modern amenities. Overnight stay at resort/hotel.\r\n\r\n ',26),(367,7,'Tirupati to Tirupathi Sightseeing','Morning after breakfast local sightseeing of temples in Tirupati including Sri Govindarajaswami Temple, Kapila Theertham, Padmavati Temple, Trimala (Tirupati Balaji) Temple Akash Ganga & Paap Vinashni Temple. Overnight at the Resort/hotel.',26),(368,8,'Chennai Departure','Morning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Tirupati  international Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n',26),(369,1,'Arrival in Srinagar & Local Sightseeing','Upon arrival at Srinagar Airport, meet our representative and transfer to your hotel. After freshening up, proceed for local sightseeing covering the famous Mughal Gardens including Nishat Bagh, Shalimar Bagh and Chashme Shahi (subject to time). Visit the beautiful Boulevard Road and enjoy a relaxing 1-hour Shikara Ride on Dal Lake. Return to the hotel for dinner and overnight stay in Srinagar. ',28),(370,2,'Srinagar â€“ Sonmarg â€“ Srinagar ','After breakfast, drive to Sonmarg, the \'Meadow of Gold\', surrounded by snow-capped mountains and glaciers. Enjoy the scenic Sindh River and optional pony rides to Thajiwas Glacier (at your own cost). Spend leisure time amidst the breathtaking landscape before returning to Srinagar for dinner and overnight stay. ',28),(371,3,' Srinagar â€“ Gulmarg â€“ Srinagar ','After breakfast, proceed to Gulmarg, one of Kashmir\'s most beautiful hill resorts. Enjoy the lush meadows, golf course and optional Gondola cable car ride (tickets at your own cost). Explore the surroundings before returning to Srinagar for dinner and overnight stay. ',28),(372,4,' Srinagar â€“ Pahalgam â€“ Houseboat Stay ','After breakfast, drive to Pahalgam, the \'Valley of Shepherds\'. En route visit saffron fields, Awantipora ruins and apple orchards (seasonal). At Pahalgam, enjoy the beauty of Lidder River. Union taxi for Aru Valley, Betaab Valley and Chandanwari is optional and payable directly. Return to Srinagar in the evening and check in to the Deluxe Houseboat on Dal Lake. Dinner and overnight stay. ',28),(373,5,'Departure ','After breakfast, check out from the houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport for your onward journey with unforgettable memories of Kashmir. ',28),(390,1,'Arrive at Madurai','On arrival at the Madurai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Madurai. Visit the famous Madurai Meenakshi Temple. There are four entrances to this amazing temple complex set in six hectares. Hit one of the stone pillars in the complex with any hard object and feel incredible on hearing sweet metal sounds. It is known as musical pillars. The total number of pillars in the temple is a staggering one thousand. Sightseeing inclusive of Thirumalai Nayak palace, Gandhi Museum and flower market.  Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n',29),(391,2,'Madurai To Rameshwaram','After breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram. Ramanathaswamy, this magnificent temple is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas situated in different parts of India. Ramanathaswamy Temple also has its name in history books as it has the largest hallway anywhere in India. The construction of Ramanathaswamy Temple which was started in the 12th century was contributed to by many rulers. During its construction period, many dynasties came and fell and each of them put their input into the temple. The list of unique features in its construction seems to be endless. There is this huge hallway that is of approximately 1220 meters in length. Throughout the length of the hall, there are brilliantly carved pillars, the alignment of which will leave you totally mesmerized. The 54 meter tall Gopuram has become the symbol of divinity in the heart of many pilgrims; such is the beauty and presence of it. Overnight stay at hotel.',29),(392,3,'Rameshwaram Day 02','After breakfast sightseeing of Rameshwaram- Visit Sri Ramanatha Swamy temple, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Museum, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman temple, Villoondi Theertham etc. Overnight at the hotel.',29),(393,4,'Rameswaram to Kodaikanal','Transfers - Rameswaram to Kodaikanal\r\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and proceed to Kodaikanal Today proceed on a sightseeing trip around Kodaikanal that include Green Valley View, Pillar Rocks, Dolphinâ€™s Nose, Murugan temple and Pillar Rocks. Kodaikanal is a city in the hills and referred as Princess of Hill stations and listed as popular romantic destination for newlyweds. Overnight at Hotel.',29),(394,5,'Kodaikanal Sightseeing Day 02','After munching some healthy breakfast in the morning, step out for a sightseeing tour of Kodaikanal. Spend the day amid the beauty and tranquility of the place.Visit attractions like Pillar Rocks and Bear-Shola falls which are known to offer breathtaking sights to the visitors. Later, you can visit places like Bryant Park and Kodai Lake. While the Bryant Park is a visited for its beautiful greenery, the Kodai Lake is known for its serenity and boat rides.After this long sightseeing tour, return back to the hotel. Enjoy a comfortable stay at night in the hotel.',29),(395,6,'Kodaikanal to Ooty','Transfers - Kodaikanal to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty (Udhagamandalam), the \"Queen of Hill Stations\" in Tamil Nadu, is famous for its cool climate, lush tea gardens, colonial charm, and the Nilgiri Mountain Railway. It is a premier honeymoon destination, renowned for botanical gardens, homemade chocolates, eucalyptus oil, and serene lakes like Ooty Lake. Overnight Stay at Hotel.',29),(396,7,'Ooty Sightseeing Day 02','After breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sightseeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory). Return to the hotel for overnight stay. Overnight Stay at Hotel. ',29),(397,8,'Coimbatore Departure Transfer','Departure Transfer - Coimbatore Departure Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel and proceed to Coimbatore for Departure.',29),(412,1,'Arrive at Madurai','On arrival at the Madurai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Madurai. Visit the famous Madurai Meenakshi Temple. There are four entrances to this amazing temple complex set in six hectares. Hit one of the stone pillars in the complex with any hard object and feel incredible on hearing sweet metal sounds. It is known as musical pillars. The total number of pillars in the temple is a staggering one thousand. Sightseeing inclusive of Thirumalai Nayak palace, Gandhi Museum and flower market.  Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n',30),(413,2,'Madurai To Rameshwaram','After breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram. Ramanathaswamy, this magnificent temple is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas situated in different parts of India. Ramanathaswamy Temple also has its name in history books as it has the largest hallway anywhere in India. The construction of Ramanathaswamy Temple which was started in the 12th century was contributed to by many rulers. During its construction period, many dynasties came and fell and each of them put their input into the temple. The list of unique features in its construction seems to be endless. There is this huge hallway that is of approximately 1220 meters in length. Throughout the length of the hall, there are brilliantly carved pillars, the alignment of which will leave you totally mesmerized. The 54 meter tall Gopuram has become the symbol of divinity in the heart of many pilgrims; such is the beauty and presence of it. Overnight stay at hotel.',30),(414,3,'Rameshwaram Day 02','After breakfast sightseeing of Rameshwaram- Visit Sri Ramanatha Swamy temple, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Museum, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman temple, Villoondi Theertham etc. Overnight at the hotel.',30),(415,4,'Rameswaram to Kodaikanal','Transfers - Rameswaram to Kodaikanal\r\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and proceed to Kodaikanal Today proceed on a sightseeing trip around Kodaikanal that include Green Valley View, Pillar Rocks, Dolphinâ€™s Nose, Murugan temple and Pillar Rocks. Kodaikanal is a city in the hills and referred as Princess of Hill stations and listed as popular romantic destination for newlyweds. Overnight at Hotel.',30),(416,5,'Kodaikanal Sightseeing Day 02','After munching some healthy breakfast in the morning, step out for a sightseeing tour of Kodaikanal. Spend the day amid the beauty and tranquility of the place.Visit attractions like Pillar Rocks and Bear-Shola falls which are known to offer breathtaking sights to the visitors. Later, you can visit places like Bryant Park and Kodai Lake. While the Bryant Park is a visited for its beautiful greenery, the Kodai Lake is known for its serenity and boat rides.After this long sightseeing tour, return back to the hotel. Enjoy a comfortable stay at night in the hotel.',30),(417,6,'Kodaikanal to Madurai Drop','Departure Transfer - Kodaikanal to Madurai Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Madurai international Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.',30),(418,1,'Arrival at KUL Airport','Transfer from KLIA-Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]',31),(419,2,'KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower (04 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower (04 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',31),(420,3,'Genting Day Tour','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',31),(421,4,'LGK Airport to Hotel','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KLIA-Airport [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from LGK Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n\r\n',31),(422,5,'Full Day Langkawi Tour','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Full Day Langkawi Tour - Ex Beach & City Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Full Day Langkawi Tour - Ex Beach & City Hotel to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',31),(423,6,'Departure','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to LGK Airport [with Private transport]',31),(430,1,'Arrival at KUL Airport','Transfer from KLIA-Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]',32),(431,2,'KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower (04 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower (04 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',32),(432,3,'Genting Day Tour','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',32),(433,4,'LGK Airport to Hotel','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KLIA-Airport [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from LGK Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n\r\n',32),(434,5,'Full Day Langkawi Tour','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Full Day Langkawi Tour - Ex Beach & City Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Full Day Langkawi Tour - Ex Beach & City Hotel to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n',32),(435,6,'Departure from Langkawi and Arrival at the DPS Airport','Transfer from the Booked Hotel to LGK Airport [with Private transport]\r\nArrival at the DPS Airport and transfer to the Booked Hotel (with Private transport)\r\nWelcome with Garland',32),(436,7,'Water Sports','Water Sports At Tanjung Benoa Beach By Indah (Parasailing,Banana Boat & Jetsky) - Ticket\r\nTanjung Benoa in Bali is a popular location for water sports, offering a variety of activities.\r\nUluwatu Tour - Ticket\r\nKecak Dance Tour - Ticket\r\nthe unique Kecak fire dance, performed by a group of men using sound techniques. Follow the story of this historical dance which embodies the romantic story of love between Rama and Sinta, a mythical giant named Ravana, and a Monkey army, all against the backdrop of the Indian Ocean at sunset.\r\n\r\n',32),(437,8,'Nusa Penida Tour','F/D Nusa Penida West Trip by Diamond (snorkeling equipment only) - Sharing Speed Boat + Transfer + Any three beach will be cover + Retribution fees Included\r\nNusa Penida Limited portion fixed menu Indian lunch at Nusa Penida\r\n',32),(438,9,'Interhotel Transfer and Sightseeing','Interhotel Transfers\r\nKintamani Volcano view - Ticket\r\nTegenungan Waterfall - Ticket\r\nTegenungan waterfall is located in the village of Kemenuh, Gianyar Regency, about a 30-minute drive from Ubud. Itâ€™s easily accessible from other parts of the island as well, such as Kuta, Seminyak, and Sanur.\r\nMy Swing (Swing + Nest + Local Lunch) - Ticket\r\n*Meal *Single Swing *Fun Adrenalin Swing *Exciting Adrenaline Swing * Ultimate Swing *Couple swing *Romantic Bed Swing *Family Bed Swing *Chicken Nest *Sweet Love Nest *Glass Floor\r\nTegalalang Rice Terrace - Ticket\r\nTegalalang Rice Terrace is a breathtaking destination in Bali that showcases the island\'s natural beauty and traditional agricultural practices! Located in Ubud\r\nUbud palace - Ticket\r\n',32),(439,10,'ATV Bali Bhumi ','ATV Bali Bhumi - 60 Mint Tandem by Bali Bhumi + Local Lunch\r\nWelcome Drink â€¢ Lunch (Fried Rice or Fried Noodles) â€¢ Safety Equipment (Helmet & Boots) â€¢ Safety Briefing â€¢ Professional ATV Guide â€¢ Towel, Soap & Shampoo â€¢ Locker â€¢ Personal Insurance\r\n',32),(440,11,'Departure','Ubud Hotel to Denpasar Airport - Departure',32),(441,1,'Rajkot to Dwarka - Arrival & Transfer via Jamnagar Sightseeing','Pick from Rajkot Airport, then proceed to Dwarka, En-route visit â€“ Lakhota Lake & Bala Hanuman, Then Drive to Dwarka, Evening reach at Dwarka, check in, then evening visit Dwarkadhish Temple. Evening Visit Market for shopping, overnight stay at the Hotel.\r\n\r\n',33),(442,2,'Dwarka - Sightseeing','Dwarkadhish Temple â€“ Main temple of Lord Krishna, famous for its tall tower and flag rituals.\r\nGopi Talav â€“ Sacred pond linked to Krishna and Gopis, known for yellow soil.\r\nNageshwar Jyotirling â€“ One of the 12 Jyotirlingas of Lord Shiva.\r\nRukmini Temple â€“ Temple dedicated to Rukmini, located 2 km away.\r\nBet Dwarka â€“ Island believed to be Krishnaâ€™s residence.\r\nShivrajpur Beach â€“ Clean Blue Flag beach, ideal for relaxation and water activities.\r\nOvernight Stay Dwarka.\r\n',33),(443,3,'Dwarka to Somnath - Trasfer via Porbandar & Sightseeing','Today after breakfast drive to Somnath, En-route visit Porbandar â€“ Kirti Mandir & Sudama Temple, then drive Somnath Check in to hotel, and then visit Bhalka Tirth Temple, Attend Evening Aarti at Somnath Jyotirling (one of the first among the twelve Jyotirlings shrines of Shiva) Evening visit Light & Sound Show at Somnath Temple, Overnight stay at Hotel',33),(444,4,'Somnath to Diu - Day Trip','After breakfast drive to Diu, Visit Shri Gangeshwar Mahadev Temple, Diu Fort, Diu Museum, visit St Paul Church, Enjoy Beach & Beach activity at Nagoa Beach, then come to Somnath, Overnight at Somnath',33),(445,5,'Somnath to Rajkot - Transfer & Departure','Check out from Hotel, Drive to Rajkot, Drop at Rajkot\r\n\r\n',33),(446,1,'ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)','On arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.',34),(447,2,'GULMARG DAY TRIP FROM SRINAGAR','After breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summerÂ  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.Â Â ',34),(448,3,'SRINAGAR - PAHALGAM','After breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous SaffronÂ  growingÂ  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. Day at leisure. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam. Â Â ',34),(449,4,'PAHALGAM',' After breakfast one can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.     ',34),(450,5,'PAHALGAM â€“ CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT','After breakfast leave from hotel and check-in at houseboat. In evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.',34),(451,6,'CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT','After breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer toÂ Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.Â Â Â Â Â Â Â Â ',34),(452,1,'Arrival in Singapore â€“ City Orientation & Sentosa Island (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time) ','Upon arrival in Singapore, you will be warmly welcomed and transferred for a Singapore City Orientation Drive, offering a glimpse of the city\'s iconic landmarks and vibrant cityscape. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island and enjoy a scenic Cable Car ride, followed by the exciting Luge & Skyride experience. Conclude the day with the spectacular Wings of Time show before returning to your hotel for an overnight stay.',35),(453,2,'Night Safari Experience','Enjoy the day at leisure before heading out in the evening to visit the world-renowned Night Safari. Experience an exciting Tram Ride through the open-concept wildlife park, where you can observe fascinating nocturnal animals in their natural surroundings, making for a memorable wildlife adventure.',35),(454,3,'Universal Studios Singapore','Spend the day exploring Universal Studios Singapore, one of Asia\'s premier theme parks. ',35),(455,4,'Gardens by the Bay','Today, visit the iconic Gardens by the Bay and explore its two signature conservatories. Wander through the beautiful Flower Dome, showcasing exotic plants and seasonal floral displays, and discover the misty Cloud Forest, home to a magnificent indoor waterfall and lush tropical vegetation.',35),(456,5,'Departure from Singapore','After breakfast, check out from the hotel and enjoy a private transfer to Singapore Changi Airport for your onward flight, bringing your memorable Singapore holiday to a pleasant conclusion.',35),(457,1,'Arrival at the SIN Airport - Night Safari Experience','Upon arrival in Singapore, you will be warmly welcomed and transferred to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening visit the world-renowned Night Safari. Experience an exciting Tram Ride through the open-concept wildlife park, where you can observe fascinating nocturnal animals in their natural surroundings, making for a memorable wildlife adventure.',36),(458,2,'City Orientation & Sentosa Island (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time)','Have Breakfast at the hotel. and proceed for Singapore City Orientation Drive, offering a glimpse of the city\'s iconic landmarks and vibrant cityscape. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island and enjoy a scenic Cable Car ride , followed by the exciting Luge & Skyride experience. Conclude the day with the spectacular Wings of Time show before returning to your hotel for an overnight stay.',36),(459,3,'Universal Studios Singapore','Have breakfast at the hotel. Spend the day exploring Universal Studios Singapore, one of Asia\'s premier theme parks.',36),(460,4,'Gardens By The Bay','Have breakfast at the hotel. Today, visit the iconic Gardens By The Bay and explore its two signature conservatories. Wander through the beautiful Flower Dome, showcasing exotic plants and seasonal floral displays, and discover the misty Cloud Forest, home to a magnificent indoor waterfall and lush tropical vegetation.',36),(461,5,'Departure from Singapore','Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out. Enjoy a private transfer to Singapore Changi Airport for your onward flight.',36),(462,1,'Arrival at the SIN Airport','Arrival at the SIN Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. Evening you can explore nearby places on your own.',37),(463,1,'Arrival at the SIN Airport','Arrival at the SIN Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. Evening you can explore nearby places on your own.',38),(464,2,'City Orientation & Sentosa Island (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time)','Have Breakfast at the hotel. and proceed for Singapore City Orientation Drive, offering a glimpse of the city\'s iconic landmarks and vibrant cityscape. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island and enjoy a scenic Cable Car ride , followed by the exciting Luge & Skyride experience. Conclude the day with the spectacular Wings of Time show before returning to your hotel for an overnight stay.',37),(465,2,'City Orientation & Sentosa Island (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time)','Have Breakfast at the hotel. and proceed for Singapore City Orientation Drive, offering a glimpse of the city\'s iconic landmarks and vibrant cityscape. Later, proceed to Sentosa Island and enjoy a scenic Cable Car ride , followed by the exciting Luge & Skyride experience. Conclude the day with the spectacular Wings of Time show before returning to your hotel for an overnight stay.',38),(466,3,' Night Safari Experience','Have breakfast at the Hotel.  In the evening visit the world-renowned Night Safari. Experience an exciting Tram Ride through the open-concept wildlife park, where you can observe fascinating nocturnal animals in their natural surroundings, making for a memorable wildlife adventure.',38),(467,3,' Night Safari Experience','Have breakfast at the Hotel.  In the evening visit the world-renowned Night Safari. Experience an exciting Tram Ride through the open-concept wildlife park, where you can observe fascinating nocturnal animals in their natural surroundings, making for a memorable wildlife adventure.',37),(468,4,'Universal Studios Singapore','Have breakfast at the hotel. Spend the day exploring Universal Studios Singapore, one of Asia\'s premier theme parks.',38),(469,4,'Universal Studios Singapore','Have breakfast at the hotel. Spend the day exploring Universal Studios Singapore, one of Asia\'s premier theme parks.',37),(470,5,'Gardens By The Bay','Have breakfast at the hotel. Today, visit the iconic Gardens By The Bay and explore its two signature conservatories. Wander through the beautiful Flower Dome, showcasing exotic plants and seasonal floral displays, and discover the misty Cloud Forest, home to a magnificent indoor waterfall and lush tropical vegetation.',37),(471,5,'Gardens By The Bay','Have breakfast at the hotel. Today, visit the iconic Gardens By The Bay and explore its two signature conservatories. Wander through the beautiful Flower Dome, showcasing exotic plants and seasonal floral displays, and discover the misty Cloud Forest, home to a magnificent indoor waterfall and lush tropical vegetation.',38),(472,1,' Istanbul - Arrival â€“ Istanbul: Dinner Cruise on Bosphorus,Â Shared Basis Transfer','Welcome to Istanbul! Meet our team at the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in and have a leisure day.\r\n\r\nEvening Visit:  Transfer to cruise port for Night Show on Bosphorus. Set Menu dinner + soft drinks.\r\n\r\nInclusions\r\nTwo-way shared (SIC) hotel transfers (pick-up & drop-off)\r\n3-hour Bosphorus dinner cruise\r\nSet menu dinner\r\nUnlimited soft drinks\r\nTurkish night show with music and dance performances\r\nOnboard lighting and scenic night views',39),(473,2,' Istanbul CityÂ TourÂ without Lunch with Private Transfer with Guide','Breakfast at the Hotel.\r\n\r\nWelcome to Istanbul â€” the city where continents meet, empires rose, and cultures blend effortlessly.\r\nThis full-day private tour gives first-time visitors the perfect mix of heritage, scenery, and serenity â€” from the dazzling domes of old Istanbul to the glittering shores of the Bosporus.\r\nWith your own private car and driver, explore iconic landmarks, stop for photos where you like, and enjoy the freedom to experience Istanbul at your own pace.\r\n\r\nVisit: Topkapi Palace,Hagia Sophia,Blue Mosque, Grand Bazaar, Bosporus Coastal Drive,Camlica Hill (Asian Side), Golden Horn & Old City Drive\r\n\r\nDuration: Approx. 08 Hours \r\nReporting Time: 08.30 AM\r\nStart Time: 09:00 AM\r\nTour Type: Private\r\nStart/End Point: City Centre Hotel , Istanbul \r\n\r\nTour Inclusions\r\nPrivate, air-conditioned vehicle (8 hours at disposal)\r\nProfessional chauffeur\r\nWithout Entry ticket\r\nSightseeing and photo stops as per itinerary\r\nPick-up and drop-off from hotel',39),(474,3,' Istanbul: Day Trip to the Princes\' Islands (Shared transfer)','Hotel pickup from Istanbul areas Transfer to the pier and board the ferryScenic cruise across the Marmara Sea to the Princes\' Islands\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nArrive at BÃ¼yÃ¼kada, the largest of the Princes\' Islands\r\n\r\nGuided walking tour through the island\'s main square and charming streets\r\n\r\nAdmire Victorian-era mansions, colorful summer houses, beaches, and pinewood landscapes\r\n\r\nEnjoy panoramic bay and coastal views\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nLunch at a local restaurant on BÃ¼yÃ¼kada (included)\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFree time to explore the island at your own pace\r\n\r\nExperience the relaxed local atmosphere near the village square\r\n\r\nTake photos of the flower-covered cottages and scenic waterfront\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nFerry cruise back across the Marmara Sea to Istanbul\r\n\r\nTransfer to your hotel\r\n\r\nHotel drop-off at central city locations\r\n\r\nInclusions: Hotel pickup & drop-off, ferry cruise, local expert guide,\r\n\r\nExclusions: Drinks during lunch, personal expenses\r\n\r\nDuration: Full Day (Approx. 8â€“10 hours)',39),(475,4,'Istanbul to Cappadocia by flight','Breakfast at the Hotel.\r\n\r\nAccording to your flight time, check out from your hotel and transfer to the airport (Flight cost is not included). Arrive at Kayseri Airport to hotel. Transfer private.',39),(476,5,'Cappadocia Full-DayÂ Private TransferÂ RedÂ TourÂ without Lunch , With guide','Breakfast at the Hotel.\r\n\r\nWelcome to Cappadocia, Turkeyâ€™s most magical landscape â€” a land of ancient valleys, volcanic wonders, and storybook towns.\r\nThis 8-hour private tour is designed for travellers who love nature, open skies, and photography, combining the regionâ€™s legendary fairy chimneys with lesser-known scenic viewpoints and tranquil valleys. No fixed schedules, no crowded buses â€” just your private vehicle, plenty of time to explore, and endless opportunities to stop where the light and landscape inspire you.\r\nVisit: Devrent Valley (Imagination Valley),Pasabag Valley (Monks Valley),Avanos â€“ Red River Town (KÄ±zÄ±lÄ±rmak River),Zelve Open-Air Museum,Love Valley,\r\nGÃ¶reme Panorama Point,Pigeon Valley\r\n\r\nDuration: Approx. 08 Hours \r\nStart Time: 10:00 AM\r\nTour Type: Private Vehicle with Driver & Entrance Fees\r\nTour Start/End Point: Cappadocia Hotel\r\n\r\nEnglish Speking Guide \r\n\r\nReturn Transfer\r\nAfter a full day of exploration, your driver will take you comfortably back to your hotel â€” filled with memories of fairy chimneys, red canyons, and golden Cappadocian light.\r\n\r\nInclusions\r\nPrivate air-conditioned vehicle (8 hours at disposal)\r\nProfessional driver\r\nHotel pick-up and drop-off',39),(477,6,' Cappadocia: GreenÂ TourÂ without Lunch & Hotel PickupÂ (Private Transfer) with GuideÂ ','Breakfast at the Hotel.\r\n\r\nCappadocia Green Region Private Tour (8 Hours | Vehicle at Disposal)\r\n\r\nBreathe in the pure Cappadocian air as you explore a world where volcanic landscapes meet lush canyons and ancient cave cities.\r\n\r\nThis full-day private journey brings together underground history, scenic hiking trails, tranquil valleys, and lake viewpoints, offering the perfect balance of adventure and serenity. With your private car and driver at disposal, stop where you wish, take your time, and capture Cappadociaâ€™s soul â€” from its secret caves to its riverside cliffs.\r\n\r\nVisit: KaymaklÄ± Underground City,Ihlara Valley,BelisÄ±rma Riverside,Selime Monastery,Yaprakhisar Viewpoint (Star Wars Valley),Nar Lake,Pigeon Valley (Panoramic Viewpoint)\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nTour Start Time: 10:00 AM\r\n\r\nDuration: 08 Hrs\r\n\r\nTour Type: Private Vehicle with Driver & Entrance Fees\r\n\r\nTour Start/End Point: Istanbul Hotel\r\n\r\n English Speking Guide \r\n\r\nVISIT\r\n\r\nKaymaklÄ± Underground City\r\n\r\nBegin your journey by descending into the KaymaklÄ± Underground City, one of Cappadociaâ€™s most fascinating archaeological sites.\r\n\r\nBuilt centuries ago as a hidden refuge, itâ€™s a maze of tunnels, kitchens, stables, and chapels carved deep into the volcanic rock.\r\n\r\nWalk through ancient passageways and imagine life underground â€” cool, mysterious, and ingeniously designed.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: A photo at the round stone door (used to seal tunnels) â€” your gateway to history.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nIhlara Valley (Nature Walk Along the River)\r\n\r\nNext, drive to the breathtaking Ihlara Valley, a lush canyon carved by the Melendiz River.\r\n\r\nWalk part of the trail (2â€“3 km, flexible) under towering cliffs and through greenery, discovering hidden cave churches and natural rock formations along the way.\r\n\r\nThe gentle sound of flowing water and birdsong makes this one of the most peaceful places in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: Capture the winding river framed by cliffs and greenery â€” natureâ€™s calm masterpiece.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nBelisÄ±rma Riverside Stop (Optional Coffee Break)\r\n\r\nPause at BelisÄ±rma Village, a riverside village in the heart of Ihlara Valley.\r\n\r\nEnjoy a refreshing Turkish tea or coffee beside the Melendiz River as ducks swim past and the valley breeze cools you down.\r\n\r\nItâ€™s the perfect rest stop to absorb the tranquil beauty of Cappadociaâ€™s greenest corner.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: A cup of Turkish tea by the water, with reflections of the valley behind.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nSelime Monastery\r\n\r\nContinue to the monumental Selime Monastery, a massive rock-cut complex that looks like a natural fortress.\r\n\r\nThis is Cappadociaâ€™s largest monastic site, complete with ancient chapels, monksâ€™ quarters, and a grand cathedral-like chamber.\r\n\r\nFrom the upper level, enjoy sweeping views of the valley below â€” itâ€™s where history and landscape meet in perfect harmony.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: Capture yourself framed by the arched cave windows overlooking the dramatic landscape.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nYaprakhisar Viewpoint (Star Wars Valley)\r\n\r\nJust beyond Selime lies Yaprakhisar Village, one of Cappadociaâ€™s most cinematic viewpoints â€” the backdrop for scenes from Star Wars.\r\n\r\nThe cone-shaped formations and dramatic cliffs look like another planet.\r\n\r\nItâ€™s a must for photographers and anyone looking for a â€œwowâ€ view thatâ€™s off the beaten path.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: A panoramic shot of the â€œStar Wars-styleâ€ rock towers rising above the plains â€” unreal and unforgettable.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nNar Lake\r\n\r\nHead next to Nar Lake, a hidden gem located inside a volcanic crater near Derinkuyu.\r\n\r\nThe lakeâ€™s emerald-blue water surrounded by steep crater walls makes it one of the regionâ€™s most unique and peaceful nature stops.\r\n\r\nItâ€™s an ideal place to pause, breathe, and enjoy the raw beauty of Cappadociaâ€™s volcanic past.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: The reflection of the sky in Nar Lakeâ€™s still waters â€” calm, mysterious, and deeply photogenic.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nPigeon Valley (Panoramic Viewpoint)\r\n\r\nConclude your journey at the Pigeon Valley viewpoint, one of Cappadociaâ€™s most iconic natural lookouts.\r\n\r\nAdmire the dovecotes carved into the cliffs, the lush valley stretching below, and Uchisar Castle rising proudly on the horizon.\r\n\r\nItâ€™s the perfect finale to a day filled with adventure and tranquility.\r\n\r\nInstagram Moment: A wide shot with pigeons flying over the valley â€” nature, architecture, and movement in one frame.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nReturn Transfer\r\n\r\nAfter a day of breathtaking views and natural discoveries, relax in your private vehicle as your driver takes you comfortably back to your hotel.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nInclusions\r\n\r\nPrivate air-conditioned vehicle (8 hours at disposal)\r\n\r\nProfessional driver\r\n\r\nEntrance fees for scheduled sites\r\n\r\nHotel pick-up and drop-off',39),(478,7,'CappadociaÂ to Istanbul by flight','Breakfast at the Hotel.\r\n\r\nAccording to your flight schedule, check out from your hotel and transfer to the airport to catch your return flight to India.',39),(490,1,'Madurai - Rameshwaram Arrival','On arrival at the Madurai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Rameswaram. On arrival check in at the hotel, after fresh-n-up full day temple tour including Ramanathaswamy, this magnificent temple is one of the 12 Jyotirlingas situated in different parts of India. Ramanathaswamy Temple also has its name in history books as it has the largest hallway anywhere in India. The construction of Ramanathaswamy Temple which was started in the 12th century was contributed to by many rulers. During its construction period, many dynasties came and fell and each of them put their input into the temple. The list of unique features in its construction seems to be endless. There is this huge hallway that is of approximately 1220 meters in length. Throughout the length of the hall, there are brilliantly carved pillars, the alignment of which will leave you totally mesmerized. The 54 meter tall Gopuram has become the symbol of divinity in the heart of many pilgrims; such is the beauty and presence of it. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.',40),(491,2,'Rameshwaram Day 02','After breakfast sightseeing of Rameshwaram- Visit Sri Ramanatha Swamy temple, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Museum, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman temple, Villoondi Theertham etc. Overnight at the Resort/hotel',40),(492,3,'Rameswaram to Madurai','Morning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive to Madurai. On Arrival check-in at Hotel. Overnight stay at Hotel.',40),(493,4,'Madurai day 2','After Breakfast, Visit the famous Madurai Meenakshi Temple. There are four entrances to this amazing temple complex set in six hectares. Hit one of the stone pillars in the complex with any hard object and feel incredible on hearing sweet metal sounds. It is known as musical pillars. The total number of pillars in the temple is a staggering one thousand. Sightseeing inclusive of Thirumalai Nayak palace, Gandhi Museum and flower market.Â  Overnight stay at hotel/resort.',40),(494,5,'Madurai Departure','Morning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Madurai international Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.',40),(495,1,'Arrival in Kuta | + Leisure day','Arrive in Kuta and check in to your hotel. Spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing after your journey. ',41),(496,2,'Water sports ( Para salling,Banana,Boat Jet ski ) + Uluwatu Temple Entrance ticket and transfers','Enjoy an exciting day of water sports, including parasailing, a banana boat ride, and a Jet Ski experience. Later, visit the iconic Uluwatu Temple, perched on a dramatic cliff overlooking the Indian Ocean. The tour includes entrance tickets and comfortable round-trip transfers.',41),(497,3,'Nusa Penida West tour - Kelingking Beach, Angel Bilabong, Broken Bay, Crystal Beach with local lunch','Embark on a full-day Nusa Penida West Island tour, visiting some of the island\'s most breathtaking attractions, including Kelingking Beach, Angel\'s Billabong, Broken Bay, and Crystal Bay. A delicious local lunch is included, along with all necessary transfers for a hassle-free experience.',41),(498,4,'Inter Hotel transfers + Ubud palace +Art marketÂ  + Kintamani Coffee Plantation + Tegenungan Waterfall + Bali swing+ Entrance ticket with transfers','After checking out, transfer to your hotel in Ubud while enjoying sightseeing along the way. Visit the historic Ubud Palace and the vibrant Ubud Art Market, followed by a stop at a Kintamani Coffee Plantation to learn about Bali\'s famous coffee. Continue to the scenic Tegenungan Waterfall and experience the thrilling Bali Swing. Entrance tickets and transfers are included.',41),(499,5,'Ulun Danu (Bedugul) +Tanha Lot Sunset tour Â Entrance ticket with transfers','Discover the natural beauty and cultural heritage of Bali with a visit to the picturesque Ulun Danu Beratan Temple in Bedugul. In the evening, head to the famous Tanah Lot Temple to witness a spectacular sunset over the ocean. The tour includes entrance tickets and round-trip transfers.',41),(500,6,'ATV ride Tandem with transfers','Experience an adrenaline-filled ATV tandem ride through Bali\'s scenic countryside, passing through lush landscapes, muddy tracks, and picturesque villages. Round-trip hotel transfers are included for your convenience.',41),(501,7,'Departure','Check out from your hotel and enjoy a comfortable transfer to the airport for your departure, taking home unforgettable memories of your Bali vacation.',41),(502,1,' TRANSFER FROM AIRPORT TO HOTEL. REST AND EVENING TOKYO SKYTREE TICKET AND  TOKYO ORIENTATION TOUR ','Upon arrival in Tokyo, you will be greeted at the airport and transferred to your hotel. After checking in, take some time to relax and recover from your journey. In the evening, enjoy a visit to the iconic Tokyo Skytree with included admission tickets, followed by a Tokyo orientation tour that introduces you to the city\'s vibrant neighborhoods, famous landmarks, and unique culture.',42),(503,2,' TEAMLAB PLANETS TICKET AND EVENING SUMO SHOW TOKYO TICKET','After breakfast, visit the world-renowned teamLab Planets, an immersive digital art museum where interactive light, water, and sensory installations create a truly unique experience. Spend the remainder of the day exploring Tokyo at your own pace before attending an exciting Evening Sumo Show, where you will witness Japan\'s traditional national sport and gain insight into its fascinating history and cultural significance.',42),(504,3,'DAY TRIP TO MT FUJI HAKONE WITH ROPEWAY TICKET AND LAKE ASHI CRUISE TICKET  ','Today, embark on a full-day excursion to the scenic Mt. Fuji and Hakone region. Enjoy spectacular views as you travel through the beautiful countryside. Your tour includes a ride on the Hakone Ropeway, offering panoramic vistas of volcanic landscapes and surrounding mountains, followed by a relaxing Lake Ashi Cruise, where you can admire the stunning scenery and, weather permitting, magnificent views of Mt. Fuji. Return to Tokyo in the evening after a memorable day of sightseeing.',42),(505,4,'Tokyo to Kyoto by Bullet Train & Tea Ceremony ','After breakfast, check out from your hotel and enjoy a private transfer to Tokyo Train Station. Board your 2nd Class Shinkansen (Bullet Train) to Kyoto, experiencing one of the world\'s fastest and most comfortable rail journeys. Upon arrival, you will be transferred to your hotel for check-in. In the evening, immerse yourself in Japanese culture with a traditional Chayu Tea Ceremony, followed by a city tour showcasing Kyoto\'s historic streets, cultural heritage, and timeless charm.',42),(506,5,'KYOTO TO OSAKA TRANSFER ENROUTE NARA, ARASHIYAMA TOUR  ','After breakfast and check-out, travel from Kyoto to Osaka with sightseeing en route. Visit the historic city of Nara, home to ancient temples and the famous free-roaming deer, before continuing to the picturesque district of Arashiyama, renowned for its scenic beauty, iconic Bamboo Grove, and tranquil surroundings. After exploring these cultural highlights, continue to Osaka and check in to your hotel.',42),(507,6,' OSAKA CITY TOUR WITH OSAKA CASTLE & UMEDA SKY BUILDING TICKETS  ','Following breakfast, enjoy a guided city tour of Osaka, one of Japan\'s most dynamic and vibrant cities. Visit the magnificent Osaka Castle, a symbol of the city\'s rich history, and admire panoramic views from the Umeda Sky Building, one of Osaka\'s most famous architectural landmarks. The remainder of the day is free for shopping, local dining, or exploring the city\'s lively entertainment districts at your own pace.',42),(508,7,'OSAKA HOTEL TO AIRPORT TRANSFER ON PVT BASIS (ONE WAY)  ','After breakfast, check out from your hotel and enjoy a private transfer to Osaka Airport for your onward flight. Depart with wonderful memories of your unforgettable journey through Japan, filled with cultural experiences, scenic landscapes, and vibrant city life.',42),(509,1,'Arrival in SIN ','â€¢ Transfer from Changi International Airport to the BOOKED HOTEL [with Private transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL to Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour [with SIC transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour to the BOOKED HOTEL  [with SIC transport]',43),(510,2,'Universal Studios Tour (Universal Studio Ticket) ','â€¢ Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL to Universal Studios Tour [with SIC transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Universal Studios Tour to the BOOKED HOTEL [with SIC transport]',43),(511,3,'Transfer from SIN hotel to SIN airport  and then transfer from KUL airport to KUL booked hotel ','Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL to Changi International Airport [with Private transport] \r\nTransfer from KLIA-Airport to the BOOKED HOTEL  [with Private transport]',43),(512,4,'KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) (KL Tower Observation Deck)','â€¢ Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL  to KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) [with Private transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) to the BOOKED HOTEL  [with Private transport]',43),(513,5,'Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) (Enroute Batu Caves (30 mins photostop)','â€¢ Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL to Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) [with SIC transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) to the BOOKED HOTEL  [with SIC transport]',43),(514,6,'Transfer from KUL hotel to KUL Airport ','â€¢ Transfer from the BOOKED HOTEL to KLIA-Airport [with Private transport]',43),(515,1,'Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)','Arrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Throughout the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. \r\n\r\nOvernight stay in Hotel.\r\n\r\n',44),(516,2,'Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02','Morning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel .\r\n\r\n',44),(517,3,'Munnar - Thekkady','Morning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit elephant junction, spice plantations. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.',44),(518,4,' Thekkady to Alleppey','Morning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Overnight stay at same hotel.',44),(519,5,'Alleppey to Kovalam','Morning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Kovalam is a premier beach destination in Kerala known for its three adjacent crescent-shaped beachesâ€”Lighthouse Beach, Hawa Beach, and Samudra Beachâ€”which are perfect for swimming, water sports, and sunset views. Enjoy surfing, snorkelling, and swimming at Lighthouse Beach. Experience traditional Kerala Ayurvedic treatments, which are popular in many local centres/resorts. Enjoy fresh seafood at the numerous beachfront cafes and restaurants. Evening proceed for Beach. Overnight stay at Kovalam. ',44),(520,6,'Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam','Morning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, NapierÂ  Museum. Overnight stay at Kovalam. ',44),(521,7,' Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop','Morning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.',44),(522,1,' ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE','You will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the hotel . In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikara s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Overnight in hotel .',45),(523,2,'DAY TRIP TO SONAMARG','Morning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Overnight in deluxe hotel .',45),(524,3,'DAY TRIPÂ  Â TO GULMARGÂ ','Morning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 3 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar . Overnight in hotel .\r\n',45),(525,4,'SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM','After breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\n',45),(526,5,'PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR','After breakfast proceed to Srinagar . Afternoon sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Overnight in hotel .',45),(527,6,'DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT','After breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.',45),(528,1,'ARRIVE SRINAGAR - PAHALGAMÂ ','Upon arrival you will be met by our representative at the Srinagar Airport . He will assist you and transfer you\r\nto Pahalgam . Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered\r\nin about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old\r\ntemple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Overnight in hotel .',46),(529,2,'DAY IN PAHALGAM','After breakfast enjoy full day in Pahalgam . Enjoy Aru , betaab and chandanwari valley by union cab . Dinner and Overnight stay in hotel . ',46),(530,3,'PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR','After breakfast proceed to Srinagar . Afternoon sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Overnight in houseboat  .',46),(531,4,'DAY TRIP TO SONAMARG Â ','Morning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Overnight in deluxe hotel .',46),(532,5,'DAY TRIPÂ  Â TO GULMARGÂ ','Morning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 3 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar . Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\n\r\nî„“\r\n',46),(533,6,'DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT','After breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\n',46),(534,1,'Day 1 | Auckland','Welcome to Auckland!! Auckland is New Zealand\'s largest city and main transport hub. The region is home to some 1.5 million people and is also the largest Polynesian city in the world. Aucklandâ€™s diverse landscapes provide countless opportunities to get immersed in nature. More than just a city, Auckland is a whole region full of things to see and do. Best of all, with so many experiences close by itâ€™s easy to hop from one adventure to the next. On arrival in Auckland, you will be met & privately transferred to a hotel in Auckland. ',47),(535,2,'Day 2 | Rotorua','Enjoy breakfast at the hotel. Todayâ€™s coach tour takes you through the rolling green hills to the iconic Hobbiton Movie Set.  See where the Lord of the Rings and Hobbit movies were filmed as your tour guide shares behind-the-scenes tales. Youâ€™ll see sights like Hobbit Holes, the Mill, and The Green Dragon Inn, and learn how farmland was transformed into a living, breathing piece of Middle-earth.  After exploring Hobbiton, tuck into a delicious lunch in the Party Marquee before continuing to Rotorua.',47),(536,3,'Day 3 | Rotorua','Enjoy breakfast at hotel. Rotorua is surrounded by a fascinating geothermal landscape with its unique steam vents, spouting geysers and bubbling mud pool set alongside freshwater lakes and majestic native forests. It is also a region immersed in fascinating Maori myths and legends.\r\nYou will be transported to Wai-O-Tapu Geothermal Wonderland for a two hour visit today.   Wai-O-Tapu is considered to be New Zealandâ€™s most colourful and diverse geothermal sightseeing attraction.  This evening youâ€™ll be transported to Te Puia for an Indigenous Evening Experience including a buffet dinner and cultural performance. The evening culminates with hot chocolate and pudding on the geyser terrace. \r\n ',47),(537,4,'Day 4 | Christchurch','Depart on your domestic flight to Christchurch. \r\nFlight Time Rotorua to Christchurch is approx. 2 hours\r\nChristchurch is set between the deep blue Pacific Ocean and the mighty snow-capped Southern Alps.  This is a vibrant, ever-changing city with inner city parks and gardens delightfully interwoven by the meandering Avon River. Upon arrival at Christchurch transfer on own to your hotel & later head to enjoy Christchurch Tram Tour which is a charming way to explore the heart of Christchurch. The historic tram rides through the city offer a unique perspective on Christchurchâ€™s attractions, history, and vibrant street life. Next, we enjoy â€œPunting on the Avon Riverâ€ Punting involves a flat-bottomed boat (the punt) guided by a punter using a long pole to propel the boat through the water. Itâ€™s a slow and gentle way to travel, perfect for taking in the surroundings and enjoying a leisurely ride.',47),(538,5,'Day 5 | Greymouth','You will be transported to the Christchurch Railway Station for the Tranz Alpine train crossing the vast expanses of the Canterbury Plains, through the dramatic gorge of the Waimakariri River to Arthurâ€™s Pass National Park. On arrival in Greymouth, you will be met and transferred to the Punakaiki Pancake Rocks and Blowholes for a short self-guided walk to view the fascinating pancake-shaped rock formations before being delivered to your accommodation.  ',47),(539,6,'Day 6 | Franz Josef','This morning, youâ€™ll be transferred to Shantytown Heritage Park for a sense of what it was like to live in New Zealand during the gold rush before returning to Greymouth for your transfer to Glacier Country.  The temperate climate at a low altitude makes Franz Josef and Fox Glaciers among the most convenient to visit in the world.  Steep valleys bear scars from where glaciers have retreated and advanced over millennia and here, the ice age is still underway.  ',47),(540,7,'Day 7 | Queenstown','This morning you will be collected from your accommodation for your transfer through wilderness towns, waterfalls and river scenery on the journey to Queenstown.  Magnificent vistas and majestic mountains dominate this compact alpine resort town and with such an expansive natural physical environment it is not surprising that Queenstown has been described as the Adventure Capital of the World. The Skyline Gondola base is situated a short five-minute walk from central Queenstown. Take in the stunning views as you ride the Skyline Gondola cable car high above Queenstown and Lake Wakatipu to the top of Bobâ€™s Peak. The best views in the region are found here, spread out in a spectacular 220-degree panorama with breath taking views of Coronet Peak, The Remarkables mountain range and across Lake Wakatipu to Cecil and Walter Peak. ',47),(541,8,'Day 8 | Queenstown','Enjoy breakfast at hotel. Queenstown is often dubbed the \"Adventure Capital of New Zealandâ€ & offers a breathtaking & wide range of activities (as per below at additional cost)\r\nBungee Jumping\r\nSkydiving\r\nZip-lining\r\nGlenorchy & Paradise Explorer Tour\r\nArrowtown Wanaka Highlights Tour\r\nGibbston Valley Wine Tours\r\nLater in the afternoon we proceed for 1 Hr Jet Boat Ride on Shotover & Kawarau River. Depart from the heart of Queenstown, and climb aboard the big yellow jet boat at the Main Town Pier. Hold on tight as you accelerate across the water and feel the exhilaration of a high-powered twin-engine boat that powers across Lake Wakatipu. Experience the twists and spins as you enter the Kawarau River and race past rocks and under bridges at speeds of up to 95 kilometers per hour.',47),(542,9,'Day 9 | Queenstown','Fiordland is one of the worldâ€™s last great wildernesses.  Today\'s stunning tour takes you past mirror lakes and waterfalls into Milford Sound, carved by ice age glaciers and famously described as the eighth wonder of the world. On arrival, board your vessel for a cruise of the fiord surrounded by towering mountains and cliffs that plunge into the sea.  Feel the refreshing spray of a waterfall as you cruise close to sheer rock faces before returning to shore.  After a big day out, reflect on memories of a lifetime on your coach return to downtown Queenstown. Lunch is included. ',47),(543,10,'Day 10 | Christchurch','Departing Queenstown, your passionate driver guide will bring todays journey to life, sharing stories and rich background knowledge. Pass through the stunning Kawarau Gorge, fruit and wine growing region of Cromwell, following beautiful Lake Dunstan and through the dramatic Lindis Pass. Travel the vast plains of the Mackenzie district alongside magnificent turquoise blue lake framed by Aoraki Mt Cook and the spectacular Southern Alps to Mt Cook Village where you have some free time. Leaving Mt Cook itâ€™s not hard to see why many Lord of the Rings scenes were filmed nearby. Your driver guide will point them out on the journey to Lake Tekapo where you will make a stop close to the popular Church of the Good Shepherd before continuing on through the amazing countryside to Christchurch.',47),(544,11,'Day 11 | Christchurch','Transfer to Christchurch Airport for your flight to onward destination. ',47);
/*!40000 ALTER TABLE `itinerary_days` ENABLE KEYS */;
UNLOCK TABLES;

