Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n',66,0,'2024-05-21 17:08:57','2024-10-23 13:17:24'),(49,693,344,15510,8,0,0,'2024-06-18','2024-06-25',NULL,'Thailand Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (18 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (19 Jun)	TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha ( With Guide ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 )  \r\nTOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom (8 Adults) 1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 )\r\n\r\n3rd Day (20 Jun)	TOURS - EX Phuket - Private Land Transfer for Phi Phi Island Tour Big Boat ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Lunch Entrance ( Exclude NPF )  8 Adults \r\n\r\n4th Day (21 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n5th Day (22 Jun)	TOURS - EX KRABI - Private Land Transfer for Krabi 4 Island Tour Long Tailed ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 )\r\n\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour 	Krabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Entrance ( Exclude NPF ) 8 Adults \r\n\r\n6th Day (23 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Krabi APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN KBV (Max 9 + Luggage)\r\n \r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n7th Day (24 Jun)	TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) \r\n	\r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  8 Adults\r\n \r\n8th Day (25 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage)\r\n',100650,47797,'\r\nEconomy Class airfare.\r\nStay for 7 nights in above mentioned hotels\r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nAll tours and sightseeing on  pvt basis.\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n\r\n\r\n','Any type of personal expensesÂ \r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','',0,'Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability\r\nDEL-HKT: 20kg baggage\r\nKBV-BKK: 25kg baggage\r\nBKK-DEL: 25kg baggage',0,0,'2024-06-06 15:20:43','2024-06-06 15:20:43'),(50,695,345,15526,3,0,0,'2024-06-29','2024-07-04',NULL,'Kashmir Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikara s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n',96900,28300,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Stay at the booked hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Shikara Ride\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ NON A/C CRYSTA (PVT)\r\n','* Any type of personal expense.\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.',66,0,'2024-06-06 15:46:15','2024-10-23 13:25:23'),(51,700,347,15496,2,0,0,'2024-06-22','2024-06-27',NULL,'Kasol & Manali Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n22nd June: Arrival and Drive to Kasol\r\n\r\n9:30 AM: Pick up from Ambala station.\r\nDrive from Ambala to Kasol (approx. 7 hours, including breaks).\r\nCheck-in at hotel in Kasol.\r\nRelax and explore the local area (if time allows)\r\n\r\n23rd June: Kasol Sightseeing (very less places are there for sightseeing)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel.\r\nExplore Kasol (visit Chalal village, walk along Parvati River).\r\nLunch at a local cafe at your own.\r\nVisit Manikaran Sahib Gurudwara and hot springs.\r\nLeisure time (shopping, relax at the cafÃ©).\r\nDinner (At your own) and relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\n24th June: Kasol to Manali\r\nBreakfast at the hotel.\r\nDrive from Kasol to Manali (approx. 3 hours).\r\nCheck-in at the hotel in Manali.\r\nLocal sightseeing (Hadimba Temple, Manu Temple, Vashisht Hot Water Springs) at your own.\r\nExplore Mall Road, shopping, and dinner at your own.\r\n\r\n25th June: Manali Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the hotel.\r\nFull day excursion to Solang Valley (adventure activities like paragliding, ropeway, etc.).\r\nReturn to Manali, rest at the hotel.\r\nVisit Old Manali (cafe hopping, shopping).\r\nDinner at your own and relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\n26th June: Manali Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the hotel.\r\nExcursion to Rohtang Pass (if open, advance permit required).\r\nLunch - Eat at a local eatery at your own.\r\nVisit Naggar Castle and Nicholas Roerich Art Gallery.\r\nReturn to Manali, free time for leisure.\r\nDinner at your own and relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\n27th June: Departure\r\nBreakfast at the hotel.\r\nDrive from Manali to Ambala station (approx. 8 hours).\r\nDrop at Ambala station for onward journey.\r\n',0,0,'Daily Breakfast.\r\n2 Nights stay in Kasol.\r\n3 Nights stay in Manali.\r\nRohtang Pass\r\nPrivate Transfers in Swift Dezire for 6 days.','Any other meal other than the mentioned one.\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions.','',0,'Hotel/rooms are subject to availability. ',66,0,'2024-06-15 00:56:49','2024-10-23 12:44:18'),(52,703,348,15539,3,0,0,'2024-06-25','2024-07-30',NULL,'Ooty Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 (25 Jun 2024 - Tuesday) Banglore Arrival to Mysore \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nArrival At Bangalore, Proceed to mysore Check in at Hotel. Mysore (or Mysuru), a city in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Visit Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo,  Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. . \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Fortune JP Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2024 - Wednesday) Mysore to Coorg \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Fortune JP Palace\r\nTransfers - Mysore to Coorg\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Coorg, which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg   (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2024 - Thrusday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 2 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat, Madikeri Fort, Dubare Elephant Camp.visit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan monasteries of India and allows visitors to learn in depth about Tibetan religion and culture. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg   (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (28 Jun 2024 - Friday) Coorg to Ooty \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg \r\nTransfers - Coorg to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty ,popularly known as the \'Queen of Hill Stations\' is nestled in the Nilgiri hills in Tamil Nadu. The lush green tea plantations, the vast meadows, the towering mountains, dense pine and eucalyptus trees, and serene lakes make Ooty a prominent part of any bucket.Overnight stay at Ooty.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Accord Highland Hotel  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29 Jun 2024 - Saturday) Ooty Sightseeing Day 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Accord Highland Hotel \r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory). Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The  Accord Highland Hotel (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (30 Jun 2024 - Sunday) Coimbatore Departure Transfer \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Accord Highland Hotel \r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Coimbatore Departure Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel and proceed to Coimbatore for Departure ',0,0,'Economy class airfare. \r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n','All those which are not mentioned above \r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc \r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature ','',0,'Airfare is dynamic.\r\nHotels/Rooms are subject to availability.',0,0,'2024-06-21 13:23:07','2024-06-21 13:23:07'),(53,710,352,2326,3,0,0,'2024-07-12','2024-07-19',NULL,'Himachal Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\n12 July : Pickup from Chandigarh Airport and drop to Shimla\r\n12th, 13th and 14th July in Shimla for a wedding \r\n15 July : Drive from Shimla to Manali, visit local market (if time permits)\r\n16 July : Trip to Solang Valley and Rohtang pass\r\n17 July : Local sightseeing, which includes a visit to the Hadimba Temple, Manali Nature Park and Mall Road\r\n18 July : A drive to Manikaran for its hot springs and Gurudwara Sahib, followed by a visit to the Kullu Shawl Factory\r\n19 July : Departure from Manali to Chandigarh Airport\r\n\r\n',42000,6473,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Pickup and drop as mentioned\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned hotels or similar\r\n* Daily Breakfast As per hotel policy( Buffet or Room Service)\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta & Swift Dezire\r\n* Toll and taxes.\r\n* Parking charges.\r\n* Driver allowances.\r\n* Local Transfers & sightseeing by mentioned vehicle Innova Crysta\r\n* Shimla to Chandigarh transfer for 1 pax by Swift Dezire\r\n ','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2024-06-29 12:39:08','2024-10-23 13:35:00'),(54,718,358,15500,2,0,0,'2024-06-25','2024-07-02',NULL,'Swiss Paris',NULL,'Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Upon arrival in Montreux, check-in at the hotel and relax. In evening, explore near by places on your own. \r\n\r\nDay 2: After breakfast, leave for Montreux train station. Board the train to Interlaken . Check-in at hotel and relax.  \r\n\r\nDay 3: After breakfast, leave for the day trip to Jungfraujoch -Top of the Europe. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4: After breakfast, leave for Interlaken train station. Board the train to Lucerne. Check-in at hotel and relax. In \r\n            evening, you can pay a visit to the Chapel Bridge, Lake Lucerne Cruise or the Lion Monument (on your own \r\n            with swiss pass).  Shopaholics can here shop at near by places. \r\n\r\nDay 5: After breakfast, leave for mesmerizing excursion to Mt. Titlis. After returning, relax at hotel. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 6: After breakfast, leave for the Lucerne train station. Board the train to Zurich and enjoy the scenic beauty of \r\n            Switzerland on the way. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Get some rest and then pamper yourself with \r\n            shopping at local places. \r\n\r\nDay 7: After breakfast, leave for Rhine Falls, FIFA World Football Museum or the Swiss National Museum Tour from \r\n             Zurich (on your own with swiss pass )\r\n\r\nDay 7: After breakfast, check-out from hotel. It\'s time to bid Good Bye to your Switzerland trip. Leave for \r\n            airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Delhi. ',121851,29224,'Economy class airfare\r\n7N stay in the mentioned hotels with daily breakfast\r\n2nd Class Sector Reservation in Golden Pass (From Montreux to Intelaken @ 12:34-15:50)\r\nInterlaken: Excursion to Mt. Jungfrau with Swiss Pass from Interlaken OST\r\nLucerne: Lake Lucerne Cruise / Chapel Bridge / Lion Monument - Free with Swiss Pass\r\nLucerne: Excursion to Mt. Titlis with Swiss Pass from Engelberg\r\nZurich: Visit Rhine Fall / FIFA World Football Museum / Swiss National Museum - Free with Swiss Pass \r\n08 Days Consecutive Swiss Pass - 2nd Class\r\nUnlimited travelling within Switzerland on Public Transportation using Swiss Pass\r\nDeparture Transfer from Zurich Hotel to Zurich Airport on Pvt. Basis - One Way\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal and medical expense. \r\nRhine Falls ticket not included (to be purchased directly)\r\nAny transfer/train/cab other than the mentioned above.\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges\r\n\r\n','',0,'Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. \r\nTrain fare is subject to change at the time of booking. \r\nThe Guests will have to manage on their own till the Pickup / Drop off point for SIC TOURS (can be covered with Swiss Pass in Switzerland)',0,0,'2024-07-17 17:53:57','2024-07-17 17:53:57'),(55,724,361,15535,3,0,0,'2024-08-17','2024-08-23',NULL,'Ladakh Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (17th Aug) : Arrive LEH\r\nArrive Leh and transfer to the hotel. Full day for complete rest for acclimatization to the high altitude of Leh. Overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 2 (18th Aug) : LEH \r\nBreakfast at hotel. After breakfast, drive to shyam valley and you\'ll be awestruck with the sight of the Indus & Zanskar river Sangam, drive along the Indus river visiting Pathar Sahib Gurdwara and Magnetic Hill (where the cars defy gravity) and further on to Leh Hall of Fame (which has a museum of the Kargil War memorabilia). Later return to Leh for visit Shanti Stupa, Leh Palace and Leh Market. Overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 3 (19th Aug) : Leh - Nubra  (160 Kms / 5 Hrs)\r\nAfter Breakfast drive to Nubra Valley via Khardungla (Highest Motorable road in the World, 18,380 ft). Arrive at Hundar by Afternoon. Rest of the day free to explore Deskit, Hunder Villages and camel Safari in Sand Dunes between Deskit and Hundar Village. One can go for camel rides (own cost). Overnight stay at Nubra Valley.\r\n \r\nDay 4 (20th Aug) : Nubra (Day Tour to Turtuk Village)\r\nDrive 70 Kms one way 3/4 hrs via various villages to Turtuk. It is the last village from Indian side. Have a look forward on Bunkers and last Indian post. Later in afternoon return to Nubra valley. Overnight stay at Nubra Valley.\r\n \r\nDay 5 (21st Aug) : Nubra â€“ Pangong\r\nHave early breakfast and proceed to Pangong via Shayok, retrace the route down for Pangong Lake through Shayok 17,350 ft., it is the third highest motorable road in the world. Arrive Pangong and enjoy the beauty of the lake on the Banks of Pangong Lake while appreciating the changing Colors and fascinating high altitude of the Lake. Overnight stay at Pangong.\r\n \r\nDay 6 (22nd Aug) : Pangong  â€“ Leh\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Leh via Changla pass. Later in the evening guest can walk to Local Bazaar . Overnight stay at Leh.                                     \r\n\r\nDay 7 (23rd Aug) : Depart Leh\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel & proceed to Leh airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n',113000,22254,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meet and Greet upon arrival \r\nâ€¢ Accommodation on MAPAI basis.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Transport by 1 Non-AC INNOVA  for arrival / departure and sightseeing as per itinerary on private basis.\r\nâ€¢ Green Fees & Environment Fees (Inner Line Permit)\r\nâ€¢ Toll and taxes\r\nâ€¢ Parking Charges\r\nâ€¢ Driver allowances\r\nâ€¢ 24/7 over the Phone support\r\nâ€¢ All taxes and GST\r\n','â€¢ Lunch\r\nâ€¢ Oxygen Cylinder.\r\nâ€¢ Any other activities not mentioned in inclusions like horse riding/tips/ extra food ordered / entry fees / liquor etc.\r\n','',0,'Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2024-08-06 13:46:19','2024-10-23 13:47:53'),(56,730,365,33,3,1,0,'2024-08-13','2024-08-17',NULL,'Hong Kong Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (13th Aug) : Airport to Hotel transfer on PVT\r\nProceed for Hong Kong City Tour : Victoria Peak by 1 Way Peak tram, Madame Tussauds, Old Clock Tower, Victoria Harbour, Symphony of Lights - SIC\r\n\r\nDay 02 (14th Aug) : Ocean Park with Entry & Return Transfer - PVT\r\n\r\nDay 03 (15th Aug) : Disney 1 Day Pass.& Return Transfers - SIC\r\n\r\nDay 04 (16th Aug) : Day at Leisure\r\n\r\nDay 05 (17th Aug) : Hotel to Airport Transfer on PVT\r\n',106388,27112,'* 4 nights accomodation\r\n* Airport return transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa \r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','',0,'',66,0,'2024-08-27 13:38:12','2024-10-23 13:51:16'),(57,738,371,15510,2,0,0,'2024-09-28','2024-10-02',NULL,'Thailand Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (28 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel ( Central Pattaya ) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (29 Sep)	\r\nDay at Leisure / Explore on your own. \r\n \r\n3rd Day (30 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage)\r\nSIC TOURS - BANGKOK -Evening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC 2 Adults  Pick-up Time 17:30 hrs (240 mins)       \r\n\r\n4th Day (1 Oct)	TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 ) \r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  2 Adults \r\nStarts: 08:00 hrsâ€¢ Duration: 9h (Ends: 17:00 hrs)\r\n\r\n5th Day (2 Oct)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) ',23900,9905,'Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nFull Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch  on pvt basis.\r\nEvening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC Basis\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nAll tours and sightseeing are on pvt and sic basis.','Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visitor fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nSurcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking) \r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','',0,'Airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability',0,0,'2024-09-18 13:17:09','2024-09-18 13:17:09'),(58,748,379,302,2,0,0,'2025-01-19','2025-01-31',NULL,'Mumbai-Kochi Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (19th Jan) : \r\nArrival at the Mumbai airport and transfer to the booked hotel. (PVT)\r\nCheck-in at the hotel and relax. \r\n\r\nDay 02 (20th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for Full-Day Highlights of Mumbai. Overnight at Mumbai Hotel.\r\n(Gateway of India, Siddhivinayak Temple, Bandra-Worli Sea Link, Haji Ali Dargah, Juhu Beach, Marine Drive) - All the places can be covered as per time availability and traffic congestion.\r\n\r\nDay 03 (21st Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Mumbai Airport for the onward journey to Kochi.\r\nArrival at the Kochi Airport and transfer to the booked hotel in Kochi. Enjoy Kathakali show in the evening. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (22nd Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nDay 05 (23rd Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level. On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India.You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (24th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 07 (25th Jan) : \r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Kumarakom. Check in at the hotel. Kumarakom is home to a wide variety of flora and fauna. where many species of migratory birds visit. Located on the banks of the Vembanad Lake, the Kumarakom Bird Sanctuary, an ornithologist\'s paradise, is a favourite haunt of migratory birds. Visit Kumarakom Birds Sanctuary and Driftwood Museum. Overnight stay at Kumarakom.\r\n\r\nDay 08 (26th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Kumarakom (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\n\r\nDay 09 (27th Jan) :\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kumarakom - Cochin Departure transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport for the onward journey to Goa.\r\nArrival at Goa Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 10 (28th Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North-Goa tour. North Goa offers a mix of adventure, history, and culture, making it a perfect destination. Visit beaches and enjoy water sports (at your own expense), temples. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 11 (29th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, get ready to experience the South-Goa Tour. Known for its pristine beaches, quiet villages, and spiritual sites, South Goa os perfect for a peaceful getaway.\r\n\r\nDay 12 (30th Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast and spend the day at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 13 (31st Jan) :\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Airport for your departure flight to Mumbai.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',208500,172690,',* Economy Class Airfare (BOM-COK), (COK-GOI), (GOI-BOM)\r\n* Daily breakfast at the booked hotel\r\n* All Meals (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) are included in Houseboat\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* All tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM (especially for Kerala)\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n* Guide charges are included for 22nd Jan (i.e., 2nd day in Kochi)\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Travel Insurance','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\nThe itinerary can be adjusted as per the final flight timings.\r\nOther than Kochi Guide is not required to visit the planned places. \r\n\r\n',66,0,'2024-10-21 18:56:46','2025-02-03 17:40:56'),(59,755,380,419,2,0,0,'2024-11-21','2024-11-25',NULL,'Kashmir Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : On arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                             \r\n\r\n                                               \r\nDay 02 : After breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg. Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                               \r\n\r\n                                   \r\nDay 03 : After breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Pahalgam, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                             \r\n\r\n                                   \r\nDay 04 : After breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.                                              \r\n\r\n                                               \r\nDay 05 : After breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.        \r\n\r\n',0,0,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation  as above.\r\n* Breakfast in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis.\r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes','* Any type of pesronal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2024-10-24 12:44:19','2024-11-26 14:23:30'),(60,766,388,33,3,0,2,'2024-11-15','2024-11-20',NULL,'Hong Kong Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 1 (15th Nov)\r\nArrival Transfer from HKG Airport to HKG Hotel Pvt\r\nCheck-in at Hotel (after 3 pm)\r\nHongKong Night Tour: Victoria peak by peak tram(1 way), Clock tower,Avenue of Star, Symphony of Light Show PVT\r\nStarts at: 4:30 pm (5 hrs tour)\r\nOvernight at Hong Kong\r\n\r\nDAY 2 (16th Nov)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nFull day Disneyland Tour with entrance ticket and return transfer (Closed on Wednesday) PVT\r\nStarts at: 10:30 am -2100 hrs\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 3 (17th Nov)\r\nBreekfast at Hotel\r\nFull day Ocean park Tour with entrance ticket and return transfer (Closed on Tuesday) PVT\r\nStarts at: 10 am - 1900 hrs\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 4 (18th Nov)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nLantau Island Tour with standard cable car and return transfer PVT\r\nStarts at: 10:30 (5 hrs tour)\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 (19th Nov)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nDay at Leisure. You can explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 6 (20th Nov)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nCheckout from Hotel (Before 12 Noon)\r\nHotel to Airport Transfer on PVT\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',244153,73947,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5 nights accomodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers by PVT basis .\r\n* Night tours by Pvt basis with one way Tram Ride to Victoria peak + star ferry rides + old clock tower .\r\n* Lantau island Tours â€“ standard cable car .\r\n* Disney tours by Pvt basis with an Entrance pass .\r\n* Ocean Park Tours by Pvt basis with an Entrance pass .\r\n* Return Airport transfers by PVT basis .\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n',66,0,'2024-11-27 09:27:04','2024-11-30 16:46:25'),(61,771,389,15511,2,0,0,'2024-12-02','2024-12-10',NULL,'Spain Diaries',NULL,'Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (02-12-2024): Ibiza Arrival - Check-in at the hotel and relax. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 (03-12-2024): After breakfast,  leave for the Oceanbeat Ibiza Boat Party . Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 (04-12-2024): After breakfast,  Day at leisure. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 (05-12-2024): After breakfast,  check-out from hotel. Leave for airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Madrid.\r\nMadrid Arrival - Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 5 (06-12-2024) : After breakfast,  leave for the Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 (07-12-2024) : \r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from hotel.\r\nLeave for Madrid train station. Board the train to Barcelona. \r\nBarcelona Arrival.\r\nCheck-in at hotel and relax.\r\nleave for the Golden Sunset and Chill-Out - Eco Catamaran Cruise.\r\n\r\nDay 7 (08-12-2024) : \r\nAfter breakfast.\r\nDay at leisure.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 8 (09-12-2024) : \r\nAfter breakfast.\r\nleave for Sagrada Familia: Fast Track Guided Tour with optional Tower\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 9 (10-12-2024) : \r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from hotel. It\'s time to bid Good Bye to your Spain trip. Leave for airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Delhi.',64722,52974,'â€¢	Economy class airfare\r\nâ€¢	Accommodation\r\nâ€¢	Daily Breakfast\r\nâ€¢	Transfer from Ibiza Airport to Hotel on PVT basis\r\nâ€¢	All-Inclusive Boat Party with Clubs Admission Included (Oceanbeat Ibiza Boat Party 14:00)\r\nâ€¢	Excursion by boat to the coves and beaches in the north of Ibiza (Excursion by boat to the coves and beaches in the north of Ibiza 10:00)\r\nâ€¢	Transfer from Ibiza Hotel to Airport on PVT basis\r\nâ€¢	Transfer from Madrid Airport to Hotel on PVT basis.\r\nâ€¢	Big Bus Madrid Hop-on Hop-off Sightseeing Tour (Panoramic Loop by Open-top Bus )\r\nâ€¢	Madrid - Transfer from Hotel to Station on PVT basis\r\nâ€¢	Barcelona - Transfer from Station to Hotel on PVT basis \r\nâ€¢	Sunset Catamaran Cruise with Live Music in Barcelona (Sunset Eco Cruise 17:00)\r\nâ€¢	Sagrada Familia: Fast Track Guided Tour with optional Tower (Guided tour with tower-English 11:00)\r\nâ€¢	Barcelona - Transfer from Hotel to Airport on PVT basis \r\nâ€¢	Train from Madrid to Barcelona (07th December)\r\nâ€¢	Travel Insurance\r\nâ€¢	Visa Charges\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal and medical expense. \r\nAny transfers to departure points of sightseeing.\r\nAny transfer for airport pick-up and drop.\r\nTCS\r\n\r\n','',0,'Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. \r\nTrain fare is subject to change at the time of booking. ',0,0,'2024-11-27 21:32:43','2024-11-27 21:32:43'),(62,777,390,241,2,0,1,'2024-12-15','2024-12-18',NULL,'Gujarat Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (15th Dec) :\r\nArrival at the BDQ Airport and transfer to the pre-booked hotel.\r\nCheck-in at the hotel and relax\r\nLater in the evening drop to Lukshmi Palace (Vadodara Fort) for attending the marriage and return to hotel at night.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (16th Dec) : Vadodara to Somnath (approx distance 480km)\r\nAfter breakfast in Vadodara, check out and drive to Somnath town. After check-in formalities, attend evening aarti at Somnath Temple and later enjoy light and sound show in Somnath. Return to your hotel for an overnight stay in Somnath.\r\n\r\nDay 03 (17th Dec) : Somnath to Dwarka (approx distance 230km)\r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel drive to Dwarka. after reaching Dwarka start temple hopping in Dwarka. Visit Nageshwar Jyotirlinga Temple, Gopi Talav, and Bet Dwarka. On the way back to Dwarka visit Rukmani Temple. Take the afternoon to explore coastal attractions including the lighthouse on the beach. Attend evening aarti at Dwarkadhish Temple followed by dinner and overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (18th Dec) : Dwarka to Rajkot Drop (approx distance 230km)\r\nAfter having breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Rajkot Airport for your homebound flight\r\n\r\n\r\n',49770,12230,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle - 1 Innova Crysta\r\n* Driver Allowance, Toll Tax Parking','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nEarly check-in is subject to availability.',66,0,'2024-11-30 12:46:35','2024-12-20 15:06:58'),(63,783,394,2690,2,0,0,'2025-01-11','2025-01-16',NULL,'Thailand Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (11 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area )  1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (12 Jan)\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Box ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On SIC\r\n\r\n3rd Day (13 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area )  1-PRIVATE CAR KBV (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n4th Day (14 Jan)\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour By Speed Boat + Khai Island + Lunch + Transfer ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC\r\n\r\n5th Day (15 Jan)\r\nPhuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC\r\nTOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom   1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 )\r\nPhuket Tiger Kingdom Big Tiger\r\n\r\n6th Day (16 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT   1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',37563,20537,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2024-12-23 16:45:57','2025-02-03 14:02:01'),(64,792,399,20507,4,0,0,'2025-02-01','2025-02-05',NULL,'Prayagraj Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Feb : At 10 pm, leave from Delhi Airport to Vrindavan. Late night check-in at hotel. \r\n\r\n2nd Feb : Early morning check-out from hotel. And cover Vrindavan and Agra as per time availability. Night stay in Agra. \r\n\r\n3rd Feb : Early Morning check-out from Agra and leave for Lucknow. Local sightseeing in Lucknow. Night stay in Lucknow. \r\n\r\n4th Feb : Early morning leave for Prayagraj. Night stay in Prayagraj at self-booked hotel. \r\n\r\n5th Feb : Early morning leave for Varanasi. After Darshan and local visit drop at Varanasi Airport around 9 pm.\r\n',40000,14000,'* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* 1N accommodation in Varanasi\r\n* 1N accommodation in Agra\r\n* 1N accommodation in Lucknow','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions','',0,'Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.',66,0,'2025-01-30 18:15:18','2025-02-07 17:00:18'),(65,794,400,349,3,0,0,'2025-01-19','2025-01-27',NULL,'Dubai Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (19th Jan) :\r\nTransfer from DXB AIRPORT to Abu Dhabi hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2 (20th Jan) :\r\nAbu Dhabi Attractions ( 2 Day 2 Park Pass (Yas Water World / Ferrari / Warner Bros/Sea World) )\r\n\r\nDay 3 (21st Jan) :\r\nTransfer from Abu Dhabi to Bur Dubai hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4 (22nd Jan) :\r\nHalf Day Dubai City Tour [with Private transport]\r\nDesert Safari With BBQ Dinner (Standard Camp) [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 5 (23rd Jan) :\r\nBurj Khalifa Tour with Dubai Mall [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 6 (24th Jan) :\r\nMiracle Garden + Global Village [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 7 (25th Jan) :\r\nDubai Frame [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 8 (26th Jan) :\r\nPvt. Yacht and Museum of the Future -Tickets (with Prvate transport)\r\n\r\nDay 9 (27th Jan) :\r\nTransfer from Bur Dubai Hotel to DXB AIRPORT [with Private transport)',150878,55922,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 8N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* All the tours and transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Abu Dhabi Attractions (2 Day 2 Park Pass (Yas Water World / Ferrari / Warner Bros/Sea World) ) (Only Ticket)(03-Adults)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\nCharges for the luxury car (Limousine) is 10500 per hour.',66,0,'2025-02-01 17:39:30','2025-02-03 11:41:25'),(66,801,401,8,2,0,0,'2025-02-18','2025-02-20',NULL,'Kolkata Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Tuesday 18th February) : Kolkata Airport to Hotel - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour\r\nOn arrival at Airport & transfer to hotel. Check-in to hotel & rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at Kolkata\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Wednesday 19th February) : Gangasagar - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours\r\nAfter early breakfast start for full day excursion to Gangasagar â€“ An island in the confluence of River Ganga & Bay of Bengal & famous for Kapil Muni Ashram which is considered to be a great religious significance. Evening return back to Kolkata. Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n \r\n+ (Contd. 2nd Day) : kachuberia â€“ Excursion (By 1 Sumo / Similar)\r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours\r\nWe will provide Ac vehicle for Kolkata to Ferry Ghat i.e. Lot No. 8 / Harwood Point (90 Km.) & back to Kolkata. After reaching Lot No. 8 you will board the ferry to cross the Muriganga River for Kachuberia. From here you will be transferred to Sagar island and back to Ferry Jetty by a private vehicle (01 ac sumo/similar car). Please do not forget to reconfirm the return ferry timings (Kachuberia to Lot No 8) with the authority as it depends on the tide timings.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Thursday 20th February) : Kolkata to Kolkata Airport - Drop\r\nApprox Distance: 30 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to the Airport for your onwards journey.\r\n\r\nVehicle\r\n\r\n1-Dzire as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nKolkata Railway Station / Airport to Hotel, \r\nGangasagar, \r\n\r\n\r\n1-SUMO / Similar as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nKachuberia Excursion \r\n',0,0,'â€¢	Economy Class airfare.\r\nâ€¢	Accommodation on twin Sharing Basis. \r\nâ€¢	Meal Plan (as per mentioned above). \r\nâ€¢	Exclusive AC Vehicle for transfers & sightseeing as per Itinerary. \r\nâ€¢	All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary). \r\nâ€¢	GST \r\n','â€¢	Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary. \r\nâ€¢	Entrance Fees & Guide charges. \r\nâ€¢	Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc. (to be borne by the client, which is directly payable on the spot). \r\nâ€¢	Insurance. \r\nâ€¢	NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','',0,'Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability.',0,0,'2025-02-01 17:48:43','2025-02-01 17:48:43'),(67,804,403,15494,4,0,0,'2025-02-06','2025-02-09',NULL,'Goa Diaries',NULL,'Day 1: Airport to Hotel Transfer\r\nDay 2: North Goa Tour\r\nDay 3: Day at leisure\r\nDay 4: Hotel to Airport Transfer',8700,6168,'Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nAirport Transfers on pvt basis\r\nNorth Goa Tours.\r\nVehicle : Innova Crysta\r\nGST\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions','Rooms are subject to availability\r\n',0,'Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability',0,0,'2025-02-05 18:28:29','2025-02-05 18:28:29'),(68,812,408,15512,5,0,1,'2025-03-16','2025-03-22',NULL,'Vietnam Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City (PVT)\r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh, transfer downtown, and check in at your hotel (14:00). Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, pick upâ€™s airport guide, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (PVT) (B)\r\nDepart at 7:30 AM (time varies by hotel) for a scenic boat ride to a historic floating market on the Tien River. Enjoy fresh fruits, folk music, and visit local businesses crafting coconut candy and rice popcorn. Explore a village by foot and bike, and admire an ancient houseâ€™s traditional architecture. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh City fly to Danang â€“ Hoi An Ancient Town Half Day (B) (PRIVATE)\r\nArrive in Da Nang and transfer to Hoi An, a historic 16th-century trading port. Check in at the hotel (14:00), then explore top attractions, including the Japanese Covered Bridge, Fujian Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Hoi An Market, and enjoy a lantern boat excursion. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, lantern boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (PVT)(B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:00 AM for Ba Na Hills (35km from Da Nang). Take the Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Old Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and Orchid Garden. Experience the hill-climbing train, Le Jardin Dâ€™Amour, and walk across the famous Golden Bridge for panoramic views. Enjoy lunch at your own expense, then explore Fantasy Park with various indoor games. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nEntrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, sharing guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Da Nang â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for a flight to Hanoi. Upon arrival, transfer to the city center and check in at the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (outside), One Pillar Pagoda, and Hanoi Train Street. Explore Hoan Kiem Lake, stroll through the Old Quarterâ€™s \"36 Streets,\" and shop at Dong Xuan Market. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) \r\nDepart at 8:00 AM for Ha Long Bay (4-hour drive). Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and check into your cabin. Enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through the bay. Stop for a swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for a sunset view before a seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nNote: The itinerary may vary by cruise.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits. \r\n\r\nDay 7 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/Brunch)\r\nWake up early to enjoy the stunning sunrise over Ha Long Bay. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a local rowboat ride. Enjoy brunch while cruising back to the pier, then return to Hanoi. Transfer to the airport (without a guide) for your flight home. Goodbye and see you again!\r\nNote: The cruise itinerary may vary.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat.\r\n\r\n',319314,61686,'* Internal sector flights included\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS \r\n','',0,'Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2025-02-25 13:29:43','2025-03-24 14:57:58'),(69,815,409,4,2,0,0,'2025-04-06','2025-04-11',NULL,'Mumbai Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (6th Apr) \r\nArrival at the Mumbai Airport and transfer to the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (7th Apr)\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Cordellia Cruise (16:30)\r\n\r\nDay 03 (8th Apr)\r\nEnjoy at the Cruise\r\n\r\nDay 04 (9th April)\r\nCheck-out from the cruise at Goa. Transfer to the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. After taking some rest, proceed for the North Goa Tour.\r\n\r\nDay 05 (10th April)\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the South Goa Tour.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (11th April)\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Goa Airport for your homebound journey.\r\n\r\n',17200,14545,'* Economy class Airfare\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Mumbai\r\n* 2N accommodation at Cruise with all meals\r\n* 2N accommodation in Goa\r\n* Airport and Cruise Transfers on Pvt.\r\n','* Any type of personal expense.\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExtra Kms/Hours will be charged extra',66,0,'2025-03-04 18:45:56','2025-06-27 15:25:15'),(70,819,411,15494,4,0,0,'2025-03-28','2025-04-01',NULL,'Goa Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 (28th march)\r\nArrival at the Goa Airport and Transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (29th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North Goa Tour. \r\n\r\nDay 03 (30th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (31st March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the South Goa Hotel. Day at leisure or you can explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 05 (1st April)\r\nHave breakfast and check-out from the hotel and proceed for the South Goa Tour and transfer to the Airport for your homebound journey.\r\n',21770,17300,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation with breakfast + lunch/dinner\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* North Goa tour on PVT\r\n* South Goa tour on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExtra hrs and extra kms charges will be extra',66,0,'2025-03-06 15:49:25','2025-04-03 17:23:17'),(71,826,414,126,3,0,2,'2025-04-08','2025-04-12',NULL,'Jaipur Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1: Leave early morning for Jaipur. After reaching, check-in at hotel. Explore the City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and Jantar Mantar as per the respective timings. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, visit Amer Fort and Jaigarh Fort. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Have breakfast and explore Nahargarh Fort and Birla Mandir. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast and relax or explore local market. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : After having breakfast, check-out and drive back to Delhi.',28500,3822,'* 4 Nights accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Toll Tax\r\n* Driver Allowance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','',0,'Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.',66,0,'2025-04-02 17:18:39','2025-06-26 16:54:41'),(72,830,415,419,4,0,0,'2025-05-23','2025-05-28',NULL,'Kashmir Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Fri 23rd May) : Arrival Srinagar to Sonamarg - Drop at Hotel\r\nOn the arrival at Srinagar Airport we will proceed towards Sonamarg, after check-in Day will be free at leisure. Overnight Stay in a Hotel.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Sat 24th May) : Sonamarg â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast, we will proceed to Sonamarg. Sonamarg, (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is 90kms northâ€“east of Srinagar. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore. Hire a ( horse or pony /Union (Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. Do not miss clicking memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. Overnight stay at Hotel .\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sun 25th May) : Sonamarg to Srinagar â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast you will depart from Sonamarg and proceed our drive towards Srinagar. From Srinagar you will be given a tour of local sightseeing of our famous Mughal gardens of Nishat and Shalimar & Chashmashahi where you can enjoy the natural beauty and the mesmerizing view of the valley amidst the mountains. Post the sightseeing, we will take you to the hotel for the overnight stay.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Mon 26th May) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Srinagar.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Tue 27th May) : Srinagar to Pahalgam â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, we\'ll journey towards Pahalgam. You\'ll have the opportunity to explore breathtaking places such as Aru, Betaab Valley, and Chandanwari, accessible through Union Cabs at your own expense, each encompassing its own unique natural beauty. While in Pahalgam, you can engage in various activities based on your preferences, including skiing, golfing, visiting the Lidder Amusement Park, trekking, or experiencing thrilling whitewater rafting. Following the tour of Pahalgam, we\'ll return to the hotel for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Wed 28th May) : Pahalgam to Srinagar â€“ Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the Airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n',113300,25000,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Sonamarg with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Srinagar with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Pahalgam with breakfast\r\n* Sightseeing by assigned vehicle (as per the package). \r\n* Vehicle : Non-AC Innova\r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg and vice versa, or to other destinations like Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Doodhpathri in the event of heavy snow, is not included in your package. \r\n* Anything not in inclusions is Excluded \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n',0,0,'2025-04-12 13:05:26','2025-04-12 13:05:26'),(73,833,417,3052,10,0,1,'2025-06-13','2025-06-21',NULL,'Sri Lanka ','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival - Kandy	\r\nTransfer to Kandy\r\nEnroute visit Pinnawala Elephant Orphange\r\nVisit Mawanella Spice Garden\r\nCheck into the Hotel\r\nLeisure\r\nDinner & stay overnight at hotel.\r\n	\r\nDay 02 : Kandy	\r\nBreakfast\r\nVisit Temple of the tooth relic\r\nOn completion visit Royal Botanical Garden\r\nEvening visit to Gem Museum\r\nWitness to the cultural dance\r\nDinner & stay overnight at hotel\r\n	\r\nDay 03 : Kandy - Bentota	\r\nBreakfast\r\nTransfer to Bentota\r\nCheck into the hotel\r\nLeisure\r\nDinner & stay overnight at hotel\r\n	\r\nDay 04 : Bentota/ Wadduwa â€“ Galle Excursion	\r\nBreakfast\r\nTransfer to Galle for a Day Excursion\r\nVisit Jungle Beach & Galle Fort\r\nOn completion Unwatuna Beach\r\nEvening enjoy Galle City Tour\r\nTransfer back to the hotel.\r\nDinner & stay overnight at hotel\r\n	\r\nDay 05 : Bentota-Wadduwa// Bentota City Tour	\r\nBreakfast\r\nVisit to Turtle Hatchery in Kosgoda\r\nVisit Kande Viharaya\r\nOn completion enjoy boat safari in Madu River\r\nDinner & stay overnight\r\n	\r\nDay 06 : Bentota - Leisure\r\nBreakfast\r\nFull Day Leisure @Bentota\r\nDinner & stay overnight in Bentota\r\n	\r\nDay 07 : Bentota - Colombo	\r\nBreakfast\r\nStay Until Checkout\r\nTransfer to Colombo\r\nCheck into the hotel & Relax\r\nDinner & stay overnight in Colombo\r\nEvening shopping tour\r\n\r\nDay 08 : Colombo City Tour	\r\nBreakfast\r\nVisit Independence Squre/ Lotus Tower/ Viharamahadevi Park/ Colombo National Museum & Galle face Green.\r\nOn completion visit to Anjaneyar Temple & Vibeeshana Temple which is related to the Ramayanaya.\r\nEvening go for a shopping tour in Colombo.\r\nDinner & stay overnight in Colombo\r\n	\r\nDay 09 : Departure\r\nBreakfast\r\nCheckout from the hotel and transfer to the Airport for the homebound journey\r\n\r\n	\r\n\r\n',0,0,'* DEL-CMB-DEL Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on Half Board basis\r\n* Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Vehicle. (Toyota Mini Coaster)\r\n* Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\n* City tours in Kandy, Bentota & Colombo.\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day                            \r\n* Welcome at the airport with Garlands                         \r\n* Express way charges wherever applicable\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','* Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.                    \r\n* Early check in or late checkout charges.                                                          \r\n* Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs                                         \r\n* Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.       \r\n* Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.       \r\n* Camera or Video permits.                                             \r\n* Expenses of a personal nature.                         \r\n* Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.                     \r\n* Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n ','',0,'Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\nTurtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride and Gangaramaya Temple tours can be done at supplementary cost. ',66,0,'2025-05-24 18:45:11','2025-06-26 14:59:29'),(74,838,418,15512,2,1,1,'2025-06-01','2025-06-06',NULL,'Vietnam Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City, City Half Day (PVT)\r\nUpon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and guide.\r\nVisit the city covering:\r\nâ€¢ Notre Dame Cathedral\r\nâ€¢ Central Post Office\r\nâ€¢ War Remnants Museum\r\nâ€¢ Ben Thanh Market\r\nHead to your hotel to check in and spend rest of the day at your own leisure.\r\nNote: Check in time 14:00\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nPlease note that your driver does not speak English.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (B) (PVT)\r\n8:00 AM: Depart from Ho Chi Minh City to My Tho.\r\nVinh Trang Pagoda: Visit this historic Buddhist temple.\r\nTien River Cruis: Embark on a boat trip to explore four beautiful islands: Dragon, Unicorn, Phoenix, and Tortoise. Experience the serene countryside by sampan, passing through small canals shaded by water coconut trees. Enjoy seasonal fruits, honey tea, and traditional Southern Vietnamese folk music performed by locals.\r\nCoconut Candy Workshop: Learn about the local production of coconut candy and sample fresh products.\r\nReturn to Ho Chi Minh City : Conclude the trip and return to the city.\r\nOvernight: Stay in Ho Chi Minh City.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : HCMC â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (PVT) \r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for your flight to Hanoi.\r\nUpon arrival, meet your guide and driver at the airport for a transfer to the city center.\r\nCheck in at your hotel.\r\nAfternoon Sightseeing\r\nVisit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (viewed from outside), the final resting place of Vietnam\'s revolutionary leader.\r\nExplore the One Pillar Pagoda, a historic Buddhist temple.\r\nStroll around HoÃ n Kiáº¿m Lake (Sword Lake), a serene spot in the city\'s heart.\r\nWander through the Old Quarter, known as \"The 36 Streets,\" each named after the traditional goods sold there.\r\nOvernight : Stay in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nDepart from Hanoi around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour shuttle bus ride to Ha Long Bay. Upon arrival at the port around noon, embark on the cruise, check into your cabin, and enjoy a fresh seafood lunch as you begin your journey through the bay. Afternoon activities include swimming, visiting a mysterious cave, and relaxing on a secluded island beach. Conclude the day with a sunset view from the top deck followed by a seafood dinner. Overnight accommodations are provided on the cruise.\r\nNote : The final cruise itinerary may vary based on the specific cruise program.\r\nInclusion : Sharing transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi (B/Brunch)\r\nEarly risers can witness the breathtaking sunrise and tranquil beauty of Halong Bay\'s towering limestone karsts. After a light breakfast around 7:00 AM, embark on a short rowboat ride with local rowers to explore the bay\'s serene waters. Enjoy a leisurely brunch on the boat as you cruise back to the pier, then begin the journey back to Hanoi.\r\nPlease note that the final cruise itinerary may vary depending on each cruise\'s program.\r\nInclusion: Sharing transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi Depature (B)\r\nHave breakfast and check out.\r\nThen we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. \r\nNote: Our driver doesnâ€™t speak English.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',12040,4660,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights (SGN-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double/triple sharing room\r\nâ€¢ Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\nâ€¢ SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2025-05-29 14:18:40','2025-06-07 14:20:52'),(75,842,419,355,5,0,0,'2025-06-13','2025-06-16',NULL,'Varanasi Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (13 Jun) : Arrival at Varanasi airport and transfer to hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 2 (14 Jun) : After having breakfast visit temple/ghat on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 3 (15 Jun) : After having breakfast check-out from the hotel. Varanasi hotel to Ayodhya hotel drop. \r\n\r\nDay 4 (16 Jun ) â€“ After having breakfast check-out from the hotel. Ayodhya hotel to Ayodhya Airport drop. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',64500,5000,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Varanasi \r\n* 1N Accommodation in Ayodhya\r\n* Breakfast and Dinner at hotel\r\n* Transfers & sightseeing by Ac XL6(No Sightseeing  )\r\n* Toll, Parking, Driver Allowance.\r\n\r\n ','* Entrances fees\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as drinks, telephone, and laundry bills etc\r\n* Tips and porter charges\r\n* Any additional expenses incurred due to any flight delay or cancellation, weather conditions, political closures, technical faults etc\r\n* Any other service/s not specified above\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2025-06-13 10:46:11','2025-06-17 14:47:38'),(76,844,420,3511,4,0,1,'2025-06-27','2025-07-01',NULL,'Gangtok Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 27th June) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup \r\nApprox Distance : 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Gangtok (5,500 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Gangtok\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 28th June) : Gangtok to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir - Excursion \r\nApprox Distance : 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft. / 37 Kms. / 02 Hrs. from Gangtok) and further drive to New Baba Mandir (13,200 ft. / 16 Kms. / 01 Hrs. from Tsomgo Lake). Evening back to Gangtok. Overnight stay at Gangtok. Note : In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing. Due to winter season (heavy snow) vehicle will be able to drive till Snow point on the way to Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 29th June) : Gangtok to Darjeeling - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Darjeeling (6,950 Ft.). On arrival check-in to hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Monday 30th June) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill \r\nApprox Distance : 130 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours \r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM, visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nNote : Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 1st July) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance : 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n',83000,11000,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section \r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan (as per mentioned above) \r\n* 1-Innova / Xylo / Similar as per itinerary & timing only\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please note that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis) \r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges \r\nâ€¢ Insurance \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','',0,'Airfare Is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2025-06-26 12:50:20','2025-07-02 11:11:35'),(77,846,421,410,2,0,0,'2025-06-27','2025-07-01',NULL,'Prague Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the PRG Airport and transfer (on your own) to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. \r\nPrague Boats 1-hour Cruise (1hr-20:00) Duration : 55 mins (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Have breakfast at the hotel and relax. Day at leisure or you can explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : After having breakfast, proceed for Small-Group Tour of Prague Castle with Visit to Interiors 13:30 Duration : 2hrs 30mins (SIC)\r\nPrague Ghosts, Legends, Medieval Underground and Dungeon Tour (ENGLISH english 20:45), Prague (Duration: 1hr 10m to 1hr 25m) (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Have breakfast at the hotel. Day at Leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5: After having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer (on your own) to the Airport for your home bound journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n,\r\n',16871,4029,'* 4N Accommodation in Prague with Breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned on SIC basis','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Airport to hotel transfer and Vice Versa\r\n* The client has to reach to the pick-up point on their own\r\n* Visa\r\n* insurance','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n',66,0,'2025-07-01 10:51:16','2025-07-02 11:06:27'),(78,850,423,15540,2,0,0,'2025-06-29','2025-07-05',NULL,'Mauritius Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival and transfer from Airport to Hotel (SIC)\r\nCheck-in at the hotel. Evening at Leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Full Day North Island Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Day at Leisure\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Transfer from One hotel to the other. Check-in and relax\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Full Day South Island Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Full Day Ile Aux Cerf Tour with speed boat transfer (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Check-out from the hotel and transfer to Airport for the homebound journey (SIC)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation with breakfast/ lunch or dinner\r\n* Airport Transfers and tours as mentioned (SIC)\r\n* Insurance\r\n  \r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n    Optional Tours/Services \r\n* Catamaran Coral Queen - Dolphin encounter in west coast on shared basis including Hotel â€“ Jetty â€“ Hotel private transfers (at supplement cost)\r\nDescription: Catamaran cruise to the west departs the Tamarin jetty , direction south to encounter the dolphins, the crystal rock and back .Grilled BBQ lunch with local alcoholic and non-alcoholic drinks are served\r\n* Casela Nature Parks Entrance fee Including Private transfers (at supplement cost)\r\nDescription: Included in the TOURIST ADMISSION package: African Safari to see zebras, ostriches, white rhinoceros, impalas, antelopes, kudus, wildebeest | Walk-Thru-Aviary | Viewing of giraffe, pygmy hippo, camels and llamas | Petting Farm |Children\'s playground \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2025-07-07 18:26:40','2025-07-07 18:59:56'),(79,856,424,3052,7,1,1,'2025-07-16','2025-07-22',NULL,'Sri Lanka Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival and Exploration// Kandy \r\nUpon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly welcomed by your driver and transferred to the cultural capital, Kandy. En route, visit the fascinating Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can witness baby elephants being fed and bathed. Continue your journey with a stop at the Mawanella spice garden, exploring Sri Lankaâ€™s rich spice heritage. Once in Kandy, check into your hotel and unwind. In the evening, visit the Gem Museum to marvel at Sri Lanka\'s precious stones and enjoy a vibrant cultural dance performance. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Kandy.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Kandy City Tour  \r\nAfter a sumptuous breakfast, embark on a cultural journey with a visit to the Temple of the Tooth Relic, a sacred site that houses a relic of the Buddha. Continue your exploration with a Royal Botanical Gardens, renowned for its diverse plant species and breathtaking landscapes. In the evening, experience the rich cultural heritage of Sri Lanka at the Gem Museum, followed by a captivating Cultural Dance performance. Enjoy dinner and spend another restful night in Kandy. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Kandy //  Nuwara Eliya  \r\nAfter breakfast transfer to the picturesque town of Nuwara Eliya. Along the way, visit the Hanuman Temple, Ramboda falls and tour a Damro Tea factory to learn about Sri Lanka\'s famed tea production. Next, visit Hanuman Temple and then enjoy a relaxing boat ride on Gregory Lake. Then, check-in to your hotel at Hatton. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hatton to Bentota \r\nAfter breakfast, embark on a scenic drive to the coastal town of Bentota. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or exploring the local area. Enjoy an overnight stay in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Bentota \r\nStart your day with a visit to the Kande Viharaya, a historic Buddhist temple. Then, head to the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery to learn about sea turtle conservation. In the evening, enjoy a Madu River Boat Ride, exploring the mangrove forests and small islands. Stay overnight in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Bentota to Colombo \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for a city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face Green. In the evening embark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic boutiques. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Departure from Colombo \r\nSavor your final breakfast before transferring to the airport for your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable memories of your Sri Lankan journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands \r\n* Vehicle : Toyota Mini Coaster \r\nâ€¢ Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Coaster.\r\nâ€¢ Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Kandy, Nuwaraeliya, Bentota & Colombo.\r\nâ€¢ All applicable government taxes.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.\r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.\r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.\r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase\r\nin surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','',0,'* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n* Entrance to Turtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride, Temple of the Tooth Relic, Gregory Lake, Hakgala Botanical Garden, Gangaramaya Temple are on supplement cost',66,0,'2025-07-16 07:29:09','2025-07-23 16:21:38'),(80,861,428,33,2,0,0,'2025-10-06','2025-10-28',NULL,'Hong Kong-China Adventures','FIT','Day 1 : 6th Oct (Hongkong-Macau) : Arrival at HKG Airport and transfer to Pier.  Hongkong to Macau by ferry.\r\nMacau Pier - Hotel - Macau Pier by PVT transfer\r\n\r\nDay 2 : 7th Oct (Macau) : Macau City tour visiting Lotus square , A-Ma temple , Ruins of St. Paul church and Fishermen Wharf. ( Macau Tower with Entry Tkt)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : 8th Oct (Macau-Hong Kong) : Transfer from Macau hotel to Pier. Macau to Hongkong by ferry.\r\nHongkong pier to hotel transfer.\r\nH.K Night tour visiting Victoria Peak with 1 way Peak Tram Ride + 1 Way Star Ferry Ride + old Clock Tower + SOL Show from TST Promenade\r\n\r\nDay 4 : 9th Oct (Hong Kong) : Full day Disneyland tour\r\n\r\nDay 5 : 10th Oct (Hong Kong) : Half Day Lantau Island tour with cable car (Standard Cabin)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : 11th Oct (Hongkong) : Day at Leisure\r\n\r\nDay 7 : 12th Oct (Hongkong-Beijing) : Transfer from hotel to Hong Kong Airport. Beijing Arrive in Beijing, Met by Representative and transferred to a hotel, Free for leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 8 : 13th Oct (Beijing) : Visit Tiananmen Square, Forbidden City, Jingshan Park, Nan Luo Gu Xiang Hutong Tour..\r\n\r\nDay 9 : 14th Oct (Beijing) : Juyongguan Great Wall, Photo stop of Olympic villages including outlook of Bird Nest and Water Cube.\r\n\r\nDay 10 : 15th Oct (Beijing) : Summer Palace, Temple of Heaven, Wangfujing Pedestrian Street.\r\n\r\nDay 11 : 16th Oct (Beijing-Chengdu) : Transferred to the railway station for bullet train to Chengdu G307(0910/1855) by 2nd class seats, picked and transferred to the hotel. Free for leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 12 : 17th Oct (Chengdu) : Visit the Giant Panda Base, Wenshu Temple, Shu Brocade & Embroidery Museum, People\'s Park, Kuan Zhai Xiang Zi.\r\n\r\nDay 13 : 18th Oct (Chengdu-Chongqing) : Transferred to the railway station for bullet train to Chongqing D2264(0905/1106) by 2nd class seats, Eling Park, Liziba Station, Jiefangbei pedestrian street, Chaotianmen Square, Evening view of Hongya Cave.\r\n\r\nDay 14 : 19th Oct (Chongqing-Zhangjiajie) : Transferred to the railway station for bullet train to Zhangjiajie G2427(0815/1042) by 2nd class seats, Transfer to visit Tianmen Mountain by cable car (worldâ€™s longest).Walk along glass skywalks, visit Heavenâ€™s Gate Cave, a natural arch on the mountain. Transfer to Wulingyuan overnight.\r\n\r\nDay 15 : 20th Oct (Zhangjiajie) : Entry into Zhangjiajie National Forest Park (UNESCO World Heritage Site). Ride the Bailong Elevator, worldâ€™s tallest outdoor lift..Explore Yuanjiajie Scenic Area, including Avatar Hallelujah Mountain. Afternoon views from Tianzi Mountain, â€œMonarch of the Peak Forest.â€\r\n\r\nDay 16 : 21st Oct (Zhangjiajie-Guangzhou) : Morning walk across Zhangjiajie Grand Canyon Glass Bridge, the longest and highest glass-bottom bridge. Transferred to the airport for your night flight to Guangzhou CZ3382(2035/2220). Picked and transferred to the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 17 : 22nd Oct (Guangzhou) : City tour of Guangzhou, Dr. Sun Yat-sen\'s Memorial Hall, Temple of the Six Banyan Trees & Flower Pagoda (Liurong Temple) , Lychee Bay Scenic Area, Canton Tower (basic observation deck).  \r\n\r\nDay 18 : 23rd Oct (Guangzhou-Shenzhen) : Transfer to take bullet train to ShenzhenC7259(0915/1036) by 2nd class seats. Pick up and visit Ganking Ke Little Town,  Luohu Commercial City, Dongmen Old Street. \r\n\r\nDay 19 : 24th Oct (Shenzhen) : Lianhua Mountain Park, Shenzhen Civic Center, Huaqiang North Road Commercial District, Shenzhen Talent Park.\r\n\r\nDay 20 : 25th Oct (Shenzhen-Shanghai) : Transferred to the airport for flight to Shanghai CZ3255(1100/1325), picked and transferred to the hotel. Free for leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 21 : 26th Oct (Shanghai) : Yu Garden and nearby Bazaar, Jade Buddha Temple, French Concession, Nanjing Road, The Bund. \r\n\r\nDay 22 : 27th Oct (Shanghai) : Zhujiajiao Water Town, back to Shanghai and visit Oriental Pearl TV Tower, Fun Collection Market. \r\n\r\nDay 23 : 28th Oct : Free Day at leisure\r\n\r\nDay 24 : 29th Oct : Transferred to the airport for your departure flight , service ends.',984712,399364,'* Economy Class Airfare (AMD-HKG, HKG-PEK,PVG-AMD)\r\n* 23 Nights Accommodation in the mentioned hotels \r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* All tours on SIC and transfers on Private Basis (Hong Kong & Macau)\r\n* Transfers: HKG Airport â€“HKG hotel â€“ HKG Pier â€“ HKG Airport\r\n* Ferry Tickets Hong Kong & Macau\r\n* H.K Night tour visiting Victoria Peak with 1 way Peak Tram Ride + 1 Way Star Ferry Ride + old Clock Tower + SOL Show from TST Promenade\r\n* Full day Disneyland tour\r\n* Half day Lantau Island tour with cable car (Standard Cabin)\r\n* Macau Pier - Hotel - Macau Pier by PVT transfer\r\n* Macau City tour visiting Lotus square , A-Ma temple , Ruins of St. Paul church and Fishermen Wharf. ( Macau Tower with Entry Tkt)\r\n* Deluxe air-conditioning transfers with excellent English speaking guide as per itinerary(for all tours on PVT) (China)	\r\n* High-speed train from Beijing to Chengdu, Chengdu to Chongqing, Chongqing to Zhangjiajie, Guangzhou to Shenzhen by second class seat	\r\n* Flights from Zhangjiajie to Guangzhou and Shenzhen to Shanghai by economic seats		\r\n* Entrance fees as per itinerary\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Tips to guide and driver(USD8 per person per day)				\r\n* Personal expenses such as laundry, drink, telex, telephone calls			\r\n* Meals not mentioned in the program				\r\n* Drinks during meals\r\n* Visa	','',228,'Airfare is dynamic\r\nThe room/s and hotel/s are subject to availability. \r\nAs per standard norms, 01 Medium Suitcase + 01 Cabin luggage is allowed per pax in vehicles for private transfers. If there is extra luggage please book a bigger vehicle at extra cost.\r\nAMD-HKG Baggage : 25 Kg Cabin : 7 kg\r\nHKG-PEK Baggage : 1 pc & Cabin : 7 kg\r\nPVG-AMD Baggage : 30 kg & Cabin : 7 Kg\r\n\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2025-10-03 18:56:08','2025-11-03 15:30:51'),(81,866,430,349,4,0,0,'2025-09-27','2025-10-01',NULL,'Dubai Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nâ€¢ Day 01 : Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner (PVT Basis)(04-Adults) (Lotus Cruise)\r\nâ€¢ Day 02 : Half Day Dubai City Tour (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Day 02 : Burj Khalifa Tour ( Burj Khalifa 124th + 125th Floor - Non Prime Hour NRF (Child Cost Applicable till 8 Years Only) ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Day 03 : Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) ( Ferrari World ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Day 04 : Desert Safari With BBQ Dinner PVT ( Premium ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Day 05 : Museum Of Future (Dynamic Pricing) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n\r\n\r\n',159310,43089,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT Basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* All Tours will be on PVT Transfers Basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nTourism Dirham is not included in the quote and shall be Directly Payable by the guest ',66,0,'2025-10-24 11:29:02','2025-11-03 15:50:46'),(82,871,432,38,5,1,3,'2025-10-01','2025-10-07',NULL,'Thailand Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrive BKK Airport to BKK hotel on Pvt  + BKK City Tour ( Golden , Marble , Gems Gallery ) on Pvt\r\n\r\nDay 02 : After having breakfast proceed for Safari World & Marine Park With Lunch (PVT)\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out. Transfer from Bangkok hotel to DMK Airport for your flight to Phuket (PVT)\r\nTransfer from HKT Airport to Krabi Hotel (PVT). Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Have breakfast at the hotel. \r\nKrabi 4 island tour with lunch By Long tail Boat ( Ex .National Park fee ) on Sic\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out.\r\nTransfer from Krabi Hotel to Phuket hotel, En-Route Tiger Kingdom (Smallest) on PVT\r\n\r\nDay 06 : Have breakfast at the hotel.\r\nPhi Phi Island tour + Khai Island with Lunch by Speed Boat ( Ex . National Park fee ) on Sic\r\n\r\nDay 07 : After having breakfast, check-out from the hotel. 4 hr disposal on pvt ( city centre only ) +Transfer to Phuket Airport on Pvt\r\n',126921,82137,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Ant type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Camera/video camera fee at monuments, medical expenses, airport departure tax, any insurance etc.\r\n* Porterage at all hotels & airports.\r\n* National Park Fees on Island Tours\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',0,0,'2025-10-31 16:51:20','2025-11-03 15:37:02'),(83,878,436,54,4,0,1,'2025-11-02','2025-11-06',NULL,'Singapore Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 :\r\nTransfer from Changi International Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Evening Mandai [with SIC transport]\r\nTransfer from Evening Mandai to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2 :\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Half Day City Tour with Guide (Drop off Little India) (3Hrs) [with SIC transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour [with SIC transport]\r\nTransfer from Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3 :\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Universal Studios [with SIC transport]\r\nTransfer from Universal Studios to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4 :\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay [with SIC transport]\r\nTransfer from MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 5 :\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Ice Cream Museum [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Ice Cream Museum to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Changi International Airport [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n',124389,25111,',* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport transfers on PVT\r\nâ€¢ Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ Half Day City Tour with Guide (Drop off Little India) (3Hrs) (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour( Madame Tussauds 5in1 + Cable Car ) (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ Universal Studios (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ MBS Sky park Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay ( MBS Non Peak (Before 4 PM) + Flower Dome + Jurassic World : The Exhibition at Cloud Forest ) (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ Ice Cream Museum (PVT Basis)\r\n* Visa\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes if applicable\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMarina Bay Sands rates are dynamic.\r\nMid-night Surcharge applicable from 11pm - 07am on Private Transfers.\r\n',66,0,'2025-11-01 12:47:32','2025-11-10 11:49:11'),(84,895,450,33,5,0,4,'2025-12-21','2025-12-27',NULL,'Hong Kong Diaries',NULL,'Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the HKG Airport and transfer to the booked hotel (PVT)\r\nH.K Night tour visiting Victoria Peak with 1 way Peak Tram Ride + 1 Way Star Ferry Ride + old Clock Tower + SOL Show from TST Promenade + Golden Bauhinia Square + Bruce Lee Avenue of star\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Full day Ocean Park tour\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Full day Disneyland tour\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Half Day Lantau Island tour with Round trip Cable Car tickets ( Standard Cabin )\r\n\r\nDay 05 : HKG Hotel to HKG Ferry Pier transfer\r\nFerry ticket to Macau\r\nMacau Pier to hotel transfer are on Pvt basis\r\n\r\nDay 06 : Macau City tour visiting Lotus square , A-Ma temple , Ruins of St. Paul church and Fishermen Warf. ( Macau Tower Outside Photo Stop ), Kun Iam Statue\r\n\r\nDay 07 : Ferry Ticket to H.K City â€“ H.K Pier to H.K Airport transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n',390451,301697,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation in Hong Kong with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Macau with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers and tours on PVT\r\n* Ferry Tickets \r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAs per standard norms, 01 Medium Suitcase + 01 Cabin luggage is allowed per pax in vehicles for private transfers. If there is extra luggage please book a bigger vehicle at extra cost.\r\nIf client is carrying stroller, need to inform in advance. As no space for strollers in Vehicle.',0,0,'2026-01-07 16:27:49','2026-01-07 16:27:49'),(85,902,453,54,9,0,4,'2026-04-18','2026-04-22',NULL,'Singapore Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the SIN Airport and transfer to the booked hotel (PVT)\r\nEvening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (PVT Basis)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Have breakfast at the hotel.\r\nMBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay( MBS Non Peak (Before 4 PM) + Supertree Observatory + Gardens by the Bay: Flower Dome & Cloud Forest featuring Jurassic World: The Experience ) (PVT Basis)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n\r\nDay 03 : After having breakfast check-out from the hotel and transfer to Sentosa Island (Pvt)\r\nAfternoon Sentosa Island Tour( Wings Of Time 2nd show) (Only Ticket)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\nAfternoon Sentosa Island Tour ( Luge & Skyride 03 Ride Combo Flexi (Peak) ) (Only Ticket)(05-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Have breakfast at the hotel.\r\nUniversal Studios Tour ( Universal Studio Ticket ) (Only Ticket)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Have breakfast and check-out from the hotel. Car at disposal for 5 hrs.\r\nTransfer to the SIN Airport for your homebound journey (PVT)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',291000,65280,'* Economy Class Airfare (7 Adults 4 Children)\r\n* Business Class Airfare (2 Adults)\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Singapore with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Sentosa with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Inter Hotel Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on Pvt\r\n* Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (PVT Basis)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay( MBS Non Peak (Before 4 PM) + Supertree Observatory + Gardens by the Bay: Flower Dome & Cloud Forest featuring Jurassic World: The Experience ) (PVT Basis)(09-Adults, 04-Child) Car at disposal for 3 hrs\r\n* Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour( Wings Of Time 2nd Show) (Only Ticket)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour ( Luge & Skyride 03 Ride Combo Flexi (Peak) ) (Only Ticket)(05-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* Universal Studios Tour ( Universal Studio Ticket ) (Only Ticket)(09-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* Car at disposal for 5 hrs approx on the day of your transfer to the Airport\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMid-night Surcharge applicable from 11pm - 07am on Private Transfers.\r\nHotels are non-refundable\r\nWheel Chair is available at an extra cost 90 SGD per day cost and 280 SGD Security Deposit',66,0,'2026-02-04 16:29:39','2026-04-29 16:48:51'),(86,923,471,17600,2,0,0,'2026-06-14','2026-06-20',NULL,'Bali Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay 1 - Arrival at the DPS Airport and transfer to Ubud + Campuhan ridge walk +  Saraswati temple + Ubud palace  ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 2 â€“ Trita Empul + Gunung Kawi Temple Valley + Tegalalang Rice Terrace + Coffee plantation Bali Swing  Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 3 â€“ Inter Hotel transfers Ubud to Nusa Dua + Goa Gajah (Elephant Cave) + Uluwatu Temple cliff views + Kacak dance Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 4 â€“ Leisure day \r\nDay 5 â€“ Leisure day \r\nDay 6 â€“ Ulan Danu Bartan temple + Jatiluwih Rice Terraces + Tanha lot temple Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 7 â€“Malestic beach  +Departure ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\n\r\n',25129,14671,'* 3N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tourism Levy IDR 150.000/ pax\r\n* Any other taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','',0,'Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking',66,0,'2026-03-11 13:35:34','2026-06-23 13:07:21'),(87,927,473,15531,10,0,0,'2026-05-31','2026-06-04',NULL,'Kanatal Dairies ','0','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 1st (Sun 31st May) : Gurgaon to Tehri - Transfer\r\nPickup from Gurugram and proceed for a scenic transfer to Tehri. Upon arrival, transfer to your hotel and check in.\r\n\r\n* Day 2nd  (Mon 1st June) : Tehri - Full day Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Tehri Lake , Tehri lake provides a hundred opportunities to the adventure lovers who throw caution to the winds by engaging in activities like Scuba Diving, Angling, Canoeing, Rowing , Boating, Water scooter, speed Boating, Rafting, Kayaking, House Boat, Cruise boating ( at your own cost) and later evening return to hotel, enjoy evening and overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n* Day 3rd (Tue 2nd June) : Tehri - Day Visit Kanatal\r\nApprox Distance: 30 Km\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from Hotel and drive to Kanatal for sightseeing.\r\n\r\n* Day 4th (Wed 3rd June) :  Tehri - Day Visit Mussoorie\r\nAfter breakfast at your hotel in Tehri, proceed for a scenic day excursion to Mussoorie, popularly known as the â€œQueen of Hills.â€ Enjoy a beautiful drive through winding hill roads and lush green surroundings. Upon arrival, begin your sightseeing with a visit to Kempty Falls, one of the most famous waterfalls in the region. Continue to Gun Hill for panoramic views of the Himalayas and the Doon Valley, followed by a leisurely walk along Mall Road Mussoorie for shopping and local experiences. Later, visit Camel\'s Back Road for a peaceful stroll and scenic sunset views. After completing the sightseeing, proceed back to Tehri. Upon arrival, you will be dropped at your hotel for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\n* Day 5th (Thu 4th June) : Drop To - Gurgaon\r\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel . Drop to Gurgaon .\r\n',58000,25000,'* 2N Accommodation in Tehri (Le Roi Lake View(Koti) )  with Daily Breakfast.\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Tehri (The Ridge House Tehri) with Daily Breakfast.\r\n* All transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* Vehicle will be provided from 8:00 am to 8:00pm\r\n* Vehicle : 12 seater Urbania Traveler \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* A/C room will not be provided in hill area.\r\n* A/C will not work on hills.\r\n* Entry fee for any monument will be paid directly by the client\r\n* Vehicle is as per itinerary and not on disposal. Additional sightseeing or transfer which are not mentioned in itinerary is payable to the driver directly.','',0,'Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking. \r\nIn Mussoorie , Vehicle will not go to Landour due to government restrictions. It will only go up to Landour Parking or can be parked in Mussoorie. Guests will need to proceed to Landour by a local union vehicle on a direct basis.\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2026-04-27 16:54:14','2026-06-23 13:00:11'),(88,931,475,15496,5,0,1,'2026-05-16','2026-05-19',NULL,'Manali Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n16th May : Arrival at Manali and pick up from bus stop and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. Evening Manali Tour.\r\n\r\n17th May : After having breakfast, proceed for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Sissu and Gramphu\r\n\r\n18th May : After having breakfast, proceed for Manikaran \r\n\r\n19th May : Check-out from the hotel and manage the transfer on your own ',9500,4000,'* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Ertiga/Sumo\r\n* Vehicle will be on point to point basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','',0,'Hotel/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\n',66,0,'2026-05-13 11:49:15','2026-05-29 11:10:53'),(89,942,481,419,2,0,0,'2026-06-20','2026-07-03',NULL,'Srinagar Diaries','0','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (20 Jun) : Arrival at the Leh Airport and transfer to the booked hotel\r\nDay 02 (21 Jun) : Leh Sightseeing \r\nDay 03 (22 Jun) : Leh to Nubra valley and sightseeing \r\nDay 04 (23 Jun) : Nubra Sightseeing \r\nDay 05 (24 Jun) : Nubra to Pangong \r\nDay 06 (25 Jun) : Pangong \r\nDay 07 (26 Jun) : Pangong To Leh \r\nDay 08 (27 Jun) : LEH - KARGIL \r\nDay 09 (28 Jun) : Kargil to Srinagar, Srinagar Local Sightseeing \r\nDay 10 (29 Jun) : Doodhpathri Day Trip from Srinagar \r\nDay 11 (30 Jun) : Srinagar - Gulmarg and Sightseeing \r\nDay 12 (1st Jul) : Gulmarg to Pahalgam and Sightseeing\r\nDay 13 (2nd Jul) : Pahalgam Sightseeing \r\nDay 14 (3rd Jul) : Pahalgam to Srinagar Airport\r\n\r\n\r\n',186000,48200,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accomodation in Leh with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Nubra Valley with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Pangong with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 3N Accommodation In Srinagar with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 1N Accommodation In Gulmarg with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Pahalgam with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* 01 Non AC Innova as per programme (Leh to Srinagar)\r\n* Shikara Ride on Dal Lake for 01 hour\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Horse Riding upto Baisaran Valley (Mini Switzerland) in Pahalgam to be done at own cost. Approximate charges - Rs. 700-1200 Per Pax. (Bargain is a must)\r\n* SNOW JEEP FROM TANGMARG - GULMARG - TANGMARG @ RS.3000 to 3500 /- PER CAR FOR RETURN JOURNEY\r\n* Only local union vehicle is allowed to do sightseeing of inner bowl in Gulmarg. It can be done on Ponies , ATV vehicles or Local Taxi\'s. Guest needs to book local union vehicle for transfers inside Gulmarg.\r\nâ€¢ Bargaining in everything is must as at most places rates are not fixed by the government and if any rates are fixed, they are widely published.\r\nâ€¢ Any other activities not mentioned in inclusions like horse riding/tips/ extra food ordered / entry fees / liquor etc.\r\nâ€¢ Local Union Car in Pahalgam for covering Aru Valley Betab Valley & Chandanwari (03 Places in 03 hours) costs from INR.2200 (Van) / INR.2600 (Etios) / INR. 2700 (Tavera/Sumo/ EECO) / INR.3000 (Innova ) / INR.4000 (Innova Crysta).\r\n* Gondola cable Ride Phase 01 ticket cost INR. 810/- Per Person and Phase 02 INR.1050/- Per Person can be booked directly by guest from https://www.jammukashmircablecar.com Booking will be opened on timely basis, please check and follow the website.\r\n\r\n ','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n',66,0,'2026-07-13 17:43:47','2026-07-28 13:34:55'),(90,943,482,17407,8,0,0,'2026-07-22','2026-07-26',NULL,'Madurai Diaries ','0','Suggested Itinerary :- \r\n\r\n* Day 1 ( 22nd July) :  Madurai - Rameshwaram Arrival\r\n\r\n* Day 2 ( 23rd July) :  Rameshwaram\r\n\r\n* Day 3 (24 July) : Rameswaram to Madurai\r\n\r\n* Day 4 (25 July) :  Madurai \r\n\r\n* Day 5 (26 July) : Madurai Departure\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',0,0,'* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Rameshwaram hotel with Breakfast \r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Madurai hotel with Breakfast \r\n* Return Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary \r\n* Vehicle considered : Tempo  Traveller  \r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n* All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n\r\n ','',0,'Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNIGHT DRIVE - AFTER 1900 HRS WILL BE CHARGED EXTRA.\r\nTransportation Vehicle KM allowed on the basis of Garage to Garage (Timing 08 AM -07 PM).\r\nIn Hill station & Forest station, room & vehicle will not be air conditioned.\r\nSightseeing Missed Subject To Weather, Political & Traffic Conditions Is Non-Refundable\r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.      \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n',66,0,'2026-07-17 17:50:34','2026-07-28 15:57:45');
