W, UK) \r\n# PVT Transfer from Hotel to Glasgow Station By Minivan \r\n# PVT Transfer from London Hotel to London Airport by Minivan \r\n\r\n','# Anything Which is not included in inclusions','Package Remarks:\r\n- Confirmation & Rates Depends On Availability At Time Of Booking.\r\n- Rates & Availability Is Subject To Change At The Time Of Booking.\r\n- City & Government Tax To Be Paid Locally On Spot.\r\n- For The Above Said Tour, There Is No Pick Up And Drop Off From The Hotel, So Client Will Have To Reach At Departure Points And Back To Hotel Also At \r\n  Their Own Arrangement.\r\n- Above Mentioned Excursions Are Unescorted.\r\n- Package Rate Is Subject To Change If There Are Changes On Number Of Pax, Number Of Nights Or Change Of Travelling Date.\r\n- Intâ€™l Check In Time For Hotel Is 1500h Onwards And Check Out Time Is 1200hrs.\r\n- No Booking Has Been Made Yet\r\n','2022-06-15','2022-06-22',1,0,0,'2022-02-08 15:50:05','2022-02-08 20:02:18'),(31,157,38,4,0,0,166400,15000,'Delhi-Bangkok','No of pax : 04 Adults\r\n\r\nTravel Start Date        : 05-03-2022  \r\n\r\nTravel End Date          : 09-03-2022\r\n\r\nNo of night : 4N+5D\r\n\r\nHotel @ Mytt Beach Pattaya (Deluxe room) + Amari Watergate Bangkok (Deluxe room)\r\n\r\n','','02 nights accommodation with ABF ,Pattaya at above mention Hotel or similar\r\n\r\n02 nights accommodation with ABF ,Bangkok at above mention Hotel or similar \r\n \r\n01 Covid Screening test (RT-PCR) \r\n\r\nTransfer from Suvarnabhumi AIrport - Pattaya Hotel on PVT basis\r\n\r\nCoral Island tour by join speedboat with lunch at indian restaurant on SIC transfer\r\n  \r\nNong Nooch Village Pattaya on PVT transfer \r\n \r\nSafari World & Marine Park with local lunch on PVT transfer \r\n \r\nHalf day Bangkok City & temple tour with English speaking guide on PVT transfer (Golden Buddha +  Marble Temple)\r\n  \r\n02nd Covid Screening test (RT-PCR) within 72 hour before departure + transfer\r\n  \r\nTransfer from Bangkok Hotel - suvarnabhumi Airport on PVT basis \r\n\r\n','Anything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-03-05','2022-03-09',1,0,0,'2022-02-09 16:43:16','2022-02-09 16:43:16'),(32,163,15530,8,0,0,277600,30000,'Andaman by Andaman experts','Day 1. Arrival - Port Blair - Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show \r\n1. Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n2. Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n3. Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\n4. Guest has to come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n5. L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs- 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n6. The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are \r\n   pleasant and happening here.\r\n \r\nDay 2. Port Blair - Visit to Ross & North Bay Islands\r\n1. Morning Breakfast, Pickup to water sports complex and board the speed boat\r\n2. The historic Ross Island will take you through the era of Japanese and British period\r\n3. North Bay Island is also known as Coral Beach is popular for water-based adventure activities such as Scuba Diving, Snorkelling, Para Sailings, \r\n   Dolphin Glass Bottom Boat ride, Coral Safari- Semi submarine etc.\r\n4. In case â€œRoss & Northâ€ not operational due to bad weather conditions or Covid-19 reason, we shall arrange alternative sightseeing, or we will \r\n   process applicable refund amount\r\n5. Evening, you can (Optional- Direct Payment basis) plan Corbinâ€™s Cove Beach, you can experience enthralling Sea Kart boat ride first time in India.\r\n \r\nDay 3. Port Blair - Havelock - Radhanagar Beach\r\n1. Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock  \r\n2. If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n3. Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n4. Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\n5. Do not forget to carry changing cloths and towel\r\n6. Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicle with wet cloths, please cooperate.\r\n7. Make your own choiceâ€¦. You can opt for Scuba Diving/ Kayaking/ Candid Photography at additional cost, booking in advance is recommended though our \r\n   local representative also can assist you.\r\n \r\nDay 4. Havelock - Elephanta beach\r\n1. Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\n2. Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n3. Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\n4. You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n5. You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n6. Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n7. Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Patthar Beachâ€ \r\n   OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\nDay 5. Havelock - Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge      \r\n1. Morning, Breakfast & proceed to jetty for onward journey to Neil Island\r\n2. Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n3. Afternoon, proceed to visit the following places:\r\n4. Bharatpura Beach: The white sand and shallow water beach is popular for swim, relaxation, and water activities such as Snorkelling, Boat diving and \r\n   boat tour.\r\n5. Laxmanpura beach: The white sand Coral Beach offers stunning sunset view\r\n6. Natural Bridge: Also known as Howrah Bridge the bridge has naturally formed by corals, its best seen during the low tide.\r\n7. Sightseeing will be based on tide and local representative will brief the final schedule.\r\n\r\n Day 6. Neil Island - Port Blair   \r\n1. Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n2. Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n3. Other places like Corbinâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and \r\n   availability (Optional)\r\n \r\nDay 7. Port Blair- Day Free at Leisure\r\n\r\nDay 8. Port Blair - Tour Ends\r\n1. Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\n2. Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.\r\n \r\n  \r\n','','â€¢Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty\r\n\r\nâ€¢Meal Plan: CP (Bed + Breakfast )\r\n\r\nâ€¢Airport & ferry terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned vehicle\r\n\r\nâ€¢All Sightseeing in Air-Conditioned vehicle (Zylo/ Ertiga/ Scorpio)\r\n\r\nâ€¢04 Nights stay on Quad sharing basis at Port Blair in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n\r\nâ€¢02 Nights stay on Quad sharing basis at Havelock in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n\r\nâ€¢01 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Neil Island in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n \r\nâ€¢Ferry tickets in catamaran Makruzz/ Green Ocean base category\r\n\r\nâ€¢Island transfers by Private ferries Makruzz/ Green Ocean/ Sea Link etc\r\n    \r\nâ€¢Entry to Cellular Jail+Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\nâ€¢Visit to Radha Nagar Beach in Havelock\r\n\r\nâ€¢Visit to Ross & North Bay Islands by Speed boat\r\n\r\nâ€¢Visit to Elephenta Beach/ Kala Patthar Beach in Havelock\r\n\r\nâ€¢Neil Island 3 points sightseeing\r\n\r\nâ€¢Applicable GST included\r\n','\r\n Anything which is not included in inclusions.','','2022-03-19','2022-03-26',1,0,0,'2022-02-11 13:50:16','2022-02-11 14:00:59'),(33,164,15530,8,0,0,0,0,'Andaman by Namho','Tentative Itinerary\r\nDay 1: Arrival at Port Blair in the morning by flight/ship and transfer to hotel. After lunch, visit the Corbyn\'s Cove Beach - 9 kms from Port Blair - a coconut palm fringed beach, ideal for swimming, sun-basking & bathing. In the evening, attend the enthralling Sound and Light Show at Cellular Jail - where the heroic saga of the Indian freedom struggle is brought alive. \r\n\r\nDay 2: Start Excursion to North Bay Island(Coral Island) - to see coral reefs, exotic varieties of beautiful ornamental fishes and other marine life. The glass bottom boat ride helps one to take a closer look at the vast coral colonies. Then, visit Ross Island - from where the Britishers\' governed the entire A&N islands, prior to Indiaâ€™s Independence. This island is an ideal destination for nature walk amidst sylvan surroundings with deers, peacocks, exotic birds, etc.)\r\n\r\nDay 3: Morning departure by inter-island ferry to Havelock Island (57 kms by sea from Port Blair). Stay here overnight amongst sandy beach and lush green forest in a comfortable beach resort. After lunch, proceed to the Asia\'s Best Beach \"Radhanagar Beach (Beach No.7).  O/N Havelock Island\r\n\r\nDay 4: After breakfast, proceed to half day trip to Elephant Beach for adventurous snorkelling experience. Snorkelling is leisure water sports in which a person swims on the surface of water wearing the face mask and view in the underwater corals.  Rest of the day at own leisure for independent activities at own cost.\r\n\r\nDay 5: After breakfast full day free on your own OR ( Optional: proceed for Kala Pathar Beach which is a long stretch of white silky sand with big black rocks beside the blue sea and it is situated on one corner of Havelock Island. The beach gets its name from the surrounding village, which is Kalapathar Village and the black rocks (known as Kalapathar in Hindi) that adorn the coastline here. Silvery sand and aqua green waters make the place exotic and exquisite and make this beach a great place to relax.)\r\n\r\nDay 6: Check out of the hotel is 09:00 Hrs. Return from Havelock Island in the morning and transfer to hotel in Neil Island. After lunch, visit Laxmanpur Beach, Bharatpur Beach and Natural Bridge Formation.     \r\n\r\nDay 7: Morning at own leisure for independent activities. Check out of the hotel is 09:00 Hrs. Return from Neil Island and transfer to hotel in Port Blair. \r\n\r\nDay 8: Transfer to Airport/Harbour for return flight/voyage.\r\n','','â€¢ Daily breakfast hotel/resort on the fixed menu\r\nâ€¢ Stay as mentioned under hotel details\r\nâ€¢ Light & Sound show entrance with transfers\r\nâ€¢ Corbyn Cove Beach transfers\r\nâ€¢ Tour : North Bay + Ross Island \r\nâ€¢ Visit to Radhanagar beach in Havelock Island\r\nâ€¢ Visit to Elephant beach in Havelock Island\r\nâ€¢ Bharatpur Beach/Sitapur Beach/Natural Bridge\r\nâ€¢ All transfers in a 01 AC SCORPIO / XYLO / ERTIGA Traveller at Port Blair\r\nâ€¢ Entry/Ferry Tickets at sightseeing places\r\nâ€¢ To and Fro Private Ferry Tickets to Havelock & Neil island\r\nâ€¢ Transfers at Havelock & Neil in a AC SCORPIO / XYLO / ERTIGA Traveller\r\nâ€¢ All excursions in a general ferry\r\nâ€¢ All applicable taxes\r\n','â€¢ Daily lunch, dinner and any special orders from the restaurant/bar apart from the suggested meal plan\r\nâ€¢ Vehicle at disposal\r\nâ€¢ Any personal expenses\r\nâ€¢ Any extra excursions apart from the suggested itinerary\r\n','*Incoming passengers arriving shall have to mandatorily carry RT-PCR negative test report issued from a ICMR approved lab, subject to condition that RT-PCR test should have been taken within 48 hours. RT-PCR timeline starts from the swab collection time. In addition to being in possession of negative RT-PCR report, all arriving passengers shall mandatorily undergo RT-PCR test upon arrival free of cost.\r\n*Passengers who are fully vaccinated i.e., those who have received both doses and completed 15 days from the receipt of the 2nd dose shall be exempted from pre-departure RT-PCR requirements and on arrival test procedures.\r\n*Covid Restrictions are applicable as per Govt authorities of respective destinations/places, Can be changed without Prior Notice. \r\n*Kindly note that if private Ferry is not operational then the passengers would be transferred to Havelock, Neil Island, Port Blair Vies versa by the govt. Ferry.\r\n*Kindly note that as per latest update from the hotels in case of any natural calamities, bad weather conditions or cancellation of ferries there would be no refund on the hotel and ferry part and all the extras would be direct payment basis. Kindly inform the clients accordingly to avoid on tour complaints. \r\n*As per update from administration once the tickets for light and sound show at cellular jail is booked on the particular day and if the show is cancelled under any condition there would be no refund. Tickets for the next show would be subject to availability and on direct payment basis. Also as per the availability light and show tickets shall be provided i.e. 01st show, 02nd show, 03rd show or 04th show. Same shall be applicable for govt. Entry permits in ross island /north bay.  Also, since the light and sound show tickets are online therefore if tickets for light and sound show are full the clients would be provided visit to cellular jail instead of light and sound show. Inform the clients accordingly.\r\n','2022-03-19','2022-03-26',1,0,0,'2022-02-11 17:07:23','2022-02-11 18:14:52'),(34,167,38,4,0,0,112000,15000,'Delhi-Pattaya','No of pax : 04 Adults\r\n\r\nTravel Start Date        : 05-03-2022  \r\n\r\nTravel End Date          : 08-03-2022\r\n\r\nNo of night : 3N+4D\r\n\r\nHotel @ Mytt Beach Pattaya (Deluxe room) \r\n','','Package Includes;\r\n\r\n03 nights accommodation with ABF ,Pattaya at above mention Hotel or similar\r\n\r\n01 Covid Screening test (RT-PCR) - Day 1\r\n\r\nTransfer from Suvarnabhumi AIrport - Pattaya Hotel on PVT basis\r\n\r\nCoral Island tour by join speedboat with lunch at indian restaurant on SIC transfer \r\n \r\nHalf day Bangkok City & temple tour with English speaking guide on PVT transfer (Golden Buddha +  Marble Temple) \r\n \r\n02nd Covid Screening test (RT-PCR) within 72 hour before departure + transfer  \r\nTransfer from Pattaya Hotel - suvarnabhumi Airport on PVT basis \r\n\r\n','Anything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-03-05','2022-03-09',1,0,0,'2022-02-14 16:39:15','2022-02-14 16:42:25'),(35,175,507,3,1,0,131500,16000,'Amazing Nepal','06 Night 07 Days Nepal (Kathmandu)Tour Package\r\n\r\nGuest Name:			UdanChoo.Com\r\n\r\nNumber of Pax:		03 Adults & 01 Child (08 Years)	\r\n		\r\nNationality:	        Indian\r\n\r\nNumber of Room:		01 Triple Sharing Bed Room\r\n\r\nArrival Date:		11 March 2022\r\n\r\nDeparture Date:		17 March 2022\r\n\r\nVehicle:		A/C SUV\r\n\r\nHotel Category:		Five Star\r\n\r\nHotel:			 	Hotel Soaltee, Kathmandu 03 Nights  (MAP Plan)\r\n\r\n				Hotel Hyatt, Kathmandu 03 Nights    (AP Plan)\r\n','','â€¢	Welcome soft drink.\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Airport pickup & drop with a/c SUV.\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Cashino Coupon provide worth INR.25000/- per person.\r\n\r\nâ€¢	03 nightâ€™s accommodation at Hotel Hyatt in Kathmandu with AP Plan. \r\n\r\nâ€¢	03 nightâ€™s accommodation at Hotel Soaltee in Kathmandu with MAP Plan.\r\n\r\nâ€¢	03 Day Dinner at hotel Soaltee.\r\n\r\nâ€¢	03 Day Lunch & Dinner at Cashino in Hotel Hyatt.\r\n','\r\n# One Time RTPCR test charge: INR. 1000/- Per Person	(Before Departing from KTM-DEL)\r\n\r\n# Anything which is not included in inclusions.','','2022-03-11','2022-03-17',1,0,0,'2022-02-20 15:56:08','2022-02-20 16:50:47'),(36,181,1616,2,1,0,0,0,'Tirupati Balaji','\r\n Day\r\n 1 	(22 Mar 2022 - Tuesday) Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\n\r\nArrival Transfer - Arrival Chennai - Tirupathi\r\n\r\nOn arrival at the Chennai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Tirupati. Tirupati is a city in the Indian state of Andhra Pradesh. Its Sri Venkateswara Temple sits atop one of the the 7 peaks of Tirumala Hills, attracting scores of Hindu pilgrims. Sri Venkateswara National Park, home to the temple, also contains the Sri Venkateswara Zoological Park with lions and primates. Nearby, next to a waterfall and cave believed to be sacred, Sri Kapileswara Swamy Temple is dedicated to Lord Shiva. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. During your free time, you can walk out to explore the surroundings, interact with locals, visit local markets or stay back in hotel to take pleasure of its modern amenities. Overnight stay at resort/hotel.\r\n\r\nDay\r\n2 	(23 Mar 2022 - Wednesday) Tirupati to Tirupathi Sightseeing Day 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Marasa Sarovar Premiere, Tirupati/Ramee Guestline Hotel\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Tirupati to Tirupathi Sightseeing Day 02\r\nMorning after breakfast local sightseeing of temples in Tirupati including Sri Govindarajaswami Temple, Kapila Theertham, Padmavati Temple, Trimala (Tirupati Balaji) Temple Akash Ganga & Paap Vinashni Temple. Overnight at the Resort/hotel. \r\n\r\nDay\r\n3 	(24 Mar 2022 - Thursday) Chennai Departure \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Marasa Sarovar Premiere, Tirupati/Ramee Guestline Hotel\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Chennai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Chennai international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories. \r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','\r\n   Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n\r\n   Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis \r\n\r\n   All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\n\r\n   All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n\r\n   Above Rate is Inclusive of GST 5% \r\n\r\n','\r\n   All those which are not mentioned above\r\n\r\n   Travel insurance \r\n\r\n   Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\n\r\n   Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc \r\n\r\n   All Items Of Personal Nature \r\n\r\n   Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc \r\n\r\n   Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport \r\n\r\n   Ayurveda Charges\r\n','','2022-02-22','2022-02-24',0,0,0,'2022-02-28 14:53:21','2022-02-28 14:53:21'),(37,183,54,2,2,0,0,0,'Delhi-Singapore',' Day 1  : Arrival \r\n\r\n Day 2 : Night Safari\r\n\r\nThe Night Safari is the world\'s first nocturnal zoo and is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Singapore. The animals of the Night Safari, ranging from Indian rhinoceros and pangolins to tarsiers and Asian elephants, are made visible by lighting that resembles moonlight. Cultural performances are a regular feature at the safari, and include tribal dances, blowpipe demonstrations and fire eating displays. Creatures of the Night Show is a performance presented by the animals in the Night Safari.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Universal Studios\r\nUniversal Studios Singapore is a theme park located within Resorts World Sentosa on Sentosa Island, Singapore.  There are a total of 24 attractions, of which 18 are original or specially adapted for the park. It features themed zones such as Hollywood, New York, Sci-Fi City, Ancient Egypt, The ost World, Far Far Away and Madagascar.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Sentosa \r\nSentosa is an island resort off Singaporeâ€™s southern coast. Attractions like Sentosa Beaches, Madame Tussauds and many more are on this island. Most of the attractions on Sentosa are located in either Resorts World Sentosa, Imbiah Lookout, or the Sentosa Beachfront.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Transfer from Hotel to Marina Bay Sands hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Departure \r\n\r\n','','05 Nights stay with breakfast\r\n \r\nNight Safari on PVT basis \r\n\r\nSentosa with Cable Car, Madam Tussauds, IOS and 4D on PVT basis\r\n\r\nUniversal Studios on PVT basis \r\n\r\nReturn airport transfers and inter hotel transfers on PVT basis \r\n\r\nMarina Bay Sands  is currently undergoing renovation works to provide new experiences for guests.\r\n\r\nDue to safe distancing measures, access to the Infinity Pool is limited to 1 hour 15 minutes per room, per day. \r\n\r\n','\r\nAnything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-03-22','2022-03-27',1,0,0,'2022-03-02 17:09:52','2022-03-02 17:09:52'),(38,188,54,2,2,0,0,0,'Delhi-Singapore',' Day 1  : Arrival \r\n\r\n Day 2 : Night Safari\r\n\r\nThe Night Safari is the world\'s first nocturnal zoo and is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Singapore. The animals of the Night Safari, ranging from Indian rhinoceros and pangolins to tarsiers and Asian elephants, are made visible by lighting that resembles moonlight. Cultural performances are a regular feature at the safari, and include tribal dances, blowpipe demonstrations and fire eating displays. Creatures of the Night Show is a performance presented by the animals in the Night Safari.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Universal Studios\r\nUniversal Studios Singapore is a theme park located within Resorts World Sentosa on Sentosa Island, Singapore.  There are a total of 24 attractions, of which 18 are original or specially adapted for the park. It features themed zones such as Hollywood, New York, Sci-Fi City, Ancient Egypt, The ost World, Far Far Away and Madagascar.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Sentosa \r\nSentosa is an island resort off Singaporeâ€™s southern coast. Attractions like Sentosa Beaches, Madame Tussauds and many more are on this island. Most of the attractions on Sentosa are located in either Resorts World Sentosa, Imbiah Lookout, or the Sentosa Beachfront.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Transfer from Hotel to Marina Bay Sands hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Departure \r\n\r\n','','05 Nights stay with breakfast\r\n \r\nNight Safari on PVT basis \r\n\r\nSentosa with Cable Car, Madam Tussauds, IOS and 4D on PVT basis.\r\n\r\nCity Tour on Pvt  basis\r\n\r\nUniversal Studios on PVT basis \r\n\r\nReturn airport transfers and inter hotel transfers on PVT basis \r\n\r\nMarina Bay Sands  is currently undergoing renovation works to provide new experiences for guests.\r\n\r\nDue to safe distancing measures, access to the Infinity Pool is limited to 1 hour 15 minutes per room, per day. \r\n\r\n','\r\nAnything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-03-22','2022-03-27',1,0,0,'2022-03-04 18:46:14','2022-03-04 19:00:59'),(39,187,2690,2,0,0,34000,12000,'Amazing Phuket','No. of pax â€“  2 adults \r\n \r\nTravel date â€“  28th May, 2022 to 2nd June, 2022\r\n \r\nHotel Option â€“ 4* Patong Resort, Phuket\r\n\r\n','','5 nightsâ€™ accommodation with ABF, Phuket at above-mentioned hotel\r\nPhi Phi Island tour by big boat + local Thai lunch + National Park fees on SIC basis\r\nPhuket City Tour on SIC basis\r\nHKT APT â€“ HKT HTL | HKT HTL â€“ HKT APT | all transfer on PVT basis','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions.','Additional costâ€“ On arrival RTPCR test at the Phuket airport (can be booked by you (https://www.thailandpsas.com/)','2022-05-28','2022-06-02',0,0,0,'2022-03-05 18:54:59','2022-03-05 19:37:42'),(40,195,2690,2,0,0,49640,12000,'Amazing Phuket','No. of pax â€“  2 adults \r\n \r\nTravel date â€“  28th May, 2022 to 2nd June, 2022\r\n \r\nHotel Option â€“ 4* Patong Resort, Phuket\r\n\r\n','','5 nightsâ€™ accommodation with ABF, Phuket at above-mentioned hotel\r\nPhi Phi Island tour by big boat + local Thai lunch + National Park fees on SIC basis\r\nPhuket City Tour on SIC basis\r\nHKT APT â€“ HKT HTL | HKT HTL â€“ HKT APT | all transfer on PVT basis\r\nRoom Decoration at the time of check-in\r\nA candle-light dinner ','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions.','Additional costâ€“ On arrival RTPCR test at the Phuket airport (can be booked by you (https://www.thailandpsas.com/)','2022-05-28','2022-06-02',0,0,0,'2022-03-07 19:30:29','2022-03-07 19:34:13'),(41,196,15530,4,0,0,60400,15000,'Incredible Andaman','Destination: Andaman Islands\r\nSectors Covered: Port Blair 2N + Havelock 2N \r\nDate of Travel: 13th Mar 2022\r\nNo. Of Pax: 04 Adults \r\nRoom Occupancy: 02 Room on Twin Sharing\r\nMeal Plan: CP (Breakfast only)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay wise Itinerary:\r\n \r\nDay 1. Arrival - Port Blair - Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show \r\n1. Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n2. Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n3. Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\n4. Guest has to come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n5. L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs- 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n6. The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n \r\nDay 2. Port Blair - Havelock - Radhanagar Beach\r\n1. Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock  \r\n2. If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n3. Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n4. Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\n5. Do not forget to carry changing cloths and towel\r\n6. Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicle with wet cloths, please cooperate.\r\n7. Make your own choiceâ€¦. You can opt for Scuba Diving/ Kayaking/ Candid Photography at additional cost, booking in advance is recommended though our local representative also can assist you.\r\n \r\nDay 3. Havelock - Elephanta beach\r\n1. Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\n2. Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n3. Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\n4. You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n5. You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n6. Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks, and changing clothes.\r\n7. Important: In case, Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Patthar Beachâ€ OR We can refund the applicable amount. \r\n \r\n \r\nDay 4. Havelock - Port Blair   \r\n1. Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n2. Arrival in Port Blair, transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n3. Other places like Corbinâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional)\r\n \r\nDay 5. Port Blair - Tour Ends\r\n1. Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\n2. Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach the airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.\r\n','','Your Package Tour Price Includes:\r\nÂ· Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty\r\nÂ· Meal Plan: CP(Bed + Breakfast)\r\nÂ· Airport & ferry terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned vehicle\r\nÂ· All Sightseeing in an Air-Conditioned vehicle (Zylo/ Ertiga/ Scorpio)\r\nÂ· 02 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Port Blair in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\nÂ· 02 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Havelock in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\nÂ· Ferry tickets in catamaran Makruzz/ Green Ocean base category\r\nÂ· Island transfers by Private ferries Makruzz/ Green Ocean/ Sea Link etc    \r\nÂ· Entry to Cellular Jail+Light & Sound Show\r\nÂ· Visit to Radha Nagar Beach in Havelock \r\n. Visit to Elephanta beach in havelock \r\n. Applicable GST included ','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions.','Covid-19 Guidelines:\r\nÂ· All fully vaccinated (Double Dose+15 Days completed) persons coming to Andaman Islands from mainland are exempted for carrying RT-PCR negative test report, irrespective of the type of vaccine received and country of origin.\r\n\r\nÂ· All children below 5 years of age are exempted from carrying RT-PCR negative test report and further RT-PCR testing at Port Blair Airport.\r\n\r\nÂ· All other passengers viz. unvaccinated and partially vaccinated passengers (those who have taken only 1st dose of COVID vaccine) shall have to produce RT-PCR negative test report to travel to Port Blair from mainland, as is the practice now. Such RT-PCR test should have been taken within 48 hours prior to commencement of journey from the origin airport connecting Port Blair. Such passengers will also have to undergo additional RT-PCR test on arrival at Port Blair.\r\n\r\nÂ· Please share all guestâ€™s ID proof Aadhar Card/ Voter ID Card/ Passport copy (Pan Card not accepted) and flight details upon confirmation of booking to ensure all services booked on time\r\n\r\nÂ· Our team is committed to work in a physical contactless environment and our local team members will wear face masks while interacting with the guests.\r\nÂ· Our vehicles will be sanitized as per administration/ government guidelines and will be equipped with hand sanitizers.\r\nÂ· All guests are required to wear face masks in public areas/ inside vehicles and to sanitize or wash their hands frequently. Masks will be available for purchase with our tour coordinators.','2022-03-13','2022-03-17',0,0,0,'2022-03-07 22:45:31','2022-03-07 22:51:00'),(42,201,507,11,0,0,161700,30000,'Amazing Nepal',' \r\n 03 Night 04 Days Nepal (Kathmandu) Tour Package\r\n\r\n Number of Pax:		11 Adults	\r\n		\r\n Nationality:	        Indian\r\n\r\n Number of Room:	05 Double & 01 Extra Bed Room\r\n\r\n Arrival Date:		18 April 2022\r\n\r\n Departure Date:	21 April