ee (Similar), Kathmandu, 02 Nights \r\n\r\n			Hotel Pokhara Grande (Similar), Pokhara 02 Nights \r\n\r\n17 April 2022:\r\n Pickup from Kathmandu International Airport and drop at hotel.\r\n Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n18 April 2022:\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara via half day sightseeing at Kathmandu covering Pashupatinath Temple & Boudhanath Stupa & drop at hotel at Pokhara.  \r\n 210 KM\r\n\r\n Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n19 April 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Full  day sightseeing in Pokhara covering Bindabashini Temple, Gupteshor Cave, Deviâ€™s Fall, Seti River, Fewa Lake & Peace Pagoda\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n20 April 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Drive from Pokhara to Kathmandu via Manakamana Temple Darshan by Cable Car) & drop at hotel. 210 KM\r\n\r\n Welcome drinks at hotel.\r\n\r\n Dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\n Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n21 April 2022:\r\n\r\n Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n\r\n Drive from hotel to Kathmandu International Airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','        \r\nâ€¢Welcome soft drink.\r\n\r\nâ€¢Airport pickup & drop with a/c Toyota Hiace.\r\n\r\nâ€¢Kathmandu One half day sightseeing.\r\n\r\nâ€¢02 nights accommodation at respective hotel in Kathmandu with MAP Plan. \r\n\r\nâ€¢02 nights accommodation at respective hotel in Pokhara with MAP Plan.\r\n\r\nâ€¢Pokhara one full day sightseeing.\r\n','Monuments and museum entrance fees for above sightseeing places.\r\n\r\nManakamana Cable Car Ticket: INR. 550 Per Person.\r\n\r\nOne Time RTPCR test charge: INR. 1000 Per Person(Before Departing from KTM-DEL)\r\n\r\n Anything which is not included in inclusions.\r\n\r\n','','2022-04-17','2022-04-21',1,0,0,'2022-03-09 18:56:12','2022-03-09 19:45:22'),(45,206,54,2,2,0,0,0,'Delhi-Singapore',' Day 1  : Arrival \r\n\r\n Day 2 : Night Safari\r\n\r\nThe Night Safari is the world\'s first nocturnal zoo and is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Singapore. The animals of the Night Safari, ranging from Indian rhinoceros and pangolins to tarsiers and Asian elephants, are made visible by lighting that resembles moonlight. Cultural performances are a regular feature at the safari, and include tribal dances, blowpipe demonstrations and fire eating displays. Creatures of the Night Show is a performance presented by the animals in the Night Safari.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Universal Studios\r\nUniversal Studios Singapore is a theme park located within Resorts World Sentosa on Sentosa Island, Singapore.  There are a total of 24 attractions, of which 18 are original or specially adapted for the park. It features themed zones such as Hollywood, New York, Sci-Fi City, Ancient Egypt, The ost World, Far Far Away and Madagascar.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Sentosa \r\nSentosa is an island resort off Singaporeâ€™s southern coast. Attractions like Sentosa Beaches, Madame Tussauds and many more are on this island. Most of the attractions on Sentosa are located in either Resorts World Sentosa, Imbiah Lookout, or the Sentosa Beachfront.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Transfer from Hotel to Marina Bay Sands hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Departure \r\n\r\n','','05 Nights stay with breakfast\r\n \r\nNight Safari on PVT basis \r\n\r\nSentosa with Cable Car, Madam Tussauds, IOS and 4D on PVT basis.\r\n\r\nCity Tour on Pvt  basis\r\n\r\nUniversal Studios on PVT basis \r\n\r\nReturn airport transfers and inter hotel transfers on PVT basis \r\n\r\nMarina Bay Sands  is currently undergoing renovation works to provide new experiences for guests.\r\n\r\nDue to safe distancing measures, access to the Infinity Pool is limited to 1 hour 15 minutes per room, per day. \r\n\r\n','\r\nAnything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-03-21','2022-03-26',1,0,0,'2022-03-10 11:13:50','2022-03-10 11:21:00'),(46,209,15530,8,2,0,0,0,'Amazing Andaman',' \r\nDestination	Andaman Islands\r\n\r\nSectors Covered	Port Blair 2N + Havelock 2N + Neil Island 1N\r\n\r\nDate of Travel	12th May \'22\r\n\r\nNo. Of Pax	08 Adults + 2 Child  \r\n\r\nRoom Occupancy	04 Dbl Room + 02 Extra Mattress\r\n\r\nMeal Plan	CP\r\n\r\nDay 1. Arrival - Port Blair - Cellular Jail - Light & Sound Show \r\n\r\n1.Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n\r\n2.Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n3.Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\n\r\n4.Guest has to come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n\r\n5.L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs- 1900hrs subject to availability\r\n\r\n6.The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant \r\n  and happening here.\r\n\r\nDay 2. Port Blair - Havelock \r\n\r\n1.Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock \r\n \r\n2.If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n\r\n3.Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3. Havelock - Elephanta beach\r\n\r\n1.Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\n\r\n2.Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n\r\n3.Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\n\r\n4.You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n\r\n5.You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\n\r\n6.Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n\r\n7.Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Patthar Beachâ€ \r\n OR We can refund the applicable amount. \r\n\r\nDay 4. Havelock - Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge  \r\n    \r\n1.Morning, Breakfast & proceed to jetty for onward journey to Neil Island\r\n\r\n2.Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\n\r\n3.Afternoon, proceed to visit the following places:\r\n\r\n4.Bharatpura Beach: The white sand and shallow water beach is popular for swim, relaxation, and water activities such as Snorkelling, Boat diving and \r\n  boat tour.\r\n\r\n5.Laxmanpura beach: The white sand Coral Beach offers stunning sunset view\r\n\r\n6.Natural Bridge: Also known as Howrah Bridge the bridge has naturally formed by corals, its best seen during the low tide.\r\n\r\n7.Sightseeing will be based on tide and local representative will brief the final schedule\r\n\r\nDay 5. Neil Island - Port Blair \r\n  \r\n1.Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n\r\n2.Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n\r\n3.Other places like Corbinâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and \r\n  availability (Optional)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6. Port Blair - Tour Ends\r\n\r\n1.Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\n\r\n2.Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','â€¢Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty\r\n\r\nâ€¢Meal Plan: CP(Bed + Breakfast )\r\n\r\nâ€¢Airport & ferry terminal Transfers in 2 Air-Conditioned vehicle\r\n\r\nâ€¢All Sightseeing in 2 Air-Conditioned vehicle (Zylo/ Ertiga/ Scorpio)\r\n\r\nâ€¢02 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Port Blair in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n\r\nâ€¢02 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Havelock in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n\r\nâ€¢01 Nights stay on Dbl sharing basis at Neil Island in Hotels as per itinerary.\r\n \r\nâ€¢Ferry tickets in catamaran Makruzz/ Green Ocean base category\r\n\r\nâ€¢Island transfers by Private ferries Makruzz/ Green Ocean/ Sea Link etc\r\n    \r\nâ€¢Entry to Cellular Jail+Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\nâ€¢Visit to Radha Nagar Beach in Havelock \r\n\r\n.Visit to Elephanta beach in havelock \r\n\r\nâ€¢Neil Island 3 points sightseeing\r\n\r\n.Applicable GST included \r\n\r\n.Visit Radhanagar beach \r\n\r\n','.Anything which is not included in inclusions','','2022-05-16','2022-05-21',1,0,0,'2022-03-11 19:41:28','2022-03-11 20:12:35'),(47,212,624,2,0,0,43000,5000,'North East','Day 01: Guwahati - Kaziranga National Park (230 KM | 4.5 Hrs)\r\nWelcome to Awesome Assam. Meet and be assisted by our representative at the airport/Railway Station. Transfer to Kaziranga National Park, the home of the One Horn Indian Rhinoceros. Check in at your hotel/Lodge/resort. Evening you may visit Orchid Park and the nearby Tea Plantations. Overnight stay at Kaziranga National Park.\r\n \r\nDay 02: Kaziranga National Park\r\nEarly morning explore Kaziranga National Park on back of elephant. Apart from world\'s endangered One Horn Indian Rhinoceros, the Park sustains half the world\'s population of genetically pure Wild Water Buffaloes, over 1000 Wild elephants and perhaps the densest population of Royal Bengal Tiger anywhere. Kaziranga National Park is also a bird watcher\'s paradise and home to some 500 species of Birds. The Crested Serpent Eagle, Palla\'s Fishing Eagle, Greyheaded Fishing Eagle, Swamp Partridge, Bar-headed goose, whistling Teal, Bengal Florican, Storks, Herons and Pelicans are some of the species found here. We will return to the resort for breakfast. Afternoon we proceed for a jeep safari. Evening come back to the hotel. Overnight stay at Kaziranga National Park.\r\n\r\nDay 03: Kaziranga National Parkâ€“ Shillong (280 Km | 6 Hrs)\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Shillong, also called \'Scotland of the East\". Reach the majestic Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which the biggest local market. Overnight stay in Shillong.\r\n \r\nDay 04: Shillong - Cherrapunji - Shillong (65 KM | 1.5 Hrs Per Way)\r\nGet up early today to enjoy the mesmerizing mornings of Shillong. After early breakfast drive to Cherrapunji, this is the wettest place in the world. Visit  Eco Park, Dainthlen Falls, Nohkalikai Falls, Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), Mawsmai Cave, Thangkharang Park. Evening return to Shillong. Visit Elephanta Falls and Shillong Peak for some breathtaking views. Overnight stay in Shillong.\r\n\r\nDay 05 â€“ Shillong â€“ Mawsynram â€“ Mawphlang Sacred Forest â€“ Shillong ( 60 KM | 1.5 Hrs Per Way)\r\nAfter breakfast visit Mawsynram which as per the new geological reports receives the highest rainfall in the world. The area is known for its many caves. Later visit Mawphlang Sacred Grove. It is one of the biggest Sacred Groves in Meghalaya.It is a well preserved forest by local community. Nothing can be taken out from the forest as this is being protected by the local deities. Visit Khasi model village. Evening return to Shillong. Visit Elephanta Falls and Shillong Peak for some breathtaking views.. Overnight stay in Shillong.\r\n \r\nDay 06: Shillong - Guwahati (100 KM | 3 Hrs)\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Guwahati. Visit Kamakhya temple(Depending upon the flight timing.Later drop to airport for onward journey.Tour ends.','','1. Accommodation on double/Twin Sharing Basis\r\n2. Pick up and drop off as per the itinerary from the respective Airport // Train Station\r\n3. Daily Breakfast\r\n4. Vehicle on point to point basis as per the itinerary\r\n5. Service of an Experience Driver for Entire Tour\r\n6. Driver allowances, toll, parking, fuel etc.\r\n7. Per Day Per Person 1-liter mineral water.\r\n8. Inner Line Permit  (Arunachal, Mizoram and Nagaland)','1. Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone, tips, gratuity, Food and drinks .\r\n2. Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n3. Camera fees, Guide / tour escort charges & Entrance Fees .\r\n4. Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances, etc (to be borne by the client, which is directly payable on the spot) .\r\n5. Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure .\r\n6. Insurance.\r\n7. Air fare // Railway Tickets.\r\n8. Anything which is not include in the inclusion // itinerary\r\n9. Jeep Safari at Kaziranga ( Additional charge of INR 3200 Per Jeep , Max 05 paxs can seat together)\r\n10. Elephant Safari at kaziranga ( Additional charges INR 1000 Per Seat irrespective of Age)\r\n11. Bomla pass, PTSO Lake and Madhuri Lake (Additonal charge INR 5500 per vechicle, Max 05 Person can seat together) Payment Can Be Done Directly At Tawang Hotel\r\n ','','2022-04-17','2022-04-22',0,0,0,'2022-03-15 17:39:24','2022-03-15 17:43:11'),(48,213,15506,3,1,0,228400,38000,'Manchester-Turkey','Day 01 |                                                               Istanbul â€“ Kayseri â€“ Cappadocia (by flight)\r\n \r\nArrival to Istanbul and take your connection flight to Kayseri ASR. Arrival to Cappadocia and transfer to your hotel (appr. 1 hrs drive). Check-in. Free time at Leisure.\r\n \r\nOvernight in Cappadocia (Dinner)\r\n \r\nDay 02 |                                                               Cappadocia\r\nDeparture from the hotel for Goreme-North Cappadocia Tour. Visit Uc Guzeller and Devrent  Valley, which has various types of Fairy chimneys. We will walk through the amazing valley. Drive to  Avanos which is famous for pottery. Then proceed to Goreme Open Air Museum, where this religious education was started.  Last stop for photos taken Uchisar Castle and Esentepe. End of the tour, return to your hotel.\r\n\r\nOvernight in Cappadocia (Breakfast-Lunch-Dinner)\r\n \r\n\r\nDay 03 |                                                               Cappadocia â€“ Konya â€“ Pamukkale (by surface)\r\n \r\nIn the early morning, check out from the hotel and travel to Konya on surface (appr. 4hrs drive). En route visit 13th century Sultanhani Caravanserai built on the famous silk route.  In Konya, we will visit the Mausoleum of Mevlana, the worldwide famous mystic. Local lunch at any Turkish Restaurant.\r\n \r\nAfter lunch, continue to Pamukkale (appr. 5hrs drive), the cotton fortress. Visit the hot mineral waters burst from the earth and cascade over cliffs forming pools and stalactites. Reach to the hotel at the evening.\r\n \r\nOVERNIGHT IN PAMUKKALE (Breakfast-Lunch-Dinner)\r\n \r\nDay 04 |                                                               Pamukkale â€“  Kusadasi (by surface)\r\n \r\nVisit to Pamukkale which is a natural site that contains hot springs and travertines, terraces or carbonate minerals left by the flowing water. Then will visit Hierapolis Ancient City where is the biggest cemetery of Anatolia. Local lunch at Turkish Restaurant. Continue drive to your Kusadasi hotel (appr. 2.5 hrs drive), check-in, free time.\r\n \r\nOvernight in Kusadasi (Breakfast-Lunch-Dinner)\r\n \r\nDay 05 |                                                               Kusadasi â€“ Ephesus â€“ Izmir â€“ Istanbul (by flight)\r\n \r\nWe visit Ephesus ruins, including The Polio Fountain, The Temple of Hadrian that dedicated to the Emperor Hadrian in 138 AD. Then we visit Great Theatre,the largets ancient theatre with 25,000 seat capacity. Lunch will be served at a local restaurant. After lunch, we visit Library of Celsius, one of the most beautiful structure of Ephesus, buit in 117 AD. Our last stop is the House of Virgin Mary, where Mary may have spent her last days.\r\n \r\nAfter the tour, drive to Izmir ADB Airport. Flight to Istanbul. Arrival to Istanbul and transfer to your hotel, check-in.\r\n \r\nOvernight in Istanbul (Breakfast-Lunch)\r\n \r\nDay 06 |                                                               Istanbul\r\n \r\nDepart for Full-Day Old City Tour. Tour of \"Sultan Ahmet Center\", the heart of the \"Old City\" from where the Byzantine and Ottoman Empires were ruled. Hagia Sophia, the Church of Divine Wisdom, one of the greatest marvels ofarchitecture, constructed as a basilica in the 6th century by Emperor Justinian. Blue Mosque (the mosque visited from outside on Friday mornings because of noon prayer) facing Hagia Sophia, famous with its blue Iznik tiles and unique with 6 minarets, built in the name of Sultan Ahmet. Hippodrome, center of sportive events (chariot races, athletics) and political activities of the old city. Serpentine Column, Obelisk of Theodosius and German Fountain of Wilhelm II are the monuments decorating the Hippodrome. Then visit Topkapi Palace, one of the biggest museum of Turkey and the Balkan Peninsula.\r\nThen visit Grand Covered Bazaar, most attractive shopping center and the biggest \"souk\" in the world with nearly 4000 shops selling antiques, jewellery, gold, carpets, leatherware and souvenir.\r\n \r\nOvernight  in Istanbul (Breakfast-Lunch)\r\n \r\nDay 07 | Istanbul\r\n \r\nFree day at leisure.\r\n \r\nOvernight in Istanbul (Breakfast)\r\n \r\nDay 08 |                                                               Istanbul â€“ FLY HOME (by flight)\r\n \r\nCheck-out from hotel. Drive to Istanbul IST. Return flight to your home.\r\n \r\n(Breakfast) \r\n\r\n**End of Services**\r\n \r\nHOTELS (4*):\r\nCappadocia â€“ MUSTAFA HOTEL (standard room) or similar on Half Board basis\r\nPamukkale â€“ NINOVA THERMAL (standard room) or similar on Half Board basis\r\nKusadasi â€“ COMFORT ADA CLASS (standard room) or similar on Half Board basis\r\nIstanbul â€“ BLACK BIRD HOTEL  (standard room) or similar on Bed and Breakfast basis','','Â·         07 nights stay at the mentioned hotels or similar in each city \r\nÂ·         Daily breakfast at the hotels except on arrival day\r\nÂ·         04 local dinners at the hotels, except in Istanbul\r\nÂ·         01 Full Day Goreme-North Cappadocia Tour with local lunch in Cappadocia\r\nÂ·         Cappadocia â€“ Pamukkale on surface transfer via FD Konya & Mevlana Museum tour with local lunch in Konya\r\nÂ·         01 Full Day Pamukkale tour with local lunch in Pamukkale\r\nÂ·         01 Full Day Ephesus city tour with local lunch in Kusadasi\r\nÂ·         01 Full Day Istanbul Old City Tour with local lunch in Istanbul\r\nÂ·         All sightseeing tours on SIC basis with local English speaking guide asistance during the tours\r\nÂ·         Airport â€“ Hotel â€“ Airport â€“ return transfer services on  SIC basis in each city','Â·         X Covid-19 PCR Test\r\nÂ·         X Any International & Internal flights\r\nÂ·         X  Any Tips to Driver & Guide\r\nÂ·         X  Drinks at Meals\r\nÂ·         X  Personal Expenses\r\nÂ·         X  Porterage\r\nÂ·         X  Surcharges as applicable if any\r\nÂ·         X  Visa Fees and Travel Insurance\r\nÂ·         X  Any services not mentioned in the inclusions list','','2022-10-22','2022-10-29',0,0,0,'2022-03-15 23:54:53','2022-03-16 14:32:26'),(49,214,15567,11,0,0,287100,30000,'Amazing Nepal','07 Night 08 Days Kathmandu, Pokhara & Chitwan Tour Package\r\n\r\nNumber of Pax:		10 Adults \r\n\r\nNationality:		Indian\r\n\r\nNumber of Room:		05 Double & 01 Extra Bed Room\r\n\r\nArrival Date:		14 April 2022\r\n\r\nDeparture Date:		21 April 2022\r\n\r\nVehicle:		A/C Totyta Hiace\r\n\r\nHotel Category		Four Star\r\n\r\nHotel:			Hotel Ramada (Similar), Kathmandu 3 Nights (MAP Plan)\r\n\r\n			Hotel B