Phuket - Del Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 02 Nights Stay in Krabi \r\n* 03 Nights Stay in Phuket \r\n* Daily Breakfast \r\n* Transfers from Phuket Airport to Krabi Hotel â€“ PVT \r\n* Transfers from Krabi Hotel to Phuket Hotel â€“ PVT \r\n* Transfers from Phuket Hotel to Phuket Airport â€“ PVT \r\n* Krabi 4 Island Tour by Speed Boat + Picnic Lunch â€“ SIC (Exclude the National Park Admission Fee THB 400 PP)\r\n* Half Day Phuket City Tour â€“ SIC \r\n* Full Day Phi Phi Island Tour by Speedboat with Local Lunch on SIC (Excl. National Marine Park Fee THB 400 PP) \r\n* Travel Insurance','* Any meal or transfers other than those mentioned above\r\n* Visa Charges\r\n* TCS \r\n','The rates are valid till 31st January, 2023. Flight fare is dynamic.','2023-02-12','2023-02-17',1,0,0,'2023-02-01 22:53:44','2023-02-01 22:57:37'),(228,593,15534,6,0,0,0,0,'Leh-Ladakh','3N Leh - 1N Nubra Valley - 1N Pangong\r\n\r\nDETAILED ITINERARY :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Leh \r\nExperience a wonderful flight over the Himalaya .On arrival,you will be receive by Our representative and transfer to hotel. After welcome tea and coffee, rest for whole day & and let your body take complete acclimatization & Overnight Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Hall Of Fame / Magnetic Hill / Gurudwara/ Sangam Point\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. After breakfast we take you for a tour of Hall of Fame, Gurudwara Patthar Sahib, Magnetic Hill, Kali Temple and Sangam. At Sangam you can enjoy rafting on Zangskar river.\r\nHall of Fame is a must visit for every patriotic Indian. It has been built by Indian army in memory of soldiers who lost their lives in Kargil war. Return to Leh in the afternoon.\r\nGurdwaraPatthar Sahib located at a distance of 40 kms from Leh, was constructed in 1571, in memory of Guru Nanak to commemorate his visit to this region.\r\nMagnetic Hill is the place where you will see your car, with its engine turned off, move upwards on a steep slope. It almost sounds unbelievable.\r\nThe Sangam is the place called Nimu where the Zanskarriver and Indus rivers merge. In the evening come back to Leh. Overnight Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Leh /Nubra Valley via Khardongla. 125km.\r\nAfter an early breakfast ,drive to beautiful NubraValley via Khardungla (Highest Motor-able road in the World, 18,380 ft) with the zig zag trail continues and drive till Hundar village. On arrival check in Hotel or camp. Afternoon enjoy the beauty of sand dune and double hump camel ride. Overnight at Camp or Hotel.\r\nKHARDUNGLA PASS: The road journey to Nubra valley leads through Khardung La pass (The highest Motorable road in the world) 18,390 ft. around 39 Kms. Away from Leh. There are two checkpoints on the both sides of the pass. Khardong is the first village of Nubra valley at higher altitude than Deskit and other villages.\r\nDESKIT VILLAGE: Deskit is the main village of headquarter of Nubra valley, which has a small market consisting of a row of shops and about 500 years old Gompa on the hilltop. Spectacular view of the valley can be seen form the monastery. DESKIT GOMPA: Deskit Gompa was founded by Lama Sherab Zangpo of Stod in about 1420 AD during the reign of King Dragspa. About 100 monks are residing in the Gompa, which is a branch of Thikse Monastery. The monastic festival called Gustor takes place on 20th and 21st days of the 12th month of Tibetan calendar.\r\nHUNDAR VILLAGE: Hundar is a beautiful village to stay with lot of trees and you will really enjoy your stay at Hundar. It has a small monastery and ruined fort above the village. The walk or Camel Safari (Double Hump bacterian camels)\r\nfrom Hundar to Deskit, through sand dunes for two hours is wonderful (on own).\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Disket/ Hunder/ Pangong Lake (Via Shayok)\r\nToday , we get up early morning visit to Diskit monastery and have wonderful view of Nubra valley. Later drive to Pangong Lake via Shayok.\r\nEnjoy the turquoise color panoramic lake and the magnificent mountains and landscapes which will leave you awestruck . Overnight at Camp.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Pangong / Leh\r\nAfter a late breakfast, we stroll in and around the lake and watch the mother nature soothes you . Later drive back to Leh by visiting Thiksay monasteries and ShayPalace, also Visit Shanti Stupa and Leh Palace if not visited the day before. Overnight Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Departure: Leh/ Delhi\r\nAfter an early breakfast, depart to the airport for your onward destination ....fly with sweet memories of Ladakh... TOUR END!!!\r\n','','Ã˜ Delhi - Leh - Delhi Airfare\r\nÃ˜ Accommodation on Twin sharing basis as per the details given above\r\nÃ˜ Meal Plan MAPAI ( Breakfast and Dinner)\r\nÃ˜ Arrival/departure transfer and all land transfers as per the itinerary\r\nÃ˜ NAC Xylo / Similar as per the itinerary.\r\nÃ˜ Pickup and Drop from Leh Airport\r\nÃ˜ Inner line permit.\r\nÃ˜ Driver allowance/toll/parking/road tax/fuel charge.\r\n','Ã˜ Any additional meals other than mentioned in the â€˜inclusiveâ€™ coloumn.\r\nÃ˜ Travel insurances. \r\nÃ˜ Monuments entrances fee and optional Activities mentioned in the itinerary.\r\nÃ˜ Items of personal nature like porterage, tips, laundry, telephone calls, mineral water etc.\r\nÃ˜ Expenses caused by factors beyond our control like rail and flight delays, roadblocks, political disturbances etc.\r\nÃ˜ Any item not specifically mentioned in Inclusions column.','The rates are valid till 10th Feb, 2023. Flight fare is dynamic.','2023-04-19','2023-04-24',1,0,0,'2023-02-06 16:25:42','2023-02-06 16:25:42'),(229,596,419,4,1,0,0,0,'Srinagar Super Saver','1N Pahalgam - 1N Gulmarg - 2N Srinagar\r\n\r\nDAY 01 - ARRIVAL + CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)                                              \r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel in Pahalgam, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.                \r\n                                               \r\nDAY 02 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)                                         \r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.                                                                                   \r\n                                               \r\nDAY 03 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOTEL                                           \r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in hotel. You can enjoy Shikara Ride for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                     \r\n                                               \r\nDAY 04 - SRINAGAR OLD CITY TOUR                                       \r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel  & proceed to Srinagar Old City Tour. Jamia Masjid is a mosque in Srinagar, situated at Nowhatta in the middle of the Old City. The Mosque was commissioned by Sultan Sikandar in 1394 CE and completed in 1402 CE, at the behest of Mir Mohammad Hamadani, son of Mir Sayyid Ali Hamadani. It is regarded as one of the most important mosques in Kashmir. After this, you can go The Hazratbal Shrine (\"Majestic Place\") is a Muslim shrine in Hazratbal, Srinagar. It contains a relic, the Moi-e-Muqqadas, believed by many Muslims of Kashmir to be Muhammad\'s hair. The name of the shrine comes from the Farsi word Hazrat, meaning \"respected\", and the Kashmiri word bal, meaning \"place\". Thus it means the place which is given high regards and is respected among the people.  Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                        \r\n\r\nDAY 05 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL                                                                                               \r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar hotel and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.    \r\n ','','âœ” Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Airfare\r\nâœ” Accommodation on twin/double/triple sharing basis\r\nâœ” Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\nâœ” Airport/station pick-up and drop facility as confirmed by the travelers.\r\nâœ” Sightseeing by non-AC Swift Dzire/Etios/Tavera/Innova Tempo as per the package selected.\r\nâœ” Cost of Shikara Ride.\r\nâœ” Driver Allowances.\r\nâœ” Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\nâœ” Hotel Taxes','âœ” Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\nâœ” Extra Meals - Meals not included in package anything not specifically mentioned under the head â€œPrices includedâ€.\r\nâœ” Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\nâœ” Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\nâœ” Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\nâœ”Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\nâœ” Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc.\r\nâœ” Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc.\r\nâœ” The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of heavy snow.','The rates are valid till 12th February, 2023. Flight fare is dynamic. ','2023-04-08','2023-04-12',1,0,0,'2023-02-08 17:01:44','2023-02-08 17:01:44'),(230,597,15530,11,0,0,0,0,'Andaman Diaries','3N Port Blair - 2N Havelock - 1N Neil Island\r\n\r\n1st Day (21 May)\r\n\r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n2nd Day (22 May)\r\n\r\nPort Blair - North Bay (Coral Island) â€“ Ross Island\r\n\r\n3rd Day (23 May)\r\n\r\nPort Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\n\r\n4th Day (24 May)\r\n\r\nHavelock - Elephenta Beach\r\n\r\n5th Day (25 May)\r\n\r\nHavelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\n\r\n6th Day (26 May)\r\n\r\nNeil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\n\r\n7th Day (27 May)\r\n\r\nPort Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n','','â€¢ Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan â€“ As mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\nâ€¢ All Sightseeing (Entry fees included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\nâ€¢ Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability)','â€¢ The services of vehicles not on a disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/Vehicles for Dinner etc.\r\nâ€¢ Anything which is not mentioned in the inclusions.\r\nâ€¢ TCS\r\n\r\n\r\n','The rates are valid till 15th Feb, 2023.','2023-05-21','2023-05-27',0,0,0,'2023-02-09 20:58:43','2023-02-09 20:58:43'),(231,606,15530,2,0,0,132800,15000,'Andaman Diaries','2N PortBlair - 2N Havelock - 1N Neil Island\r\n\r\n1st Day (7th May)\r\n\r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show\r\n\r\n