are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\nBroad Bean Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nStarlit Suites Kochi (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 May 2023 - Wednesday) Cochin - Thekkady\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi/Broad Bean Hotel\r\nTransfers - Cochin - Thekkady\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping.Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nPeriyar Meadows Leisure Hotels (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nSpicegrove (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 May 2023 - Thursday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Spicegrove/Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nOxygen Resort Alleppey (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nPagoda Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 May 2023 - Friday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Pagoda Resort/Oxygen Resort Alleppey\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nAadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort, (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nJasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (27 May 2023 - Saturday) Kovalam â€“ Thiruvananthapuram â€“ Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\nAadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort, (Option 2) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\nJasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (28 May 2023 - Sunday) Kovalam to Thiruvananthapuram Drop\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Thiruvananthapuram Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Thiruvananthapuram Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Cochin and Thiruvananthapuram-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* 5 Nights stay in 3/4 Star hotels/resorts mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeings and transfers\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n\r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n\r\n','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. ','2023-05-23','2023-05-28',1,0,0,'2023-05-08 10:52:20','2023-05-08 17:19:13'),(289,691,4818,2,0,0,0,0,'Bhutan Diaries','7N/8D Bhutan Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 23rd June) : NJP Railway Station/IXB Airport to Phuentsholing - Pick up \r\nApprox Distance: 157 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nMeet & Greet on arrival at NJP Railway Station / IXB Airport and transfer to Phuentsholing (961 ft.) - The Gateway of Bhutan by Road from India. It is a thriving commercial centre on the northern edge of the Indian Plains. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 24th June) : Phuentsholing to Thimphu - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, complete the immigration formalities and transfer to Thimphu (7,710 ft.) the capital city of Bhutan. On the way, stop at places to view scenery and for Photography. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or take a leisure walk around the Thimphu City. Overnight stay at Thimphu.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 25th June) : Thimphu - Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast, visit Kuenselphodrang (Buddha Dordenma) for a panoramic view of Thimphu valley and see the largest Buddha statue in Bhutan. Then, visit the National Memorial Chorten and Folk Heritage Museum. In the afternoon, visit Sangaygang View Point for a stunning view of Thimphu, Takin Preserve Centre to see the national animal of Bhutan, and Changangkha Lhakhang, a popular Buddhist temple. In the evening, visit Tashichho Dzong, the seat of the National Government and Central Monastic Body. Overnight stay in Thimphu.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Monday 26th June) : Thimphu to Punakha/Wangdue - Transfer and Sightseeing \r\nApprox Distance: 78 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Punakha/Wangdue and stop at Dochu-La-Pass to view the Himalayas and the 108 Druk Wangyel Chortens. Check in at the hotel upon arrival and visit Punakha Dzong, the former seat of the Government and winter residence of Je-Khenpo. Take a short hike to visit Chhimi Lhakhang, also known as â€œThe Temple of Fertilityâ€. Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay in Punakha/Wangdue.\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 27th June) : Punakha/Wangdue to Paro - Transfer and Sightseeing \r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast drive to Paro (7,483 ft.). On the way stop at Lamperi to visit Royal Botanical Park. This park is a treat for nature lovers as the 36 species of exotic rhododendron and approximately 220 types of charming birds will make your day unforgettable. On arrival check in at the hotel. Afternoon visit Ta Dzong - National Museum with an excellent collection of arts, relics, religious thangkha, etc. Then visit the Rinpung Dzong - Meaning \"fortress of the heap of jewels\". The dzong now serves as the administrative and judicial seat of Paro. Rest of the evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Paro\r\n\r\n6th Day - (Wednesday 28th June) : Paro - Taktshang Monastery Excursion \r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour 30 minutes \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Taktshang Monastery and hike uphill for 2-3 hours to reach the primary Lhakhang built surrounding Guru Rinpocheâ€™s meditation cave. Legend has it that Guru Rinpoche flew here on the back of a tigress, giving the monastery its name â€œTigerâ€™s Nestâ€. In the afternoon, visit Drukgyel Dzong to explore the ramparts and enjoy the view of Mt. Jhomolhari, and then visit Kichu Lhakhang, one of the oldest temples in Bhutan. Overnight stay in Paro\r\n\r\n7th Day - (Thursday 29th June) : Paro to Phuentsholing - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 145 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Phuentsholing. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n \r\n8th Day - (Friday 30th June) : Phuentsholing to NJP Railway Station/IXB Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance: 170 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and drive to NJP Railway Station / IXB Airport for your onward journey.','','* 7 Nights stay in hotel mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeing and transfers on Pvt/SIC as mentioned above\r\n* Exclusive Non-a/c vehicle for all transfers & sightseeing as per itinerary. \r\n* Guide / Escort charges. \r\n* Accommodation on double/twin sharing basis. All the rooms are base category, if not mentioned otherwise ','* Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone bills, bar bills, tips & gratuity, bottled water and cost for \r\n  other activities such as rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porterage, etc. \r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary. \r\n* Entrance Fees for museums and monuments. \r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-12 13:46:09','2023-05-13 17:06:48'),(290,692,15535,2,0,0,89000,24000,'Wonderful Tour of Ladakh','7N Ladakh Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDAY 01: ARRIVE LEH  \r\nArrival Leh by morning flight and transfer to the hotel. After welcome drink take a complete rest for acclimatization to the height altitude of Leh (3500 meters). In the late afternoon drive to the city for an orientation walk in the marketsâ€š followed by a visit to Shanti Stupaâ€š Leh palace. Dinner and overnight in hotel. \r\n\r\nDAY 02: LEH TO SHAM VALLEY (75 KMS / 4 HRS)  \r\nAfter breakfast you drive downstream along the River Indus on Leh â€“ Kargil Highway. Enroute visiting Gurudwara Patthar Sahib Nestled deep in the Himalayas, A drive of another 4 km took us to Magnetic Hill which defies the law of gravity & further Driving through a picturesque landscape we reached the Confluence Of The Indus And Zanskar River, Just before Saspul a road to the right takes you for your visit to the Likir Monastery, Likir is one of the most active monasteries in the region. As you drive up to the monastery a recently installed colossal gilded image of the Maitreya out in the open is one of the most impressive sights in Ladakh. After visiting the Monastery, you continue your drive along the River Indus to Tingmosgang en route visiting Ridzong Monastery, there is the option to walk up to the Monastery for those that wish to do so. Hidden at the end of a steep valley, the first view of the Monastery is dramatic. After visiting above places we drive further and check in at our camp / hotel for overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDAY 03: SHAM VALLEY TO LEH VIA LAMAYURU (180 KMS / 05 â€“ 06 HRS)  \r\nPost breakfast you drive to the 11th Century Lamayuru Monastery en route visiting the mesmerizing Moon Landscapes (you will believe why the name of this area is Moonland. Exactly the same formations of Land are visible as on the moon), Lamayuru is spectacularly located along the valley plain and surrounded by mountains on all sides. On your return drive to Leh you first visit the Alchi Gompa. The complex of temples located within the village is the most celebrated of Ladakhâ€™s monasteries and dates back to the 11th century. After visiting Alchi we drive back to Leh. Finally, you arrive back at Leh for an overnight stay at your Hotel. \r\n \r\nDAY 04: LEHâ€“NUBRA VALLEY VIA KHARDUNG LA 18,390 FT. (120 KMS / 4 â€“ 5 HRS)  \r\nPost breakfast we drive to Nubra Valley. The road journey from Leh to Nubra Valley passes over Khardung La (The Highest Motorable Road In The World) at 5,602 Mtrs / 18,390 Ft, around 39 km from Leh. From the pass, one can see all the way south over the Indus valley to seemingly endless peaks and ridges of the Zanskar range, and north to the giants of the Saser massif. Nubra Valley is popularly known as Ldumra or the valley of flowers. It is situated in the north of Ladakh between the Karakoram and Ladakh ranges of the Himalayas. The average altitude of the valley is 10,000 Ft. above sea level. Upon arrival in Nubra we check in at our Camp / Hotel in Hunder for Overnight stay. In the evening you can walk around the tiny villages to see how the locals live in this part of the world. Overnight Stay at the Camp or Hotel \r\n \r\nDAY 05: IN NUBRA (HUNDER VILLAGE) â€“EXCURSION TO TURTUK \r\nAfter an early breakfast, proceed to Turtuk (A village that was won by India in the 1971 war with Pakistan) and extremely close to the border. Visit a 16th Century Mosque, (comprising of a touch of Turkish & Iranian culture), ruined fort of Dhards and Monastery. Admire the magnificent view of the famous K2 peak (The second highest peak in the world after Mount Everest). Later back to hotel for overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDAY 06: NUBRA VALLEY TO PANGONG LAKE (150 KMS / 5 HRS) \r\nDrive to Hunder after breakfast, ride a bacterian camel in the sand dunes and stop at Diskit for some shopping. Later, take a tough yet scenic drive via Agham & Shyok Valley to reach Pangong Tso passing through Changthang villages. Enjoy the sudden view of the lake at 14,000 feet upon arrival and check in at Camp/Hotel. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n \r\nDAY 07: PANGONG LAKE TO LEH VIA CHANGLA (140 KMS / 6 HRS) \r\nMorning at leisure to explore the beauty of lake and later we drive back to Leh via Changla Pass 5486 Mtrs en route visiting Hemis Gompa, the largest monastic foundation of Drukpa Kagyu Order of Tibetan Buddhism. And futher to Thiksey an impressive complex rising tier upon tier on a hill above the village and another 5 Kms driving through a picturesque landscape we reach to Shey Palace, The ancient capital of Ladakh & 3 Idiots Rancho School. Drive further to Leh. Dinner & Overnight at Hotel. \r\n \r\nDAY 08: DEPART LEH (FLY OUT) \r\nTour concludes. Through a punctual transfer to the Domestic Airport to catch the flight for your onward destination. \r\n\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* Delhi-Leh-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation in Deluxe room on Double/twin sharing.\r\n* Assistance upon arrival at Leh Hotel  \r\n* Traditional welcome in the Hotel with Welcome Drink (Hot Tea / Coffee / Kahwa) on arrival  \r\n* 07 Nights Accommodation twin/double sharing basis as per the Itinerary \r\n* Meal Plan - 07 Breakfast & 07 Dinner \r\n* Return airport and round-trip transfers along with all sightseeing tours by Non-Ac Innova \r\n* Wild Life fees & Red Cross fee \r\n* All toll taxes/Parking fee/Driver allowance \r\n* Ladakh Entry Fee  \r\n* Ecological development fee  \r\n\r\n\r\n','* Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone bills, bar bills, tips & gratuity, bottled water and cost for\r\n  other activities such as rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porterage, etc.\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. The rates are valid till 16th May, 2023.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-12 16:01:41','2023-05-12 23:17:33'),(291,693,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries ','7N/8D Kerala Stay in hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23 Jun 2023 - Friday) Cochin Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Broad Bean Hotel (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (24 Jun 2023 - Saturday) Cochin to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Park\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Munnar\r\n\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Misty Lake Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (25 Jun 2023 - Sunday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Misty Lake Resort/Trivers Resort\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. \r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Misty Lake Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Trivers Resort\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Periyar Meadows Leisure Hotels\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Pagoda Resort (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Punnamada Backwater Resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 (29 Jun 2023 - Thursday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Jasmine Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 (30 Jun 2023 - Friday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\n\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Cochin and Thiruvananthapuram-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* 7 Nights stay in hotels/resorts mentioned above\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sightseeings and transfers\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expense like laundary, grooming, souvenir, etc.\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-23','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-05-13 15:03:11','2023-05-13 15:03:11'),(292,694,14820,3,0,0,462700,80000,'Norway-Iceland-Denmark','4N Norway - 4N Iceland - 4N Denmark','','Inclusion:-\r\n# Flights\r\n# Accommodation\r\n# Daily Breakfast\r\n# Oslo- Transfer from Airport to Hotel on PVT\r\n# 24hrs City Sightseeing Oslo Hop-On Hop-Off Tour\r\n# The original Norway, in a nutshell, 08:25 Oslo- MYRDAL- FLÃ…M- GUDVANGEN- VOSS- BERGEN 20:40\r\n# Oslo- Transfer from Hotel to Airport on PVT\r\n# Reykjavik - Transfer from Airport to Hotel on PVT\r\n# Golden Circle Classic Day Trip from Reykjavik (10:00 with Pick up at 09:30 10:00), Reykjavik\r\n# Northern Lights Premium Tour From Reykjavik (Pickup at designated locations 21:30)\r\n# Reykjavik - Transfer from Hotel to Airport on PVT\r\n# Copenhagen - Transfer from Airport to Hotel/Accommodation on PVT\r\n# Copenhagen - Transfer from Hotel/Accommodation to Airport on PVT\r\n# Visa Charges\r\n# Travel Insurance\r\n\r\n\r\n# 24-Hour Bergen Hop-On Hop-Off Sightseeing Tour\r\n\r\n\r\n','','','2023-09-03','2023-09-15',1,0,0,'2023-05-15 11:32:14','2023-05-15 11:33:10'),(293,695,16002,2,0,0,0,0,'Bali Diaries','6 Nights Bali Stay with transfers and sightseeing.\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (05 Jul 2023 - Wednesday)\r\nTransfer in to Select Hotel 	 \r\nPick up from Airport and drop to Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 2 (06 Jul 2023 - Thrusday)\r\nTanjung Benoa Water Sports + Uluwatu Tour\r\nwater creation center (carry 1 pair of cloth with you)	 \r\n1 Round Banana Boat	 \r\n[other activities on your own account]	 \r\nUluwatu Temple\r\n\r\nDay 3 (07 Jul 2023 - Friday)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Pick up early morning at hotel for Nusa Penida West Island Tour with\r\n06.30 AM : Driver pick up time from your hotel (depending of the hotel location)	 \r\nVisit -Crystal bay, Broken beach ,Angel billabong, Lunch at Local Restaurant.	 \r\nKelingkinhg Kliff, Kelingkinhg Kliff Selfie, \r\n\r\nDay 4 (08 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\nBedugul + Tanah lot tour	\r\nBedugul - ulun danu temple at britain lake 	 \r\nTanha lot temple \r\n\r\nDay 5 (09 Jul 2023 - Sunday)\r\nInter Hotel Transfer + Kintamani + Ubud Tour	\r\nFull Day Tour Visit:Mas/Celuk for local art & craft market	 \r\ncontinue visit Kintmani mount batur volcano, Spices Garden and Ubud Market	 \r\nTegalalang rice terrace 	 \r\n 	 \r\nDay 6 (10 Jul 2023 - 