rs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-09',1,0,0,'2023-05-20 15:01:48','2023-05-20 15:01:48'),(302,707,16002,2,0,0,68000,21200,'Bali Diaries','6 Nights Bali Stay with transfers and sightseeing.\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (05 Jul 2023 - Wednesday)\r\nTransfer in to Select Hotel 	 \r\nPick up from Airport and drop to Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 2 (06 Jul 2023 - Thrusday)\r\nTanjung Benoa Water Sports + Uluwatu Tour\r\nwater creation center (carry 1 pair of cloth with you)	 \r\n1 Round Banana Boat	 \r\n[other activities on your own account]	 \r\nUluwatu Temple\r\n\r\nDay 3 (07 Jul 2023 - Friday)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Pick up early morning at hotel for Nusa Penida West Island Tour with\r\n06.30 AM : Driver pick up time from your hotel (depending of the hotel location)	 \r\nVisit -Crystal bay, Broken beach ,Angel billabong, Lunch at Local Restaurant.	 \r\nKelingkinhg Kliff, Kelingkinhg Kliff Selfie, \r\n\r\nDay 4 (08 Jul 2023 - Saturday)\r\nBedugul + Tanah lot tour	\r\nBedugul - ulun danu temple at britain lake 	 \r\nTanha lot temple \r\n\r\nDay 5 (09 Jul 2023 - Sunday)\r\nInter Hotel Transfer + Kintamani + Ubud Tour	\r\nFull Day Tour Visit:Mas/Celuk for local art & craft market	 \r\ncontinue visit Kintmani mount batur volcano, Spices Garden and Ubud Market	 \r\nTegalalang rice terrace 	 \r\n 	 \r\nDay 6 (10 Jul 2023 - Monday)\r\nDay at leisure \r\n\r\nDay 7 (11 Jul 2023 - Tuesday)\r\nTransfer Out','','* Delhi-Bali-Delhi Economy class airfare	\r\n* All Transfer on private basis\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Inter hotel transfer on private basis\r\n* Daily Breakfast \r\n* One Lunch at Local Restaurant','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, \r\n  Visiter fee ect.)\r\n* Other personal expenses\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon \r\n  booking)\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as \r\n  drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-07-04','2023-07-11',1,0,0,'2023-05-20 16:46:52','2023-05-20 17:01:19'),(303,708,15512,2,1,0,0,0,'5D/4N NORTHERN VIETNAM TOUR','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1- Hanoi Arrival - city highlights (-/-/-)\r\nDay 2- Ninh Binh day trip (B/L/-) - SIC\r\nDay 3- Hanoi â€“ Halong Bay (B/L/D) - SIC tour\r\nDay 4- Halong Bay â€“ Hanoi (Brunch/-)\r\nDay 5- Hanoi Departure (B/-/-)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 - Wed 01 Mar 2023: Hanoi Arrival - city highlights (-/-/-)\r\nWelcome to Hanoi, the capital city of Vietnam. Upon arrival, greeted by the local tour guide and transfer to downtown. Check in your hotel. Afternoon, visit Ba Dinh Square â€“ the biggest square in Hanoi where all the biggest cultural, political events of the cities, especially demonstrations, take place. Start our visit at the Complex of Ho Chi Minh including Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (from outside only as it closes in the afternoon), Ho Chi Minhâ€™s house-on-stilts, his fish pond and the One-Pillar Pagoda. Then, the Temple of Literature which is considered as the first university of Vietnam.\r\nLater, we have an overall view of the capital by cyclo in 1 hour, which wanders around the Old Quarter of Hanoi and the Hoan Kiem Lake (the â€œSwordâ€ Lake). From here wandering on the narrow streets of the Old Quarter to experience the daily life of the local people. Transfer back to your hotel. Overnight in Hanoi. Please note: the standard check in time is\r\n14:00 â€“ 15:00pm. Early check in is not included and subject to hotel availability. Night activities suggestion: enjoy local beer at Ta Hien Streets, experience the ambience of sleepless street with life music, the young people of Hanoi and also foreign tourists. Hundred of bars and pubs in the Old Quarter are also at your disposal Or just simple spend your time at shopping malls or various boutique Shops.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 - Thu 02 Mar 2023: Ninh Binh day trip (B/L/-) - SIC\r\n\r\n7:15-7:45am Our driver and tour guide pick you up at hotels in the Old Quarter Area, Hanoi. Head the south of Hanoi for 110 km. After 2 hours, you will arrive in Ninh Binh. First stop at Hoa Lu, you will have quick visit two temples built in honor of the emperors Dinh Le, their sons, and the Queen... to know why Hoa Lu was build as capital of Vietnam in ending of nine century.\r\n\r\n12:00 â€“ Enjoy lunch at our restaurant with the great local cuisine.\r\n\r\n13:30 â€“ Boarding a small sampan to visit Tam Coc which means literally â€œthree cavesâ€ (1.5 hour boat trip). With Halong bay type views of majestic limestone cliffs and mysterious caves, as well as countryside landscape like peaceful streams, rice paddies and deserted green fields, Tam Coc really has it all. You will feel the fresh air and peaceful moments, very good opportunities for photo lovers, freezing the special moments and scenery.\r\n\r\n17:15 â€“ Return to our bus and then come back to Ha Noi\r\n\r\n19:30 â€“ Drop you off at your hotel/stay. Trip ends.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 - Fri 03 Mar 2023: Hanoi â€“ Halong Bay (B/L/D) - SIC tour\r\n08.00-09.00: Shuttles bus pick up and departure in the morning from Hanoi. We drive across the Red River delta and reach the coast a little before noon. We then embark on a beautifully crafted junk for an overnight cruise in the legendary seascape of Ha Long Bay. Once on board, we are served a delicious seafood-based lunch, while the surrounding limestone outcrops make for a truly magical setting. In the afternoon, we reach a less travelled area where we will devote ourselves to pure relaxation. The program is not fixed and depends on the time of the year and weather, but there will be an opportunity to visit a cave as well as explore a floating village or do a little bit of kayaking over the course of these 2 days. We end the day on the sundeck as the sun sets on this magical seascape. This evening, you can enjoy an aperitif or attend a cooking demonstration before dinner. Overnight in a comfortable private cabin with an en-suite bathroom.\r\n\r\nNote: Cruise itinerary and schedule are subject to change due to weather, tide levels and operating conditions. Swimming or kayaking excursions may be cancelled due to poor weather.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 - Sat 04 Mar 2023: Halong Bay â€“ Hanoi (Brunch/-)\r\nFor those early birds, start the day with a proposed Tai Chi session, while tea and coffee are served as the sun rises and illuminates the surrounding seascape. We then continue our exploration of the bay. Upon returning to the boat, check-out of your cabin and enjoy a light brunch while cruising back to the pier. We disembark and transfer back to Hanoi.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 - Sun 05 Mar 2023: Hanoi Departure (B/-/-)\r\nThe day is free at your leisure until transfer without guide to Noi Bai International Airport for your departure flight. We wish you a pleasant flight!\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Return Airfare (Delhi - Hanoi - Delhi)\r\n* Accommodation in twin/double room with daily breakfast\r\n* 2Days/1Night cruise on board a cruise in Ha Long Bay (private cabin on shared boat).\r\n* Boat trip - as per program\r\n* All entrance fees - as per program\r\n* Shuttle bus from/to Hanoi - Ha Long- Ha Long\r\n* Government tax and service charge\r\n* Bottles of mineral water on tour day\r\n* Meals (B/L/D) (Breakfast/Lunch/Dinner) as indicated in the program\r\n* Local ENGLISH speaking guides\r\n* Enjoy lunch at a local restaurant\r\n* All transfers and transportation with Air-Con vehicles\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','* Early check-in or late check-out\r\n* Optional excursions and activities\r\n* Drinks\r\n* Meals (other than mentioned in the program)\r\n* Additional transfer required due to any emergency situation\r\n* Items of a personal nature (Phone calls, laundry, beverages, etc.)\r\n* Mineral water beyond that which is supplied\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking)\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n ','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-19','2023-06-24',1,0,0,'2023-05-22 19:55:24','2023-05-23 15:11:45'),(304,709,15506,2,1,0,0,0,'Turkey Diaries','6 Nights / 7 Days | 3N Istanbul / 3N Cappadocia \r\n\r\nISTANBUL (COMFORT 4 STAR OPTIONS)\r\nRamada Grand Bazaar // Nova Plaza Crystal // Metropolitan Taksim // Golden Age // Elite World Comfy // Nippon OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nCAPPADOCIA (COMFORT 4 Star OPTIONS)\r\nSelcuklu Evi Cave // Dedeli Konak Cave // Doors of Cappadocia // Alfina Cave // Mithra Cave // Fresco Cave OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nISTANBUL (LUXURY 5 STAR OPTIONS)\r\nSura Hagia Sophia // Crown Plaza Old City // Crown Plaza Harbiye // Radisson Blu Pera // Elite World Istanbul // Point Hotel OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\nCAPPADOCIA (LUXURY 5 Star OPTIONS)\r\nMDC Cave // Exedra Cave // Elika Cave Suites // Dere Suites // Utopia Cave OR Similar Hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDAY 1: ISTANBUL\r\nArrival to Istanbul and transfer to the hotel. Free rest of the day. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 2: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, depart for a full-day tour of Istanbul. Visit Blue Mosque, Hagia Sophia, Hippodrome, Grand Bazaar, Topkapi Palace and Sultansâ€™ Tombs. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 3: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Egyptian Bazaar (spice bazaar) and cruise along the Bosphorus. Lunch. Beylerbeyi Palace visit which is summer residence of Ottoman Sultans. Then Camlica Hill. Highest point of Istanbul. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n \r\nDAY 4: ISTANBUL/CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Kayseri/Nevsehir. Arrival and transfer to the hotel. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 5: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia North Tour. Visit Dervent Valley, Pasabag fairy chimneys, Avanos, Goreme open air museum and Uchisar rock castle. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 6: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia South Tour. Visit Red Valley, Pigeon Valley, Cavusin Village, Underground City. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia\r\n\r\nDAY 7: CAPPADOCIA/AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Istanbul to take the international flight.\r\n,ITINERARY\r\nDAY 1: ISTANBUL\r\nArrival to Istanbul and transfer to the hotel. Free rest of the day. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 2: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, depart for a full-day tour of Istanbul. Visit Blue Mosque, Hagia Sophia, Hippodrome, Grand Bazaar, Topkapi Palace and Sultansâ€™ Tombs. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n\r\nDAY 3: ISTANBUL\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Egyptian Bazaar (spice bazaar) and cruise along the Bosphorus. Lunch. Beylerbeyi Palace visit which is summer residence of Ottoman Sultans. Then Camlica Hill. Highest point of Istanbul. Overnight in Istanbul.\r\n \r\nDAY 4: ISTANBUL/CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Kayseri/Nevsehir. Arrival and transfer to the hotel. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 5: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia North Tour. Visit Dervent Valley, Pasabag fairy chimneys, Avanos, Goreme open air museum and Uchisar rock castle. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia.\r\n\r\nDAY 6: CAPPADOCIA\r\nAfter breakfast depart for Cappadocia South Tour. Visit Red Valley, Pigeon Valley, Cavusin Village, Underground City. Dinner and overnight in Cappadocia\r\n\r\nDAY 7: CAPPADOCIA/AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the airport for the flight to Istanbul to take the international flight.','','* Economy Class Return Airfare (Delhi - Istanbul - Delhi)\r\n* Economy Class Return Airfare (Istanbul - Nevsehir - Istanbul)\r\n* 03 Nights in Istanbul at Selected Category of Hotel OR Similar on BB basis \r\n* 03 Nights in Cappadocia at Selected Category of Hotel OR Similar on HB basis\r\n* R/T Transfer in Istanbul (IST AIRPORT) and Cappadocia on PVT basis.\r\n* FD Istanbul Old City Tour with Local lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Bosphorus & 2 Continents Tour with lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Cappadocia North tour with Local Lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* FD Cappadocia South tour with Local Lunch on SIC basis.\r\n* Entrance Fees	\r\n* Travel Insurance','* Optional excursions and activities\r\n* Meals (other than mentioned in the program)\r\n* Items of a personal nature (Phone calls, laundry, beverages, etc.)\r\n* Surcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking)\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-18','2023-06-25',1,0,0,'2023-05-23 16:24:29','2023-05-23 18:58:36'),(305,710,54,2,1,0,0,0,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (3 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (4 Aug)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (5 Aug)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n4th Day (6 Aug)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n5th Day (7 Aug)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (8 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-08-02','2023-08-08',1,0,0,'2023-05-23 17:15:03','2023-05-23 18:52:29'),(306,712,54,5,0,0,0,0,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (7 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (8 June)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (9 June)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (10 June)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n5th Day (11 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (12 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-07','2023-06-12',1,0,0,'2023-05-24 00:08:19','2023-05-24 17:59:25'),(307,713,54,2,0,0,144000,35000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 -Arrive - Singapore\r\nSingapore - a sunny, tropical island in Southeast Asia, off the southern tip of the Malay Peninsula. Singapore, officially the\r\nRepublic of Singapore, is known as the Lion City (Singapura) .On arrival pick up from airport and transfer to hotel.\r\n(Standard check in time is 14:00 to 15:00 PM). \r\nIn Evening pick up from hotel lobby and proceed to Night Safari - the world\'s first\r\nnocturnal zoo and is one of the most popular tourist attractions in Singapore. The Night Safari currently houses over 900\r\nanimals representing over 100 species, of which 41% are threatened species.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 02 - Singapore\r\nBreakfast at hotel.\r\nPick up from Hotel lobby and proceed to Universal Studios- Singapore is Southeast\r\nAsia\'s first and only movie theme park, features thrilling attractions, rides and entertainment for everyone.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 03- Singapore- City tour- Cruise\r\nBreakfast at hotel.\r\nAfter breakfast at Hotel, pick up from hotel lobby and proceed for Singapore city tour- visit Central district Orchard road,\r\nvisit at Chinese temple in China town, Merlion park at marina bay (photo stop only).\r\nAround 4pm , pick up from hotel and transfer to Cruise terminal.\r\nCruise sailing starts at 8 pm.\r\nOnBoard Cruise\r\n\r\nDay 04 - Cruise\r\nOnBoard Cruise/ High Seas\r\n\r\nDay 05- Singapore\r\nCruise arrives back to Singapore at 10:00 am.\r\nPick up from Cruise terminal and transfer to hotel.\r\nAfternoon pick up for Sentosa island tour- offers a variety of attractions to provide variety of experiences, recreation & entertainment to visitors. \r\nSky ride - a chair lift which offers bird eye view of Sentosa island. \r\nLuge ride - features a self steering, gravity driven three wheel cart, Cable car, 4D Adventure, SEA Aquarium, Wings of time.\r\nOvernight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 06- Singapore Departure\r\nEnjoy breakfast at Hotel. Day at leisure.\r\n(Standard hotel check out time: 12pm)\r\nPick up from hotel lobby and transfer to airport for flight back to Surat.','','* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar.\r\n* 03 nights Singapore stay with breakfast\r\n* 02 nights stay on Cruise (Genting Dream Cruise-Inside Stateroom)\r\n* All meals on Cruise\r\n* Airport - hotel- airport transfers\r\n* Hotel- cruise terminal- hotel transfers\r\n* Night safari tour\r\n* Universal Studio tour\r\n* Sentosa Island tour with wings of time, sky ride, luge ride, 4d adventure, cable car, SEA Aquarium\r\n* Singapore city tour-03 hrs approx\r\n* All transfers & tours on seat in coach/ sharing basis\r\n* Singapore Visa Charges\r\n* Port charges\r\n* One time pick up & delivery is included.','* Dinner & Lunch\r\n* Gratuity of Cruise to be paid directly onboard cruise SGD 21 per person per night\r\n* Cost for shore excursion on port of halt of Cruise\r\n* Door step delivery/ Pick up (Document & Payment Collection charges)-Pay Rs 700 per visit\r\n* TCS\r\n','','2023-06-26','2023-07-03',1,0,0,'2023-05-24 18:13:58','2023-05-24 18:45:31'),(308,714,54,2,0,0,57100,13000,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (30 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (1 July)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Flower Dome + Supertree Ticket Only) \r\n\r\n3rd Day (2 July)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (3 July)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n5th Day (4 July)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (5 July)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-30','2023-07-05',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 09:14:18','2023-05-25 09:14:18'),(309,715,54,2,0,0,38200,9000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (24 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - PRIVATE\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n2nd Day (25 June)\r\nSingapore City Orientation Drive and Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (26 June) \r\nSentosa Tour (Inclusion Cable Car,Luge & Skyride,Wings of Time)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n4th Day (27 June)\r\nUniversal Studio\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n5th Day (28 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (29 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer - PRIVATE','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense\r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS\r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-23','2023-06-29',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 16:28:47','2023-05-25 16:53:35'),(310,717,15526,2,1,0,50000,18000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.	 	\r\n		\r\nDay  4 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.	 	\r\n		\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.','','* Economy class return airfare\r\n* Accommodation  as above.\r\n* Daily Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis. \r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of heavy snow. \r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-13','2023-06-19',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 17:36:06','2023-05-25 19:12:50'),(311,719,54,2,0,0,38200,9000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (24 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - PRIVATE\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n2nd Day (25 June)\r\nSingapore City Orientation Drive and Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (26 June) \r\nSentosa Tour (Inclusion Cable Car,Luge & Skyride,Wings of Time)\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n4th Day (27 June)\r\nUniversal Studio\r\nReturn Transfers - SIC  \r\n\r\n5th Day (28 June)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (29 June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer - PRIVATE','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Any type of personal expense\r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS\r\n\r\n','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-23','2023-06-29',1,0,0,'2023-05-25 18:14:24','2023-05-25 18:14:24'),(312,720,15526,4,0,0,66800,18000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: On arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmasha