023-06-03 16:20:34'),(338,753,15526,2,0,1,37000,5000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)	 	\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.	 	\r\n			\r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR	 	\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.	 	\r\n				\r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.	 	\r\n					\r\nDay  4 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.	 							\r\n\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.	 	\r\n				\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.	 	','','* Economy class return fare.\r\n* Accommodation  as above.\r\n* Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis. \r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Extra Meals \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. \r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2023-06-19','2023-06-24',1,0,0,'2023-06-03 18:05:44','2023-06-03 18:05:44'),(340,756,54,4,3,0,141900,35000,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (12th June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (13th June)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (14th June)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n4th Day (15th June)\r\nHotel 1 to Hotel 2 Transfers (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\nDay at Leisure\r\n\r\n5th Day (16th June)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n6th Day (17th June)\r\nSingapore Zoo Return Transfers - SIC\r\nSingapore Zoo (Tickets)\r\n\r\n7th Day (18th June)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','6 nights stay in the mentioned hotel/s\r\n6 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance','Airfare\r\nAny type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than that mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-06-12','2023-06-18',1,0,0,'2023-06-05 23:38:20','2023-06-06 13:59:40'),(341,758,54,4,0,0,0,0,'Singapore And Malaysia Diaries','3N Singapore 3N Kuala Lumpur','','DEL-SIN, SIN-KUL and KUL-DEL economy class airfare\r\n06 nights accommodation at hotel                                                                                                                                            \r\nDaily Breakfast                                                                                                                                    \r\nNight Safari with Tram ride                                                                                                                                           \r\nSingapore City Orientation Drive                                                                                                                                 \r\nSentosa Island (01 way cable car + Madame Tussauds 5 in 1 Combo + WOT 1st Show)                                                                                                                                             \r\nGardens By The Bay ( Flower Dome + Cloud forest with Avatar experience)\r\nHalf Day Kulalumpur City Tour + KL Tower ticket                                                                                                                                  \r\nGenting Full Day Tour Enroute Batu Caves + Two Ways Cable Car                                                                                                                                 \r\nKuala Lumpur Return airport transfers on seat-in-coach basis                                                                                                                                                                 \r\nReturn airport transfers (SIC in Kuala Lumpur)                                                                                                                                  \r\nAll Tours and transfers on a seat-in-coach basis    \r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance \r\n','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* TCS','The airfare is dynamic. This quote doesn\'t mean any confirmation for the booking. ','2023-06-15','2023-06-21',1,0,0,'2023-06-06 00:08:11','2023-06-06 00:08:11'),(342,759,38,3,0,0,0,0,'Bangkok-Thailand','4 Nights stay in Bangkok\r\n\r\n\r\nTours:\r\nHalf day BKK Temple & Tour (2 TEMPLE)  - SIC\r\nEvening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise - SIC\r\nFull Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch - SIC','','DEL-BKK-DEL return economy class airfare \r\nSUVARNABHUMI APT - BANGKOK HOTEL - PVT Transfers\r\nBANGKOK HOTEL - SUVARNABHUMI APT - PVT Transfers\r\nAll sightseeing on SIC basis\r\n4 night stay in the mentioned hotel\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nTravel Insurance','Expenses of personal nature, such as: Laundry, telephone calls, mini-bar bills, etc.\r\nAny other tours apart from those listed under inclusions\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','The hotel and flight rates are dynamic','2023-06-15','2023-06-19',1,0,0,'2023-06-07 00:46:36','2023-06-07 00:46:36'),(343,761,54,2,1,0,0,0,'Singapore Diaries','\r\nTransports and Activities\r\n\r\n1st Day (3 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer - 1 PRIVATE COMBI\r\nNight Safari Transfer - Return Transfers - SIC (Night Safari Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (4 Aug)\r\nSingapore Half Day City Orientation Drive - SIC\r\nGardens By The Bay - Return Transfers - SIC (Cloud Forest + Flower Dome Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (5 Aug)\r\nUniversal Studios Return Transfers- SIC (Universal Studio Ticket Only)\r\n\r\n4th Day (6 Aug)\r\nSentosa Afternoon Return Transfers- SIC\r\nSentosa Attractions Ticket (Combo 2 - Cable Car + Madame Tussauds Combo (5 in 1) + WOT)\r\n\r\n5th Day (7 Aug)\r\nDay at leisure\r\n\r\n6th Day (8 Aug)\r\nSingapore - Airport Departure Transfer (1 PRIVATE COMBI)\r\n\r\n','','Economy class return airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n5 breakfasts\r\nAirport transfers\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any type of personal expense \r\nAny expense due to natural calamity or change in flight\r\nAny meal other than mentioned above\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','The rates are subject to change','2023-08-02','2023-08-08',1,0,0,'2023-06-07 15:11:36','2023-06-07 15:26:30'),(344,762,15510,2,0,0,49000,24000,'Thailand Adventure','2N Krabi - 3N Phuket ','','Delhi-Phuket-Delhi Economy class return airfare\r\n02 Nights stay in Krabi\r\n03 Nights stay in Phuket\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\n03 Ways Transfers â€“ PVT (Phuket Airport â€“ Krabi Hotel â€“ Phuket Hotel â€“ Phuket Airport)\r\n4 Island Tour with Lunch (Speed Boat) + SIC Transfer (Not Incl. Park Fee)\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour  by Speed Boat + Khai Island + Indian Lunch + Transfer on SIC + National Park Free\r\nTravel Insurance','* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* TCS','The flight fare is dynamic. ','2023-06-10','2023-06-15',1,0,0,'2023-06-07 17:47:19','2023-06-07 17:49:11'),(345,764,15530,4,0,0,0,0,'Andaman Iconic Nature','6 Nights / 7 Days | 3N Port Blair with Barathang + 2N Havelock Island + 01 N Neil Island\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival â€“Chidiya Tapu - Cellular Jail Light & Sound Show\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel/ resort\r\n* Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\n* Please note, we will drop guest at parking area near jail and guest must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\n* Guest must come out after visiting jail and re-enter for L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in free time.\r\n* L&S show timing is in between 1800 Hrs.- 1900hrs subject to availability.\r\n* The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilized in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Havelock â€“ Visit Radha Nagar Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock.\r\n* If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\n* Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort.\r\n* Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\n* Do not forget to carry changing cloths and towel.\r\n* Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicle with wet cloths, please cooperate.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Havelock â€“ Elephenta Beach\r\nHavelock Island\r\n* Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\n* Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkeling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\n* Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkeling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\n* You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\n* Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\n* Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Patthar Beachâ€.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Havelock - Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\nNeil Island\r\n* Morning, Breakfast & proceed to jetty for onward journey to Neil Island\r\n* Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort.\r\n* Afternoon, proceed to visit the following places:\r\n* Bharatpura Beach: The white sand and shallow water beach is popular for swim, relaxation, and water activities such as Snorkeling, Boat diving and boat tour.\r\n* Laxmanpura beach: The white sand Coral Beach offers stunning sunset view.\r\n* Natural Bridge: Also known as Howrah Bridge the bridge has naturally formed by corals, its\r\nbest seen during the low tide.\r\n* Sightseeing will be based on tide and local representative will brief the final schedule.\r\n\r\nDay 5: Neil Island- Port Blair- Day at leisure\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\n* Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Port Blair- Trip to Baratang- Visit to Limestone caves & Mud Volcano\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Get up early as your journey to Baratang begun at 0400 am.\r\n* Ask your hotel to provide a packed cold breakfast (subject to hotelâ€™s policy)\r\n* You will cover around 100 kms journey through dense forest and tribal reserve area.\r\n* You are not allowed to click photograph or deboard vehicle on the way to destination.\r\n8 You will board a sharing ferry & speed boat and some 1.5 kms walk to reach Limestone\r\nCaves.\r\n* For Mud Volcano, there will be a sharing non-AC vehicle and a 500+ metre walk.\r\n8 We recommend: Please check the health conditions as getting up early morning, long walks\r\nand humid weather conditions can be tiring specially to aged tourists.\r\n\r\nDay 7: Port Blair - Tour Ends\r\nPort Blair\r\n* Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\n* Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach airport at least 2 hrs.\r\nprior to your flight timing.','','* Economy Class Return Airfare.\r\n* Well-appointed accommodation\r\n* Meal Plan â€“ CP (Bed & Breakfast)\r\n* Sightseeing as per itinerary\r\n* All Monuments, Museums, Cultural Events, and activities fees as per itinerary\r\n* Return airport/ jetty Transfers in AC vehicle as per itinerary.\r\n* All Transportation for local sight-seeing tours by AC Vehicle as per itinerary.\r\n* Cruise transfers Port Blair â€“Neil Island - Havelock â€“ Port Blair by private ferry Subject\r\nto availability (base category)','','Airfare is dynamic.','2023-06-22','2023-06-28',1,0,0,'2023-06-14 17:11:30','2023-06-14 18:05:30'),(346,767,15518,4,0,0,64100,25000,'Scenic Kerala','Munnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Kovalam: 2 Nights\r\n\r\nDay 1:\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 2:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 3:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nDay 4:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Peppervine Hotel\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nDay 5:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Punnamada Backwater Resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 6:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 7:\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Trivandrum Dep\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the Hotel and transferred to Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','Delhi-Kochi and Trivandrum-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n6 night stay with breakfast in the mentioned hotels/resorts\r\nAll sightseeings and transfers on private basis (Innova Car)\r\nAll taxes which are currently applicable','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expenses\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in Inclusions','The rates are subject to availability. \r\nThe flight fare is dynamic','2023-06-22','2023-06-28',1,0,0,'2023-06-15 08:22:05','2023-06-15 08:23:11'),(347,765,15526,4,0,0,78000,20000,'Kashmir Diaries','6 Nights / 7 Days | 4N Srinagar / 2N Pahalgam\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDAY 1 ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin\r\nyour tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal\r\nspring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 2 SONMARG DAY TRIP FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\". Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by\r\nmountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and\r\nsledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 3 GULMARG DAY TRIP FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during\r\nsummer (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad\r\nmountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view\r\nin winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at\r\nhotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 4 CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (2 NIGHTS STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds.\r\nThe mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron\r\ngrowing fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. Day at leisure.\r\nOvernight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\nDAY 5 EXPLORING CHANDANWARI, BETAB VALLEY, AND ARU VALLEY\r\nAfter a satisfying breakfast, enjoy a leisurely day at your own pace. Take the time to relax and indulge in various activities of your choice. Later,\r\nreturn to your comfortable hotel in Pahalgam for an overnight stay.\r\nRecommendation (At own cost)) :-\r\n* Visit Chandanwari, Betab Valley, and Aru Valley\r\n* These destinations offer picturesque meadows and stunning scenery\r\n* They serve as starting points for treks to Liddarwat, Kolahoi Glacier, and Tarsar Lake\r\n* Overnight stay at a hotel in Pahalgam\r\n\r\nDAY 6 CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. You can enjoy Shikara Ride on lake for 1 hour and\r\nexplore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDAY 7 CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\nTour Ends But Sweet Memories Remains Always','','* 06 Nights sty in above mentioned hotel\r\n* Daily Breakfast & dinner at hotel.\r\n* Shikara ride.\r\n* Airport/station pick-up and drop facility as confirmed by the travelers.\r\n* Sightseeing by Non-AC Innova\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc.\r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of\r\nheavy snow.\r\n* Any meal other than that mentioned above\r\n* Expenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n* Other personal expenses','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change.','2023-06-22','2023-06-28',1,0,0,'2023-06-15 13:07:21','2023-06-15 13:18:27'),(348,768,15518,11,1,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries','Munnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Kovalam: 2 Nights\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (25 Jun 2023 - Sunday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday) Munnar Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Fog Resorts & Spa Munnar/Trivers Resort\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Trivers Resort\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nDay 4 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Mountain Courtyard Resort\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29 Jun 2023 - Thursday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Southern Panorama Cruises\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 6 (30 Jun 2023 - Friday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Uday Samudra Leisure Beach Hotel\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 7 (01 Jul 2023 - Saturday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Aadisaktthi Ayurveda Leisure Village Resort,/Uday Samudra Leisure Beach Hotel\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Kochi and Trivandrum-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions','* Rates are subject to availability\r\n* Airfare is dynamic','2023-06-25','2023-07-01',1,0,0,'2023-06-15 16:30:37','2023-06-15 16:30:37'),(349,770,16512,13,1,0,348100,77000,'Karnatka Diaries','Mysore: 1 Nights, Ooty: 2 Nights, Coorg: 2 Nights\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (25 Jun 2023 - Sunday) Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nArrival At Bangalore, Proceed to mysore Check in at Hotel. Mysore (or Mysuru), a city in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Mysore is also home to the centuries-old Devaraja Market, filled with spices, silk and sandalwood. Arrive and check into the hotel . Some of the places that you can visit in Mysore depends upon the timming are Chamundeshwari temple, Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo, Jaganmohan Palace, Melody World Wax Museum, Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Sri Ranganathaswamy Temple, Chamundi Hills & Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2023 - Monday) Mysore to Ooty\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - QUORUM\r\nTransfers - Mysore to Ooty\r\nAfter morning breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty, on arrival check in to hotel. Ooty lake, Botanical Garden. Overnight stay at Ooty.\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2023 - Tuesday) Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - La Montana By TGI\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory) and Doddabetta Peak. Overnight stay at Ooty.\r\n\r\nDay 4 (28 Jun 2023 - Wednesday) Ooty to Coorg\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - La Montana By TGI\r\nTransfers - Ooty to Coorg\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Coorg, which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty. On arrival, check in at hotel. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29 Jun 2023 - Thursday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 1\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Yellow Bamboo Resort & Spa\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 1\r\nMorning after breakfast, sightseeing of Kodagu. Kodagu, also known as Coorg, is a rural district in the southwest Indian state of Karnataka. In the areaâ€™s north, Madikeri Fort has 2 life-size elephant statues at its entrance, plus a Gothic-style church with a museum on its grounds. Nearby, the Hindu Omkareshwara Temple dates back to the 19th century. Farther north are the domed Rajaâ€™s Tomb, a burial place of Kodava kings, and cascading Abbi Falls. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 6	(30 Jun 2023 - Friday) Coorg to Bangalore Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Yellow Bamboo Resort & Spa\r\nDeparture Transfer - Coorg to Bangalore Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Bangalore international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Delhi-Bangalore-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Twin Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions','* Rates are subject to availability\r\n* Airfare is dynamic\r\n','2023-06-25','2023-06-30',1,0,0,'2023-06-16 12:38:03','2023-06-16 13:08:28'),(350,774,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries ','Munnar: 2 Nig