s one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.	 	\r\n				\r\n		\r\nDay 4 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.	 	\r\n				\r\n\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.	 	\r\n		\r\n		\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT	 	\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.	 	','','* Economy class airafare.\r\n* Accommodation as above.\r\n* Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis.\r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Extra Meals\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. ','','2023-06-26','2023-07-01',1,0,0,'2023-06-20 16:24:32','2023-06-20 16:24:32'),(355,782,15500,2,0,0,445500,35000,'Europe Package','4N Switzerland - 3N France - 3N Germany\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nSightseeing:\r\nExcursion to Mt Titlis with Swiss Pass\r\nExcursion to Jungfraujoch â€“ Top of Europe With Swiss Pass\r\nZurich City Tour Experience\r\nBig Bus Paris Hop-On-Hop With Eiffel Tower 2 Floor access and Seine River Cruise\r\nLouvre Museum - Skip-the-Line Ticket with Digital Audioguide\r\n\r\n\r\nTrains:\r\nSwiss Pass 04 Days on 2nd Class\r\nTrain From Zurich to Paris on 2nd Class\r\nTrain From Paris to Frankfurt  on 2nd Class\r\n\r\nTransfers:\r\nTransfers From Paris Station to hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Paris Hotel to Statiojn on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt station to Hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt Hotel to Airport on pvt basis ','','Delhi-Zurich and Frankfurt-Delhi Economy class airfare \r\n11 night stay in above mentioned hotels on breakfast basis\r\nTrain tours as mentioned above\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing as mentioned above\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense (like laundary, medical expense, personal grooming etc.)\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','â€¢ This is just a quote; no Rooms or Services have been blocked and the same are subject to availability.\r\nâ€¢ Above rates are valid for Indian National only\r\nâ€¢ Rates & Availability is subject to change without any prior Notice\r\nâ€¢  At most Hotels Standard check-in time will be 1500hrs & checkout will be 1100 hrs .\r\nâ€¢  Early check is subject to availability & can incur additional charges.\r\nâ€¢  Please check all inclusions as any additions will occur in extra charges.\r\nâ€¢  Station / Airport transfers are not included unless mentioned.\r\nâ€¢ If your Travel period falls during a fair or Event period, A supplement cost will be applicable if any.\r\nâ€¢ The airfare is dynamic. ','2023-09-13','2023-09-23',1,0,0,'2023-06-21 18:39:38','2023-06-21 18:39:38'),(356,781,15512,3,0,0,227586,45000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“ 27 July: Arrival Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City highlights\r\nYour English-speaking guide will meet you at Noi Bai International Airport and welcome you. They will then take you on a city tour, starting with a visit to the beautiful Tran Quoc Pagoda located on the shores of West Lake. Afterward, you will proceed to the Ho Chi Minh complex, which includes Ho Chi Minh\'s Mausoleum (only open in the morning) and his stilt house where he lived from 1958 to 1969. The tour will continue to the One Pillar Pagoda, a unique structure situated in the middle of a square lake. Returning to downtown, you will have a chance to relax by Hoan Kiem Lake and visit Ngoc Son Temple. Finally, you will embark on a walking tour through the Old Quarter, also known as the 36 streets, a vibrant area filled with small businesses and shops. It\'s a fantastic place to explore and capture memorable photos.\r\nCheck in and overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 28 July: Hanoi â€“ Ninh Binh: Trang An â€“ Bai Dinh Pagoda (B)\r\nAfter breakfast, your guide will meet you at the hotel for a 110km (2-hour) journey through the beautiful countryside. You will arrive at the magnificent Bai Dinh pagoda complex, the largest pagoda in Vietnam and Southeast Asia. Nestled at the foot of Dinh Mountain, the pagoda offers breathtaking views of the surrounding river valley and limestone karsts. In the afternoon, you will visit the Trang An Grottoes, an impressive natural wonder with towering limestone formations spanning 20 square kilometers. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 29 July: Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nAt around 8:00 AM, you will depart from your hotel in a private car for a 4-hour journey to Ha Long Bay. Upon arrival at the port around noon, you will be warmly welcomed on board and shown to your cabin. After a trip briefing, you will savor a delicious seafood lunch while cruising through the enchanting Bai Tu Long Bay. There will be a stop for swimming and a visit to a mysterious cave, followed by relaxation at a secluded island beach. In the evening, you will return to the boat in time to witness a stunning sunset from the top deck, followed by a delectable seafood dinner. You will spend the night on the cruise ship.\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 30 July: Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ Hanoi â€“ Da Nang (B/L)\r\nEarly risers can witness the stunning sunrise over the majestic limestone formations of the bay. Breakfast is served at around 8:00 AM, followed by a short rowboat ride guided by the locals. Enjoy brunch on the boat while cruising back to the pier. Return to Hanoi by road.\r\nUpon reaching the center of Hanoi, our driver will pick you up and transfer you to Hanoi airport for your flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival in Da Nang, you will be picked up and transferred to your hotel for check-in. The evening is free for you to relax and explore. Overnight stay in Danang.\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 31 July: Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast at your hotel, you will be transferred to Ba Na Hills, located 35km from Danang center. Board the Sunworld Cable Car, which has received 5 world records, to reach Ba Na Hills station. Along the way, you will stop at By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and the Old Villas of French. Continue ascending to Nui Chua Mountain, the highest peak of the Ba Na range, to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and the Orchid Garden. Experience a unique hill climbing train, visit the flower garden Le Jardin D\'amour, and marvel at the famous Golden Bridge with its panoramic views. Lunch is at your own leisure. In the afternoon, enjoy the various games and attractions at Fantasy Park, the third largest indoor games zone in Vietnam. Around 5pm, return to your hotel.Overnight in Danang.\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 01 Aug: Da Nang - fly to Ho Chi Minh City, city highlights (B)\r\nHave a breakfast at your hotel. Meeting our driver and transfer to the Da Nang airport for flight to Ho Chi Minh. Upon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and transfer to the city downtown (30 minutes) for the city must-not-miss sites including Notre Dame Cathedral, the historic Central Post Office, City Hall, Ben Thanh Market, Nguyen Hue walking boulevard.\r\nHead to your hotel to check in and spend rest of the day at your own leisure.\r\nNote: Check in time 14:00\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 02 Aug: HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (B)\r\nt 8:30 AM, you\'ll be picked up for a trip to the Mekong Delta. Board a motorboat in My Tho City to explore canals and observe local life. Visit Thoi Son Island for traditional music, paddle boat rides, coconut candy making, and a bee farm. Enjoy fresh honey and fruits. On the return, visit Vinh Trang Pagoda. Return to Ho Chi Minh City for overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 8 â€“ 03 Aug: HCMC departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at hotel. Depending on your flight you may have some more time for shopping by your own. Then we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. Goodbye, and hope to see you again soon!','','* Economy Class airfare.\r\n* Flight Includes Hanoi â€“ Da Nang â€“ Ho Chi Minh.\r\n* Private airport transfer\r\n* Accommodation based on triple sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Private airport transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Personal expenses \r\n* TCS','Airafare is dynamic.\r\nThe final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruiseâ€™s program.','2023-07-26','2023-08-03',1,0,0,'2023-06-22 14:50:22','2023-06-22 16:02:37'),(357,786,15500,2,0,0,290800,35000,'Europe Package','3N Paris - 3N Switzerland - 3N Germany\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nTrains:\r\nSwiss Pass 04 Days on 2nd Class\r\nTrain ticket  Paris Gare de Lyon  -   Basel  (2nd class)\r\nTrain ticket  Basel  -   Frankfurt am Main Hbf  (2nd class)\r\n\r\nTransfers:\r\nTransfers From Paris Airport to hotel on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Paris Hotel to Statiojn on pvt basis\r\nTransfers From Frankfurt Hotel to Airport on pvt basis ','','* Delhi-Paris and Frankfurt-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Private transfer from Paris Airport to Hotel\r\n* Eiffel Tower Skip the Line Tour & River Cruise with Champagne (Eiffel Tower & Seine River 16:00) (Departure Point) 1 Port de Suffren, 75007 Paris, France\r\n* Versailles Gardens & Palace from Paris with Priority Access (Versailles Gardens & Palace from Paris with Priority Access 10:00)(Departure Point) Javel - AndrÃ© CitroÃ«n, 75015 Paris, \r\n* Notre Dame Outdoor Walking Tour with Crypt Entry (Walking Tour in English 13:00) Dep Point: Statue de Charlemagne et ses Leudes, Ãle de la CitÃ©, 75004 Paris, France\r\n* 04 Days Swiss pass consecutive 2nd Class \r\n* Jungfraujoch with Swiss pass\r\n* Mt. Titlis with Swiss pass\r\n* Rhine Fall with Swiss pass (Entry fee pay locally)\r\n* Train tours as mentioned above\r\n* All transfers and sightseeing as mentioned above\r\n* Visa Charges\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense (like laundary, medical expense, personal grooming etc.)\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\nTCS','â€¢ This is just a quote; no Rooms or Services have been blocked and the same are subject to availability.\r\nâ€¢ Above rates are valid for Indian National only\r\nâ€¢ Rates & Availability is subject to change without any prior Notice\r\nâ€¢  At most Hotels Standard check-in time will be 1500hrs & checkout will be 1100 hrs .\r\nâ€¢  Early check is subject to availability & can incur additional charges.\r\nâ€¢  Please check all inclusions as any additions will occur in extra charges.\r\nâ€¢  Station / Airport transfers are not included unless mentioned.\r\nâ€¢ If your Travel period falls during a fair or Event period, A supplement cost will be applicable if any.\r\nâ€¢ The airfare is dynamic. ','2023-09-13','2023-09-22',1,0,0,'2023-06-23 13:44:51','2023-06-23 14:51:04'),(358,787,15526,2,0,0,67400,21000,'Kashmir - the heaven on earth','2N Srinagar - 1N Gulmarg - 1N Pahalgam - 1N Srinagar\r\n\r\n\r\nITINERARY\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHTSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\n \r\nUpon arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer you to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of the Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), and Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at a hotel in Srinagar.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of the Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding up to Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at a hotel in Srinagar.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg. Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-hole golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow-clad mountains, a Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view of the natural beauty of the summer and a full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at a hotel in Gulmarg.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay  4 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breathtaking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in the evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n \r\n \r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\n \r\nAfter breakfast check out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\n \r\n ','','âœ” Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\nâœ” accommodation  as above.\r\nâœ” Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\nâœ” Airport - pick-up and drop facility on a pvt basis.\r\nâœ” Sightseeing by a non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\nâœ” Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in the same houseboat\r\nâœ” Driver Allowances.\r\nâœ” Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry fee at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\nâœ” Hotel Taxes','âœ” Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\nâœ” Extra Meals - Meals not included in package anything not specifically mentioned under the head â€œPrices includedâ€.\r\nâœ” Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\nâœ” Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\nâœ” Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\nâœ” Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\nâœ” Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, minibars, etc.\r\nâœ” Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc.\r\nâœ” The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg & Gulmarg to Tangmarg or Sonamarg in case of heavy snow.','The flight fare is dynamic.\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability.','2023-07-12','2023-07-17',1,0,0,'2023-06-23 16:36:23','2023-06-23 17:09:54'),(359,788,15518,3,0,0,66400,17000,'Kerala Diaries ','Cochin: 1 Nights, Munnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Kovalam: 2 Nights\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (09 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Broad Bean Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (10 Nov 2023 - Friday) Cochin to Munnar\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Broad Bean Hotel\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Arbour Resort (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (11 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Arbour Resort\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Arbour Resort (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (12 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Arbour Resort\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Patio (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (13 Nov 2023 - Monday) Thekkady to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Patio\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places for 21hrs in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Royal Rivers Cruises (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (14 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Royal Rivers Cruises\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 (15 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace  (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 (16 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Trivandrum Dep\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Trivandrum Dep\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the Hotel and transferred to Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Triple Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n','* Rates are subject to availability\r\n* Airfare is dynamic','2023-11-09','2023-11-16',1,0,0,'2023-06-24 17:18:24','2023-06-24 17:31:42'),(360,790,15518,3,0,0,58500,13000,'Kerala Diaries ','Cochin: 1 Nights, Munnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Kovalam: 2 Nights\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (09 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Cochin Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Broad Bean Hotel (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (10 Nov 2023 - Friday) Cochin to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Broad Bean Hotel\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Munnar Summer Castle (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (11 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Munnar Summer Castle\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Munnar Summer Castle (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (12 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Munnar Summer Castle\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Patio (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (13 Nov 2023 - Monday) Thekkady to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Patio\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places for 21hrs in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Royal Rivers Cruises (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (14 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Royal Rivers Cruises\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel SAMUDRATHEERAM (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 (15 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - SAMUDRATHEERAM\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel SAMUDRATHEERAM (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 (16 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Trivandrum Dep\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - SAMUDRATHEERAM\r\nDeparture Transfer - Trivandrum Dep\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the Hotel and transferred to Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.','','* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n* Accommodation on Triple Sharing Basis\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n','* Rates are subject to availability\r\n* Airfare is dynamic','2023-11-09','2023-11-16',0,0,0,'2023-06-26 11:52:19','2023-06-26 12:04:13'),(361,793,15530,4,0,0,202400,40000,'Andaman Diaries','\r\n1st Day (10 Nov)\r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show (Tickets & Transfers)\r\n\r\n\r\n2nd Day (11 Nov)\r\nPort Blair - North Bay (Coral Island) â€“ Ross Island (Boat charge & Transfers)\r\n\r\n\r\n3rd Day (12 Nov)\r\nPort Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n4th Day (13 Nov)\r\nHavelock - Elephenta Beach (Boat charge & Transfers)\r\n\r\n5th Day (14 Nov)\r\nHavelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n6th Day (15 Nov)\r\nNeil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\nPrivate Catamaran Ferry : Premium\r\n\r\n7th Day (16 Nov)\r\nPort Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n','','â€¢ Delhi-Port Blair -Delhi Economy class airfare\r\nâ€¢ Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan â€“ As mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\nâ€¢ All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle.\r\nâ€¢ Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability)\r\nâ€¢ 1 Xylo/Ertiga for transfers\r\n','â€¢ The services of vehicles not on a disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/Vehicles for Dinner etc.','The airfare is dynamic and subject to change. \r\nThe rooms are subject to availability.','2023-11-10','2023-11-16',1,0,0,'2023-06-28 15:29:01','2023-07-03 16:33:04'),(362,794,16260,4,0,0,190700,39000,'Europe Package','2N Lucerne - 2N Interlaken - 1N Zurich\r\n\r\n','','6 Days Swiss Pass\r\n5 Nights accommodation in above mentioned hotels\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nMt. Titlis Excursion with Swiss Travel Pass incl. Ice Flyer (Return from Engelberg - Mt. Titlis)\r\nJungfraujoch, Train Trip and the Bernese Oberland - Tour\r\nRhine Falls with Swiss Pass (Ferry tickets to be purchased there itself)\r\nZurich City Tour Experience (Start Times 14:00)\r\nAll transfers to be done with swiss pass\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any other meal other than mentioned above\r\nAny excursion other than mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense\r\nTCS (5%)\r\n\r\n','The rooms are subject to availability.\r\n\r\nOptional Tour:\r\nChapel Bridge or Lion Monument in Lucerne (Can be done with Swiss Pass)','2023-08-11','2023-08-16',0,0,0,'2023-06-29 14:47:35','2023-06-29 15:17:22'),(363,795,419,2,2,0,86400,19000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - ARRIVAL + SRINAGAR LOCAL SIGHSEEING (CHECK-IN HOTEL)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 2 - SONMARG DAY TRIP  FROM SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Sonamarg \"Golden Meadow\".  Sonmarg lies in Sind Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude of Himalayan Lakes. Enjoy horse riding upto Thajiwas glacier and sledge riding on snow (own cost). Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - CHECK-IN AT PAHALGAM (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\nDay 4 - CHECK-IN AT GULMARG (1 NIGHT STAY)\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.\r\n\r\nDay 5 - CHECK-IN AT SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.\r\n\r\nDay 6 - CHECK-OUT FROM SRINAGAR HOUSEBOAT\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.','','* Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation as above.\r\n* Breakfast and Dinner in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis.\r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n* Vehicle: Etios (NON AC)\r\n','* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Extra Meals\r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonamarg.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument.\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. ','Airfare is dynamic','2023-07-28','2023-08-02',1,0,0,'2023-07-01 12:21:41','2023-07-01 12:59:06'),(364,797,15512,2,0,0,155200,26000,'IMPRESSION OF VIETNAM','Day 1 â€“ 10 Aug: Arrival Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City highlights\r\n\r\nUpon arrival at Noi Bai International Airport, meet your tour guide and transfer to the city center. Embark on a city tour starting with a visit to the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum to learn about the life of Ho Chi Minh, followed by a stop at the One Pillar Pagoda. Explore the Temple of Literature, the oldest university in Vietnam, and stroll through the Hanoi Old Quarter, admiring the French colonial architecture and local shops. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 11 Aug: Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (B,L,D)\r\n\r\nDepart from Hanoi in the morning and travel to Ha Long Bay by private van. Arrive at the port, board your cruise, and enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through Bai Tu Long Bay. Swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded island-beach. Watch the sunset from the boat and savor a delicious seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 12 Aug: Explore Ha Long Bay â€“ Hanoi â€“ Flight to Da Nang (B,L/Br)\r\n\r\nWake up early to witness the sunrise and the breathtaking beauty of Ha Long Bay. Enjoy breakfast before taking a rowboat ride and having brunch on the cruise. Return to the pier and proceed to the airport for a flight to Da Nang. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 13 Aug: Ba Na Hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\n\r\nVisit Ba Na Hills, taking the Sunworld Cable Car and exploring attractions like Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and the Old Villas of French. Experience a hill climbing train and admire the Golden Bridge with its panoramic views. Enjoy games at Fantasy Park before returning to your hotel in the afternoon. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 14 Aug: Da Nang - Fly to Ho Chi Minh City, city highlights (B)\r\n\r\nFly from Da Nang to Ho Chi Minh City. Start your city tour with a visit to downtown HCM City and the bustling Binh Tay Market. Stop at Thien Hau Temple and explore a lacquer-wares workshop and the Jade Emperor Pagoda. Visit the Notre Dame Cathedral and the Central Post Office. Return to your hotel after the tour. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh City.\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 15 Aug: Cu Chi Tunnel â€“ Ho Chi Minh Departure (B)\r\n\r\nDepart for the Cu Chi Tunnels, where you\'ll learn about their construction and the survival tactics employed during the war. Explore the tunnel systems, experience guerilla life, and taste tea and cassava. Optionally, try shooting a real gun. Afterward, relax before being transferred to the airport for your departure.\r\n\r\nNote: This itinerary includes private transfers, guides, entrance fees, accommodation, and meals as specified. The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruise\'s program.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDomestic Flights:\r\n12 AUG: HAN â€“ DAD (20:15 â€“ 21:35)\r\n14 AUG: DAD â€“ SGN (09:00 - 10:25)\r\n\r\n','','* Delhi-Hanoi and Ho Chi Minh - Delhi Economy class airfare \r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local