 known in India and is stuffed with history and legends. Mehrangarh Fort still bears the engravings of cannonball assaults used by the armed forces of Jaipur on its second entryway.(If time permits) Evening is free for leisure. Overnight stay at Jodhpur Hotel.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n4th Day (21st Nov Tuesday) : Jodhpur to Udaipur - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the hotel . Later drive to Udaipur. Upon your arrival, complete your check-in process. Get Relaxed. Head back to the hotel for the night. Dinner & Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day (22nd Nov Wednesday) : Udaipur - Sightseeing\r\n\r\nBegin your day with breakfast at the hotel and then start your city tour. Visit the City Palace which is the biggest castle complex in Rajasthan. Partake in the boat ride on the tranquil waters of Lake Pichola. Also visit Sahelion ki Bari or Garden of the Maids of Honor, Jagdish sanctuary. Local Market Visit. Later in the evening Fateh Sagar Lake, Shilpgram.Once sightseeing is over, head back to the hotel. Dinner & Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6th Day (23rd Nov Thursday) : Udaipur - Departure\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Hotel Visit MAHARANA PRATAP MEMORIAL with local market visit and take a transfer to Udaipur Airport as you will be heading back to your home with the good memory.','','Delhi-Jaipur and Udaipur-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n5 nights accommodation at above mentioned hotels\r\nDaily breakfast\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing with an AC vehicle (Innova Crysta)\r\nToll Tax, Parking and Driver allowances\r\nGST','Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions','The airfare is dynamic and hence  subject to vary.\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability. \r\nThis quotation does not represent any booking. ','2023-11-18','2023-11-23',1,0,0,'2023-09-22 21:56:35','2023-09-22 22:00:44'),(453,927,6,4,0,0,3500,0,'Delhi Diaries','Suggested Places to be visited: \r\n\r\n1. Lotus Temple\r\n2. India Gate\r\n3. Raj Ghat\r\n4. AkshardhamÂ Temple\r\n5. Qutub Minar (If time permits)','','* Innova Crysta for sightseeing.\r\n* Breakfast.\r\n* 1 night stay in the selected hotel.','','','2023-12-21','2023-12-22',1,0,0,'2023-09-23 13:19:14','2023-09-25 15:46:04'),(454,929,15510,2,0,0,65000,15000,'Thailand Adventure','','','* 9 nights stay\r\n* Daily breakfast\r\n* Transfers from Phuket airport to Phuket hotel PVT basis\r\n* Transfers from Phuket hotel to Krabi hotel PVT basis\r\n* Transfers from Krabi hotel to Krabi airport PVT basis\r\n* 3 way transfers from BKK airport  (Suvarnabhumi)) to Pattaya hotel to BKK hotel to BKK airport \r\n  PVT basis\r\n* Phuket Half Day City Tour on SIC - (Including Big Buddha) (PU/10:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Full Day James Bond Island by Speed Boat + Sea Canoe + Lunch + Transfer + Incl. National Marine * \r\n  Park FEE (Ao Por Pier) SIC basis\r\n* Hot spring, Emerald Pool and tiger cave temple with local lunch on SIC (Exclude the National \r\n  Park *Admission Fee) SIC basis\r\n* Coral Island Tour by Speedboat with Indian Buffet Lunch (PU/ 09:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Alcazar Show with Transfers + 1 Soft Drink (VIP Seat) (Evening) PVT basis PVT basis\r\n* Under waterworld with Transfers PVT basis\r\n* Bangkok city tour with Golden Buddha and Marvel Buddha with Gems Gallary SIC basis\r\n* Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch (PU/ 08:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Mahanakhon SkyWalk + Digitel Photo + Soft Drink at 74TH Floor (Sunset Ticket 16:00-19:00 Hrs) \r\n  PVT basis\r\n* Travel Insurance','* (Exclude the National Park *Admission Fee) SIC basis\r\n* (Including Big Buddha) (PU/10:00AM) SIC basis\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in the Inclusions.\r\n* TCS (5%)','','2023-11-15','2023-11-24',0,0,0,'2023-09-26 13:07:56','2023-09-29 17:06:01'),(455,928,15512,2,0,0,93100,23000,'Vietnam Package','Day-wise itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 - 15 Nov: Arrival in Hanoi, Vietnam (B)\r\n\r\nOur English-speaking guide will greet you at Noi Bai International Airport and provide a transfer to Hanoi downtown for early check-in. In the afternoon, we\'ll explore Hanoi\'s hidden heritage, including visits to the Temple of Literature, a walk through the old quarter, Ngoc Son Temple, and a cyclo ride around Hoan Kiem Lake and the Old Quarter, offering an authentic Hanoian experience. The tour concludes around 4:30 PM, after which you can enjoy dinner at your leisure. You\'ll spend the night in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nInclusions: Transfer, guide, water, hotel, entrance fees, and early check-in.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 - 15 Nov: Hanoi to Ha Long Bay, Boarding the Boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\n\r\nAt around 8:00 AM, you\'ll depart for Ha Long Bay in a shared van, which takes approximately 4 hours from your hotel. Upon arriving at the port around noon, you\'ll be warmly welcomed aboard the boat. After settling into your cabin, there will be a trip briefing.\r\n\r\nYou\'ll savor a delicious seafood lunch made from local ingredients while cruising through the enchanting Bai Tu Long Bay. The day includes a swim break and a visit to a mysterious cave. Relax on a secluded island beach, and later, return to the boat just in time to witness a stunning sunset from the top deck. Then, enjoy a fresh seafood dinner. You\'ll spend the night on the cruise.\r\n\r\nInclusions: Transfer, guide on the boat, entrance fees, boat/junk accommodation, all meals, and permits.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - 17 Nov: Explore Bai Tu Long Bay, Return to Hanoi, Fly to Da Nang (B, BR)\r\n\r\nFor early risers, there\'s a chance to witness the breathtaking sunrise over the magnificent limestone formations in the bay. Breakfast is served around 8:00 AM, followed by a short rowboat excursion led by locals from the bay. Enjoy brunch on the boat as we leisurely cruise back to the boat pier.\r\n\r\nUpon returning to Hanoi, you\'ll be transferred to Hanoi airport for your flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival in Da Nang, our driver will pick you up and transfer you to your hotel for check-in. You\'ll spend the night in Danang.\r\n\r\nInclusions: Transfer, guide on the boat, entrance fees, boat/junk accommodation, breakfast, brunch, and hotel transfer.\r\n\r\nDay 4 - 18 Nov: Da Nang - Hoi An Sightseeing (B)\r\n\r\nStart your day with breakfast at the hotel. Today\'s itinerary includes a visit to Marble Mountain, where you\'ll explore natural caves, mysterious pagodas, and the Stone Carving Village.\r\n\r\nIn the afternoon, experience the timeless charm of Hoi An\'s ancient town as you stroll through its narrow streets along the banks of the Thu Bon River. Don\'t miss the Japanese Covered Bridge to learn about the lives of Japanese immigrants in the 17th century. Explore the Fujian Assembly Hall, the original place of worship for those who came to Hoi An from Fujian, China, also in the 17th century. Afterward, you\'ll have free time to enjoy the Hoi An lantern market for shopping and dinner. Spend the night in Hoi An.\r\n\r\nInclusions: Private transfer, guide, breakfast, entrance fees, and hotel accommodation.\r\n\r\nDay 5 - 19 Nov: Ba Na Hill - Golden Bridge Full Day\r\n\r\nStart your day with breakfast at your hotel. At 8:00 AM, you\'ll be transferred to Ba Na Hills, which is located 35km from Danang center. Hop on the Sunworld Cable Car, known for its world records, to reach Ba Na Hills station. Along the way, stop at By Night station to explore Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and the Old French Villas.\r\n\r\nContinue your ascent by cable car to Nui Chua Mountain, the highest point of Ba Na range. Visit Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and the Orchid Garden. Experience a unique hill climbing train, the first of its kind in Vietnam, and explore the Flower Garden Le Jardin D\'amour and Linh Ung Pagoda. Don\'t miss a walk across the famous Golden Bridge, offering panoramic views of the mountains and lush trees. Afterward, you\'ll have free time for lunch on your own.\r\n\r\nIn the afternoon, enjoy various games at Fantasy Park, the third-largest indoor games zone in Vietnam, featuring 4-5D films, skiver, the death race, and a dinosaur park. You\'ll spend the night in Danang.\r\n\r\nInclusions: Private transfer, guide, entrance fees, cable car ticket, and breakfast.\r\n\r\nDay 6- 20 Nov: Hoi An Departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at hotel. We transfer you to the airport in time for your flight back to Hanoi and\r\nyour connection elsewhere. Goodbye, and hope to see you again soon!\r\nInclusion: Private transfer , breakfast','','* Delhi-Hanoi and Da Nang-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n* Internal flight from Hanoi-Da Nang is included\r\n* 4 nights accommodation in hotels on breakfast basis\r\n* 1 night stay in cruise with all meals\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Enterance fee as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for touring day (500ml/per pax/per day)  \r\n* Visa charges and assistance\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n ','* Early Check-in/late check-out if not mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Beverages \r\n* Personal expenses\r\n* Surcharge in peak season\r\n* Tips (to be paid there directly, $3 per day/ per pax)\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions','','2023-11-15','2023-11-20',1,0,0,'2023-09-26 14:27:31','2023-09-26 14:58:51'),(457,932,15595,2,0,1,76440,16000,'Sri Lanka Package','Suggested Tours:\r\n\r\n1. Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage\r\n\r\n2. Temple of the tooth relic\r\n\r\n3. Peradeniya Botanical Garden\r\n\r\n4. Maduriver boat Safari\r\n\r\n5. Turtle Hatchery\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy class airfare\r\n* Welcome at the airport\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on BB / CPAI\r\n* Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned vehicle (sedan car).\r\n* Service of an English-speaking chauffeur\r\n* City tour which is mentioned above in the itinerary\r\n* Government Tax (VAT 12%)\r\n* Toll charges','* Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\n* Visa Fees (please log on to www.eta.gov.lk)\r\n* Visa will be on arrival charges USD 25 per person  \r\n* Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\n* Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\n* Camera or Video permits.\r\n* Expenses of a personal nature.\r\n* Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\n* Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring','The airfare is dynamic. \r\nThe rooms are subject to availability.\r\nThe rates are valid till 5th October, 2023.\r\nThe entrance fee of Lotus Tower (USD 20) will be charged extra if it is to be added.','2023-11-28','2023-12-04',1,0,0,'2023-09-29 16:02:22','2023-09-29 16:02:22'),(458,931,557,2,0,0,35300,15000,'Sri Lanka Diaries','','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on BB/CPAI\r\n* Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned vehicle.\r\n* Service of an English-speaking chauffeur\r\n* City tour which is mentioned above in the itinerary\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\n* Government Tax (VAT 12%).\r\n* Toll charges.','* Visa','','2024-02-08','2024-02-11',1,0,0,'2023-09-29 16:31:11','2023-09-29 17:17:29'),(459,933,6,4,0,0,3500,0,'Delhi Diaries','Suggested Places to be visited: \r\n\r\n1. Lotus Temple\r\n2. India Gate\r\n3. Raj Ghat\r\n4. AkshardhamÂ Temple\r\n5. Qutub Minar (If time permits)','','* Innova Crysta for sightseeing.\r\n* Breakfast.\r\n* 1 night stay in the selected hotel.','','','2023-12-21','2023-12-22',1,0,0,'2023-09-29 22:57:40','2023-09-29 22:57:40'),(460,935,2094,2,0,0,12500,8000,'Puri-Bhubaneshwar','Daywise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDAY-1: ARRIVE AT BHUBANESWAR â€“ PURI\r\nOur cab will receive guests at Bhubaneswar Station/Airport, then drive to puri En-route visit Dhauli (the Peace pagoda). 108 Shivling Temples, Lingaraj Temple. After reach at Puri, Check in at the hotel and enjoy at puri beach. Overnight at Puri.\r\n\r\nDAY-2: PURI (JAGANNATH TEMPLE) CHILIKA LAKE \r\nAfter breakfast visit for darshan at shri jagannath temple, Gundicha Temple, Loknath temple then depart for Satpada, Chilka. The fancy land of Irwadi Dolphins. Entire day sightseeing of Satpada. Evening return to Puri, enjoy it at Puri beach. Overnight at Puri.\r\n\r\nDAY-3: PURI â€“ KONARK â€“ BHUBANESWAR \r\nMorning after Breakfast guest will leave for Bhubaneswar, on the way visit Dhaulagiri, Ramachandi Temple, Chandrabhaga Beach, Konark Temple. Check in at Hotel in Bhubaneswar Overnight stay at Bhubaneswar. \r\n\r\nDAY -4: BHUBANESWAR LOCAL\r\nAfter breakfast Bhubaneswar sightseeing Lingaraj Temple, Rajarani Temple, Mukteswar Temple. aKhandagiri & Udaygiri Caves Evening will be at leisure, Overnight stay at Bhubaneswar.\r\n\r\nDAY-5: BHUBANESWAR DEPARTURE \r\nMorning after Breakfast guest will leave for Bhubaneswar and visit few more places like Nandankanan Zoo (Monday Closed) Tribal museum (Monday Closed) Then drop at Bhubaneswar airport happy ending journey with sweet memories.','','* Economy class airfare\r\n* 4 nights accommodation on breakfast basis\r\n* All tours and sightseeing in an AC vehicle (Sedan car)\r\n* Airport transfers\r\n* All toll and taxes\r\n','* Any meal other than mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses.\r\n* Tips\r\n* Anything which is not mentioned in Inclusions.\r\n','The airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability\r\nThe rates are valid till 3rd October, 2023\r\n','2023-10-05','2023-10-09',1,0,0,'2023-09-30 12:28:17','2023-09-30 12:39:39'),(461,936,349,2,0,0,28730,10000,'Dubai Diaries','Day wise Itinerary â€“\r\n\r\n18 Oct â€“Arrival transfers + Dhow cruise Marina With Dinner\r\n19 Oct â€“Dubai Half Day City Tour + Burj Khalifa Evening slot\r\n20 Oct- Desert safari with BBQ dinner on sic\r\n21 Oct -Day at leisure\r\n22 Oct -Departure Transfers\r\n','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Dubai half day city tour on sic\r\n* Desert safari with bbq dinner on sic\r\n* Marina Dhow Cruise with dinner on sic\r\n* Burj khalifa 124 floor non prime ticket on sic\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Visa','TCS','','2023-10-18','2023-10-22',1,0,0,'2023-10-03 17:18:55','2023-10-03 18:36:49'),(462,938,349,2,0,0,28800,5000,'Dubai Diaries','\r\n10 Dec â€“Arrival transfers + Dhow cruise Marina With Dinner\r\n11 Dec â€“Day at leisure\r\n12 Dec -Dubai Half Day City Tour + Burj Khalifa Evening slot\r\n13 Dec -Desert safari with bbq dinner on sic\r\n14 Dec -Day at leisure\r\n15 Dec -Departure Transfers\r\n','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Dubai half day city tour on sic\r\n* Desert safari with bbq dinner on sic\r\n* Marina Dhow Cruise with dinner on sic\r\n* Burj khalifa 124 floor non prime ticket on sic\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Visa','TCS*As Per law Applicable,TCS* As per law applicable','','2023-12-10','2023-12-15',1,0,0,'2023-10-05 11:24:18','2023-10-05 18:06:48'),(463,940,54,2,0,0,38200,22000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (12 Nov) - Arrival Transfer + Night Safari with Tram Ride\r\nDay 2 (13 Nov) - SIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa \r\nDay 3 (14 Nov) - Universal Studio\r\nDay 4 (15 Nov) - Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree )\r\nDay 6 (16 Nov) - Return Transfers.','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* 4 nights stay in hotel.\r\n* Night Safari with Tram Ride.\r\n* SIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings Of Time) \r\n* Universal Studio\r\n* Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree )\r\n* All Sightseeing on sharing basis.\r\n* Return airport transfers on pvt.','* TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2023-11-12','2023-11-16',1,0,0,'2023-10-07 14:23:36','2023-10-07 14:42:57'),(464,941,419,7,0,0,66800,19000,'Srinagar Package','Day 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR-AFTERNOON SIGHTSEEING OF MUGHAL GARDEN\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat.Afternoon sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. In the evening you will take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hoouseboat.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar.. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\n','','Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi economy class airfare\r\nMeal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n01 Shikara Ride.\r\nSightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nAll Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nAll present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nAny future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\n1 Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA','Any Medical/rescue evacuation due to mishaps.\r\nAny personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nMineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 Entrance Free\r\nRoom Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\nHorse Riding\r\nSightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\nGondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\nAny other things that is not included in the Package','The airfare is dynamic. \r\nThe rooms are subject to availability.','2023-10-24','2023-10-28',1,0,0,'2023-10-09 16:56:19','2023-10-12 18:54:10'),(465,943,15512,2,0,0,196560,30440,'Vietnam Package','\r\nDay 1 â€“ 23 Dec: Arrival in Hanoi, Vietnam\r\n\r\nMeet at Noi Bai International Airport\r\nTransfer to Hanoi downtown for check-in (2 PM)\r\nVisit Temple of Literature, Vietnam\'s first University\r\nExplore Dong Xuan Market\r\nStroll around Hoan Kiem Lake and Hanoi\'s Old Quarter\r\nFree evening for dinner and overnight stay in Hanoi\r\nInclusions: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 24 Dec: Hanoi to Ninh Binh â€“ Hoa Lu â€“ Tam Coc Boat Tour (SIC) (B/L)\r\n\r\n07:30-08:00: Meet your guide at your hotel\r\nJourney 120km by modern bus through scenic landscapes\r\nArrive at Hoa Lu, ancient capital dating back to the 11th century\r\nExplore King Dinh and Le Temple ruins\r\nEnjoy a buffet lunch at a local restaurant\r\nTake a boat trip in Tam Coc along Ngo Dong river\r\nAdmire Karst hills, rice fields, and villages\r\nCycle leisurely through the village\r\nReturn to Hanoi by shuttle bus\r\n18:30: Drop-off at your Hanoi Old Quarter accommodation\r\nInclusions: Shared transfer, guide, entrance fees, rowboat trip, breakfast, lunch, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 25 Dec: Hanoi to Ha Long, Boat Welcome (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\n\r\nDepart for Ha Long Bay around 8:00 AM by shared van (4-hour journey)\r\nArrive at the port around noon and board the boat\r\nReceive a cabin assignment and attend a trip briefing\r\nEnjoy a seafood lunch while cruising in Bai Tu Long Bay\r\nSwim and explore a mysterious cave\r\nRelax on a secluded island beach\r\nWatch the sunset from the top deck\r\nSavor a fresh seafood dinner on the boat\r\nOvernight on the cruise\r\nInclusions: Transfer, onboard guide, entrance fee, boat/junk, all meals, permits\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 26 Dec: Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ Hanoi â€“ Flight to Da Nang (SIC) (B/L)\r\n\r\nEnjoy a sunrise view and breakfast on board\r\nTake a short rowboat ride by the locals\r\nHave brunch on the boat while returning to the pier\r\nReturn to Hanoi by road\r\nTransfer to Hanoi airport for a flight to Da Nang\r\nUpon arrival, transfer to your Da Nang hotel for check-in\r\nOvernight in Da Nang\r\nInclusions: Transfer, onboard guide, entrance fee, boat/junk, breakfast, brunch, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 27 Dec: Explore Ba Na Hills & Golden Bridge Full Day (B)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at your hotel\r\n8:00 AM: Transfer to Ba Na Hills (35km from Da Nang)\r\nRide the Sunworld Cable Car to Ba Na Hills station\r\nVisit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas\r\nExplore Nui Chua Mountain, Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and Orchid Garden\r\nExperience the hill climbing train and visit Le Jardin D\'amour and Linh Ung Pagoda\r\nWalk across the famous Golden Bridge for panoramic views\r\nLunch at your own choice\r\nFree time for games at Fantasy Park, one of Vietnam\'s largest indoor games zones\r\nOvernight in Da Nang\r\nInclusions: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, cable car ticket, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 28 Dec: Coconut Forest & Hoi An Walking Tour (B)\r\n\r\nBreakfast at your hotel\r\nVisit Bay Mau water coconut forest, row a basket boat, and enjoy the tranquility\r\nLunch on your own\r\nExplore Hoi An ancient town, including Japanese Covered Bridge, Chinese Assembly Halls, Phuoc Kien Pagoda, Sa Huynh Museum, and the local market\r\nGo shopping in Hoi An market\r\nReturn to your hotel at 5 pm for an overnight stay in Da Nang\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, Basket Boat, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 29 Dec: Da Nang to Siem Reap (B)\r\n\r\nAfternoon transfer to Da Nang airport for flight to Siem Reap\r\nArrival at Siem Reap International Airport and immigration procedures\r\nTransfer to the city hotel for check-in (2 pm check-in time)\r\nOvernight in Siem Reap\r\nInclusion: Transfer, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8 â€“ 30 Dec: Angkor Highlights (B)\r\n\r\nVisit Angkor Thom, Bayon Temple, Terrace of the Leper King, and Baphuon\r\nExplore Angkor Wat, the world\'s largest religious building\r\nOvernight in Siem Reap\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 9 â€“ 31 Dec: Grand Circuit & Banteay Srei (B)\r\n\r\nVisit Preah Khan Temple, Neak Poan, Tasom, and Banteay Srei\r\nStop at Pradark Village to see local handicrafts\r\nExplore Banteay Samre and experience sunset at Pre Rup\r\nOvernight in Siem Reap\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 10 â€“ 1 Jan: Siem Reap Departure (B)\r\n\r\nTransfer to Tonle Sap Lake for a boat trip to Kompong Pluk\r\nLearn about life on the lake, visit floating houses, and impressive flooded forests\r\nTransfer to Siem Reap airport for departure\r\nFarewell and thank you for traveling with us\r\nInclusion: Transfers\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Delhi-Hanoi and Siem Reap-Delhi economy class airfare\r\nHanoi-Da Nang and Da Nang-Siem Reap economy class airfare\r\n9 nights accommodation on double sharing basis with daily breakfast\r\nMeals other than breakfast as mentioned above.\r\nAll sightseeing and transfers on pvt/sharing basis as mentioned above.\r\n1 Bottles water for the touring day (350- 500ml/bottle/pax/day)\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n\r\n','Early Check-in/ Late check-out\r\nSurcharge in peak season\r\nMeals other than the mentioned in the itinerary\r\nAny type of personal expenses. \r\nDrinks during meals\r\nTips (mandatory to be paid there only - $3 per person per day)\r\nTCS','The airfare is dynamic.\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability. ','2023-12-23','2024-01-01',1,0,0,'2023-10-09 22:29:29','2023-10-10 13:15:48'),(466,944,15518,4,2,0,85200,16000,'South India','Day 1	(16 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2	(17 Nov 2023 - Friday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3	(18 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Amuse Vista Resorts and Spa\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jungle Park Resorts (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4	(19 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jungle Park Resorts\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters.  Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters.Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Pagoda Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5	(20 Nov 2023 - Monday) Alleppey to Varkala\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Pagoda Resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Varkala\r\nMorning after breakfast Head to one of the famous beach destination Varkala. Varkala is the only place in southern Kerala where cliffs are found adjacent to Arabian sea. Varkala is famous for the 2000 year old Janardana Swami Temple , Ayurveda treatment centres and off course for Varkala Beach. Varkala beach is god place for sun bathing and swimming, the evening views of the sunset are worth lingering over. Overnight at the Resort/hotel.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel KRISHNA THEERAM (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6	(21 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Varkala to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - KRISHNA THEERAM\r\nTransfers - Varkala to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and  transfer to Kovalam. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7	(22 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier Museum. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Jasmine Palace (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 8	(23 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Jasmine Palace\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','Any type of personal expense. \r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions.\r\n','','2023-11-16','2023-11-22',0,0,0,'2023-10-10 16:40:14','2023-10-10 16:48:17'),(467,945,15567,8,0,0,143200,32500,'Nepal Package','15 Jan. 2024:\r\n* Pickup from Kathmandu International Airport and drop at hotel.\r\n* Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n* Half day sightseeing at Kathmandu covering Swyambhunath Stupa (Monkey Temple) & Kathmandu Durbar Square.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n16 Jan 2024:â€‹\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Half day sightseeing at Kathmandu covering Pashupatinath Temple & Bauddhanath Stupa. Drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara & drop hotel.	210 KM	(6-7 Hours)\r\n* Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n17 Jan. 2024:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Full day sightseeing at Pokhara covering Bindabashini Temple, Gupteshor Cave, Deviâ€™s fall, Seti River, Fewa Lake & Peace Pagoda.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n18 Jan. 2024:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel\r\n* Drive from Pokhara to Kathmandu via Manakamana Temple darshan	(Cable Car) & drop at hotel. 210 KM (6-7 Hours)\r\n* Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\n* Dinner at hotel.\r\n* Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n19 Jan. 2024:\r\n* Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Drive from hotel to Kathmandu International Airport.','','Delhi-Kathmandu-Delhi Economy class airfare.\r\nWelcome soft drink.\r\nAirport pickup & drop with a/c Toyota Hiace.\r\n02 nightâ€™s accommodation at respective hotel in Kathmandu with MAP Plan.\r\n02 nightâ€™s accommodation at respective hotel in Pokhara	with MAP Plan.\r\nKathmandu two half day sightseeing.\r\nPokhara one full day sightseeing.','Monuments and museum entrance fees for above sightseeing places.\r\nManakamana Cable Car Ticket:	INR. 700 Per Person\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions.\r\nTCS','The airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability. ','2024-01-15','2024-01-19',1,0,0,'2023-10-10 18:26:11','2023-10-10 18:34:25'),(468,947,419,3,0,0,42600,15800,'Srinagar Package','Day 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc.  Overnight in deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO PAHALGAM\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains.Drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.','','Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi economy class airfare\r\n4 nights accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n01 Shikara Ride.\r\nSightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nAll Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nAll present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nAny future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\n1 Non Ac Sedan (PVT)\r\n','Any Medical/rescue evacuation due to mishaps.\r\nAny personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nMineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 Entrance Free\r\nRoom Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\nGST Not included \r\nHorse Riding\r\nSightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\nGondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\nAny other things that is not included in the Package','Airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability. ','2023-11-11','2023-11-15',1,0,0,'2023-10-11 15:18:06','2023-10-11 15:28:53'),(469,948,15518,2,0,0,73000,16000,'Kerala Package','\r\nDay 1 (18 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nArrival at Trivandrum Airport /Railway Station and  transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel.  Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Travancore Heritage (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (19 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Travancore Heritage\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier Museum. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Travancore Heritage (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (20 Nov 2023 - Monday) Kovalam to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Travancore Heritage\r\nTransfers - Kovalam to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel  HouseBoat (Option 1) (Meal Plan - APAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (21 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -  HouseBoat\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level. On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Cloud Castle Resort & Spa,Munnar (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (22 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Cloud Castle Resort & Spa,Munnar\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Cloud Castle Resort & Spa,Munnar (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (23 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Cloud Castle Resort & Spa,Munnar\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport / Railway Station for departure\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Accommodation for 5 nights\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges\r\n  Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n  Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','The rooms are subject to availability.','2023-11-18','2023-11-23',0,0,0,'2023-10-12 20:08:14','2023-10-12 20:08:14'),(470,949,15518,2,0,0,53200,12000,'Kerala Package','\r\nDay 1 (18 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Trivandrum - Kovalam Arrival\r\nArrival at Trivandrum Airport /Railway Station and  transfer to Kovalam. Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Travancore Heritage (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (19 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Kovalam â€“ Alleppey (House boat)\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Travancore Heritage\r\nTransfers - Kovalam to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel  HouseBoat (Option 1) (Meal Plan - APAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (20 Nov 2023 - Monday) Alleppey Day 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - /Relax HouseBoat\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Alleppey Day 02\r\nAfter Breakfast Proceed to Sight seeing in Alleppey. Overnight stay at Alleppey.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n| Relax HouseBoat (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (21 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Relax HouseBoat\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level.On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (22 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (23 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport / Railway Station for departure\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Accommodation for 2 nights\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges\r\n  Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n  Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','The rooms are subject to availability.','2023-11-18','2023-11-23',0,0,0,'2023-10-13 18:01:24','2023-10-13 18:11:41'),(471,950,50,2,0,0,78650,25050,'Vietnam Package','Day 1 â€“ 26 Oct : Good morning HCM City Vietnam\r\nChao Ban!	\r\nWelcome to HCM City, we\r\nmeet you at the airport and take you to\r\nyour hotel for check-in. Today free at\r\nyour leisure to rest or explore,\r\ndiscovering your own first impressions	of\r\nVietnam. Overnight in HCMC.\r\n*Early check in will be booked upon\r\nyour request with surcharge\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide pick up, hotel	, breakfast\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 27 Oct	: HCM free day (B)\r\nToday you are free at your leisure to discover city on your own. Overnight in HCMC.\r\nInclusion : hotel , breakfast\r\n\r\nDay 3- 28 Oct	: Cu chi tunnels - Ho Chi Minh city tour full day	(B)\r\nGet started at 8:30 AM from your hotel venturing out to the Cu Chi countryside.\r\nSee what life was like for the guerrilla warriors who lived and fought underground during the war. Crawlâ€‹ through 50 m of the 200 km tunnel system below. This morning you also pay a visit to a rice paper workshop. In the afternoon see the real HCM City through the eyes of a local. Visit the bustling Cho Lon market and a hidden Chinese pagoda, the Notre Dame Cathedral, the historic\r\nCentral Post Office, and City Hall. We drop you off at your hotel around 5:30 PM. Overnight in HCMC Inclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 -29 Oct	: HCM City â€“ Mekong (My Tho) â€“ HCM City	(B)\r\nAfter breakfast	at hotel, we are leaving the hustle and bustle of Ho Chi Minh City and start your trip to depart for My Tho, the town lies on the left side of the Mekong River. On arrival at My Tho, after visiting VinhTrang pagoda. Boarding the sampan and cruising down the river around	the four beautiful islands known as Dragon, Unicorn,Phoenix and Tortoise islands. Stop	over\r\nat Unicorn Island, go walking around country lane and seeing orchards, enjoy tropical fruits, folk song music which performed by the local people. Visit the fruit plantation. Have	lunch on your own (No Indian restaurant in Mekong Delta area) Riding a hand-rowed sampan through	Thoi Son canal and treat yourself in the beauty	of the countryside, visit the family business, visit\r\nhoney-bee farm, enjoy honey tea and coconut candy workshop.. Break time.\r\nIn the afternoon, time for cycling around the village, meet the local villagers\r\nto experience the local daily life in the	Mekong delta tour. Hammock relaxing\r\nand enjoy cool breeze for those canâ€™t join the cycling trip.\r\nArrive at Ho chi minh city around 6:00 PM. Overnight in Ho chi minh city.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat and breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 -30 Oct: HCMC â€“ Vung Tau day trip (SIC) (B,L)â€‹\r\n06:00 am, pick you up from hotel depart for Vung Tau. Breakfast en route.\r\n9:00 am , on arrival Vung Tau and leisure time at Thuy Van beach (Back beach) - one\r\nof the nicest beaches in Vietnam with the shore runs for almost 10km, full with fine\r\nsands and white waves. Vietnamese buffet will be served for lunch.\r\nIn the afternoon, visit the Jesus Christ Statue, Thang Tam Temple (Whale Temple),\r\nBach Dinh (a.k.a. Villa Blanche in French or White Palace in English),	Cape Nghinh\r\nPhong. Taking a short break. Back to Ho Chi Minh City around 18:00pm. End trip.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, lunch, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6- 31 Oct	: HCM City departure	(B)\r\nFree for shopping until late afternoon we head back to Tan Son Nhat airport around for\r\nyour evening flight back home. Goodbye and hope to see you again soon!\r\nInclusion: Transfer drop off, hotel','','Delhi-Ho Chi Minh-Delhi economy class airfare\r\n5 nights accommodation with breakfast\r\nMeals as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nPrivate Air-Conditioned vehicle with driver\r\nSIC Tours as mentioned\r\nBottled water (500ml/per person/per day)\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n','Any type of personal expenses.\r\nEarly Check-in/Check-out if not mentioned in Inclusions\r\nSurcharge applicable for peak season\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\nTCS (20%)','','2023-10-26','2023-10-31',1,0,0,'2023-10-18 14:28:31','2023-10-18 16:42:28'),(472,952,15494,8,0,0,10000,3000,'Goa Diaries','Day wise Itinerary â€“\r\n\r\n21 Dec -Arrival transfers \r\n22 Dec -South Goa sightseeing\r\n23 Dec -North Goa sightseeing\r\n24 Dec -Departure Transfers','','* 3 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* transfers','','','2023-12-21','2023-12-24',1,0,0,'2023-10-22 13:23:09','2023-10-25 12:05:33'),(473,959,15494,4,0,0,10000,4000,'Goa Diaries','Day wise Itinerary â€“\r\n\r\n31 Dec -Arrival transfers\r\n1 Dec -South Goa sightseeing\r\n2 Dec -North Goa sightseeing\r\n3 Dec -\r\n4 Dec -Departure Transfers','','* 4 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* transfers','','','2023-12-31','2024-01-04',1,0,0,'2023-10-27 13:42:58','2023-10-27 13:42:58'),(474,960,17498,2,1,0,77400,15000,'Ahmedabad','\r\n\r\n1st Day (24 Dec)\r\n\r\nAhmedabad to Dwarka - Arrival & Transfer via Jamnagar & Sightseeing\r\n\r\n2nd Day (25 Dec)\r\n\r\nDwarka - Sightseeing\r\n\r\n3rd Day (26 Dec)\r\n\r\nDwarka to Somnath - Trasfer via Porbandar & Sightseeing\r\n\r\n4th Day (27 Dec)\r\n\r\nSomnath to Diu - Transfer & Sightseeing\r\n\r\n5th Day (28 Dec)\r\n\r\nDiu to Gir - Transfer & Sightseeing\r\n\r\n6th Day (29 Dec)\r\n\r\nGir to Ahmedabad - Transfer & En-route Sightseeing & Departure\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDaywise Itinerary\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n1st Day (Sun 24th December) : Ahmedabad to Dwarka - Arrival & Transfer via Jamnagar & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 480 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 9 hours 20 minutes\r\n\r\nArrival Ahmedabad Airport/Railway Station. then proceed to Dwarka, En-route visit â€“ Lakhota Lake & Bala Hanuman, Then Drive to Dwarka, Evening reach at Dwarka, check in, then evening visit Dwarkadhish Temple. Evening Visit Market for shopping, overnight stay at the Hotel.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day (Mon 25th December) : Dwarka - Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hours 30 minutes\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, starting you day at Devbhoomi by travelling to Bet Dwarika a journey by road and crossing the sea you reach at the beautiful place of lord Krishna. You also wonâ€™t miss out from the places like Nageshwar Mahadev Temple, Krishna everywhere in your environment. Later Return back to hotel and overnight stay at Dwarka.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day (Tue 26th December) : Dwarka to Somnath - Trasfer via Porbandar & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 250 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours\r\n\r\nToday after breakfast drive to Somnath, En-route visit Porbandar â€“ Kirti Mandir & Sudama Temple, then drive Somnath Check in to hotel, and then visit Bhalka Tirth Temple, Attend Evening Aarti at Somnath Jyotirling (one of the first among the twelve Jyotirlings shrines of Shiva) Evening visit Light & Sound Show at Somnath Temple, Overnight stay at Hotel\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n4th Day (Wed 27th December) : Somnath to Diu - Transfer & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hours\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Diu, Visit Diu Fort, Diu Museum, visit St Paul Church, Enjoy Beach & Beach activity at Nagoa Beach Overnight at Diu\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day (Thu 28th December) : Diu to Gir - Transfer & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 80 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour 40 minutes\r\n\r\nToday after breakfast, Drive to Sasan Gir, check into Hotel then enjoy the Gir National Park to visit Asiatic Lion, Gir Jungle Trail (Jeep Safari) or Devaliya Safari (Bus Safari). Guest have book Online Permit on www.girlion.in. Dinner & Overnight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6th Day (Fri 29th December) : Gir to Ahmedabad - Transfer & En-route Sightseeing & Departure\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 400 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours 20 minutes\r\n\r\nToday after Breakfast, proceed to Ahmedabad. En-route visit Jalaram Temple at Virpur and Swaminarayan temple, Navlakha Palace and Vintage Car museum at Gondal. Then drive to Ahmedabad, Drop at Ahmedabad\r\n\r\n','','Delhi-Ahmedabad-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotels\r\nDaily breakfasts\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing by a Sedan Car\r\nTaxes.','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions. \r\n','Airfare is dynamic','2023-12-24','2023-12-29',1,0,0,'2023-10-30 16:22:52','2023-10-30 16:22:52'),(475,963,15518,2,0,0,30000,6500,'Kerala Package','\r\nDay\r\n1	(18 Nov 2023 - Saturday) Trivandrum Arrival to Ashtamudi via Varkala\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Trivandrum Arrival to Ashtamudi via Varkala\r\nOn arrival at the Trivandrum airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to Ashtamudi. On the way visit Varkala,one of the famous beach destination. Varkala is the only place in southern Kerala where cliffs are found adjacent to Arabian sea. Varkala is famous for the 2000 year old Janardana Swami Temple a Hindu pilgrimage site dedicated to Vishnu, Ayurveda treatment centers and off course for Varkala Beach. Farther inland, the Sivagiri Mutt monument memorializes the social reformer Sree Narayana Guru, who is buried here. Varkala beach is god place for sun bathing and swimming, the evening views of the sunset are worth lingering over. visit local markets. After Varkala sight seeing proceed to Ashtamudi.Overnight at the Resort/hotel.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n2	(19 Nov 2023 - Sunday) Ashtamudi Day 02\r\n\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ashtamudi Day 02\r\nAfter Breakfast explore Ashtamudi  the well known for its houseboat and backwater resorts. Ashtamudi Wetland was included in the list of wetlands of international importance, as defined by the Ramsar Convention for the conservation and sustainable utilization of wetlands.Along both banks of the lake and its backwater canals, coconut groves and palm trees interspersed with towns and villages are seen. Visit Kollam beach,Adventure park etc.After sightseeing come back to the resort and relax. over night at Hotel.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n3	(20 Nov 2023 - Monday) Ashtamudi to Arookutty  (Transfer)\r\n\r\nTransfers - Ashtamudi to Arookutty (Transfer)\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Ashtamudi. On the way visit Kumarakom. Kumarakom is home to a wide variety of flora and fauna. where many species of migratory birds visit. Located on the banks of the Vembanad Lake, the Kumarakom Bird Sanctuary, an ornithologist\'s paradise, is a favorite haunt of migratory birds. Visit Kumarakom Birds Sanctuary. Check in to hotel. Overnight stay at Kumarakom.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n4	(21 Nov 2023 - Tuesday) Arookutty to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -\r\nTransfers - Arookutty to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level.On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n5	(22 Nov 2023 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n6	(23 Nov 2023 - Thursday) Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel -\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Munnar - Cochin Departure Transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport / Railway Station for departure','',' All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges','The rooms are subject to availability.','2023-11-18','2023-11-23',0,0,0,'2023-11-06 19:06:11','2023-11-06 19:13:03'),(476,964,17498,2,1,0,72500,18000,'Ahmedabad','Day - 1 Arrival at Vadodara. Local Vadodara sightseeing. Night stay at Vadodara.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay - 2 Check out and leave for Sasan Gir. Enjoy at sasan . Night stay at sasan\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay - 3 Early morning safari ( to be booked by guest).\r\n\r\nCheck out and leave for somnath. Night stay at Somnath.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay - 4 Check out and leave for Dwarka. On way visit Porbandar. Night stay at Dwarka.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay - 5 Nageshwar Jyortirlinga, Shivrajpur Beach, Dwarkadhish Temple, Bet Dwarka.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nDay - 6 Check out and drop off at Ahmedabad by evening 6pm.','','Delhi-Vadodara and Ahmedabad-Delhi Economy Class Airfare\r\n5 nights stay in the mentioned hotels\r\nDaily breakfasts\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing by a Sedan Car\r\nTaxes.','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions. \r\nSafari Cost\r\n','Airfare is dynamic','2023-12-25','2023-12-30',1,0,0,'2023-11-07 14:06:35','2023-11-07 14:23:04'),(477,965,349,2,0,0,64100,12000,'Dubai Package','Day-wise itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival Transfer followed by check-in\r\n       BURJ KHALIFA 124TH FLOOR NORMAL TICKET ON SIC \r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2: Abu Dhabi & Ferrari World\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3: Dubai Aquarium and Underwater Zoo\r\n       Marina Cruise Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 4: Miracle Garden and Global Village\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5: Dubai Frame \r\n       Desert Safari with BBQ dinner\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6: Check out and departure transfer','','Delhi-Dubai-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n5 night accommodation in a 4 star hotel \r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nReturn Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\nAll tours and sightseeing on SIC\r\nTours and sightseeing as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges\r\n\r\n','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\nTCS (20%)','Airfare is dynamic. \r\nThe rooms are subject to availability. ','2024-01-04','2024-01-09',1,0,0,'2023-11-09 00:56:48','2023-11-14 12:59:03'),(478,969,1105,2,2,0,119510,25490,'Rajasthan Diaries','2N Udaipur - 1N Jodhpur - 1N Jaisalmer - 1N Sam Sand Dunes Jaisalmar\r\n\r\n\r\nDay-wise Itinerary\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n1st Day (Fri 29th December) : Udaipur - Arrival and Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km\r\n\r\nUpon arrival, meet our representative and take a transfer to the hotel,Complete your check-in process. Get Relaxed,You can partake in the boat ride on the tranquil waters of Lake Pichola / Fateh Sagar Lake,(Ticket not included) Head back to the hotel for the night,Dinner & Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day (Sat 30th December) : Udaipur - Sightseeing\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 50 Km\r\n\r\nBegin your day with breakfast at the hotel and then start your city tour,Visit the City Palace which is the biggest castle complex in Rajasthan,Partake in the boat ride on the tranquil waters of Lake Pichola,Also visit Sahelion ki Bari or Garden of the Maids of Honor, Jagdish sanctuary,Local Market Visit,Later in the evening Fateh Sagar Lake, Shilpgram,Once sightseeing is over, head back to the hotel,Dinner & Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sun 31st December) : Udaipur to Jodhpur - City Sightseeing and Transfer\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 350 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Hotel Head out for City sight seeing then Drive to Jodhpur,Jodhpur is a beautiful city that displays the rich crafts and culture of Rajasthan,Overnight stay at Jodhpur Hotel.\r\n\r\n\r\n4th Day (Mon 1st January) : Jodhpur to Jaisalmer - Transfer and Sightseeing with Evening at Gadisar Lake\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 350 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the hotel and Drive to Jaisalmer,Arrival, Check-In to the Hotel,Popularly known as the â€˜heartâ€™ of Thar Desert, Jaisalmer is a medieval town with marvellous structures,Evening is free for leisure,You can spend it as per your own liking on your own.ORAfter Freshen Up in the evening visit Gadisar Lake,Dinner &Overnight stay at Jaisalmer Hotel.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day (Tue 2nd January) : Jaisalmer to Sam Sand Dunes - Sightseeing and Evening at Sand Dunes\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 45 Km\r\n\r\nAfter Breakfast at the Hotel, Check out from the Hotel, Take a transfer to the Sam Sand Dunes â€“ 45 km away, Arrival & check into tents, Sam Dunes is known for its sand rises and is the scene for the Desert celebration, Get the genuine feel of the desert by getting a charge out of a camel ride on the sand rises and witness a brilliant nightfall, After enjoying the rides, enjoy the cultural programme, Dinner & Overnight stay in Tents.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6th Day (Wed 3rd January) : Sam Sand Dunes to Jaisalmer - Departure\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 45 Km\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast & check out process, you will be heading back to your home with beautiful memories.','','Delhi-Udaipur and Jaisalmer-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\n5  nights accommodation in 4 star hotels\r\nMeals as mentioned above\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing by 1 AC Sedan\r\nCamel ride and Cultural evening at Sam Sand dunes\r\nParking Toll Tax and Driver Bata\r\n\r\n','All personal expenses, optional tours and extra meal\r\nAny monument or sight-seeing Entry fee / Charges\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n','Child above 11 years to consider as an adult\r\nAirfare is dynamic\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2023-12-29','2024-01-03',1,0,0,'2023-11-22 14:58:52','2023-11-22 15:21:22'),(479,970,2326,2,0,0,13000,3000,'Shimla Package','Day 1 : Shimla pick up and transfer to hotel! After proceed for Mall Road, Christ church, gaiety theatre, scandal point, ridge \r\n\r\nDAY 2: SHIMLA LOCAL : Advance Study Sankat Mochan Temple in (1885),Jakhu Temple, Tara Devi temple, at SHIMLA. \r\n\r\nDay 3: SHIMLA KUFRI TOUR:- After Breakfast Excursion to Kufri. Kufri is famous for its Himalayan National Park, Poney and Yak Ride (Extra cost) and One can see the endless Himalayan Panorama from Kufri, Shimla \r\n\r\nDay 4: Shimla volvo stand drop!','','3 nights stay in the mentioned hotel\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nAll transfers and sightseeing by a Sedan Car\r\nAll taxes and parking charges','Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions','','2023-12-01','2023-12-04',1,0,0,'2023-11-23 15:56:08','2023-11-23 15:56:08'),(480,971,419,2,0,0,21000,5617,'Srinagar Package','Day 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\n\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the hotel/deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in hotel / deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : DAY TRIP TO PAHALGAM\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains.Drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel / deluxe houseboat.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\n\r\nMorning sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities In evening Srinagar airport for onward flight..','','Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Economy Class Airfare\r\nMeal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n01 Shikara Ride.\r\nSightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nAll Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nAll present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nAny future taxes levies will be charged extra.','Any Medical/rescue evacuation due to mishaps.\r\nAny personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nMineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 Entrance Free\r\nRoom Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\nGST Not included \r\nHorse Riding\r\nSightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\nGondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\nAny other things that is not included in the Package','','2023-12-09','2023-12-11',1,0,0,'2023-11-24 13:30:44','2023-11-28 18:15:38'),(481,972,419,4,0,0,68000,18500,'Srinagar Package','Day 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in  deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY IN PAHALGAM\r\nEnjoy Full day in Pahalgam. Enjoy ABC Valley at your own cost , Dinner overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.','','Delhi-Srinagar-Delhi Economy Class airfare\r\nMeal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n01 Shikara Ride.\r\nSightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nAll Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nAll present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nAny future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nNon Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA\r\n','Any Medical/rescue evacuation due to mishaps.\r\nAny personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nMineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 Entrance Free\r\nRoom Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\nGST Not included \r\nHorse Riding\r\nSightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\nGondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\nAny other things that is not included in the Package','','2023-12-09','2023-12-14',1,0,0,'2023-11-25 11:29:12','2023-11-25 15:55:36'),(482,974,302,7,2,0,143700,15000,'Kerala Package','\r\nDay\r\n1\r\n\r\n(02 Jan 2024 - Tuesday) Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Kochi (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n2\r\n\r\n(03 Jan 2024 - Wednesday) Cochin to Munnar\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum.  Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Trivers Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n3\r\n\r\n(04 Jan 2024 - Thursday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Trivers Resort\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Trivers Resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n4\r\n\r\n(05 Jan 2024 - Friday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Trivers Resort\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Peppervine Hotel (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n5\r\n\r\n(06 Jan 2024 - Saturday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Peppervine Hotel\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Relax HouseBoat (Option 1) (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\nDay\r\n6\r\n\r\n(07 Jan 2024 - Sunday) Alleppey -Cochin departure transfer\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Relax HouseBoat\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Alleppey -Cochin departure transfer\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and Transferred to Cochin Airport / Railway station for the for the departure.','','Delhi-Kochi-Delhi Economy class airfare\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAccommodation on Twin Sharing Basis\r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\nAbove Rate is Inclusive of GST 5%','All those which are not mentioned above\r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\nAll Items of personal use\r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\nAny Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\nAny Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n