\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n05-Jan (FRI): 1430 - 1500 Hrs\r\n\r\nTrio Desert safari with BBQ dinner on sharing basis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n06-Jan (SAT): 1430 - 1500 Hrs\r\n\r\nMiracle garden + Global village combo entry tickets & transfers on sharing basis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n07-Jan (SUN): 0830 - 0900 Hrs\r\n\r\nAbu Dhabi City Tour (with a break at Yas Mall) on sharing basis\r\n\r\n\r\n08-Jan (MON): Based On Flight Details\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer From Bur Dubai Hotel To Dubai International Airport On Private Basis','','Kolkata-Delhi-Kolkata Economy Class airfare\r\nAccommodation in above mentioned hotel with daily breakfast\r\nTransfers and sightseeing as mentioned above\r\nVisa and Travel Insurance charges are included\r\n','Tips / Gratitude\r\nAny expense of Personal nature\r\nAny meals / transfers / excursions not mentioned in the inclusion','The airfare is dynamic\r\nThe rooms are subject to availability','2024-01-03','2024-01-08',1,0,0,'2023-12-27 20:52:55','2023-12-27 21:13:30'),(499,999,16002,2,0,0,56100,16000,'Glimpse of Bali','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival & transfer to hotel with private transfers\r\nArrive in Bali and transfer to your hotel with private transportation. This is likely a day for rest and settling in.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Water Sports Activity + Uluwatu Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Engage in water sports activities such as Jet Ski, Banana Boat, and Single Parasailing (subject to availability).\r\n* Visit Uluwatu Temple with private transfers. This temple is known for its stunning location on a cliff overlooking the Indian Ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 3: 02 Hrs Bali Spa @ Grand Inna Kuta + Tanah Lot Temple with private transfers\r\n\r\n* Enjoy a 2-hour spa session at Grand Inna Kuta for relaxation.\r\n* Visit Tanah Lot Temple, a beautiful sea temple located on a rock formation in the ocean.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Ubud & Kintamani + Bali Swing Pioneer with private transfers + Interhotel\r\n\r\n* Explore Ubud and Kintamani, known for their cultural and scenic attractions.\r\n* Experience the Bali Swing Pioneer.\r\n* Transfer to another hotel (Interhotel).\r\n\r\nDay 5: Leisure\r\nThis day seems to be free for leisure, allowing for flexibility in your plans. You can explore more on your own or relax at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure with private transfers\r\nDepart from Bali with private transportation to the airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nEnjoy your trip to Bali!','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* 05 Nights Accommodation as per above with breakfast basis\r\n* Return airport transfers on pvt basis\r\n* All tours and sightseeings in pvt basis\r\n* Travel Insurance.\r\n','* TCS','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-21','2024-01-26',1,0,0,'2023-12-30 12:36:02','2023-12-30 13:01:36'),(500,1002,419,3,1,0,74000,15000,'Srinagar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in hotel \r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY IN PAHALGAM\r\nEnjoy Full day in Pahalgam. Dinner overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar.. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride.\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\n* Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\n* Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA','* Room Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\n* Horse Riding\r\n* Sightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n* Any other things that is not included in the Package','Airfare is Dynamic','2024-01-26','2024-01-30',1,0,0,'2024-01-03 18:12:00','2024-01-04 17:48:39'),(501,1004,204,3,1,0,616700,60000,'United States of America','','','Accommodation on quad sharing basis as per mentioned above or similar\r\nBig Bus Panoramic night tour of Vegas â€“ 20th May\r\nGrand Canyon West Rim Helicopter tour with sky walk on shared basis â€“ 21st May\r\nLos Angeles city tour on seat in coach basis â€“ 23rd May \r\n1Day Disneyland Resort ticket with return transfers on private basis â€“ 24th May \r\nOne way transfer from Las Vegas Airport to Las Vegas Hotel on private basis â€“ 20th May \r\nOne way coach ticket from Las Vegas to Los Angeles â€“ 22nd May \r\nOne way transfer from Los Angeles Hotel to Los Angeles Airport on private basis â€“ 25th May \r\n','* Visaâ€™s and Taxes.\r\n* Resort Fee / City Tax / Utility Charges wherever applicable must be paid directly\r\n* Any Meals like Lunch / Dinner unless specified in inclusions\r\n* Bottled Water on coaches and in hotel rooms\r\n* Tips to drivers and Gratuities as expected by Bell Staff, Tour Coach Drivers, Guides etc \r\n* Telephone calls, Laundry, and other expenses\r\n* Travel Insurance - recommended.  We request Tour Operator to secure a signed Waiver in the event client declines your offer to sell Travel Insurance\r\n* Any items not mentioned in Package inclusions column  ','Rooms are subject to availability\r\nHotel / Coach Station / Hotel transfers to be managed on own.','2024-05-20','2024-05-25',1,0,0,'2024-01-04 16:16:37','2024-01-04 21:45:38'),(502,1005,419,3,1,0,76000,15000,'Srinagar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR TRASFER TO PAHALGAM\r\nArrive Srinagar proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in deluxe houseboat .\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.','','* Economy Class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride.\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\n* Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\n* Non Ac SUV ','* Room Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\n* Horse Riding\r\n* Sightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n* Any other things that is not included in the Package','Airfare is Dynamic','2024-03-26','2024-03-30',1,0,0,'2024-01-05 13:30:42','2024-01-05 14:35:05'),(504,1011,15498,3,0,0,52300,16400,'Malaysia Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (5 Mar)\r\nTRANSFER: EX KLIA - KL Hotel        ( 1-PRIVATE CAR (KL) )\r\n KUALA LUMPUR - Half Day KL City Tour + KL Tower - SIC\r\nKL Tower Ticket - Obersevation Deck Ticket Only\r\n\r\n2nd Day (6 Mar) \r\nKUALA LUMPUR - Genting Highland Tour (Enroute Batu Caves )- SIC\r\nGenting Attractions - Two ways Cable Car Ticket Only\r\n\r\n3rd Day (7 Mar) \r\nTRANSFER: LGK Airport - Beach & City Hotels         1-PRIVATE CAR (LGK) \r\nTRANSFERS : EX KL HOTEL - KLIA   1-PRIVATE CAR (KL) \r\n\r\n4th Day (8 Mar) \r\nTOURS - EX LANGKAWI - Half Day Langkawi island Tour  ( 1-PRIVATE 10 SEATER (LGK))\r\nLangkawi Underwater World Ticket  (Undewater World Ticket Only )\r\n\r\n5th Day (9 Mar) \r\nTRANSFER: Beach & City Hotels Langkawi - LGK Airport   (1-PRIVATE 10 SEATER (LGK) )','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Daily Breakfast.\r\n* Undewater World Ticket.\r\n* Two ways Cable Car Ticket.\r\n* Obersevation Deck Ticket.\r\n* All hotels and airport transfers in Pvt basis.\r\n* All tours and sightseeing in Sic basis.','','Airfare is dynamic in nature.','2024-03-05','2024-03-09',1,0,0,'2024-01-10 13:14:26','2024-01-10 15:00:20'),(506,1015,419,22,0,0,154000,28000,'Srinagar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the hotel/deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in hotel / deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : DAY TRIP TO PAHALGAM\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains.Drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel / deluxe houseboat.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride.\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\n* Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.','','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-26','2024-01-28',1,0,0,'2024-01-19 18:26:08','2024-01-19 18:26:08'),(507,1017,419,22,0,0,682350,75000,'Srinagar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR TRASVER TO PAHALGAM\r\nArrive srinagar proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel / houseboat.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.','','* Economy class airfare.\r\n* Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\n* 01 Shikara Ride(PVT).\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* 2 NON A/C TEMPO TRAVELLER (PVT)\r\n* All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\n* All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\n* Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.','','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-01-26','2024-01-29',1,0,0,'2024-01-20 14:39:27','2024-01-20 16:27:39'),(508,1019,6,2,0,0,12000,5000,'Delhi-Agra-Jaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n12th Feb : Delhi to Agra. Hotel Check-in and local sightseeing \r\n\r\n13th Feb: Check-out and move to Jaipur for 2 nights. Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n14th Feb: Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n15th Feb: After Check-out Jaipur to Delhi. \r\n,Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n12th Feb : Delhi to Agra. Hotel Check-in and local sightseeing \r\n\r\n13th Feb: Check-out and move to Jaipur for 2 nights. Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n14th Feb: Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n15th Feb: After Check-out Jaipur to Delhi. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sedan Car,* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sedan Car\r\n','','','2024-02-12','2024-02-15',0,0,0,'2024-01-23 16:01:16','2024-01-23 16:01:16'),(509,1020,15518,4,0,0,67900,17000,'Kerala Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nMunnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Cochin: 1 Nights \r\n\r\nDay 1 (06 Feb 2024 - Tuesday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival) \r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Munnar Queen (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2 (07 Feb 2024 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02 \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Munnar Queen\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Munnar Queen (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3 (08 Feb 2024 - Thursday) Munnar - Thekkady \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Munnar Queen\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Spices Lap Thekkady  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 4 (09 Feb 2024 - Friday) Thekkady to Alleppey \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Spices Lap Thekkady \r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Haveli Resorts (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (10 Feb 2024 - Saturday) Alleppey to Cochin \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Haveli Resorts\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Cochin\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel and Transferred to Cochin. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Kochi  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (11 Feb 2024 - Sunday) Cochin to Cochin Departure \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi\r\nDeparture Transfer - Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport / Railway Station for departure.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost ','','Airfare is Dynamic.','2024-02-06','2024-02-11',1,0,0,'2024-01-24 12:06:15','2024-01-24 15:33:21'),(510,1021,15530,4,0,0,0,0,'Andaman Iconic Nature','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (Tue 6th February) : Port Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show\r\nâ€¢ Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel / resort\r\nâ€¢ Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\nâ€¢ Please note, we will drop guests at the parking area near jail and guests must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\nâ€¢ Guests must come out after visiting jail and re-enter for the L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in their free time.\r\nâ€¢ L&S show timing is in between 1800hrs - 1900hrs subject to availability\r\nâ€¢ The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated Marina Park and the Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Wed 7th February) : Port Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\nâ€¢ Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\nâ€¢ If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\nâ€¢ Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\nâ€¢ Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\n* Do not forget to carry changing clothes and towels\r\nâ€¢ Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicles with wet clothes, please cooperate.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Thu 8th February) : Havelock - Elephenta Beach\r\nâ€¢ Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\nâ€¢ Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\nâ€¢ Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\nâ€¢ You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\nâ€¢ You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\nâ€¢ Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\nâ€¢ Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Pathar Beachâ€ OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Fri 9th February) : Havelock to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\nâ€¢ Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\nâ€¢ Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\nâ€¢ Other places like Corbynâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional - Direct payment basis)\r\n\r\n5th Day (Sat 10th February) : Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\nâ€¢ Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\nâ€¢ Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach the airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty.\r\n* Meal Plan â€“ As mentioned above. \r\n* Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\n* All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\n* Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability) ','* Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/ Vehicle for Dinner etc. ','Airfare is Dynamic','2024-02-06','2024-02-10',1,0,0,'2024-01-24 17:44:53','2024-01-24 18:03:53'),(511,1022,6,2,0,0,11500,950,'Delhi-Agra-Jaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n12th Feb : Delhi to Agra. Hotel Check-in and local sightseeing \r\n\r\n13th Feb: Check-out and move to Jaipur for 2 nights. Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n14th Feb: Local sightseeing \r\n\r\n15th Feb: After Check-out Jaipur to Delhi. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Sedan Car\r\n','* Any meal other than mentioned above\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n','','2024-02-12','2024-02-15',0,0,0,'2024-01-25 17:12:29','2024-02-01 17:45:57'),(512,1025,15518,4,0,0,79700,19000,'Kerala Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nMunnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Cochin: 1 Nights \r\n\r\nDay 1 (07 Feb 2024 - Tuesday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival) \r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Munnar Queen (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2 (08 Feb 2024 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02 \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Munnar Queen\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Munnar Queen (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3 (09 Feb 2024 - Thursday) Munnar - Thekkady \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Munnar Queen\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady .Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Spices Lap Thekkady  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 4 (10 Feb 2024 - Friday) Thekkady to Alleppey \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Spices Lap Thekkady \r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Haveli Resorts (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (11 Feb 2024 - Saturday) Alleppey to Cochin \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Haveli Resorts\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Cochin\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel and Transferred to Cochin. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Kochi  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (12 Feb 2024 - Sunday) Cochin to Cochin Departure \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi\r\nDeparture Transfer - Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport / Railway Station for departure.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost ','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges\r\n  Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n  Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','Airfare is Dynamic.','2024-02-07','2024-02-12',1,0,0,'2024-01-27 16:37:01','2024-01-27 17:06:57'),(513,1026,15518,4,0,0,85700,22000,'Kerala Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nMunnar: 2 Nights, Thekkady: 1 Nights, Alleppey: 1 Nights, Cochin: 1 Nights \r\n\r\nDay 1 (07 Feb 2024 - Tuesday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival) \r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Mu