nâ€¢	Marina Park and the Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Mon 18th March) : Port Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\nâ€¢	If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\nâ€¢	Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\nâ€¢	Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\nâ€¢	Do not forget to carry changing clothes and towels\r\nâ€¢	Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicles with wet clothes, please cooperate.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Tue 19th March) : Havelock - Elephenta Beach\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\nâ€¢	Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\nâ€¢	Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\nâ€¢	You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\nâ€¢	You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\nâ€¢	Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\nâ€¢	Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions OR COVID-19 reasons, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Pathar Beachâ€ OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Wed 20th March) : Havelock to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\nâ€¢	Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\nâ€¢	Other places like Corbynâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional - Direct payment basis)\r\n\r\n5th Day (Thu 21st March) : Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\n\r\nâ€¢	Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\nâ€¢	Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach the airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.','','â€¢	Economy Class airfare.\r\nâ€¢	Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty. \r\nâ€¢	Meal Plan â€“ As mentioned above. \r\nâ€¢	Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\nâ€¢	All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\nâ€¢	Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability) \r\nâ€¢	Luggage van \r\n\r\n','â€¢	The services of vehicles not on disposal basis & finishing the sightseeing tour as per the itinerary \r\nâ€¢	Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/ Vehicle for Dinner etc. \r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-03-17','2024-03-21',1,0,0,'2024-03-07 18:35:55','2024-03-08 11:01:50'),(544,1073,15530,5,0,0,100200,20000,'Andaman Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrive Port Blair - Cellular jail with Light & Sound Show\r\nArrive at Veer Savarkar Airport, Port Blair. Meet our local representative and get transferred to your pre-booked hotel. Check in & fresh up Visit Cellular jail. Famously known as \"Kala Paani\" which is a national memorial now. Also, eyewitness the enthralling light and sound show at the cellular jail where heroic saga of our great freedom fighters bought alive. Later return back to our hotel. Overnight at Port Blair\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Port Blair to Havelock Island - Visit Radha Nagar Beach.\r\nToday, get transferred to the jetty to catch your luxury tourist ferry (By Private/Govt.) to Havelock Island (57 km by sea). If ferry timings are early morning then Do not forget to ask your hotel for a Packed breakfast and put a request at previous night only. On arrival at Havelock jetty, meet our local representative and board our vehicle to visit world famous Radha Nagar beach. It truly is a mesmerizing curve of white sand with perfectly colored blue waters, all lined by lush forest and palm trees. An ideal beach for sun basking and bathing. Later return back to your hotel. Overnight at Havelock Island.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Havelock Island - Kala Pathar Beach Trip\r\nAfter breakfast, Board your vehicle as we will take you to Kala Patthar beach. This is an ideal spot for photography or picnic. One can spend time there as this beach offers some umbrellas, hammock & wooden chairs. Kalapathar beach is not ideal for swimming but it gives you a picture-perfect backdrop. Return back to the hotel. Overnight at Havelock.\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Havelock Island to Port Blair - City Tour of Port Blair\r\nAfter breakfast, this morning, check out from your hotel & return back to Havelock jetty to catch your luxury tourist ferry (By Private/Govt.) to Port Blair. Upon arrival, board your vehicle as we are taking you for a city tour of Port Blair. Your vehicle to experience the glory of this city during the city tour of Port Blair. The city tour will cover Anthropological museum, Fisheries museum . Later, return back to the hotel. Overnight at Port Blair. Note : This itinerary strictly depends upon the availability of seats.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Port Blair hotel to Airport Drop.\r\nAfter breakfast, get transferred to Veer Savarkar airport, Port Blair to catch your return flight back to home. Return home with wonderfulÂ memories.\r\n','','Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast \r\nAirport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\nFerry Tickets : Port Blair - Havelock - Port Blair\r\n','â€¢ Any kind of personal expenses or optional tours/extra meals/ Vehicle for Dinner etc. ','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-03-17','2024-03-21',1,0,0,'2024-03-07 18:45:25','2024-03-08 11:13:52'),(545,1078,15520,2,0,0,14000,5000,'Uttarakhand Diaires','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n16th March: Delhi to Almora\r\n17th March: Almora to Nainital\r\n18th March: Nainital to Delhi','','1Â SedanÂ car\r\nDaily Breakfast \r\n1 night stay in Nainital\r\n1 night Stay in Almora','','','2024-03-16','2024-03-18',0,0,0,'2024-03-09 18:22:19','2024-03-12 11:03:19'),(547,1080,419,6,0,0,120000,25000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR TRASVER TO PAHALGAM\r\nArrive Srinagar proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in deluxe houseboat .\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\n','','â€¢	Economy Class airfare.\r\nâ€¢	Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\nâ€¢	01 Shikara Ride.\r\nâ€¢	Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢	All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary\r\nâ€¢	All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢	Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢	Non AC SUV','â€¢	Any personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nâ€¢	Mineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.                                                                                                 \r\nâ€¢	Entrance Free\r\nâ€¢	Room Heating Charges in Houseboats\r\nâ€¢	Horse Riding\r\nâ€¢	Sightseeing of Chandanwadi, Aru and Baisaran in Pahalgam.\r\nâ€¢	Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\nâ€¢	Any other things that is not included in the Package\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-03-17','2024-03-21',1,0,0,'2024-03-11 13:37:50','2024-03-11 13:37:50'),(548,1083,419,6,0,0,120000,25000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR TRASVER TO PAHALGAM\r\nArrive Srinagar proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in deluxe houseboat .\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\n','','â€¢	Economy Class airfare.\r\nâ€¢	Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\nâ€¢	01 Shikara Ride.\r\nâ€¢	Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢	All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary\r\nâ€¢	All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢	Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢	Non AC SUV','â€¢	Any personal nature items like Laundry, bar bills, table bills, camera fee, tips or any other item.\r\nâ€¢	Mineral water / Soft or hard drinks / Starters.          