untryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar.. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\nTOUR DETAILS\r\n\r\nSightseeing : 18-06-2024 To 23-06-2024 Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA\r\nSightseeing : 18-06-2024 Shikara Ride (PVT)\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\nâ€¢ 01 Shikara Ride.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ 1 Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA\r\n','â€¢ Any other things that is not included in the Package\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic.','2024-06-18','2024-06-23',1,0,0,'2024-03-22 12:05:28','2024-03-22 12:24:32'),(562,1105,419,4,2,1,73400,21500,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO SRINAGAR HOTEL.\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar.. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n\r\nTOUR DETAILS\r\n\r\nSightseeing : 18-06-2024 To 23-06-2024 Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA\r\nSightseeing : 18-06-2024 Shikara Ride (PVT)\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\nâ€¢ 01 Shikara Ride.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ 1 Non Ac SUV (PVT) TAVERA\r\n','â€¢ Any other things that is not included in the Package\r\n* Gondola Ride in Gulmarg\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic.','2024-06-18','2024-06-23',1,0,0,'2024-03-22 16:19:36','2024-03-22 16:58:15'),(563,1106,17386,3,0,0,640000,80000,'Kenya Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\n26th June: One transfer from Mombasa Airport to a local residence in Mombasa\r\n\r\n30th June: 2nd transfer from the local residence to Mombasa Train Station.On arrival transfer to hotel in Nairobi for overnight stay.(BB)\r\n\r\n01 July :-Breakfast,drive to Naivasha 2-3 hrs .Arrive in time for lunch.Have a good lunch in NAivasha and boating drive back to NAirobi small city tour.Stop somewhere for dinner and then drop off to same hotel in Nairobi for overnight..(FB)\r\n\r\n02 July :-Breakfast and leave for the Masai Mara game reserve, approx. 4-5 hrs. drive. Arrive in time of lunch, afternoon game drive, dinner and overnight at the camp. (FB)\r\n\r\n03 and 04  July : After breakfast, head out for a full day game drive at the Masai Mara reserve, dinner and overnight at the camp. ( FB)\r\n\r\n05 July :- Breakfast,drive to Nairobi 4-5 hrs.On arrival transfer to Airport for outbound flight.(B)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Accommodation as stipulated in the itinerary or similar.\r\nâ€¢ Private transportation in  4x4 Safari Land cruisers with pop-up roof for easy game viewing & photography\r\nâ€¢ Game drives as indicated in the itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Services of experienced English-speaking driver-guides.\r\nâ€¢ All Government taxes, parks entrance fees (Subject to change) and levies as per itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Bottled drinking water while on safari \r\n* Also includes Transfers as indicated in Itinerary\r\n* Train tickets from Mombasa to NAirobi First class\r\n\r\n','â€¢ Activities not mentioned above\r\n* Any meal which is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n* Any type of personal expenses\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-26','2024-07-05',0,0,0,'2024-03-27 16:44:21','2024-03-28 15:18:05'),(564,1107,7060,7,1,0,541500,45000,'Greece Diaries','','','â€¢ Athens Airport to hotel private transfer\r\nâ€¢ Athens hotel to Ferry port private transfer\r\nâ€¢ Athens to Mykonos Ferry ticket (Economy Class)\r\nâ€¢ Mykonos Ferry port to hotel private transfer\r\nâ€¢ Mykonos old town walking tour\r\nâ€¢ Mykonos to Santorini Ferry ticket (Economy Class)\r\nâ€¢ Mykonos hotel to Ferry port private transfer\r\nâ€¢ Santorini Bus tour with Sunset in Oia - Full day\r\nâ€¢ Santorini hotel to airport Pvt Transfer\r\nâ€¢ Istanbul Airport to hotel transfer Pvt\r\nâ€¢ Full Day Istanbul Tour with Topkapi Palace, Hagia Sophia Mosque, Blue Mosque, Hippodrome, Obelisk, Sultanahmet, Old Bazaar. Lunch atLocal Restaurant.\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Istanbul hotel to Keysari Airport Pvt\r\nâ€¢ Keysari Airport to hotel pvt transfer\r\nâ€¢ Full Day Cappadocia Red Tour with Zelve Open Air Museum, Dervent Valley, Pasabag, Avanos. Lunch at local Restaurant.\r\nâ€¢ Transfer to Kayseri Airport for flight to Istanbul to catch homebound flight.\r\nâ€¢ All transfers on Pvt basis & tours on SIC basis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any expense of personal nature\r\n* Any type of tip, tour guide charges. \r\n* TCS','Price is subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nQuote is valid for 5 Days ','2024-05-21','2024-06-03',0,0,0,'2024-03-27 17:37:30','2024-03-27 17:53:16'),(565,1111,2690,2,1,0,26550,7000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:-\r\n\r\n1st Day (01 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage)\r\n \r\n2nd Day (02 Jul)	\r\n        SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (03 Jul)\r\n	SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC \r\n. \r\n4th Day (04 Jul)\r\n	TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n	Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	Phuket Tiger Kingdom Smallest Tiger \r\n\r\n5th Day (05 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) \r\n* TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT \r\n* SIC TOURS - PHUKET  Phuket Half Day City Tour\r\n* SIC TOURS - PHUKET  Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch\r\n* TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom \r\n* Insurance',',* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS',',Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n','2024-07-01','2024-07-05',0,0,0,'2024-04-01 17:17:06','2024-04-02 11:06:08'),(566,1113,557,27,0,0,572500,115000,'Sri Lanka Diaries','\r\nDay 01 : Arrival - Colombo	\r\nOn arrival you will be welcomed by our representative and transfer to Colombo. Check into the hotel & leisure. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Colombo City Tour	\r\nBreakfast at the hotel & go for a Colombo city tour. Visit Colombo national museum, Gangaramaya temple, Lotus tower, Independence squre & Galleface green. On completion go for a guided shopping tour in Colombo. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Colombo Leisure\r\nAfter having breakfast lesiure at the hotel. Visit Dehiwala Zoological garden. On completion evening visit for a shopping tour. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Colombo - Airport\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. If time permits leisure at the hotel till checkout time. Transfer to airport to catch the departure flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3 night stay in above mentioned hotel\r\n* Daily Breakfast & Dinner\r\n* Vehicle - Toyota 37 Seaters Coaster\r\n* Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa will be on arrival charges USD 25 per person\r\n* TCS  \r\n\r\n\r\n','* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability\r\n+ Bentota Day Excursion - It can be included on request. Separate charges will be applied on this','2024-10-17','2024-10-20',0,0,0,'2024-04-03 15:55:44','2024-04-03 20:42:29');
INSERT INTO `udn_pkg_manual_quotation` VALUES (567,1114,15530,4,0,0,0,0,'Andaman Diaries','Day-wise Vehicle, Ferry & Sightseeing :-\r\n\r\n1st Day (17 Apr) :\r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show 	(1-Sedan / SUV) \r\nCellular Jail - Light & Sound Show 	Tickets \r\n\r\n2nd Day (18 Apr) : \r\nPort Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach 	(1-Sedan / SUV) \r\nPort Blair To Havelock 	(Private Catamaran Ferry : Premium) \r\n\r\n3rd Day (19 Apr) :  \r\nHavelock - Elephenta Beach 	(1-Sedan / SUV) \r\nElephanta 	(Boat Charge  4A.) \r\n \r\n4th Day (20 Apr) : \r\nHavelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge 	(1-Sedan / SUV )\r\nHavelock To Neil Island 	(Private Catamaran Ferry : Premium) \r\n \r\n5th Day (21 Apr) :	\r\nNeil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure   (1-Sedan / SUV) \r\nNeil Island To Port Blair 	(Private Catamaran Ferry : Premium) \r\n\r\n6th Day (22 Apr)	\r\nPort Blair Departure - Tour Ends 	1-Sedan / SUV \r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\n1st Day (Wed 17th April) : \r\nPort Blair Arrival - Cellular Jail â€“ Light & Sound Show\r\nâ€¢ Arrival, Meet-Greet with our airport representative and Transfer to your booked hotel / resort\r\nâ€¢ Evening, visit to historic Cellular Jail followed by Light & Sound Show\r\nâ€¢ Please note, we will drop guests at the parking area near jail and guests must walk around 200 metre and return after completion of L&S show.\r\nâ€¢ Guests must come out after visiting jail and re-enter for the L&S show, Guests can walk around the bay side in their free time.\r\nâ€¢ L&S show timing is in between 1800hrs - 1900hrs subject to availability\r\nâ€¢ The free time between jail visit & L&S show can be utilised in self-exploration of illuminated\r\nâ€¢ Marina Park and the Sea shore area, evenings are pleasant and happening here.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Thu 18th April) : \r\nPort Blair to Havelock - Radha Nagar Beach\r\nâ€¢ Pick up from hotel to Port Blair Jetty for your onward journey to Havelock\r\nâ€¢ If you have morning ferry, ask hotel to provide Packed breakfast (Subject to hotel policy)\r\nâ€¢ Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\nâ€¢ Afternoon, Visit to Blue Flag certified â€œRadha Nagar Beachâ€ for swim and relaxation.\r\nâ€¢ Do not forget to carry changing clothes and towels\r\nâ€¢ Itâ€™s not permitted to board vehicles with wet clothes, please cooperate.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Fri 19th April) : \r\nHavelock - Elephenta Beach\r\nâ€¢ Morning, Breakfast and proceed for â€œElephenta Beachâ€ also known as Coral Beach.\r\nâ€¢ Elephenta beach is popular for Snorkelling and other water-based activities such as Jet Ski ride, Banana Ride, Sea Walk.\r\nâ€¢ Usually boat operators provide a 5-minute snorkelling experience complimentary, however the same cannot be guaranteed\r\nâ€¢ You reach Elephenta beach via small 11 pax capacity sharing basis boat board at jetty\r\nâ€¢ You will be allotted a time for boat a day before and you need to get ready accordingly\r\nâ€¢ Do not forget to carry a water bottle, snacks and changing cloths.\r\nâ€¢ Important: In case Elephenta Beach is not operational due to weather conditions, we will provide a trip to â€œKala Pathar Beachâ€ OR We can refund the applicable amount.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sat 20th April) : \r\nHavelock to Neil Island - Laxmanpura Beach, Bharatpura Beach & Natural Bridge\r\nâ€¢ Morning, Breakfast & proceed to jetty for onward journey to Neil Island\r\nâ€¢ Arrival, Meet- Greet by our local representative and transfer to your booked hotel/ Resort\r\nâ€¢ Afternoon, proceed to visit the following places:\r\nâ€¢ Bharatpura Beach: The white sand and shallow water beach is popular for swim, relaxation, and water activities such as Snorkelling, Boat diving and boat tour.\r\nâ€¢ Laxmanpura beach: The white sand Coral Beach offers stunning sunset view\r\nâ€¢ Natural Bridge: Also known as Howrah Bridge the bridge has naturally formed by corals, its best seen during the low tide.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing will be based on tide and local representative will brief the final schedule.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Sun 21st April) : \r\nNeil Island to Port Blair - Day at Leisure\r\nâ€¢ Breakfast, check out and proceed for jetty and onward journey to Port Blair\r\nâ€¢ Arrival in Port Blair, Transfer to your booked hotel, Day free for shopping/ leisure.\r\nâ€¢ Other places like Corbinâ€™s Cove Beach/ Chidiya Tapu/ Wandoor Beach/ Museums & Parks can be covered at additional cost subject to time and availability (Optional: at direct payment basis).\r\n\r\n6th Day (Mon 22nd April) :\r\n Port Blair Departure - Tour Ends\r\nâ€¢ Breakfast, Transfer to airport, Tour Ends.\r\nâ€¢ Port Blair airport is small with heavy traffic, we recommend you reach the airport at least 2 hrs prior to your flight timing.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meet & Greet services by our local representatives at Airport & Jetty. \r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan â€“ As mentioned above. \r\nâ€¢ Airport & Ferry Terminal Transfers in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\nâ€¢ All Sightseeing (Entry fess included) as per itinerary in Air-Conditioned Vehicle. \r\nâ€¢ Inter-Island ferry transfers By Private Catamaran Ferries Makruzz (Preferred)/ Nautika/ Green Ocean/ ITT Majestic etc (Subject to Availability) \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-04-17','2024-04-22',1,0,0,'2024-04-04 13:03:36','2024-04-04 14:27:25'),(568,1115,557,27,0,0,68850,14950,'Sri Lanka Diaries','\r\nDay 01 : Arrival - Colombo	\r\nOn arrival you will be welcomed by our representative and transfer to Colombo. Check into the hotel & leisure. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Colombo City Tour	\r\nBreakfast at the hotel & go for a Colombo city tour. Visit Colombo national museum, Gangaramaya temple, Lotus tower, Independence squre & Galleface green. On completion go for a guided shopping tour in Colombo. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Colombo Leisure\r\nAfter having breakfast lesiure at the hotel. Visit Dehiwala Zoological garden. On completion evening visit for a shopping tour. Dinner & stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Colombo - Airport\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. If time permits leisure at the hotel till checkout time. Transfer to airport to catch the departure flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3 night stay in above mentioned hotel\r\n* Daily Breakfast & Dinner\r\n* Vehicle - Toyota 37 Seaters Coaster\r\n* Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa will be on arrival charges USD 25 per person\r\n* TCS \r\n\r\n\r\n','* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability\r\n+ Bentota Day Excursion - It can be included on request. Separate charges will be applied on this','2024-10-17','2024-10-20',0,0,0,'2024-04-05 16:25:34','2024-04-05 17:11:21'),(569,1116,54,4,0,0,93400,18700,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 - Airport to Hotel Transfer (PVT)\r\n              Night Safari (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 2 - City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 3 - Full Day Universal Studio (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 4 - Gardens by the Bay (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 5 - Singapore zoo (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 - Day at Leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 7 - Departure from Hotel to Airport (PVT)\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers (PVT)\r\n* All sightseeing on SIC basis\r\n* Insurance\r\n* VISA\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-06-08','2024-06-14',0,0,0,'2024-04-09 17:35:45','2024-04-09 19:02:42'),(570,1117,38,7,4,0,167700,42800,'Bangkok Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (25 May)\r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel ( Central Pattaya ) 1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\nTOURS - EX PATTAYA - Tiger Park Pattaya 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) \r\nPattaya Tiger Park 	Pattaya Tiger Park ( Small Tiger )  (7Ad. + 4Ch.)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (26 May)	\r\nTOURS - EX PATTAYA - Coral Island Tour By Speedboat With Indian Buffet Lunch  (1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) \r\nCoral Island Tour  (Coral Island Tour By Speedboat With Indian Buffet Lunch 7Ad. + 4Ch.)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (27 May)	\r\nTOURS - EX PATTAYA - Nong Nooch Garden Admission + Show + Lunch 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) \r\nNong Nooch Garden 	Nong Nooch Garden Admission + Show + Lunch  7Ad. + 4Ch. \r\n\r\n4th Day (28 May)	TRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n5th Day (29 May) TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Sealife BKK + Madame Tussauds ( Peak Hour ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 )\r\n Sea Life Bangkok + Madame Tussauds 	Sea Life Bangkok + Madame Tussauds Ticket ( Peak Time ) 7Ad. + 4Ch. \r\n\r\n6th Day (30 May) TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch  1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 ) \r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  7Ad. + 4Ch. \r\nTOURS - EX BANGKOK - Evening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise  1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 ) \r\nChaopraya Dinner Cruise 	Chaopraya Dinner Cruise Ticket  7Ad. + 4Ch. \r\n\r\n7th Day (31 May)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) + 1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 + Luggage) ','','Economy class airfare.\r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nPattaya Tiger Park \r\nCoral Island Tour By Speedboat With Indian Buffet Lunch \r\nNong Nooch Garden Admission + Show + Lunch \r\nSea Life Bangkok + Madame Tussauds Ticket ( Peak Time ) \r\nFull Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch \r\nChaopraya Dinner Cruise Ticket \r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel \r\nTRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel\r\nTRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT \r\n1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) \r\n1-PRIVATE Seden (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\nAll tours and sightseeing on pvt basis.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Expenses of personal nature, such as Laundry, telephone calls, mini-bar bills, etc.  \r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-05-25','2024-05-31',0,0,0,'2024-04-10 16:56:59','2024-04-10 23:12:23'),(571,1118,19122,3,0,0,386000,60000,'South Korea Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : INCHEON TO SEOUL\r\nArrival ICN INTL Airport. Upon arrival driver meeting and drive to Seoul. Day is free for Leisure.\r\n\r\nDAY 02 : SEOUL TO JEJU\r\nDrop for Seoul Airport for flight to Jeju.\r\nJeju airport arrival. Pick up for Jeju Tour (East Course)\r\n* Seongsan Ilchul Bong\r\n* Haenyeo Museum\r\n* Seongup Folk Village\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 03 : JEJU\r\nJeju City Tour (South Course)\r\n* Hallasan National Park\r\n* Mysterious Road\r\n* Alive Museum\r\n* Cheonjiyeon Fall\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 04 : JEJU TO BUSAN\r\nJeju AIrport drop for flight to Busan\r\nBusan airport arrival. Pick up for Busan Tour\r\nâ–¶Gamcheon Culture Village\r\nâ–¶Biff Square\r\nâ–¶Haeundae Beach\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 05 : BUSAN TOUR\r\n* Songdo Air Cruise (02Way Close Floor)\r\n* Busan Tower\r\n* Trick Eye Museum Busan\r\n* Haedong Yonggungsa Temple\r\n* Busan Gukje Market\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 06 : BUSAN TO SEOUL\r\nDrop for Busan station for train to Seoul\r\nSeoul station arrival pick up for Seoul Tour\r\nâ–¶Gyeongbokgung Palace\r\nâ–¶Blue House (Pass By)\r\nâ–¶Myeongdong Market\r\nâ–¶Han River Cruise (1600 ~ 1640HRS)\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 07 : SEOUL - NAMI -  SEOUL\r\nNami Tour\r\n* Nami Island\r\n* Petite France\r\nBack to Seoul\r\n\r\nDAY 08 : SEOUL\r\nSeoul Tour\r\nâ–¶N Seoul Tower (Return Cable Car)\r\nâ–¶Myeongdong Market\r\nBack to Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 09 : SEOUL TO INCHEON\r\nDeparture to Incheon AIirport for your onward journey\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 8N/9D stay in 4 Star hotel with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Return airport transfers on Private basis. \r\n* KTX Train fare on Economy class (SEL - PUS - SEL) \r\n* English speaking driving guide on Sightseeing day. \r\n* Entrance fees as mentioned in below itinerary. \r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any train other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCs','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-06-09','2024-06-17',0,0,0,'2024-04-11 11:34:01','2024-04-12 09:11:02'),(572,1119,15595,7,4,0,52000,6800,'Sri lanka Diaries','2n KANDY - 1n NUWARA - 2n BENTOTA - 1n COLOMBO\r\n\r\nDay 01: Bandaranayke Airport â€“ Kandy \r\nïƒ˜	On arrival you will be met and welcomed by our representative and transferred to Kandy \r\nïƒ˜	En-route Visit Pinnawela Elehant Orphanage  & Spice Garden \r\nïƒ˜	Check-in to hotel & Leisure at the hotel\r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel-Kandy \r\n\r\nTime table of the Elephant Orphanage \r\n \r\nâ€¢             08.30am Opening the orphanage for visitors \r\nâ€¢             09.15am Bottle-feeding the baby elephants\r\nâ€¢             10.00am Morning bath at â€˜Ma Oyaâ€™\r\nâ€¢             12noon Elephants return to the orphanage after the bath\r\nâ€¢             01.15pm Bottle-feeding the baby elephants\r\nâ€¢             02.00pm Afternoon bath at â€˜Ma Oyaâ€™\r\nâ€¢             04.00pm Elephants return to the orphanage after the bath\r\nâ€¢             05.00pm Bottle-feeding the baby elephants\r\nâ€¢             06.00pm closing the orphanage to visitors\r\n\r\nOpening hours:\r\nÂ·         Temple 5.30am-8pm,\r\nÂ·         Puja 5.30-6.45am, 9.30-11am & 6.30-8pm\r\nÂ·         Dress code: Wear clothes that cover your legs and your shoulders, and remove your shoes outside the temple.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Kandy\r\nïƒ˜	Breakfast at the hotel & proceed to royal Botanical garden , Tooth relic temple ,Gem Museum , Cultural dance show & Leisure at the hotel \r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel- kandy\r\n\r\nDay 03: Nuwara Eliya     \r\nïƒ˜	Breakfast at the hotel & proceed to Nuwara eliya ,En-route visit Tea factory , Tea plantation , Hanuman Temple  and Ramboda falls \r\nïƒ˜	Check-in to hotel & Leisure at the hotel \r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel- Nuwara Eliya\r\n\r\nDay 04: Nuwara Eliya  Bentota    \r\nïƒ˜	Breakfast at the hotel & transfer to bentota En route visit devon wall falls ,Tea plantation\r\nïƒ˜	Kithul kala white water rafting \r\nïƒ˜	Leisure at the hotel\r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel- Bentota \r\n\r\nDay 05: Bentota   \r\nïƒ˜	Breakfast at the hotel & transfer to Water sports ,Madu river boat ride & turtle farm \r\nïƒ˜	Leisure at the hotel\r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel- Bentota \r\n\r\nDay 06:  Bentota to colombo   \r\nïƒ˜	Breakfast at the hotel & transfer to Colombo\r\nïƒ˜	Transfer to Gangarama temple , Colombo museum \r\nïƒ˜	Proceed to Colombo City Tour & Shopping  \r\nïƒ˜	Check-in & Leisure at the hotel\r\nïƒ˜	Overnight stay at hotel- Colombo \r\n\r\nCity Tour: While on your city tour in Colombo you may visit famous places including Galle Face Green, the Viharamahadevi Park, National Museum, Twin World Trade Center towers, Old Parliament Building, Fort district, Independence Hall at Independence Square, and prominent Buddhist, Hindu, Islam and Christian places of worship. (Entrance fees to sites not included). For shopping, you may visit Odel, House of Fashion, Beverly Street, Majestic City, Noritake, etc          \r\n\r\nDay 07:  Colombo   -Airport for Departure \r\nïƒ˜	After breakfast at the hotel & proceed to Airport for departure \r\n\r\nValue added services from Udanchoo Tourism on Complementary basis\r\n \r\nâ€¢         Room Upgrade on Availability\r\nâ€¢         02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nâ€¢         Welcome at the airport with Garlands\r\nâ€¢         Express way charges wherever applicable\r\nâ€¢         Free Woodcarvings visit, Kandy\r\nâ€¢         Free Silk & Batik shop visit at Kandy.  \r\nâ€¢         Free Cultural Show Tickets (Clients should visit a Gem shop which will be direct by us) at Kandy. \r\nâ€¢         Free Gem Factory visit and explanation about the gem progress at Kandy. \r\nâ€¢         Free head and shoulder massage at Spice Garden & explanation about the spices In Sri Lanka which will be direct by us.\r\nâ€¢         Free Tea plantation visit.\r\nâ€¢         Free Tea factory visit and explanation about the tea progress. \r\n','','â€¢         Economy class airfare.\r\nâ€¢         Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on BB\r\nâ€¢         Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned vehicle.\r\nâ€¢         Service of an English-speaking driver\r\nâ€¢         City tours in Kandy, Nuwara Eliya, Bentota, Colombo\r\nâ€¢         All applicable Government Tax \r\nâ€¢         Travel Insurance\r\n','â€¢         TCS\r\nâ€¢         Entrance Fee to any sites.\r\nâ€¢         Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\nâ€¢         Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\nâ€¢         Camera or Video permits.\r\nâ€¢         Expenses of a personal nature.\r\nâ€¢         Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion\r\n \r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-05-25','2024-05-31',0,0,0,'2024-04-11 12:43:33','2024-04-11 18:30:56'),(573,1120,54,4,0,0,97400,23600,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 - Airport to Cruise (PVT)\r\n              Overnight stay in Cruise\r\n\r\nDay 2 - Stay in Cruise\r\n\r\nDay 3 - Cruise Port to hotel (PVT)\r\n              Gardens by the Bay (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 4 - City Orientation Drive and Afternoon Sentosa\r\n\r\nDay 5 - Singapore zoo (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 - Universal Studios (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 7 - Day-Time at leisure\r\n              Night Safari (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 8 - Departure from Hotel to Airport (PVT)\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N stay in Cruise with all meals and activities\r\n* 5 night stay in a 4-star hotel with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Airport and Cruise transfers on private\r\n* All sightseeing on SIC basis\r\n* Insurance\r\n* VISA\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-06-13','2024-06-21',1,0,0,'2024-04-12 11:38:34','2024-04-12 13:49:55'),(574,1123,2690,2,1,0,26550,13050,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:-\r\n\r\n1st Day (04 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage)\r\n \r\n2nd Day (05 Jul)	\r\n        SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (06 Jul)\r\n	SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC \r\n. \r\n4th Day (07 Jul)\r\n	TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n	Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	Phuket Tiger Kingdom Smallest Tiger \r\n\r\n5th Day (08 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Daily Breakfast\r\n* TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) \r\n* TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT \r\n* SIC TOURS - PHUKET  Phuket Half Day City Tour\r\n* SIC TOURS - PHUKET  Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch\r\n* TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom \r\n* Insurance',',* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS',',Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n','2024-07-04','2024-07-08',0,0,0,'2024-04-15 12:46:31','2024-04-19 15:18:10'),(575,1124,15526,3,0,0,98100,20000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikaraâ€™s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in  deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive through the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY IN PAHALGAM\r\nFull day in Pahalgam. Enjoy ABC at your own cost . Dinner overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel \r\n\r\nDay 6 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 7 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan: MAPAI (Room + Breakfast + Dinner )\r\nâ€¢ 01 Shikara Ride.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ 1 Non Ac Sedan (PVT)','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-06-08','2024-06-14',0,0,0,'2024-04-15 16:25:47','2024-04-15 16:57:00'),(576,1126,19185,7,4,0,389200,70000,'South India','Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1:	(25 May 2024 - Saturday) Chennai to Mahabalipuram Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Chennai to Mahabalipuram Arrival\r\nOn arrival at the Chennai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Mahabalipuram, Overnight stay at hotel/resort\r\n\r\nDay 2:	(26 May 2024 - Sunday) Mahabalipuram sightseeing day 2\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Grande Bay Resort And Spa\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Mahabalipuram sightseeing day 2\r\nAfter breakfast, guided tour of Mahabalipuram, Mahabalipuram, named after the Pallava king Narasimhbavaam excavated many cave temples, the most remarkable being the seven monolithic temples, each carved from a single granite Boulder standing on the sea shore followed by stone made sculptures, caves, chariots and temples of the Pallava period. You will also visit Arjuna\'s Penance - the largest bas-relief in the world these various historic monuments built largely between the 7th and the 9th centuries, and has been classified as a UNESCO World Heritage Site\r\n\r\nDay 3: (27 May 2024 - Monday) Mahabalipuram to Pondicherry\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Grande Bay Resort And Spa\r\nTransfers - Mahabalipuram to Pondicherry\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Pondicherry and on arrival check in at the hotel. Pondicherry (or Puducherry), a French colonial settlement in India until 1954, is now a Union Territory town bounded by the southeastern Tamil Nadu state. Its French legacy is preserved in its French Quarter, with tree-lined streets, mustard-colored colonial villas and chic boutiques. A seaside promenade runs along the Bay of Bengal and passes several statues, including a 4m-high Gandhi Memorial. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 4:  (28 May 2024 - Tuesday) Pondicherry Sightseeing Day 02\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Promenade Hotel Pondicherry\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Pondicherry Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast city tour of Pondicherry. Although the French influence is gradually fading, Pondicherry retains a few Gallic accents. Pondicherry\'s main sights are the Rai Nivas, the Sacred Heart Church and the Sri Aurobindo Ashram. The ashram retreat was founded in 1926 by Sri Aurobindo after whose death the spiritual authority passed to one of his disciples, a French woman known as the Mother. visit Aurobindo Ashram near Pondicherry. After lunch, visit Auroville - a unique heaven for all; irrespective of caste,creed,colour and nationality. Evening transfer to hotel. Overnight at resort/hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5:  (29 May 2024 - Wednesday) Pondicherry Sightseeing Day 03\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Promenade Hotel Pondicherry\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 03 - Pondicherry Sightseeing Day 03\r\nVisit Rock beach,Paradise beach,Promenade beach ,the famous Pondicherry lighthouse,Botanical garden.Overnight at resort/hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6:  (30 May 2024 - Thursday) Chennai Departure\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Promenade Hotel Pondicherry\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Chennai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Chennai international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Economy Class return airfare\r\n5 nights accommodation as mentioned above\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary (Breakfast & Dinner)\r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges','The airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2024-05-25','2024-05-30',1,0,0,'2024-04-18 18:58:21','2024-04-22 11:39:38'),(577,1127,2690,2,1,0,39800,15500,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:-\r\n\r\n1st Day (04 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage)\r\n        SIC TOURS - PHUKET   Phuket Fantasea Show + Dinner (pickup time between 0500-0530 pm)\r\n \r\n2nd Day (05 Jul)	\r\n        SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (06 Jul)\r\n	SIC TOURS - PHUKET 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC \r\n. \r\n4th Day (07 Jul)\r\n	TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n	Phuket Tiger Kingdom 	Phuket Tiger Kingdom Smallest Tiger \r\n\r\n5th Day (08 Jul)\r\n	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfa