L - Phuket Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 (27th May): Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC\r\n\r\nDay 5 (28th May): Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC\r\n\r\nDay 6 (29th May): TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT','','DEL-HKT-DEL economy class airfare\r\n5 night stay in above mentioned hotels with daily breakfast\r\nPhuket APT to Krabi hotel Transfer on private basis\r\nKrabi hotel to Phuket hotel transfer on private basis\r\nPhuket hotel to Phuket APT transfer on private basis\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Box ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On SIC\r\nPhuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC\r\nInsurance charges','Visa Charges\r\nExpenses of personal nature, such as Laundry, telephone calls, mini-bar bills, etc. \r\nAny other tours apart from those listed under inclusions\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2024-05-24','2024-05-29',1,0,0,'2024-05-06 18:12:25','2024-05-07 10:36:23'),(594,1152,15512,2,2,0,156300,23000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“ (21 May) : Arrival Hanoi Vietnam â€“ Morning city highlights \r\nUpon your arrival in Noi Bai International Airport, meet up with your tour guide and then transfer to city centre for a city tour. (Early check in is NOT included â€“ Hotel check in time: 2 - 3PM)\r\nHeading out for city tour to visit Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (from the outside) your tour guide will brief you about the revolutionary life of the monumental Ho Chi Minh leader. \r\nOn the way back to your car, make a quick stop at One Pillar Pagoda â€“ a unique architecture which was inspired by the pure beauty of the lotus flower. \r\nNext drive takes you to the Temple of Literature, the first university of Vietnam, which was built in the 11th Century and follows Confucius philosophy. \r\nContinue walking to explore the Hanoi Old Quarter. Walk through narrow and evocative streets; you will have the closest view to the French-colonial architectures of ancient buildings and family-run vendor stores.\r\nOvernight in Hanoi\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ (22 May) : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, Welcome on the boat SIC (B,L,D)\r\nDeparture for Ha Long Bay is around 8:00 AM in a private van (about 3.5 hours) from your hotel. Arrive at the port around noon. Welcomed on board, you are taken to your cabin before the trip briefing. You enjoy a fresh and local seafood lunch while cruising to explore the magic Bai Tu Long Bay. Stop for a swim and visit the mysterious cave. Relax at our secluded island-beach. Later you return back to the boat just in time to watch the beautiful sunset from the top deck before enjoying the bayâ€™s freshest seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nNote: The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruiseâ€™s program.\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ (23 May) : Explore Ha Long Bay â€“ Hanoi â€“ Flight to Da Nang (B,L/Br)\r\nEarly risers can enjoy the sunrise and the quiet breath-taking beauty of Bayâ€™s landscape with towering limestone. You have breakfast at around 8:00 AM before our short rowboat by the locals of the bay. Have brunch on the boat as we slowly cruise back to boat pier. \r\nNote: The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruiseâ€™s program.\r\nHit the road straight to the airport for the flight to Da Nang.\r\nOvernight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ (24 May) : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge (B)\r\nHave breakfast at your hotel. 8:00AM Transfer to Ba Na hills (35km from Danang center) and get on the Sunworld Cable Car which gains 5 world scores to Ba Na hills station. Stop at By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, The Old Villas of French. Continue moving up by cable car to the Nui Chua Mountain â€“ the top of Ba Na range, visiting Nghinh Phong top, Le Nim Villas, Orchid Gardenâ€¦ Experience hill climbing train (first and unique funicular in Vietnam) and visit flower garden Le Jardin Dâ€™amour and Linh Ung Pagoda. \r\nEnjoy a walk across the famous Golden Bridge and admire the panoramic view over the area of mountain and lush trees. \r\nFree for joining games in Fantasy Park â€“ the third biggest indoor games zone in Vietnam with a series of interesting games. \r\nPlease note: Wax Museum, Debay ancient wine cellar, cotton animal game and carnival skill at Fantasy Park is not included in my quotation, joining them will be at your own account.\r\nAround 4pm, return to your hotel.\r\nOvernight in Danang.\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ (25 May) : Da Nang - Fly to Ho Chi Minh City, City highlights (B)\r\nHave a breakfast at your hotel. Meeting our driver and transfer to the Da Nang airport for flight to Ho Chi Minh.\r\nUpon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and transfer to the city downtown: begins with a glimpse of downtown HCM City and the Binh Tay Market in Cho Lon, with stop over at Thien Hau - a 150 year old Chinese Temple. Visits to a Lacquer-wares workshop and the Jade Emperor Pagoda as well.\r\nThen visit the Notre Dame Cathedral and the historic Central Post Office. Back to your hotel after the tour. \r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ (26 May) : Ho Chi Minh Departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. \r\nPrepare on your own until our driver picks you up for airport transfer flight back home. (Hotel check out time: Noon 12PM)\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Daily breakfast at the booked hotel\r\n* Accommodation based on double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Early check in/Late check out\r\n* Visa\r\n* Beverages\r\n* Personal expenses \r\n* Tips (3 USD/pax/day â€“ compulsory)\r\n* Other not mentioned in the written details above.\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability','2024-05-21','2024-05-26',0,0,0,'2024-05-07 15:23:42','2024-05-08 16:43:51'),(595,1153,54,4,0,0,93000,20000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Airport to Hotel Transfer on PVT. Night Safari with Tram Ride on SIC Basis.\r\nDay 2 : Universal Studio on SIC Basis.\r\nDay 3 : SIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time) on SIC Basis.\r\nDay 4 :  Gardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree) on SIC Basis.\r\nDay 5 :  Singapore Zoo  on SIC Basis. Rest of the time on leisure. \r\nDay 6 :  Hotel to Airport Transfers on PVT Basis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Economy Class airfare.\r\n05 Nights Accommodation at Singapore Hotel V Hotel Lavender.\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nReturn Airport Transfers on PVT Basis\r\nSIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time) \r\nNight Safari with Tram Ride\r\nUniversal Studio\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree) \r\nSingapore Zoo \r\nAll Tours on SIC Basis\r\nVisa\r\nTravel Insurance','Any other meal other than mentioned above.\r\nAny expense of personal nature.\r\nAny additional transfer/s\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2024-06-08','2024-06-14',0,0,0,'2024-05-08 13:38:41','2024-05-08 13:38:41'),(596,1154,15511,2,0,0,25100,7000,'Spain Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (6th Aug)  Arrival at Barcelona\r\nCheck in at the booked hotel. Evening at Leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (7th Aug) After having breakfast proceed for the excursions in Barcelona.\r\nBarcelona Catamaran Cruise (19:00-21:00) Sunset tour\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (8th Aug) After having breakfast visit La Sagrada Familia  English Guided Tour without Tower Access (Departure Time 15:30) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (9th Aug) After having breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed for your onward journey towards Madrid through the booked train. Check in at the booked hotel. Evening at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (10th Aug) After breakfast proceed for Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (11th Aug) After breakfast check out from the hotel. Proceed for your onward journey towards Paris.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N/6D stay at the mentioned hotels with breakfast\r\n* Train Fare from Barcelona to Madrid\r\n* Sightseeing as mention on SIC basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n','2024-08-06','2024-08-11',0,0,0,'2024-05-08 15:31:48','2024-05-08 19:38:07'),(597,1155,419,10,4,0,174500,33800,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE JAMMU -TRANSFER TO SRINAGAR\r\nUpon arrival you will be met by our representative and drive to Srinagar. The distance is about 270 kms, will be covered in about 6 7 hours, upon arrival in Srinagar you will be transferred to the hotel. . Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HALFDAY SIGHTSEEING OF SRINAGAR\r\nMorning sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO DOODHPATRI\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Doodhpatri , Doodhpatri means valley of milk , In the evening drive back to Srinagar  Overnight stay in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DAY TRIP TO YUSMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Yusmarg , Yusmarg means valley of Jesus , In the evening drive back to Srinagar , Overnight stay in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 7 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO JAMMU RAILWAY\r\nDROP .\r\n\r\n','','* 5 days stay at the booked hotel including daily breakfast \r\n* Shikara Ride\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ NON AC TEMPO TRAVELLER 17 SEATER (PVT)','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any transfer other than the mentioned above\r\n','Above quotes are valid 07 days from the date of quotation.\r\nRoom subject to availability \r\n\r\n','2024-06-10','2024-06-15',0,0,0,'2024-05-08 16:20:10','2024-05-09 15:30:57'),(598,1156,54,7,0,0,162860,30040,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1  (25th June) : Airport To Hotel transfer (PVT)\r\n Night Safari (Pickup time 1715-1745 hrs) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26th Jun) : SIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (SiC)\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27th Jun) : Universal Studio (SIC) \r\n\r\nDay 4 (28th Jun) : Gardens by the Bay (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29th Jun) : Singapore Zoo and rest time at leisure (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (30th Jun) : After check-out, leave the luggage in the hotel lobby and enjoy the self 