4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Box ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (10 June) : TRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	(PVT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (11 June) : Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC \r\n\r\n5th Day (12 June) :  Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC \r\n\r\n6th Day (13 June) : TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT (PVT)\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N/6D stay at the booked hotel with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on private basis.\r\n* All the mentioned tours on sharing basis\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic.\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-06-08','2024-06-13',0,0,0,'2024-05-09 16:12:05','2024-05-13 10:41:26'),(601,1160,15539,2,1,0,63000,15000,'Ooty Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (08 Jun 2024 - Saturday) Bangalore Arrival to Coorg \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Bangalore Arrival to Coorg\r\nPick up from Bangalore Airport/ Railway Station transfer to Coorg,which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination.Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (09 Jun 2024 - Sunday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 2 \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat - Raja\'s Seat has such an unerring location that it overlooks a valley bathing in green and a horizon doused in all shades of blue and orange.This place was used by the Kings and the Queens of Kodagu who were the rulers of Karnataka for over 200 years from 1600 to 1834 CE.\r\nVisit  Madikeri Fort- Madikeri Fort is one of the many forts built or rebuilt by Tipu Sultan during his reign in the second half of the 18th century. Notable structures in the fort include two stone statues of elephants at the northeast entry and a church in the southeast corner. \r\nVisit Dubare Elephant Camp- Dubare Elephant Camp is a worth visiting place. It is situated on the banks of river Kaveri.Dubare is an untamed beauty, popular for its elephant training camp where visitors can watch, learn about and get involved in a number of activities with the elephants creating a unique, enjoyable and memorable experience.\r\nvisit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan monasteries of India and allows visitors to learn in depth about Tibetan religion and culture. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 	(10 Jun 2024 - Monday) Coorg to Ooty \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg\r\nTransfers - Coorg to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty ,popularly known as the \'Queen of Hill Stations\' is nestled in the Nilgiri hills in Tamil Nadu. The lush green tea plantations, the vast meadows, the towering mountains, dense pine and eucalyptus trees, and serene lakes make Ooty a prominent part of any bucket. Visit Ooty lake and Botanical garden.Overnight stay at Ooty.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel La Montana By TGI (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (11 Jun 2024 - Tuesday) Ooty Sightseeing Day 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - La Montana By TGI\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory) and Doddabetta Peak. Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel La Montana By TGI (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (12 Jun 2024 - Wednesday) Ooty to Bangalore \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - La Montana By TGI\r\nTransfers - Ooty to Bangalore\r\nAfter Breakfast proceed to Bangalore. Bangalore officially known as Bengaluru is the capital of Karnataka state of India. The city is famous for its ample of green spaces. It is blessed with many tourist destinations and attracts lot of tourists every year from across the globe. Visit  Lal Bagh, Cubbon Park and Vidhana Soudha. Check in at Hotel.Overnight Stay at Hotel \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel AKSHAYA AURA (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (13 Jun 2024 - Thursday) Bangalore to BANGALORE - DEPARTURE \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - AKSHAYA AURA\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Bangalore to BANGALORE - DEPARTURE\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Bangalore international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories. ','','* Economy Class airfare.\r\n* Daily Breakfast.\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n\r\n','  All those which are not mentioned above\r\n  Visa charges\r\n  Travel insurance\r\n  Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n  Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n  All Items Of Personal Nature\r\n  Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n  Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n  Ayurveda Charges\r\n  Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n  Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-08','2024-06-13',0,0,0,'2024-05-09 17:31:50','2024-05-10 14:02:44'),(602,1161,15511,2,0,0,25100,7200,'Spain Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (6th Aug)  Arrival at Barcelona\r\nCheck in at the booked hotel. After resting for a while proceed for Barcelona Catamaran Cruise (19:00-21:00) Sunset Tour\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (7th Aug)  After breakfast, Experience the beauty of Barcelona on your own. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : (8th Aug) After having breakfast visit La Sagrada Familia  English Guided Tour without Tower Access (Departure Time 15:30) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (9th Aug) After having breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed for your onward journey towards Madrid through the booked train. Check in at the booked hotel. Evening at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (10th Aug) After breakfast proceed for Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (11th Aug) After breakfast check out from the hotel. Proceed for your onward journey towards Paris.\r\n,Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (6th Aug)  Arrival at Barcelona\r\nCheck in at the booked hotel. After resting for a while proceed for Barcelona Catamaran Cruise (19:00-21:00) Sunset Tour\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (7th Aug)  Breakfast in hotel. Day at leisure for self exploration. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : (8th Aug) After having breakfast visit La Sagrada Familia  English Guided Tour without Tower Access (Departure Time 15:30) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (9th Aug) After having breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed for your onward journey towards Madrid through the booked train. Check in at the booked hotel. Evening at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (10th Aug) After breakfast proceed for Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (11th Aug) After breakfast check out from the hotel. Proceed for your onward journey towards Paris.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N/6D stay at the mentioned hotels with breakfast\r\n* Train Fare from Barcelona to Madrid\r\n* Sightseeing as mention on SIC basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n','2024-08-06','2024-08-11',0,0,0,'2024-05-10 14:40:11','2024-05-14 18:19:20'),(603,1163,419,10,4,0,154900,28000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE JAMMU -TRANSFER TO SRINAGAR\r\nUpon arrival you will be met by our representative and drive to Srinagar. The distance is about 250 kms, will be covered in about 5-6 hours, upon arrival in Srinagar you will be transferred to the hotel. . Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HALFDAY SIGHTSEEING OF SRINAGAR\r\nMorning sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : DAY TRIP TO GULMARG\r\nMorning leave for Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 60 kms will be covered in about 2 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. In the evening drive back to Srinagar. Overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO DOODHPATRI\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Doodhpatri , Doodhpatri means valley of milk , In the evening drive back to Srinagar  Overnight stay in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DAY TRIP TO YUSMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Yusmarg , Yusmarg means valley of Jesus , In the evening drive back to Srinagar , Overnight stay in hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 7 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO JAMMU RAILWAY\r\nDROP .\r\n\r\n','','* 5 days stay at the booked hotel including daily breakfast \r\n* Shikara Ride\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ NON AC TEMPO TRAVELLER 17 SEATER (PVT)','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any transfer other than the mentioned above\r\n','Above quotes are valid 07 days from the date of quotation.\r\nRoom subject to availability \r\n\r\n','2024-06-10','2024-06-15',0,0,0,'2024-05-11 12:49:41','2024-05-11 13:07:40'),(604,1164,15526,3,0,0,174000,35000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikara s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Stay at the booked hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Shikara Ride\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ AC CRYSTA (PVT\r\n','* Any type of personal expense.\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2024-06-27','2024-07-02',0,0,0,'2024-05-11 17:39:06','2024-05-11 19:09:48'),(605,1165,15510,2,0,0,23300,8000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\n1st Day (28 May) : TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area ) (PVT)\r\n 	\r\n2nd Day (29 May) : Krabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Box ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (30 May) : TRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	(PVT)\r\n\r\n4th Day (31 May) : Phuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC \r\n\r\n5th Day (01 June) :  Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Local Lunch ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC \r\n\r\n6th Day (02 June) : TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT (PVT)\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N/6D stay at the booked hotel with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on private basis.\r\n* All the mentioned tours on sharing basis\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic.\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-05-28','2024-06-02',0,0,0,'2024-05-13 10:37:18','2024-05-13 21:26:45'),(606,1166,15526,3,0,0,96900,28300,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : ARRIVE SRINAGAR - EVENING BOATRIDE\r\nYou will be met by our representative at the Srinagar airport. He will assist and transfer you to the deluxe houseboat. In the afternoon you take a Shikara ride on Dal Lake, where you visit the floating vegetable gardens. While riding the Shikara s there are plenty of opportunities for bird watching with plentiful species including Kingfisher, Little Bittern, Common Pariah Kites, Grebe etc. Dinner and Overnight in deluxe houseboats.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : SRINAGAR TO PAHALGAM.\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Pahalgam (The valley of shepherds).The total distance is about 96 kms, will be covered in about 3 hours. En-route, visiting the saffron fields of pampore, Awantipura Ruins (1100 years old temple of Lord Vishnu built by the King Awantivarman), and enjoy the beautiful countryside.Drive throught the pine forests. Arrive at Pahalgam and enjoy Lidder stream. Later walk along pony trails with a magnificent view of the mountains. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : PAHALGAM TO GULMARG\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers) 2730 mts. above the sea level. The distance of 130 kms will be covered in about 5 hours. Gulmarg has one of the best ski slopes in the world and highest golf course with 18 holes. If weather permits one can also have the view of Nanga Parbat, the naked mountain that is over 26,000 feets and dominates the entire region, also enjoy cable car (Gondola) for mountain ride upto khilangmarg. Dinner and overnight in hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : GULMARG TO SRINAGAR\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Srinagar. sightseeing of the Mughal Gardens, visiting Nishat Bagh built by Asaf Khan, the brother -in- law of Jehangir in 1632 AD, and Shalimar Bagh built by Jehangir for his wife empress Nur Jahan. All the gardens are situated on the banks of the Dal Lake with the Zabarwan hills in the background. Afternoon will be at your leisure for individual activities. Dinner and overnight in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : DAY TRIP TO SONMARG\r\nMorning proceed for Sonmarg (Meadow of Gold). The distance of about 83 kms, will be covered in about 3 hrs. Sonmarg lies in Sindh Valley streamed with flowers and surrounded by mountains. Sonmarg is also the base for some interesting treks to the high altitude Himalayan Lakes. In the evening drive back from Sonmarg. Dinner and overnight in deluxe hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 : DEPARTURE FROM SRINAGAR HOTEL TO SRINAGAR AIRPORT\r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Srinagar airport for onward flight.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Stay at the booked hotel with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Shikara Ride\r\n* Sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All Arrival/Departure transfer as mentioned in Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ All present applicable taxes as on date.\r\nâ€¢ Any future taxes levies will be charged extra.\r\nâ€¢ NON A/C CRYSTA (PVT)\r\n','* Any type of personal expense.\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2024-06-29','2024-07-04',1,0,0,'2024-05-13 11:39:24','2024-06-06 15:44:38'),(607,1167,15539,4,4,0,76000,20000,'Ooty Diaries','\r\nSuggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 (20 Jun 2024 - Thursday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival) \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Camellia & Elettaria Munnar (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2 (21 Jun 2024 - Friday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Camellia & Elettaria Munnar\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Madupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Camellia & Elettaria Munnar (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3 (22 Jun 2024 - Saturday) Munnar to Alleppey \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Camellia & Elettaria Munnar\r\nTransfers - Munnar to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, and enjoy sunset.Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\" \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Paloma Backwater resort (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 4 (23 Jun 2024 - Sunday) Alleppey to Kovalam \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Paloma Backwater resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel Houseboat and transfer to Kovalam.Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Travancore Heritage (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 (24 Jun 2024 - Monday) Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Travancore Heritage\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kovalam â€“ Trivandrum â€“ Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed for Sightseeing. Visit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, Napier Museum. Overnight stay at Kovalam. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Travancore Heritage (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 (25 Jun 2024 - Tuesday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Travancore Heritage\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\nVehicle - Innova.\r\nAll tours and sightseeing are on pvt basis.\r\n\r\n','All those which are not mentioned above \r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature \r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\nAyurveda Charges \r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-20','2024-06-25',1,0,0,'2024-05-13 13:19:15','2024-05-21 17:29:49'),(608,1169,16002,4,0,0,92800,21600,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\n1st Day (Thursday, 18 July)\r\nâ€¢ Pick up from Denpasar Airport to Kuta Hotel - Transfer In (1-Hiace)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Friday, 19 July)\r\nâ€¢ Vehicle at Disposal Basis - Full day tour and drop back to Hotel (08 Hrs) (1-Hiace)\r\nâ€¢ Tanjung Benoa Water Sports - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Banana Boat - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Uluwatu Temple - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Saturday, 20 July)\r\nâ€¢ Vehicle at Disposal Basis - Full day tour and drop back to Hotel (10 Hrs) (1-Hiace)\r\nâ€¢ Kintamani Volcano, view - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Tegenungan Waterfall - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Ubud Market - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Bali Swing Alas Harum - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sunday, 21 July)\r\nâ€¢ Pick up and drop from bali hotel to sanur harbour - private (1-Hiace)\r\nâ€¢ West Nusa penida Day trip including Local Lunch (The Retribution Fees (Compulsory Donation), for Nusa Penida for IDR 25000 / adult ) - Private - Full Day Ecursion (4 Adults)\r\n\r\n5th Day (Monday, 22 July)\r\nâ€¢ Vehicle at Disposal Basis - Full day tour and drop back to Hotel (08 Hrs) (1-Hiace)\r\nâ€¢ Ulun Danu Beratan Temple - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Tanah lot - Private Tour with Ticket (4 Adults)\r\n\r\n6th Day (Tuesday, 23 July)\r\nâ€¢ Pick up from Kuta Hotel to Denpasar Airport - Transfer Out (1-Hiace)                                                     \r\n','','* Economy Class Air