huket - Phuket Half Day City Tour - No Big Buddha ( No Guide ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n\r\n\r\n3rd Day (10 Jun)	TOURS - EX Phuket - Private Land Transfer for Phi Phi Island Tour Big Boat ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\nPhi Phi Island Tour 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Lunch Entrance ( Exclude NPF )  8 Adults \r\n\r\n\r\n4th Day (11 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n\r\n5th Day (12 Jun)	TOURS - EX KRABI - Private Land Transfer for Krabi 4 Island Tour Long Tailed ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour 	Krabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Entrance ( Exclude NPF ) 8 Adults \r\n\r\n\r\n6th Day (13 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Krabi APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN KBV (Max 9 + Luggage) \r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n\r\n7th Day (14 Jun)	TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 ) \r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  8 Adults \r\n\r\n\r\n8th Day (15 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE VAN (Max 10 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','Economy Class airfare.\r\nStay for 7 nights in above mentioned hotels\r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nAll tours and sightseeing on  pvt basis.\r\nTravel Insurance\r\n\r\n','Any type of personal expensesÂ \r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2024-06-08','2024-06-14',1,0,0,'2024-05-20 18:29:35','2024-05-21 16:01:45'),(619,1181,68,8,0,0,460200,50000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival Hanoi Vietnam â€“City highlights in the afternoon.\r\nOur English-speaking guide will greet you at Noi Bai International Airport and transfer you to Hanoi Capital. In the afternoon, we\'ll visit Ba Dinh Square, including Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (outside only), One Pillar Pagoda, and Ho Chi Minh\'s Stilt House. Then, explore Sword Lake, Ngoc Son Temple, and The Huc Bridge. Enjoy shopping at Old Quarter and Dong Xuan Market. Return to the hotel for overnight stay in Hanoi.\r\n\r\nDay 2  : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nDeparture for Ha Long Bay around 8:00 AM in a private car (4-hour drive). Arrive at the port around noon, welcomed on board and briefed on the trip. Enjoy fresh seafood lunch while cruising Bai Tu Long Bay, with stops for swimming and cave exploration. Relax at a secluded island-beach before returning to watch the sunset from the deck. Indulge in a seafood dinner and overnight on the cruise.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ Hanoi (B/Brunch)\r\nEarly risers enjoy the sunrise over the stunning limestone landscape. Breakfast at 8:00 AM, followed by a rowboat excursion. Brunch on board as we cruise back to the pier, then return to Hanoi for overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 4  : Ha Noi â€“ Fly to Da Nang (B)\r\nBreakfast at hotel, then transfer to Hanoi airport for flight to Da Nang. On arrival, transfer to hotel (20 mins) for check-in. Overnight in Da Nang\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Coconut forest and Hoi An Ancient  Town (B)\r\n\"After breakfast, enjoy a free morning. At 2:00 PM, visit the coconut forest, then explore vibrant Hoi An, renowned for its evening charm. Experience local specialties, Vietnamese coffee, and sunset views. Enjoy a boat trip on the Hoai River, witnessing Hoi An\'s beauty from the water. Stroll the streets and visit the night market adorned with lanterns and street food. Return to the hotel around 8:00 PM. Overnight in Da Nang\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Ba Na Hills (35km from Danang center) and take the Sunworld Cable Car to Ba Na Hills station. Visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas. Explore Nui Chua Mountain, including Nghinh Phong Top and Le Nim Villas. Experience the hill climbing train, Le Jardin D\'amour, and Linh Ung Pagoda. Walk across the Golden Bridge for panoramic views. Lunch is at your own choice. Enjoy games at Fantasy Park, Vietnam\'s third-largest indoor games zone. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\nDay 7 \r\nDa Nang airport - fly to Ho Chi Minh City â€“ City highlights half day\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Da Nang airport for flight to Ho Chi Minh City. Upon arrival, transfer to downtown (30 mins) for must-see sites: Notre Dame Cathedral, Central Post Office, City Hall, Ben Thanh Market, Nguyen Hue Boulevard. Check into your hotel (check-in time 14:00) and enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\n\r\nDay 8 \r\nHCMC â€“ Mekong Delta \r\nAt 8:30 AM, embark on a journey to the Mekong Delta, Vietnam\'s largest rice bowl. Board a motorboat in My Tho City, navigating through canals to Thoi Son Island. Enjoy traditional music and paddle boat rides, visiting households making coconut candy and rice wine. Explore a bee farm, tasting fresh honey and fruits. Visit Vinh Trang Pagoda before returning to Ho Chi Minh City. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\"\r\n\r\nDay 9\r\nHCMC departure\r\nBreakfast at hotel. Then we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. Goodbye, and hope to see you again soon! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','â€¢ Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\nâ€¢ Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\nâ€¢ SIC tours as mentioned\r\nâ€¢ Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Cost for flight ticket Hanoi - Da Nang included\r\n* Cost for flight ticket Da-Nang - Ho Chi Minh included\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n      \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Early check in/Late check out\r\nâ€¢ Visa\r\nâ€¢ Personal expenses \r\nâ€¢ Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.)\r\nâ€¢ Others not mentioned in the written details above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS\r\n       \r\n','Airfare and schedule are subject to modification without prior notice from the airline\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability.\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\n\r\nâ€¢ TOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n\r\n','2024-12-17','2024-12-25',0,0,0,'2024-05-20 18:49:53','2024-05-30 17:20:44'),(620,1185,15511,2,0,0,99600,21900,'Spain Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (6th Aug)  Arrival at Barcelona\r\nCheck in at the booked hotel. After resting for a while proceed for Barcelona Catamaran Cruise (19:00-21:00) Sunset Tour\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (7th Aug)  After breakfast, Experience the beauty of Barcelona on your own. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : (8th Aug) After having breakfast visit La Sagrada Familia  English Guided Tour without Tower Access (Departure Time 15:30) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (9th Aug) After having breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed for your onward journey towards Madrid through the booked train. Check in at the booked hotel. Evening at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (10th Aug) After breakfast proceed for Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (11th Aug) After breakfast check out from the hotel. Proceed for your onward journey towards Paris.\r\n,Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (6th Aug)  Arrival at Barcelona\r\nCheck in at the booked hotel. After resting for a while proceed for Barcelona Catamaran Cruise (19:00-21:00) Sunset Tour\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (7th Aug)  Breakfast in hotel. Day at leisure for self exploration. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : (8th Aug) After having breakfast visit La Sagrada Familia  English Guided Tour without Tower Access (Departure Time 15:30) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (9th Aug) After having breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed for your onward journey towards Madrid through the booked train. Check in at the booked hotel. Evening at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (10th Aug) After breakfast proceed for Madrid City Tour Hop-On Hop-Off Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (11th Aug) After breakfast check out from the hotel. Proceed for your onward journey towards Paris.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N/6D stay at the mentioned hotels with breakfast\r\n* Train Fare from Barcelona to Madrid\r\n* Sightseeing as mention on SIC basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\n','2024-08-06','2024-08-11',1,0,0,'2024-05-21 16:52:55','2024-05-21 17:00:07'),(621,1186,16002,2,0,0,0,0,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itienary\r\n\r\nDay 1 : check in hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Benoa water sports including 1 x round of Banana boat, flying fish and Jet skii  + Parasailing Adventure  followed by Uluwatu sunset temple Tour including Kecak dance with private transfers \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Bali - Gili by Ferry \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Gili Stay \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Gili - Bali by Ferry \r\n\r\nDay 6 :   West Nusa Penida tour with transfer and ferry ( 1 point snorkelling day trip) on private basis (Guest can upg Lunch at Local Indian Resto with USD 10 pp additional .. Restro Name : Delhi 66)  (Hotel - Bali Port - Hotel - with SIC transfers)                                                                                                                     Meeting Point Pelabuhan Sanur.                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                           â€¢ Destination : Broken Beach, Angel Billabong, Klingking Clif & Crystal Bay (1 point Snorkeling)    - Boat start at 08.00 AM and back at 04.00 PM. (SIC basis)                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                              Tour Include : Car for tour island, Driver as Guide, Local Lunch (Vegetarian Only), Return Boat Free entrance all destination, only Snorkeling Equipment, Life Jacket                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                                 Tour Exclude : Retribution fee to Island Nusa Penida IDR 25.000,-/person.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Kintamani tour with Ubud Village with private transfers (Tegalalang Rice Field / Tegenungan waterfall) + My SWING - (2 Single Swing, Fun Adrenaline Swing, Exciting Adrenaline Swing, Ultimate Swing,  Couple Swing, Romantice Bed Swing,  Family Bed Swing,  Chicken Nest,  Bird Nest,  Sweet Love Nest, Glass Floor) WITH TRANSFERS\r\n\r\nDay 8 : check out \r\n','','* Economy class Airfare\r\n* 07 Nights Accommodation\r\n* BB Basis\r\n* Meet & Greet assistance with Welcome with Garland, 1x 500ml Mineral Water at the airport \r\n* Return Airport & Inter Hotel transfer by Pvt Basis\r\n* Bali - Gili - Bali by speed boat (EkaJaya)\r\n* Transfers with air-conditioned vehicle\r\n* English speaking driver cum guide assistance\r\n\r\nNOTE: ROUNDTRIP TRANSFER FROM JETTY â€“ HOTEL â€“ JETTY BY CIDOMO (TRADITIONAL TRANSPORTATION IN GILI TRAWANGAN) â€“ PAYMENT IS OWN ARRANGEMENT ON THE SPOT ONLY.\r\n','TCS\r\nCompulsory dinner supplements incase of hotel surcharge\r\nAny surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visiter fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\n\r\n','','2024-06-20','2024-06-27',1,0,0,'2024-05-22 14:36:06','2024-07-18 10:46:55'),(622,1187,15535,2,0,0,0,0,'Ladakh Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrival Leh\r\nI Arrived in Leh in the morning and transferred to the hotel. Full day of rest for acclimatization to the high altitude of Leh (11,500 ft / 3500 meters)Later, in the evening by walking visit Shanti Stupa or Leh Local Market O/N Leh.\r\n \r\nDay 02: Leh Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. After breakfast we take you for a tour of the hall of fame, gurudwara pathar sahib, magnetic hill, kali temple and sangam. At sangam you can enjoy rafting on the zanskar river. \r\nHall of fame is a must visit for every patriotic indian. It was built by the Indian army in memory of soldiers who lost their lives in the Kargil war. Return to leh in the afternoon. \r\nGurdwara Pathar sahib located at a distance of 40 kms from leh, was constructed in 1571, in memory of guru nanak to commemorate his visit to this region. \r\nMagnetic hill is the place where you will see your car, with its engine turned off, move upwards on a steep slope. It almost sounds unbelievable. \r\nThe sangam is the place called nimu where the zanskar river and indus rivers merge. In the evening come back to leh. Overnight hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 03: Leh - Nubra Valley (128 Kms | 4-5 hrs approx)\r\nAfter Breakfast drive to Nubra Valley via Khardungla (Highest Motorable road in the world, 18,380 ft). You can take short breaks at roadside cafes and scenic points for photography. On arrival check in to the hotel/camp. Post lunch, enjoy a camel safari (double humped camels which are found only in Ladakh & Mongolia) at the Sand Dunes between Deskit & Hundur Village. O/N Nubra Valley\r\n \r\nDay 04: Nubra - Pangong Lake via Shyok River road (150 Kms | 6-7 Hrs approx)\r\nAfter Breakfast leave for Pangong Lake 14,500 ft, drive of 6 â€“ 7 Hrs. Arrival at Camp, Later free time at Leisure and enjoy the color changing lake and the sun set on the banks of lake. O/N Pangong Lake\r\n \r\nDay 05: Pangong Lake â€“ Leh (140 Kms | 4-5 hrs approx)\r\nEarly morning enjoy the picturesque view of the Sun rise on the lake. After Breakfast drive back to Leh, en route visit Thiksey Monastery and Shey Palace on additional Cost if guests are interested, Day Free for Leisure Evening by walk visit Leh Market for Shopping(Own Cost). O/N Leh\r\n\r\nDay 06: Leh Departure\r\nEarly morning transfer to the airport for taking the flight back home. Tour ends.','','Economy class airfare.\r\nArrival & Departure Transfer from Leh Airport by Non-Ac Innova | Xylo | SUV. \r\nTraditional welcome in the hotel with welcome drink (Hot tea | Coffee | Kahwa)\r\nAccommodation in well-appointed guest selected rooms & camps.\r\nDaily Buffet/TDH Breakfast & Dinner\r\nAll Transfer & Sightseeing tours (Point to Point) by Non-Ac Innova | Xylo | SUV or Tempo Traveler in all Categories as per the itinerary.\r\nAll toll taxes / parking fee / driver allowance\r\nMorning Tea / Coffee with Biscuits on the day of departure\r\nInner line Permit\r\nWildlife fee & Red Cross fee\r\nLadakh Entry Fee\r\nLadakh Ecological Development Fee\r\n','Any expenses of personal nature such as tips, laundry, telephone calls, fax etc.\r\nEntrance Fees for Monument, Monasteries & Museums\r\nAny kind of drinks (Alcoholic, Mineral, Aerated)\r\nRafting charges, Camel Safari Charges, Guide charges, if any.\r\nAnything not specifically mentioned under the head â€œTour Package Inclusionsâ€\r\nAny expenses incurred on extra transport, apart from the ones covered in the package\r\nRoom service & additional meals\r\nMedical & Travel insurance\r\nOxygen Cylinder\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-17','2024-06-22',1,0,0,'2024-05-22 15:26:37','2024-05-22 16:45:18'),(623,1188,15583,2,0,0,101000,15000,'Haridwar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 01 = Delhi - Haridwar \r\nDay 02 = Haridwar - Barkot \r\nDay 03 = Barkot - Jankichatti - Yamunotri - Jankichatti - Barkot \r\nDay 04 = Barkot - Uttarkashi \r\nDay 05 = Uttarkashi - Gangotri - Uttarkashi \r\nDay 06 = Uttarkashi - Guptkashi \r\nDay 07 = Guptkashi - Kedarnath \r\nDay 08 = Kedarnath - Guptkashi \r\nDay 09 = Guptkashi - Joshimath \r\nDay 10 = Badrinath full day night stay in badrinath \r\nDay 11 = Badrinath - Rishikesh \r\nDay 12 = Rishikesh - Delhi drop ','','* Delhi to Delhi \r\n* Breakfast and Dinner Included \r\n* 3 star hotels\r\n* Transportation for local sightseeing by sedan \r\n* All road taxes\r\n* State Taxes Fuel Charges\r\n* Driver Charges\r\n','Any type of personal expense\r\nAny meal other than the mentioned above','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2024-06-15','2024-06-26',0,0,0,'2024-05-22 15:39:59','2024-05-30 18:02:05'),(624,1189,2,30,0,0,2782000,600000,'USA Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n6 Nights â€“ 7 Days : New York â€“ Washington â€“ Niagara Falls\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrive New York\r\nWelcome to the \"Big Apple,\" the \"City That Never Sleeps\". On arrival you will be transferred to the Hotel. The day is free at leisure to explore the city on your own. Overnight stay in New York.\r\n\r\nDay 02: New York City Tour\r\nBreakfast at hotel and proceed for New York City tour with entrance to Empire State Building & Statue of Liberty Ferry Ride on Seat in Coach basis. \r\nHighlights of the tour: Statue of Liberty Express One hour, Non-stop Cruise (Ferry Ticket Only), Empire State Buildingâ€™s 86th floor Observatory (Admission Included), Rockfeller Center/St. Patrickâ€™s Cathedral, Ground Zero/WTC/911 Memorial, etc. Overnight stay in New York.\r\n	\r\nDay 03: New York - Washington\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.  Depart to Washington DC the Capital of the United States of America and a Guide to the Historic Neighbourhoods and Monuments. Other than the federal government, tourism is DC`s biggest industry. The city attracts almost twenty million visitors each year. Arrive Washington, transfer to the Hotel. The day is free at leisure. Overnight in Washington. \r\n\r\nDay 04: Washington City Tour\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Union Station for Washington DC city tour on Seat in Coach basis. \r\nThe most famous sights in Washington DC are the stars of this tour of the US capital. Tour the Capitol Building and visit the White Houseâ€™s south lawn and visitor centre. Spend time at the Smithsonian Museums, before heading to the World War II and Dr Martin Luther King, Jr. memorials in addition to much more in between.\r\nThroughout the trip you see much of DC\'s finest monuments and structures including: the FBI Building, Federal Triangle, Ellipse, Tidal Basin, National Archives, Washington Monument, House and Senate Office Building, National Gallery of Art, and Grant Memorial. Enjoy lunch at your leisure at one of the stops.\r\n\r\nDay 05: Washington - Buffalo - USA Side Niagara Falls\r\nCheck out from hotel and we transfer you to airport for flight to Buffalo. On arrival we transfer to Niagara the town of the world famous falls, which forms one of the natural wonders of the World. Transfer to Niagara Falls. The evening is free at leisure. Overnight stay in Niagara Falls. \r\n\r\nDay 06: Niagara Falls Discovery Pass\r\nWhat else can be a better way than Niagara Discovery Pass to explore the Niagara Falls. \r\nDiscovery Pass allows admission to Maid of the Mist, Cave of the Winds, Niagara Adventure Theater, Gorge Discovery Centre & Aquarium of Niagara. \r\n\r\nDay 07: Departure from Niagara - Buffalo.\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to the Buffalo Airport fly back home or to the next destination.','','â€¢	06 Nightâ€™s Accommodation with breakfast as per mentioned or similar\r\nâ€¢	Guided City tour of New York with entrance to Empire State Building & Statue of Liberty ferry Ride only on Seat in Coach basis \r\nâ€¢	Guided Washington city tour on Seat in Coach basis\r\nâ€¢	Niagara Discovery Pass\r\nâ€¢	New York Airport / Hotel transfers on Seat in Coach basis\r\nâ€¢	New York Hotel / Coach Station Transfers on Private basis\r\nâ€¢	One way Coach Ticket New York to Washington \r\nâ€¢	Washington Coach Station / Hotel transfers on Private basis\r\nâ€¢	Washington Hotel / Airport transfers on Seat in Coach Basis\r\nâ€¢	Buffalo Airport / Niagara Hotel round trip transfers on Private basis\r\nâ€¢	Travel Insurance\r\n','Airfare \r\nResort fee / City Tax / Utility Charges wherever applicable has to be paid directly\r\nMeals, Lunch, Dinner unless specified\r\nAny item not mentioned in Package inclusions\r\nTips to drivers and Gratuities \r\nAny items not mentioned in includes column  \r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. ','2024-07-29','2024-08-04',1,0,0,'2024-05-22 16:09:55','2024-05-23 18:43:04'),(625,1191,15535,2,0,0,0,0,'Ladakh Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrival Leh\r\nI Arrived in Leh in the morning and transferred to the hotel. Full day of rest for acclimatization to the high altitude of Leh (11,500 ft / 3500 meters)Later, in the evening by walking visit Shanti Stupa or Leh Local Market. O/N Leh\r\n\r\nDay 02: Leh Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. After breakfast we take you for a tour of the hall of fame, gurudwara pathar sahib, magnetic hill, kali temple and sangam. At sangam you can enjoy rafting on the zanskar river. \r\nHall of fame is a must visit for every patriotic indian. It was built by the Indian army in memory of soldiers who lost their lives in the Kargil war. Return to leh in the afternoon. \r\nGurdwara Pathar sahib located at a distance of 40 kms from leh, was constructed in 1571, in memory of guru nanak to commemorate his visit to this region. \r\nMagnetic hill is the place where you will see your car, with its engine turned off, move upwards on a steep slope. It almost sounds unbelievable. \r\nThe sangam is the place called nimu where the zanskar river and indus rivers merge. In the evening come back to leh. Overnight hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 03: Leh to Nubra Valley (128 Kms | 4-5 hrs approx)\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Nubra Valley, also known as Valley of flowers via Khardungla, the highest motorable road in the World, (18,380 ft). On your arrival in Nubra Valley check in the hotel / camp After a sumptuous lunch take a walk on the banks of Shayok river, you can also enjoy a ride on double humped camels on the Sand Dunes between Deskit & Hundur Village, by yourself. O/N Nubra Valley\r\n\r\nDay 04: Nubra â€“ Turtuk â€“ Nubra (170 Kms |5-6 hrs approx.)\r\nAfter breakfast, I drove to Turtuk (the first time it opened for tourists since 2010) . This village was captured by the Indian Army in 1971 from Pakistan, O/N Nubra Valley.\r\n\r\nDay 05: Nubra - Pangong Lake via Shyok River road (150 Kms | 6-7 Hrs approx)\r\nAfter Breakfast leave for Pangong Lake 14,500 ft, drive of 6 â€“ 7 Hrs. Arrival at Camp, Later free time at Leisure and enjoy the color changing lake and the sun set on the banks of lake. O/N Pangong Lake\r\n\r\nDay 06: Pangong Lake â€“ Leh (140 Kms | 4-5 hrs approx)\r\nEarly morning enjoy the picturesque view of the Sun rise on the lake. After Breakfast drive back to Leh, en route visit Thiksey Monastery and Shey Palace on additional Cost if guests are interested, Day Free for Leisure Evening by walk visit Leh Market for Shopping (Own Cost). O/N Leh\r\n\r\nDay 07: Leh Departure\r\nEarly morning transfer to the airport for taking the flight back home. Tour ends.\r\n\r\n','','Economy class airfare.\r\nArrival & Departure Transfer from Leh Airport by Non-Ac Innova | Xylo | SUV. \r\nTraditional welcome in the hotel with welcome drink (Hot tea | Coffee | Kahwa)\r\nAccommodation in well-appointed guest selected rooms & camps.\r\nDaily Buffet/TDH Breakfast & Dinner\r\nAll Transfer & Sightseeing tours (Point to Point) by Non-Ac Innova | Xylo | SUV or Tempo Traveler in all Categories as per the itinerary.\r\nAll toll taxes / parking fee / driver allowance\r\nMorning Tea / Coffee with Biscuits on the day of departure\r\nInner line Permit\r\nWildlife fee & Red Cross fee\r\nLadakh Entry Fee\r\nLadakh Ecological Development Fee','Any expenses of personal nature such as tips, laundry, telephone calls, fax etc.\r\nEntrance Fees for Monument, Monasteries & Museums\r\nAny kind of drinks (Alcoholic, Mineral, Aerated)\r\nRafting charges, Camel Safari Charges, Guide charges, if any.\r\nAnything not specifically mentioned under the head â€œTour Package Inclusionsâ€\r\nAny expenses incurred on extra transport, apart from the ones covered in the package\r\nRoom service & additional meals\r\nAny other thing that is not mentioned in inclusions. \r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-17','2024-06-23',1,0,0,'2024-05-22 18:13:27','2024-05-22 19:24:21'),(626,1190,419,3,1,0,0,0,'Srinagar Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 01 : (01 June)\r\nOn arrival at Srinagar airport, our representative will meet you to pick you up and transfer to your hotel. Welcome to Srinagar, the Lake City. Begin your tour of \'Exotic Kashmir. After check-in proceed to Local Sightseeing of Srinagar with a tour of Mughal Gardens visiting Cheshmashahi (the royal spring), Nishat (the garden of pleasure), Shalimar (the abode of love), Pari Mahal. Overnight stay at hotel in Srinagar.                                              \r\n \r\nDay 02 : (02 June)\r\nAfter breakfast leave from hotel and proceed to Gulmarg . Gulmarg is also known as â€œMeadow Of Flowers â€œ & has a famous Golf course during summer  (which is one if the highest 18-holes golf course in the world) & Ski Resort during winter. One can enjoy the breathtaking views of snow clad mountains, Gondola (cable car) ride from Gulmarg to Khilanmarg (own cost) to have a real view in natural beauty of the summer and full snow view in winter. You can have a pony ride in the open fields to seven springs (own cost) and to a lake, which remains frozen until June. Overnight stay at hotel in Gulmarg.                                               \r\n\r\nDay 03 : (03 June)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Pahalgam hotel, VILLAGE OF SHEPHERDS â€œ Pahalgam is known as the land of shepherds. The mountain town is located along the bank of River Lidder. Here you can visit many breath taking places enroute visiting the world famous Saffron  growing  fields . Pahalgam is famous for Indian film industry, some trekking routes & also base camp for Amarnath pilgrimage. One can visit chandanwari,  Betab Valley and Aru Valley (own cost) has a fine Meadows of Picturesque scenery & starting point of trekking of Liddarwat , Kolahoi Glacier , Tarsar Lake. Overnight stay at hotel in Pahalgam.                                         \r\n                                                                        \r\nDay 04 : (04 June)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from hotel and transfer to Srinagar. Upon arrival check-in houseboat. After rest in evening enjoy Shikara Ride on Dal lake for 1 hour and explore the beauty of the lake. Overnight stay at houseboat in Srinagar.                                               \r\n                                                \r\nDay 05 :  (05 June)\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from Srinagar houseboat and transfer to Srinagar Airport to board the flight for onward destination.                                                                     \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation  as above.\r\n* Breakfast in the hotel.\r\n* Airport - pick-up and drop facility on pvt basis.\r\n* Sightseeing by non-AC vehicle on pvt basis\r\n* Shikara Ride (01 hour) will be given in same houseboat\r\n* Driver Allowances.\r\n* Toll tax and State tax & Parking (Without Guest entry free at Gulmarg & Aru)\r\n* Hotel Taxes\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc.\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances.\r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru.\r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-06-01','2024-06-05',1,0,0,'2024-05-22 18:36:14','2024-05-23 11:51:22'),(629,1196,2,30,0,0,6403050,1100000,'USA Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrival in Orlando\r\n* Welcome to Orlando.\r\n* Transfer to hotel.\r\n* Evening transfer for dinner.\r\n* Meals: Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 02: Kennedy Space Center & Shopping\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit NASAâ€™s Kennedy Space Center: attractions, 3D films, simulators.\r\n* Afternoon shopping at Florida Mall (1.5 hrs).\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 03: Kennedy Space Center & Cocoa Beach\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit Kennedy Space Center: Heroes of Legends Tour, Space Shuttle Atlantis.\r\n* Optional Astronaut Training Experience (25 pax minimum).\r\n* Visit Cocoa Beach (1 hr).\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 04: SeaWorld & Helicopter Ride\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit SeaWorld: attractions, rides, shows, Shark Wreck Reef.\r\n* Helicopter ride: Disney Springs, Typhoon Lagoon, â€œOld Townâ€.\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 05: Epcot\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit Epcot: Future World, World Showcase, Test Track, Frozen Ever After.\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 06: Orlando to Niagara Falls\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Transfer to Orlando airport for flight to Buffalo.\r\n* Transfer to Niagara Falls.\r\n* Evening free at leisure.\r\n* Enjoy Niagara by night: Illumination, fireworks.\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch Coupon, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 07: Niagara Falls\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Maid of the Mist boat ride.\r\n* Cave of the Winds exhibit.\r\n* Explore Niagara Falls on your own.\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 08: Niagara Falls to Washington via Hershey\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit Hershey Chocolate World.\r\n* Continue to Washington, D.C.\r\n* Dinner in Washington, D.C.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 09: Washington, D.C. to New York\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* City tour of Washington, D.C.: Capitol Building, White House, Jefferson Memorial, Washington Monument, Lincoln Memorial.\r\n* Travel to New York.\r\n* Overnight in New York.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 10: New York City Tour\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Visit Statue of Liberty (ferry ride, no stop at Ellis Island).\r\n* City tour: Rockefeller Center, St. Patrickâ€™s Cathedral, Ground Zero, Wall Street.\r\n* Visit One World Observatory, M&M Store, Times Square.\r\n* Evening dinner.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 11: Departure from New York\r\n* Breakfast at hotel.\r\n* Transfer to JFK Airport for departure.\r\n* Meals: Breakfast','',' â€¢ 10 Nightâ€™s Accommodation with breakfast as per mentioned or similar\r\nâ€¢ 2Days at Kennedy Space Centre \r\nâ€¢ Visit to cocoa beach and Florida mall \r\nâ€¢ 1Day Sea World Orlando Base Ticket + Helicopter Ride \r\nâ€¢ 1Day Disney Orlando Base Ticket (Disney Epcot Centre)\r\nâ€¢ Tickets to Maid of the Mist, Cave of the Winds, Adventure Theatre\r\nâ€¢ Tickets to One World Observatory & Liberty Cruise Ride (No Landing) \r\nâ€¢ 10 Continental Lunches\r\nâ€¢ 9 Indian Dinners and 01 Italian Dinner with Transfers\r\nâ€¢ Orlando Airport to Hotel and Hotel to Airport\r\nâ€¢ Niagara Illumination Tour\r\nâ€¢ Maid of the Mist Boat Ride, Niagara Adventure Theatre and Cave of Winds \r\nâ€¢ Hershey Chocolate Visit ( No Tour Included its to be paid direct )\r\nâ€¢ Washington DC City Tour \r\nâ€¢ Point to Point Transfers in Orlando\r\nâ€¢ Buffalo Airport to Hotel in Niagara\r\nâ€¢ Niagara Falls Illumination\r\nâ€¢ Niagara â€“ Hershey â€“ Washington Dc â€“ New York intercity\r\nâ€¢ New York City Tour Guided \r\nâ€¢ New York Hotel to Airport\r\nâ€¢ Travel Insurance','* TCS\r\n* Visa\r\n* Airfare\r\n* Internal Airfare\r\n* Any item not mentioned in Package inclusions\r\n* Bottled Water & hotel rooms\r\n* Telephone calls, Laundry, and other expenses\r\n* Any personal expenses, Any Sightseeing/Tours/Services which is not mentioned/specified in inclusions column or on email.\r\n* Baggage Handling\r\n* Driver Tips of 2 Dollar Per Person for the coach will be added to the Invoice\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. \r\n','2024-07-29','2024-08-08',1,0,0,'2024-05-23 14:17:45','2024-05-23 18:28:15'),(630,1195,16260,10,50,0,6047160,900000,'Europe Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival in Zurich\r\n- Arrive in Zurich and check into the hotel\r\n- Explore the city on a guided tour, visiting attractions such as Lake Zurich, the Old Town, and the GrossmÃ¼nster church\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Zurich\r\n- Visit the Swiss National Museum to learn about the history and culture of Switzerland\r\n- Take a boat cruise on Lake Zurich for stunning views of the city and surrounding mountains\r\n- Visit the Lindt Chocolate Factory for a guided tour and tasting\r\n- Optional : Visit the Uetliberg mountain for panoramic views of the city and the Alps\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Zurich to Interlaken/Lucerne\r\n- Travel by coach to Lucerne/Interlaken, stopping at scenic spots along the way for photo opportunities\r\n- Check into the hotel and explore the charming town of Lucerne or the adventure capital of Interlaken\r\n- Visit the Chapel Bridge, Lion Monument, and Swiss Museum of Transport\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Interlaken/Lucerne\r\n- Spend the day exploring the surrounding area, such as the Jungfrau region, Grindelwald, or Lauterbrunnen Valley\r\n- Visit the TrÃ¼mmelbach Falls, a series of stunning waterfalls inside a mountain\r\n\r\nDay 5 \r\n- Evening time for Industrial visit\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Interlaken/Lucerne to Berlin\r\n- Travel by Train to Berlin from Interlaken or Zurich, the capital city of Germany\r\n- Check into the hotel and explore the city at your own pace\r\n- Visit famous landmarks such as the Brandenburg Gate, Berlin Wall, and Museum Island\r\n- Enjoy a traditional German dinner at a local restaurant\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Berlin\r\n- Day free for Industrial visit\r\n\r\nDay 8 : Berlin to Frankfurt\r\n- Travel by coach to Frankfurt, a modern city known for its futuristic skyline and historic sites\r\n- Check into the hotel and explore the city, visiting attractions such as RÃ¶merberg Square, St. Bartholomew\'s Cathedral, and the Palmengarten botanical garden\r\n- Enjoy a dinner cruise on the Main River for panoramic views of the city at night\r\n\r\nDay 9 : Frankfurt\r\n- Take a guided tour of Frankfurt, visiting the Goethe House, the Alte Oper concert hall, and the Zeil shopping street\r\n- Visit the Frankfurt Cathedral and the Hauptwache plaza\r\n\r\nDay 10 : Departure\r\n- Check out of the hotel and transfer to the airport for your flight back home\r\n- Departure from Frankfurt filled with memories of your unforgettable trip through Switzerland and Germany. \r\n','','* Daily Breakfast\r\n* Explore the city on a guided tour of Zurich\r\n* Entrance to Swiss National Museum\r\n* Boat cruise on Lake Zurich \r\n* Visit the Lindt Chocolate Factory \r\n* Orientation Tour of Zurich \r\n* Visit the TrÃ¼mmelbach Falls\r\n* Traditional German dinner at a local restaurant (Day 6, Subject to availability) \r\n* Orientation tour of Frankfurt\r\n* Dinner cruise on the Main River in Frankfurt (Subject to availability) \r\n* Take a guided tour of Frankfurt,\r\n* Transfer to the airport \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any flights\r\n* Tips to Guide & Driver\r\n* Any expenses of personal nature for e.g. tel calls, laundry, Tips , porterage, mineral water, Excess baggage charge or any other services not mentioned above \r\n* Meals other then mentioned in program\r\n* Any other services not mentioned in above Itinerary\r\n* Train ticket from Lucerne/Interlaken to Berlin is not included \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Room/s and room/s category are subject to availability. At the time of booking if these hotels are not available similar hotels of same category will be provided.\r\nRooms offered on triple occupancy are for idea only. These many rooms on triple are not possible in all the hotels in Europe. ','2024-07-26','2024-08-04',0,0,0,'2024-05-23 14:48:22','2024-05-25 14:17:55'),(632,1193,19541,2,0,0,92000,20000,'Bhutan Diaries','Suggested itienary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Phuentsholing from Bagdogra 170 km 4 â€“ 5 hrs drive\r\nUpon arrival at Bagdogra Airport, transfer to Phuentsholing. En-route, visit Bengal Safari and Torsa Tea Garden. Bengal Safari offers a glimpse into North Bengal\'s wildlife, with sightings of various animals like deer, boars, and even tigers possible. Torsa Tea Garden, near the India-Bhutan border, offers serene walks amidst lush greenery (no tea tasting/factory visit). Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Phuentsholing - Thimphu â€“ capital city 179 km 5 -6 hrs drive\r\nMorning : Obtain route permit and journey to Thimphu, the capital, through breathtaking mountain landscapes. The road winds through Indian tea plantations, sharp bends, and daring stretches carved into the mountains via Chukka. Check-in at the hotel. Afternoon: Relax, and in the evening, explore the clock tower square. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Thimphu sightseeing with 45 minutes Wangditse Nature Trail walk\r\nIn Thimphu, experience the charm of traffic control by colonial-style policemen. They use elaborate hand gestures, sometimes surprising but always with a smile. Morning: Enjoy a leisurely 45-minute walk on Wangditse Natural Trail through pine forests overlooking Tashichho Dzong and Thimphu valley. Visit Takin Reserve on return. Optional visits to Folk Heritage Museum, Painting School, and Paper Factory. Explore National Memorial Chorten and Buddha statue, Kaja Throm, and Handicraft market. Free time for shopping or leisure. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Thimphu â€“Dochula pass 10,000 ft â€“ Punakha 77 km 3 hrs\r\nMorning : Drive to Dochula pass (10,000 ft), the first mountain pass in western Bhutan. Enjoy stunning views of the highest peaks including Gangar Punsum (24,000 ft) on clear days. Visit Royal Botanical Park, a biological corridor between two national parks, with 46 species of rhododendron. Stop at Lamperi Royal Botanical Park for 30 minutes (additional cost) to possibly see red pandas and birds, and watch a documentary. Proceed to Punakha, visit Chimi Lhakhang (additional cost), Punakha Dzong, and Suspension bridge. Evening : Explore Kaja Throm. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Punakha - Paro 142 km 4 hrs \r\nMorning : Transfer to Paro. Enroute, visit Tachog Lhakhang Iron Bridge and Paro Dzong (Rinpung Dzong). Optional visit to the National Museum (additional cost), housed in Ta Dzong, renowned as one of Asia\'s finest natural history museums. Short drive to viewpoint for a glimpse of Tigers Nest Monastery. Evening: Leisure time. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Paro\r\nAfter early breakfast, opt for an additional cost hike to the renowned Tigers Nest Monastery. The round trip takes 5-6 hours over a 12kms stretch, but the experience is truly unforgettable. Afternoon: Leisure time or explore the town for shopping. Evening: Relax at leisure. Dinner & Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Paro â€“ Jaldapara 180 km 4.5 hrs - 5 hrs drive & Exit Bhutan\r\nMorning transfer to Phuentsholing and exit Bhutan. On reaching Jaldapara, check in at the hotel. Rest of the day at\r\nleisure. Dinner & Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\n Day 8 : Jaldapara â€“ Bagdogra Airport 130 kms 4 hrs approx\r\nDeparture transfer to Bagdogra Airport for onwards connection.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy class Airfare.\r\n* 07 Breakfast and 07 Dinner.\r\n* All transfers and tour as per above mentioned itinerary, on sharing/ SIC (seat-in-coach basis)\r\nâ€¢ Bengal Safari (jeep/canter) & Tea Garden Enroute Phuentsholing\r\nâ€¢ Thimpu - Memorial Chorten, Takin Zoo, Trashi Chho Zong, Kaja Throm, Buddha Statue, Wangditse Nature Trail 45\r\nmin hike in Thimphu,Hindu Temple\r\n* Punakha- Punakha Dzong,Dochula 108 Drukwangyel Chorten,Hike to Khamsum Yulley Namgyel Chorten\r\nâ€¢ Paro-Paro Dzong\r\n* English speaking guide during tour.\r\n* SDF charges\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* All govt.taxes.\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa charges\r\n* TCS','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2024-06-15','2024-06-22',1,0,0,'2024-05-23 16:48:51','2024-05-24 15:55:22'),(633,1198,15510,8,0,0,87500,49350,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (18 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (19 Jun)	TOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Half Day City Tour - No Big Buddha ( No Guide ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n\r\n3rd Day (20 Jun)	TOURS - EX Phuket - Private Land Transfer for Phi Phi Island Tour Big Boat ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 ) \r\n\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour 	Phi Phi Island Tour By Big Boat with Lunch Entrance ( Exclude NPF )  8 Adults \r\n\r\n4th Day (21 Jun)	TRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n5th Day (22 Jun)	TOURS - EX KRABI - Private Land Transfer for Krabi 4 Island Tour Long Tailed ( Hotel - Pier - Hotel ) 	1-PRIVATE VAN HKT(Max 10 )\r\n\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour 	Krabi 4 Island Tour By Long Ta