esâ€™ section\"\r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability\r\nDEL-HKT: 20kg baggage\r\nKBV-BKK: 25kg baggage\r\nBKK-DEL: 25kg baggage','2024-06-18','2024-06-25',1,0,0,'2024-05-26 17:51:03','2024-06-04 13:14:32'),(638,1208,15539,6,2,0,243400,48000,'Ooty Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Meet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nArrival At Bangalore, Proceed to mysore Check in at Hotel. Mysore (or Mysuru), a city in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Visit Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo,  Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 2: Transfers - Mysore to Coorg\r\nPick up from Bangalore Airport/ Railway Station transfer to Coorg,which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination. Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Coorg Sightseeing \r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat, Madikeri Fort, Dubare Elephant Camp.visit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan monasteries of India and allows visitors to learn in depth about Tibetan religion and culture. Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Coorg to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty ,popularly known as the \'Queen of Hill Stations\' is nestled in the Nilgiri hills in Tamil Nadu. The lush green tea plantations, the vast meadows, the towering mountains, dense pine and eucalyptus trees, and serene lakes make Ooty a prominent part of any bucket. Visit Ooty lake,Botanical garden. Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\n \r\nDay 5: Ooty Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory) and Doddabetta Peak. Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\n\r\nDay 6: Coimbatore Departure Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel and proceed to Coimbatore for Departure.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy class Airfare\r\n* 5N stay in above mentioned hotels with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\n* All Transfers and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle (12 seater Tempo traveler) as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost.\r\n\r\n\r\n','* All those which are not mentioned above \r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\n* Ayurveda Charges \r\n* Entry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest.\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-16','2024-06-21',1,0,0,'2024-05-29 15:01:16','2024-05-29 16:16:20'),(639,1209,15500,2,0,0,187000,40000,'Swiss Paris','Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Zurich Arrival and Train to Interlaken. \r\n            Upon arrival in Interlaken, check-in at the hotel and relax. In evening, explore near by places on your own. \r\n\r\nDay 2: After breakfast, leave for the day trip to Jungfraujoch -Top of the Europe. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: After breakfast, leave for Interlaken train station. Board the train to Lucerne. Check-in at hotel and relax. In \r\n            evening, you can pay a visit to the Chapel Bridge or the Lion Monument. Shopaholics can here shop at near \r\n            by places. \r\n\r\nDay 4: After breakfast, leave for mesmerizing excursion to Mt. Titlis. After returning, relax at hotel. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 5: After breakfast, leave for the Lucerne train station. Board the train to Zurich and enjoy the scenic beauty of \r\n            Switzerland on the way. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Get some rest and then pamper yourself with \r\n            shopping at local places. \r\n\r\nDay 6: After breakfast, leave for Zurich train station. Board the train to Paris. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Pamper \r\n            yourself with some me time in Paris. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 7: After Breakfast, prepare yourself for visit to Eiffel tower tour followed by Louvre Museum and Seine River Cruise.\r\n            Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 8: After breakfast, proceed for day trip to Disneyland. Overnight at Paris Hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 9: After breakfast, check-out from hotel. It\'s time to bid Good Bye to your Switzerland and Paris trip. Leave for \r\n            airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Delhi. ','','Economy class airfare\r\n7N stay in the mentioned hotels with daily breakfast\r\nJungfraujoch Top of Europe Day Trip from Interlaken (with Swiss Pass)\r\nMount Titlis excursion from Engelberg incl. Ice Flyer (with Swiss Pass)\r\nEiffel Tower Access Tour to 2nd Floor with Summit Option by Lift (12:30 pm)\r\nLouvre Museum Ticket & Optional Seine River Cruise (Departure time 16:00)\r\nDisneylandÂ® Parks with Departure from Central Paris (1 day 2 parks) (09:00-20:00)\r\nTrain fare from Zurich to Interlaken (25th June) --with Swiss Pass\r\nTrain fare from Interlaken to Lucerne (27th June) -- with Swiss Pass\r\nTrain fare from Lucerne to Zurich (29th June) -- with Swiss Pass\r\nTrain Fare from Zurich to Paris (30th June) -- Fare included\r\n6 Days Consecutive Swiss Pass (2nd Class)\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal and medical expense. \r\nSpecial train fare not included. \r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. \r\nTrain fare is subject to change at the time of booking. \r\nThe Guests will have to manage on their own till the Pickup / Drop off point for SIC TOURS (can be covered with Swiss Pass in Switzerland)','2024-06-24','2024-07-03',1,0,0,'2024-05-30 13:14:07','2024-05-30 15:11:47'),(641,1211,15500,2,0,0,187000,41050,'Swiss Paris','Day-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Zurich Arrival and Train to Interlaken. \r\n            Upon arrival in Interlaken, check-in at the hotel and relax. In evening, explore near by places on your own. \r\n\r\nDay 2: After breakfast, leave for the day trip to Jungfraujoch -Top of the Europe. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: After breakfast, leave for Interlaken train station. Board the train to Lucerne. Check-in at hotel and relax. In \r\n            evening, you can pay a visit to the Chapel Bridge or the Lion Monument. Shopaholics can here shop at near \r\n            by places. \r\n\r\nDay 4: After breakfast, leave for mesmerizing excursion to Mt. Titlis. After returning, relax at hotel. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 5: After breakfast, leave for the Lucerne train station. Board the train to Zurich and enjoy the scenic beauty of \r\n            Switzerland on the way. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Get some rest and then pamper yourself with \r\n            shopping at local places. \r\n\r\nDay 6: After breakfast, leave for Zurich train station. Board the train to Paris. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Pamper \r\n            yourself with some me time in Paris. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 7: After Breakfast, prepare yourself for visit to Eiffel tower tour followed by Louvre Museum and Seine River Cruise.\r\n            Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 8: After breakfast, proceed for day trip to Disneyland. Overnight at Paris Hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 9: After breakfast, check-out from hotel. It\'s time to bid Good Bye to your Switzerland and Paris trip. Leave for \r\n            airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Delhi. ','','Economy clas