nd relax.  \r\n\r\nDay 3: After breakfast, leave for the day trip to Jungfraujoch -Top of the Europe. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4: After breakfast, leave for Interlaken train station. Board the train to Lucerne. Check-in at hotel and relax. In \r\n            evening, you can pay a visit to the Chapel Bridge, Lake Lucerne Cruise or the Lion Monument (on your own \r\n            with swiss pass).  Shopaholics can here shop at near by places. \r\n\r\nDay 5: After breakfast, leave for mesmerizing excursion to Mt. Titlis. After returning, relax at hotel. Overnight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 6: After breakfast, leave for the Lucerne train station. Board the train to Zurich and enjoy the scenic beauty of \r\n            Switzerland on the way. Upon arrival, check-in at hotel. Get some rest and then pamper yourself with \r\n            shopping at local places. \r\n\r\nDay 7: After breakfast, leave for Rhine Falls, FIFA World Football Museum or the Swiss National Museum Tour from \r\n             Zurich (on your own with swiss pass )\r\n\r\nDay 7: After breakfast, check-out from hotel. It\'s time to bid Good Bye to your Switzerland trip. Leave for \r\n            airport.  Board the flight and fly back to Delhi. ','','Economy class airfare\r\n7N stay in the mentioned hotels with daily breakfast\r\n2nd Class Sector Reservation in Golden Pass (From Montreux to Intelaken @ 12:34-15:50)\r\nInterlaken: Excursion to Mt. Jungfrau with Swiss Pass from Interlaken OST\r\nLucerne: Lake Lucerne Cruise / Chapel Bridge / Lion Monument - Free with Swiss Pass\r\nLucerne: Excursion to Mt. Titlis with Swiss Pass from Engelberg\r\nZurich: Visit Rhine Fall / FIFA World Football Museum / Swiss National Museum - Free with Swiss Pass \r\n08 Days Consecutive Swiss Pass - 2nd Class\r\nUnlimited travelling within Switzerland on Public Transportation using Swiss Pass\r\nDeparture Transfer from Zurich Hotel to Zurich Airport on Pvt. Basis - One Way\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal and medical expense. \r\nRhine Falls ticket not included (to be purchased directly)\r\nAny transfer/train/cab other than the mentioned above.\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa Charges\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability. \r\nTrain fare is subject to change at the time of booking. \r\nThe Guests will have to manage on their own till the Pickup / Drop off point for SIC TOURS (can be covered with Swiss Pass in Switzerland)','2024-06-25','2024-07-02',1,0,0,'2024-06-17 13:18:55','2024-07-17 17:52:46'),(673,1248,33,3,0,0,135200,10000,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : (22nd June)\r\nMeet at Hong Kong Airport, then proceed to the Hong Kong Ferry Terminal (SIC) to board a ferry to Macau Outer Ferry Pier. Upon arrival at Macau Ferry Pier, clear customs and make your own way to the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : (23rd June)\r\nHave breakfast at the booked hotel. Pick-up for a half-day Macau city tour will be arranged on a shared (SIC) basis.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : (24th June)\r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel, guests will transfer on their own to Macau Outer Ferry Pier, take a ferry to Hong Kong Ferry Terminal, and meet at the arrival hall. They will then be transferred to the hotel on a shared (SIC) basis. Around 5:00 PM, there will be a pick-up from the hotel lobby to commence a night tour on a shared (SIC) basis.\r\n\r\nDay 04 : (25th June)\r\nBreakfast at hotel. Around 10:00 AM, gather at the hotel lobby for pick-up and embark on a full-day Ocean Park tour, including entrance passes, on a shared (SIC) basis.\r\n\r\nDay 05 : (26th June)\r\nBreakfast at hotel  Around 10:00 AM, gather at the hotel lobby for pick-up and begin a full-day Disneyland tour, including entrance passes, on a shared (SIC) basis.\r\n\r\nDay 06 : (27th June)\r\nPick up at the hotel lobby and transfer on a shared (SIC) basis to Hong Kong Airport for departure.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare.\r\n* Daily breakfast at the booked hotel.\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense.\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2024-06-22','2024-06-27',1,0,0,'2024-06-19 11:35:08','2024-06-19 12:02:27'),(674,1250,15539,3,0,0,70000,17000,'Ooty Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 (25 Jun 2024 - Tuesday) Banglore Arrival to Mysore \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nArrival At Bangalore, Proceed to mysore Check in at Hotel. Mysore (or Mysuru), a city in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Visit Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo,  Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. . \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Fortune JP Palace (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2024 - Wednesday) Mysore to Coorg \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Fortune JP Palace\r\nTransfers - Mysore to Coorg\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Coorg, which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination.Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2024 - Thrusday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 2 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat, Madikeri Fort, Dubare Elephant Camp.visit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan monasteries of India and allows visitors to learn in depth about Tibetan religion and culture. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (28 Jun 2024 - Friday) Coorg to Ooty \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg\r\nTransfers - Coorg to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty ,popularly known as the \'Queen of Hill Stations\' is nestled in the Nilgiri hills in Tamil Nadu. The lush green tea plantations, the vast meadows, the towering mountains, dense pine and eucalyptus trees, and serene lakes make Ooty a prominent part of any bucket.Overnight stay at Ooty.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel FORTUNE SULLIVAN COURT (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29 Jun 2024 - Saturday) Ooty Sightseeing Day 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - FORTUNE SULLIVAN COURT\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory). Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel FORTUNE SULLIVAN COURT (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (30 Jun 2024 - Sunday) Coimbatore Departure Transfer \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - FORTUNE SULLIVAN COURT\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Coimbatore Departure Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel and proceed to Coimbatore for Departure ','','Economy class airfare. \r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n','All those which are not mentioned above \r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc \r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature ','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nHotels/Rooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-25','2024-07-30',1,0,0,'2024-06-19 12:13:26','2024-06-19 12:47:44'),(675,1252,15539,3,0,0,0,0,'Ooty Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 1 (25 Jun 2024 - Tuesday) Banglore Arrival to Mysore \r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Banglore Arrival to Mysore\r\nArrival At Bangalore, Proceed to mysore Check in at Hotel. Mysore (or Mysuru), a city in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Visit Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo,  Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. . \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Fortune JP Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2024 - Wednesday) Mysore to Coorg \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Fortune JP Palace\r\nTransfers - Mysore to Coorg\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Coorg, which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Marriott Resort & Spa  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2024 - Thrusday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 2 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Marriott Resort & Spa \r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat, Madikeri Fort, Dubare Elephant Camp.visit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan