 in India\'s southwestern Karnataka state, was the capital of the Kingdom of Mysore from 1399 to 1947. In its center is opulent Mysore Palace, seat of the former ruling Wodeyar dynasty. The palace blends Hindu, Islamic, Gothic and Rajput styles. Visit Lalitha Mahal Palace, Mysore Zoo,  Jaganmohan Palace Art and Gallery, Mysore Rail Museum, St. Philomena\'s Church, Brindavan Gardens. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. . \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Fortune JP Palace (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 2 (26 Jun 2024 - Wednesday) Mysore to Coorg \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Fortune JP Palace\r\nTransfers - Mysore to Coorg\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Coorg, which is a famous tourist destination of Karnataka known for its stunning hill views and abundant natural beauty.  Coorg, popularly known as the Scotland of India,It is one of the most beautiful hill stations of South India. With the temperature ranging between 15 degree Celsius and 20 degree Celsius throughout the year, Coorg is a year-round destination. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg   (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 3 (27 Jun 2024 - Thrusday) Coorg Sightseeing Day 2 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Coorg Sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast in the morning, Visit Rajah Seat, Madikeri Fort, Dubare Elephant Camp.visit the Golden temple nestled near Kushalnagar in the region of Coorg. It is one of the biggest Tibetan monasteries of India and allows visitors to learn in depth about Tibetan religion and culture. Overnight stay at hotel/resort. \r\nOvernight Stay at Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg   (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 (28 Jun 2024 - Friday) Coorg to Ooty \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Gokulam Grand Resorts & Spa Coorg \r\nTransfers - Coorg to Ooty\r\nAfter breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty ,popularly known as the \'Queen of Hill Stations\' is nestled in the Nilgiri hills in Tamil Nadu. The lush green tea plantations, the vast meadows, the towering mountains, dense pine and eucalyptus trees, and serene lakes make Ooty a prominent part of any bucket.Overnight stay at Ooty.  \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Accord Highland Hotel  (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 5 (29 Jun 2024 - Saturday) Ooty Sightseeing Day 02 \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Accord Highland Hotel \r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Ooty Sightseeing Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast Proceed to Coonoor. Coonoor Sight seeing(Sim\'s Park, Lam\'s Rock, Dolphin Nose and Tea factory). Overnight stay at Ooty. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The  Accord Highland Hotel (Meal Plan - MAPAI)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 (30 Jun 2024 - Sunday) Coimbatore Departure Transfer \r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Accord Highland Hotel \r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Coimbatore Departure Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel and proceed to Coimbatore for Departure ','','Economy class airfare. \r\nDaily Breakfast.\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary \r\nAll Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM \r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost \r\n','All those which are not mentioned above \r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc \r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature ','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nHotels/Rooms are subject to availability.','2024-06-25','2024-07-30',1,0,0,'2024-06-20 17:56:10','2024-06-20 17:56:10'),(682,1259,2326,4,0,0,0,0,'Himachal Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : -\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Chandigarh - SHIMLA: Pick up and drive to Shimla. O/N Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 02 : SHIMLA KUFRI :- After Breakfast Excursion to Kufri. Kufri is famous for its Himalayan National Park, Poney and Yak Ride (Extra cost) and One can see the endless Himalayan Panorama from Kufri, Shimla\r\n\r\nDay 03 : SHIMLA- MANALI (265 Km Approx 8-10 Hrs) After breakfast check out from hotel and drive to Manali \r\n\r\nDay 04 : MANALI - LOCAL SIGHT SEEING: -Walk through town visiting newly constructed Buddhist Monastery. Hadimba Devi temple-It is small temple situated in the dense forest is very interesting. Hadimba is said to be the wife of Bhima from the epic of Mahabharata. Vashist, it is an extremely picturesque little place clinging to the steep hill side. On the way up to the village you come upon the Vashishat hot baths where a natural Sulphur spring is piped into a modern bathhouse \r\n\r\nDay 05 : MANALI: â€“ SOLANG VALLEY : Wake up to the sweet sound of nature and after breakfast head towards Solang Valley. This valley is famous for its adventure activities, and you can try your hand at Paragliding, Zorbing, ATV Rides, Horse-riding, Trail-rides and so much more at own expense.\r\n\r\nDAY 06 : Manali â€“ Dharamshala : Drive to Dharamshala by Cab. Reach Dharamshala in the evening. On arrival at Dharamshala check in to the hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 07: Dharamshala â€“Local- Dharamshala. After Breakfast, drive to local sightseeing including official residence of Dalai lama in McLeod Ganj, St John church, Monasteries & Bhagsunath temple, the oldest temple in Dharamshala.\r\n\r\nDay 8: Dharmshala to Chandigarh drop.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Pickup and drop as mentioned\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned hotels or similar\r\n* Daily Breakfast As per hotel policy( Buffet or Room Service)\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Toll and taxes.\r\n* Parking charges.\r\n* Driver allowances.\r\n* Local Transfers & sightseeing by mentioned vehicle\r\n ','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-07-12','2024-07-19',1,0,0,'2024-06-21 18:47:53','2024-06-22 00:36:19'),(683,1260,2326,4,0,0,0,0,'Himachal Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Chandigarh - SHIMLA: Pick up and drive to Shimla. \r\n\r\nDay 2 : SHIMLA with in the cit