'Tcs\r\nCompulsory dinner supplements in case of hotel surcharge\r\nAny surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visiter fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2024-08-04','2024-08-08',0,0,0,'2024-07-25 15:14:35','2024-07-25 15:20:06'),(733,1322,15518,4,0,0,92200,20000,'Kerala Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (25 Aug 2024 - Sunday) Cochin to Athirapilly\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and proceed to Athirappilly. Its a breathtakingly beautiful falls situated very close to Athirapally - Valparai road. At the entrance of the Sholayar forest range, 2 waterfall is formed on Chalakkudy River named Athirapally Waterfalls & Vazhachal Waterfalls. The surroundings of the waterfalls offer rich natual views. Unlike Athirapally Waterfalls, Vazhachal flows through an inclined slope of more than 300 feet to descend into huge pool. Overnight stay at hotel/resort\r\n\r\nDay 02 (26 Aug 2024 - Monday)  Athirapally \r\nAfter the breakfast from the hotel proceed to Athirapally waterfalls, which is one of the beautiful waterfall in India. You can reach top of the waterfall by 5 minutes walk from the main road. You can also reach the bottom of the falls by about 15 minutes trek down from the top of the falls where the greatest beauty of waterfalls can be experienced. Evening leisure at hotel and night stay over there.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 03 (27 Aug 2024 - Tuesday) Athirappilly to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum. Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 04	(28 Aug 2024 - Wednesday) Munnar Sightseeing \r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 05 (29 Aug 2024 - Thursday) Munnar to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (30 Aug 2024 - Friday) Alleppey -Cochin departure transfer\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and Transferred to Cochin Airport / Railway station for the departure.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','',' *Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accomodation with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* All sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2024-08-25','2024-08-30',1,0,0,'2024-07-26 16:24:49','2024-07-26 16:48:04'),(734,1324,15510,2,0,0,25400,7000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (28 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel ( Central Pattaya ) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (29 Sep)	\r\nDay at Leisure / Explore on your own. \r\n \r\n3rd Day (30 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage)\r\nSIC TOURS - BANGKOK -Evening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC 2 Adults  Pick-up Time 17:30 hrs (240 mins)       \r\n\r\n4th Day (1 Oct)	TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 ) \r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  2 Adults \r\nStarts: 08:00 hrsâ€¢ Duration: 9h (Ends: 17:00 hrs)\r\n\r\n5th Day (2 Oct)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) ','','Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nFull Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch  on pvt basis.\r\nEvening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC Basis\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nAll tours and sightseeing are on pvt and sic basis.','Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visitor fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nSurcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking) \r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability','2024-09-28','2024-10-02',1,0,0,'2024-07-27 16:26:14','2024-07-27 16:26:14'),(736,1329,15535,3,0,0,80000,17500,'Ladakh Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (15th Aug) : Arrive LEH\r\nArrive Leh and transfer to the hotel. Full day for complete rest for acclimatization to the high altitude of Leh. Overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 2 (16th Aug) : LEH \r\nBreakfast at hotel. After breakfast, drive to shyam valley and you\'ll be awestruck with the sight of the Indus & Zanskar river Sangam, drive along the Indus river visiting Pathar Sahib Gurdwara and Magnetic Hill (where the cars defy gravity) and further on to Leh Hall of Fame (which has a museum of the Kargil War memorabilia). Later return to Leh for visit Shanti Stupa, Leh Palace and Leh Market. Overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 3 (17th Aug) : Leh - Nubra  (160 Kms / 5 Hrs)\r\nAfter Breakfast drive to Nubra Valley via Khardungla (Highest Motorable road in the World, 18,380 ft). Arrive at Hundar by Afternoon. Rest of the day free to explore Deskit, Hunder Villages and camel Safari in Sand Dunes between Deskit and Hundar Village. One can go for camel rides (own cost). Overnight stay at Nubra Valley.\r\n \r\nDay 4 (18th Aug) : Nubra (Day Tour to Turtuk Village)\r\nDrive 70 Kms one way 3/4 hrs via various villages to Turtuk. It is the last village from Indian side. Have a look forward on Bunkers and last Indian post. Later in afternoon return to Nubra valley. Overnight stay at Nubra Valley.\r\n \r\nDay 5 (19th Aug) : Nubra â€“ Pangong\r\nHave early breakfast and proceed to Pangong via Shayok, retrace the route down for Pangong Lake through Shayok 17,350 ft., it is the third highest motorable road in the world. Arrive Pangong and enjoy the beauty of the lake on the Banks of Pangong Lake while appreciating the changing Colors and fascinating high altitude of the Lake. Overnight stay at Pangong.\r\n \r\nDay 6 (20th Aug) : Pangong  â€“ Leh\r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Leh via Changla pass. Later in the evening guest can walk to Local Bazaar . Overnight stay at Leh.                                     \r\n\r\nDay 7 (21st Aug) : Depart Leh\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel & proceed to Leh airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Meet and Greet upon arrival \r\nâ€¢ Accommodation on MAPAI basis.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Transport by 1 Non-AC INNOVA  for arrival / departure and sightseeing as per itinerary on private basis.\r\nâ€¢ Green Fees & Environment Fees (Inner Line Permit)\r\nâ€¢ Toll and taxes\r\nâ€¢ Parking Charges\r\nâ€¢ Driver allowances\r\nâ€¢ 24/7 over the Phone support\r\nâ€¢ All taxes and GST\r\n','â€¢ Lunch\r\nâ€¢ Oxygen Cylinder.\r\nâ€¢ Any other activities not mentioned in inclusions like horse riding/tips/ extra food ordered / entry fees / liquor etc.\r\n','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-08-15','2024-08-21',1,0,0,'2024-07-29 17:58:51','2024-07-29 21:13:44'),(737,1332,15510,2,0,0,23900,9905,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day (28 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS: EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel ( Central Pattaya ) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (29 Sep)	\r\nDay at Leisure / Explore on your own. \r\n \r\n3rd Day (30 Sep)	\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE Sedan BKK (Max 3 + Luggage)\r\nSIC TOURS - BANGKOK -Evening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC 2 Adults  Pick-up Time 17:30 hrs (240 mins)       \r\n\r\n4th Day (1 Oct)	TOURS - EX BANGKOK - Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 ) \r\nSafari world + Marine Park 	Safari world + Marine Park Ticket  2 Adults \r\nStarts: 08:00 hrsâ€¢ Duration: 9h (Ends: 17:00 hrs)\r\n\r\n5th Day (2 Oct)	TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) ','','Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nFull Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch  on pvt basis.\r\nEvening Chaopraya Princess Dinner Cruise on SIC Basis\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nAll tours and sightseeing are on pvt and sic basis.','Any surcharge at the hotel (Mini bar, Visitor fee ect.)\r\nOther personal expenses\r\nSurcharge for peak season if any (Upon booking) \r\nExpenditure of a personal nature such as drinks, souvenirs and laundry\r\nAny cost not mentioned in the â€˜Cost Includesâ€™ section\"\r\nVisa Charges\r\nTCS','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability','2024-09-28','2024-10-02',1,0,0,'2024-07-30 12:18:00','2024-09-18 13:14:12'),(739,1333,54,8,2,0,1267300,80000,'Singapore and Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\nSINGAPORE (07th Aug)\r\n\r\nSingapore - Airport Arrival Transfer  (1-23 SEATER P