er itinerary on private basis.\r\nâ€¢ Green Fees & Environment Fees (Inner Line Permit)\r\nâ€¢ Toll and taxes\r\nâ€¢ Parking Charges\r\nâ€¢ Driver allowances\r\nâ€¢ 24/7 over the Phone support\r\nâ€¢ All taxes and GST\r\n','â€¢ Lunch\r\nâ€¢ Oxygen Cylinder.\r\nâ€¢ Any other activities not mentioned in inclusions like horse riding/tips/ extra food ordered / entry fees / liquor etc.\r\n','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-08-17','2024-08-23',1,0,0,'2024-08-02 14:17:10','2024-08-06 13:45:41'),(743,1340,54,4,0,0,114600,15000,'Singapore and Kuala Lumpur  Diaries','Itinerary for Singapore :\r\n\r\nâ€¢ Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Sentosa Island Tour (Cable Car + Wings of Time 1st Show)  (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Dolphin Island Tour (Encounter With Sea Aquarium ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay ( Cloud Forest + SuperTree ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Universal Studios ( Sea Aquarium ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n\r\nItinerary for Kuala Lumpur :\r\n\r\nâ€¢ Genting Day Tour (8 Hrs) ( Cable Car 2 Way + Genting Skytropolis (Indoor Theme Park) + Enroute Batu Caves (20 mins photostop) ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ KUL Half Day City Tour + KL Tower (04 Hours) ( KL Tower Observation Deck ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Accomodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on Pvt basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-08-09','2024-08-16',0,0,0,'2024-08-02 17:37:37','2024-08-03 17:37:06'),(744,1343,126,2,0,0,0,0,'Rajasthan Diaries','Day Wise Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day : (Sun 1st December) : Jaipur - Arrival\r\nAfter arrival at Jaipur Transfer to your hotel. Jaipur is the capital of Rajasthan, It was painted in pink shading a century back to pay tribute to a meeting sovereign, This city is 260 years of age and was built by Maharaja Jai Singh  Overnight stay at Jaipur.\r\n\r\n2nd Day : (Mon 2nd December) : Jaipur - Sightseeing\r\nEarly Morning After breakfast, head out for the Amber Fort. Also, visit the Jai Garh, Jal Mahal, Hall of triumph, Sheesh Mahal & Jantar Mantar. Drive past the Hawa Mahal. While in Jaipur also visit Maharajaâ€™s City Palace and Ram Niwas Gardens. Overnight at Jaipur Hotel.\r\n\r\n3rd Day : (Tue 3rd December) : Jaipur to Jodhpur - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast Check out from hotel & then drive to Jodhpur after check inn get relaxed at Hotel then head out for City sight seeing of Jodhpur\r\n\r\n4th Day : (Wed 4th December) : Jodhpur to Sam Sand Dunes - Transfer and Evening at Sand Dunes\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the hotel and drive to Jaisalmer, Later Drive to Sam Sand Dunes â€“ 45 km away, Sam Dunes is known for its sand rises and is the scene for the Desert celebration, Get the genuine feel of the desert by getting a charge out of a camel ride on the sand rises and witness a brilliant nightfall, After enjoying the rides, enjoy the cultural programme, Dinner & Overnight stay in Tents.\r\n\r\n5th Day : (Thu 5th December) : Sam Sand Dunes to Jaisalmer - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\nBreakfast at Tents, Check out from Tents, Then Voyage through Jaisalmer, Visit the fortress â€“ the Fort worked by Rawal Jaisal, The beautifully designed houses Jain temples of the twelfth to fifteenth hundreds of years, Patwon Ki Haveli â€“ a five story chateau with cut columns and paintings of Salim Singh, Arrival, Check-In to the Hotel, Popularly known as the â€˜heartâ€™ of Thar Desert, Jaisalmer is a medieval town with marvelous structures, Evening is free for leisure, You can spend it as per your own liking on your own, Dinner & Overnight stay at Jaisalmer Hotel.\r\n\r\n6th Day : (Fri 6th December) : Jaisalmer to Udaipur - Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the hotel. Drive to Udaipur, up on your arrival, complete your check-in process, Get Relaxed. Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n7th Day : (Sat 7th December) : Udaipur - Sightseeing\r\nBegin your day with breakfast at the hotel and then start your city tour. Visit the City Palace which is the biggest castle complex in Rajasthan, Partake in the boat ride on the tranquil waters of Lake Pichola. Also visit Sahelion ki Bari or Garden of the Maids of Honor, Jagdish sanctuary, Local Market Visit, Later in the evening Fateh Sagar Lake, Shilpgram, Once sightseeing is over, head back to the hotel, Overnight stay at Udaipur.\r\n\r\n8th Day : (Sun 8th December) : Udaipur - Departure\r\nAfter Breakfast check-out from the Hotel and take a transfer to Udaipur Airport \r\n','','* 7 nights accomodation \r\n* Welcome Drink on Arrival \r\nâ€¢ Hotel checks in & check out time as per the hotel policy \r\n* Vehicle : Sedan Car\r\nâ€¢ All transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ All Toll taxes, One time Parking of Each Destination , State Tax & Driver allowance \r\nâ€¢ Vehicle will be provided 8:00 am to 8:00pm \r\nâ€¢ Camel ride and cultural evening at sam Sand dunes. \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any monument or sight-seeing Entry fee / Charges ','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-12-01','2024-12-08',0,0,0,'2024-08-07 13:21:14','2024-08-07 14:31:31'),(745,1344,18797,3,0,0,0,0,'Ayodhya Diaries','Daywise Itinerary \r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“ Varanasi Arrival â€“\r\nPickup from Varanasi Airport / Station and transfer to hotel . Check in hotel and Later in the evening enjoy the Ganaga aarti  by boat ride(Charges Included). Stay overnight in Hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ Varanasi  â€“\r\n\"After breakfast, early in the morning on the second day you will be taken on a temple tour to enjoy the morning rituals in famous temples like, Kashi Vishwanath temple, Annapurna temple, and others. Later, you will be taken back to the hotel for breakfast and later proceed SankatMochan Hanuman temple , ManasMandir , BHU nd then drive to Sarnath. Sarnath is the spot where Lord Buddha delivered his sermon after getting enlightenment. Top attractions visited in Sarnath are an archeological museums, Buddha temples, stupas .\" Over night stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ Varanasi â€“ Ayodhya\r\nAfter breakfast drive to Ayodhya and check in hotel and in evening  will proceed for attending the Saryu Aarti & laser light show at Ram ki Paidi. Stay overnight in Hotel .\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“Ayodhya \r\nAfter breakfast \"In morning, after breakfast will go to temple tour - Ramjanambhoomi, Hanumangarhi, kanak Bhawan & Dashrath Mahal.Then will go for Guptarghat, Nandigram. Later on will go for Surya kund  and then  drop at Ayodhya  Airport.\r\n','','Economy Class airfare.\r\nAccommodation on the above-mentioned hotels or similar as per itinerary .\r\nBreakfast at hotel\r\nMeal Plan as per above in Hotels / Resorts.\r\nTransfers & sightseeing by Ac Sedan .  (Vehicle Service from 08:00 Am to 08:00 PM after that additional cost will be applicable )\r\nToll, Parking, Driver Allowance.\r\nAll Applcable Tax.\r\nEvening Aarti by motor boat with in Varanasi (1:30 hours)  \r\n1 Day guide in Varanasi \r\n1 E ricksha and 1 guide for one day Ayodhya temple tour \r\n','Entrances fees\r\nExpenses of personal nature such as drinks, telephone, and laundry bills etc\r\nTips and porter charges\r\nAny other service/s not specified above\r\n','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRooms and hotels are subject to availability.','2024-08-12','2024-08-15',1,0,0,'2024-08-07 16:14:01','2024-08-07 17:30:50'),(746,1346,17407,2,0,0,0,0,'Madurai Diaries','Day Wise Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day : (20th Oct) : Arrive at Madurai\r\nOn arrival at the Madurai airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Madurai. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n2nd Day : (21th Oct) : Madurai Sightseeing \r\nAfter Breakfast, Visit the famous Madurai Meenakshi Temple. There are four entrances to this amazing temple complex set in six hectares. Hit one of the stone pillars in the complex with any hard object and feel incredible on hearing sweet metal sounds. It is known as musical pillars. The total number of pillars in the temple is a staggering one thousand. Sightseeing inclusive of Thirumalai Nayak palace, Gandhi Museum and flower market. Overnight at Hotel.\r\n\r\n3rd Day : (22nd Oct) : Madurai to Srirangam\r\nAfter breakfast, Transfer to Srirangam, visit Srirangam ,Local Sightseeing and shopping. Over night stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n4th Day : (23rd Oct) : Srirangam to Srirangam\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Srirangam ,Local Sightseeing and shopping. Over night stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n5th Day : (24th Oct) : Tanjore to Rameswaram\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram. The full day is for leisure. After sightseeing proceed to Rameshwaram for overnight stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n6th Day : (25th Oct) : Rameshwaram Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast sightseeing of Rameshwaram- the most sacred temple town of India is an island hallowed by the epic Ramayana, where Lord Rama is said to have visited before going into battle of Srilanka. The presiding deity is the Linga Of Sri Ramanatha Swamy, which happens to be one of the twelve Jyotirlingas of India. Rameswaram is also popularly referred to as the \'Benaras of the south\'. In order to attain Moksha it is believed that the visit to Rameswaram is mandatory. Overnight at the hotel.\r\n\r\n7th Day : (26th Oct) : Madurai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Madurai international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','',' * Meal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\n 