i Phi Island Tour\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2024-10-05','2024-10-10',1,0,0,'2024-09-20 14:45:25','2024-09-20 16:33:28'),(779,1383,355,4,0,0,0,0,'Varanasi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : Pickup from Railway station or Airport in Varanasi. Later in the evening enjoy boat ride (charges optional) Overnight stay in Hotel. \r\n\r\nDAY 02 : After breakfast, early in the morning on the second day, you will be taken on an early morning boat ride (optional charges). This boat ride is the best way to enjoy top ghats and rituals performed in each ghat. You can find many people bathing in the river. After the boat ride, you will be taken on a temple tour to enjoy the morning rituals in famous temples like, Kashi Vishwanath temple, Annapurna temple, and others. Overnight stay in Varanasi.\r\n\r\n                                                         \r\nDAY 03: In the morning, after breakfast proceed to Ayodhya. After reaching we will go on a temple tour - Ramjanmabhumi, Hanumangarhi, kanak Bhawan & Dashrath Mahal. After lunch, We will go to Guptar ghat, Nandigram. Overnight stay in Ayodhya.\r\n\r\n\r\nDAY 04: Departure from Ayodhya ','','* Economy class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation on the above-mentioned hotels or similar as per itinerary .{Hotel cannot be hold without Advance payment}\r\n* Breakfast at hotel\r\n* Meal Plan as per above in Hotels / Resorts.\r\n* Transfers & sightseeing by Innova Crysta.  (Vehicle Service from 08:00 Am to 08:00 PM after that additional cost will be applicable )\r\n* Toll, Parking, Driver Allowance.\r\n* All Applicable Tax.\r\n* Evening Aarti by motor boat with Guide in Varanasi(1:30 hours)  \r\n* 1 day Guide for Temple Tour Varanasi\r\n* 1E ricksha and 1 guide for one day Ayodhya temple tour\r\n\r\n \r\n','* Entrances fees\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as drinks, telephone, and laundry bills etc\r\n* Tips and porter charges\r\n* Any other service/s not specified above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2024-12-18','2024-12-21',1,0,0,'2024-09-20 17:36:20','2024-09-20 18:35:38'),(780,1385,2690,2,0,0,39100,14000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (11 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Krabi Hotel ( Ao- Anang Area )  1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (12 Jan)\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour By Long Tailed Boat + Lunch Box ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On SIC\r\n\r\n3rd Day (13 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Phuket Hotel ( Patong Area )  1-PRIVATE CAR KBV (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n4th Day (14 Jan)\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour By Speed Boat + Khai Island + Lunch + Transfer ( Excl. National Park Fee) on SIC\r\n\r\n5th Day (15 Jan)\r\nPhuket Half Day City Tour - Big Buddha on SIC\r\nTOURS - EX Phuket - Phuket Tiger Kingdom   1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 )\r\nPhuket Tiger Kingdom Big Tiger\r\n\r\n6th Day (16 Jan)\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket APT   1-PRIVATE CAR HKT (Max 2 + Luggage)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n\r\n','2025-01-11','2025-01-16',1,0,0,'2024-09-27 16:39:21','2024-09-27 21:00:12'),(781,1386,349,3,0,0,95000,24000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (10 Oct) :\r\nTRANSFERS : EX DXB Airport - Bur Dubai Hotel  1-MPV PVT (UAE)\r\n\r\n2nd Day (11 Oct) :\r\nHalf Day Dubai City Tour (SIC)\r\n\r\n3rd Day (12 Oct) :\r\nBurj Khalifa + DAUZ Return Transfer SIC\r\nCombo Burj Khalifa 124th + 125th Floor (non prime time)+ Dubai Aquarium with Penguin Cove SIC\r\n\r\n4th Day (13 Oct) :\r\nDesert Safari with BBQ Dinner (Trio) SIC\r\n\r\n5th Day (14 Oct) :\r\nPRIVATE TOUR : EX DUBAI - Museum of Future Return Transfer  1-MPV PVT (UAE)\r\nMuseum of Future Ticket Only (Slot Booking required -Subject to Avaialbility)\r\nPRIVATE TOUR : EX DUBAI - IMG World of Adventure One Way Transfer  1-MPV PVT (UAE)\r\nIMG Worlds of Adventure Ticket Only\r\n\r\n6th Day (15 Oct) :\r\nAIRPORT TRANSFER : EX DXB HOTEL - Bur Dubai - DXB Airport  1-MPV PVT (UAE)\r\nPRIVATE TOUR : EX DUBAI - Ski Dubai Return Transfer   1-MPV PVT (UAE)\r\nSnow Park Plus Ticket Only \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2024-10-10','2024-10-15',1,0,0,'2024-09-28 16:07:24','2024-09-28 18:39:19'),(782,1387,302,2,0,0,209400,143000,'Mumbai-Kochi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (19th Jan) : \r\nArrival at the Mumbai airport and transfer to the booked hotel. (PVT)\r\nCheck-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (20th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for Full-Day Highlights of Mumbai. Overnight at Mumbai Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 03 (21st Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Mumbai Airport for the onward journey to Kochi.\r\nArrival at the Kochi Airport and transfer to the booked hotel in Kochi. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (22nd Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nDay 05 (23rd Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level. On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India.You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (24th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 07 (25th Jan) : \r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Kumarakom. Check in at the hotel. Kumarakom is home to a wide variety of flora and fauna. where many species of migratory birds visit. Located on the banks of the Vembanad Lake, the Kumarakom Bird Sanctuary, an ornithologist\'s paradise, is a favourite haunt of migratory birds. Visit Kumarakom Birds Sanctuary and Driftwood Museum. Overnight stay at Kumarakom.\r\n\r\nDay 08 (26th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Kumarakom (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\n\r\nDay 09 (27th Jan) :\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kumarakom - Cochin Departure transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport for the onward journey to Goa.\r\nArrival at Goa Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 10 (28th Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North-Goa tour. North Goa offers a mix of adventure, history, and culture, making it a perfect destination. Visit beaches and enjoy water sports (at your own expense), temples. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 11 (29th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, get ready to experience the South-Goa Tour. Known for its pristine beaches, quiet villages, and spiritual sites, South Goa os perfect for a peaceful getaway.\r\n\r\nDay 12 (30th Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast and spend the day at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 13 (31st Jan) :\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Airport for your departure flight to Mumbai.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','',',* Economy Class Airfare (BOM-COK), (COK-GOI), (GOI-BOM)\r\n* Daily breakfast at the booked hotel\r\n* All Meals (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) are included in Houseboat\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* All tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM (especially for Kerala)\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Travel Insurance','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\nThe itineary can be adjusted as per the final flight timings.\r\n','2025-01-19','2025-01-31',1,0,0,'2024-09-30 16:58:23','2024-09-30 19:09:39'),(783,1389,302,2,0,0,28500,0,'Mumbai-Kochi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (19th Jan) : \r\nArrival at the Mumbai airport and transfer to the booked hotel. (PVT)\r\nCheck-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (20th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for Full-Day Highlights of Mumbai. Overnight at Mumbai Hotel.\r\n(Gateway of India, Siddhivinayak Temple, Bandra-Worli Sea Link, Haji Ali Dargah, Juhu Beach, Marine Drive) - All the places can be covered as per time availability and traffic congestion.\r\n\r\nDay 03 (21st Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Mumbai Airport for the onward journey to Kochi.\r\nArrival at the Kochi Airport and transfer to the booked hotel in Kochi. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (22nd Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nDay 05 (23rd Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level. On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India.You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (24th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 07 (25th Jan) : \r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Kumarakom. Check in at the hotel. Kumarakom is home to a wide variety of flora and fauna. where many species of migratory birds visit. Located on the banks of the Vembanad Lake, the Kumarakom Bird Sanctuary, an ornithologist\'s paradise, is a favourite haunt of migratory birds. Visit Kumarakom Birds Sanctuary and Driftwood Museum. Overnight stay at Kumarakom.\r\n\r\nDay 08 (26th Jan) :\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Kumarakom (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timming. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\n\r\nDay 09 (27th Jan) :\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kumarakom - Cochin Departure transfer\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport for the onward journey to Goa.\r\nArrival at Goa Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 10 (28th Jan) : \r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North-Goa tour. North Goa offers a mix of adventure, history, and culture, making it a perfect destination. Visit beaches and enjoy water sports (at your own expense), temples. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 11 (29th Jan) :\r\nAfter having breakfast, get ready to experience the South-Goa Tour. Known for its pristine beaches, quiet villages, and spiritual sites, South Goa os perfect for a peaceful getaway.\r\n\r\nDay 12 (30th Jan) :\r\nHave breakfast and spend the day at leisure.\r\n\r\nDay 13 (31st Jan) :\r\nAfter breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive to Airport for your departure flight to Mumbai.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','',',* Economy Class Airfare (BOM-COK), (COK-GOI), (GOI-BOM)\r\n* Daily breakfast at the booked hotel\r\n* All Meals (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner) are included in Houseboat\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* All tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM (especially for Kerala)\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n* Guide charges are included for 22nd Jan (i.e., 2nd day in Kochi)\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Travel Insurance','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\nThe itinerary can be adjusted as per the final flight timings.\r\nOther than Kochi Guide is not required to visit the planned places. \r\n\r\n','2025-01-19','2025-01-31',1,0,0,'2024-10-04 12:51:34','2024-10-04 19:52:43'),(784,1390,33,3,2,0,285300,60000,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 1 (13th Jan)\r\nArrival Transfer from HKG Airport to HKG Hotel Pvt\r\nCheck-in at Hotel (after 3 pm)\r\nHongKong Night Tour: Victoria peak by peak tram(1 way), Clock tower,Avenue of Star, Symphony of Light Show PVT\r\nStarts at: 4:30 pm (5 hrs tour)\r\nOvernight at Hong Kong\r\n\r\nDAY 2 (14th Jan)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nFull day Disneyland Tour with entrance ticket and return transfer (Closed on Wednesday) PVT\r\nStarts at: 10:30 am -2100 hrs\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 3 (15th Jan)\r\nBreekfast at Hotel\r\nFull day Ocean park Tour with entrance ticket and return transfer (Closed on Tuesday) PVT\r\nStarts at: 10 am - 1900 hrs\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDAY 4 (16th Jan)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nLantau Island Tour with standard cable car and return transfer PVT\r\nStarts at: 10:30 (5 hrs tour)\r\nOvernight at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 (17th Jan)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nDay at Leisure. You can explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 6 (18th Jan)\r\nBreakfast at Hotel\r\nCheckout from Hotel (Before 12 Noon)\r\nHotel to Airport Transfer on PVT\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5 nights accomodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT basis\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availa