r the departure flight - Pvt basis\r\n 	Arrive Brisbane Airport, transfer to the Gold Coast Hotel - Pvt Basis\r\n 	Check in at the Hotel\r\n 	Day is free at Leisure\r\n 	\r\n09-Jun :	After Breakfast, proceed for the tour - SIC Basis Point to Point Trfs\r\n 	Full Day Movie World Tour with Admission Tickets\r\n 	Overnight stay at the Hotel\r\n 	 \r\n10-Jun :	Early breakfast in the morning - SIC Basis Point to Point Trfs\r\n 	Full Day Sea World Tour with Admission Tickets\r\n 	Overnight stay at the Hotel\r\n 	 \r\n11-Jun : Early breakfast in the morning - SIC Basis Point to Point Trfs\r\n 	Full Day Dream World Tour with Admission Tickets\r\n 	Overnight stay at the Hotel\r\n 	 \r\n12-Jun : After Breakfast, proceed to the airport for the departure flight - Pvt Basis\r\n 	Arrive Melbourne Airport, transfer to the Hotel - Pvt Basis\r\n 	Check in at the Hotel\r\n 	Day is free at Leisure\r\n 	\r\n13-Jun :	After Breakfast, proceed for the tour\r\n 	Half day MEL City tour - SIC Basis\r\n 	Afternoon Philip Island tour with 3 Park pass (Penguin Parade, Koala Conservation Reserve, and Churchill Island) - SIC Basis\r\n 	Overnight stay at the Hotel\r\n 	 \r\n14-Jun :	Early breakfast in the morning\r\n 	Full day Great Ocean Road Tour - SIC Basis\r\n 	Overnight stay at the Hotel\r\n 	 \r\n15-Jun : After Breakfast, proceed to the airport for the departure flight - Pvt Basis\r\n','','* 10N/11D accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-06-05','2025-06-15',0,0,0,'2025-01-15 15:24:38','2025-01-15 17:03:49'),(848,1485,15506,2,0,0,155000,25000,'Turkey Diaries','Detailed Itinerary:\r\n \r\nDay 01:   Istanbul - Arrival â€“ Dinner Cruise on Bosphorus, SIC Basis\r\nWelcome to Istanbul! Meet our team at the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in and have a leisure day.\r\nEvening transfer to cruise port for Night Show on Bosphorus. Set Menu dinner + soft drinks.\r\n \r\nDay 02:   Istanbul City Tour with Lunch \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nHead back in time and discover the old world of the Sultanahmet area during this full-day small-group guided walking tour in Istanbul. This tour explores the amazing UNESCO World Heritage-listed Blue Mosque which exemplifies why Istanbul is the city where east meets west. Enjoy a walk through the famous Topkapi Palace where Sultan\'s roamed and harems flourished. Plus, spend time observing Hagia Ireneâ€™s Byzantine architecture and stroll through the Grand Bazaar to witness handicrafts created by local artists.\r\nâ€¢  Topkapi Palace closed on Tuesdays / Grand Bazaar closed on Sundays / Blue Mosque outside visit on Fridays!\r\n \r\nDay 03:   Istanbul to Cappadocia by flight\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nAccording to your flight time, check out from your hotel and transfer to the airport (Flight cost is included). Arrive at Airport and drive to your hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 04:   Cappadocia Red Tour with Lunch\r\nMeet your guide and visit the Devrent and Pasabag valleys, to see the amazing fairy chimneys of Cappadocia. Then you will be driven to the famous pottery town called Avanos. After lunch, drive to the Zelve Open Air Museum. Our last stop will be Uchisar town.\r\n \r\nDay 05: Cappadocia to Antalya by flight\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nAccording to your flight time, check out from your hotel and transfer to the airport (Flight cost is included). Arrive at Antalya Airport and drive to your hotel. \r\n \r\nDay 06:   Antalya City Tour with Boat Trip and Duden Waterfall with Lunch\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nDiscover Antalya on this full-day Sightseeing tour. Enjoy the boat trip from the ancient harbor to the Lower Duden Waterfall cascading into the sea. Take advantage of 1 hour of free time to explore the Old Town of Antalya (Kaleici): Hadrianus Gate, city walls, Clock Tower, and Ancient Harbor.\r\n \r\nDay 07:   Pamukkale Hierapolis and Cleopatra\'s Pool Tour with lunch from Antalya\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel. \r\nHierapolis (\"Holy City\") was an ancient Greco-Roman city in Phrygia located on hot springs in South West Anatolia. Its ruins are adjacent to modern Pamukkale. Hierapolis is a UNESCO World Heritage Site. The hot springs there have been used as a spa since the 2nd Century B.C.E. and people came to soothe their ailments with many of them retiring or dying here. Some of the highlights; the large necropolis is filled with sarcophagi, the main street with the gates and latrines, cathedral, the theatre and St. Philipâ€™s tomb. The hot springs causing cascades which are called the Cotton Castle. Because of the distance we have to leave Antalya early and return late but itâ€™s worth it to experience this wonderful place. beginning to end for base approx walking time over 45 min with theatre visit.\r\nNote: Cleopatraâ€™s Pool entrance ticket is not included.\r\n \r\nDay 08:  Antalya to Istanbul by flight\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nAccording to your flight time, check out from your hotel and transfer to the airport (Flight cost is included). Arrive at Istanbul Airport and drive to your hotel.\r\n \r\nDay 09:   Departure        \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel.\r\nAccording to your flight time transfer to Airport. End of our service.\r\n\r\n\r\nOptional Tours cost:\r\n\r\nHot Air Balloon ride cost - INR 24000 per person (dynamic rates)\r\n','','â€¢	Daily Breakfast\r\nâ€¢	Economy Class airfare\r\nâ€¢	Return Airport transfers in Istanbul, PVT Basis\r\nâ€¢	Return Airport transfers in Cappadocia, PVT Basis\r\nâ€¢	Return Airport transfers in Antalya, PVT Basis\r\nâ€¢	Dinner Cruise on Bosphorus, SIC Basis\r\nâ€¢	Istanbul City Tour with Lunch, SIC Basis\r\nâ€¢	Cappadocia Red Tour with lunch, SIC Basis\r\nâ€¢	Pamukkale & Hierapolis Tour from Kusadasi, SIC Basis\r\nâ€¢	Antalya City Tour with Boat Trip and Duden Waterfall with Lunch, SIC Basis\r\nâ€¢	Cappadocia Sunset ATV Tour (2 hrs)\r\nâ€¢	GST\r\n','TCS\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nAll the services are subject to availability & price may vary at the time of booking.','2025-02-09','2025-02-17',1,0,0,'2025-01-17 18:17:43','2025-01-20 16:43:19'),(849,1487,15518,2,2,0,55700,12000,'Kerala Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n Day 1 :(22 Mar 2025 - Saturday) Cochin Arrival\r\n\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (23 Mar 2025 - Sunday) Cochin Hotel to Alleppey\r\n\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi\r\nTransfers - Cochin Hotel to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (24 Mar 2025 - Monday) Alleppey to Kanyakumari\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Lemon Tree Vembanad Lake Resort\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kanyakumari\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Kanyakumari. Upon arrival check into the hotel. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (25 Mar 2025 - Tuesday) Kanyakumari sightseeing 2\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Annai Celestial resorts\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kanyakumari sightseeing 2\r\nMorning after breakfast sightseeing of Kanyakumari - Kanyakumari is the southernmost end of Tamil Nadu, the Landâ€™s End of India or the point where the three seas meet - the Bay of Bengal, The Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean. Later visit Kumari amman temple dedicated to the virgin goddess Kanyakumari (Parvati) who stands guard over the country. The temple is built at the spot where the goddess is believed to have waited for her consort Lord Siva. Gandhi Memorial, constructed at the spot where the ashes of Mahatma Gandhi were kept for public view in an urn before a portion was immersed into the three seas. Vivekananda Memorial built on the Vivekananda Rock where the great Philosopher and guide Swami Vivekananda went into meditation that transformed him into one of the most charismatic spiritual leader. The Thiruvalluvar Statue, or the Valluvar Statue, is a 133-feet tall stone sculpture of the Tamil poet and philosopher Valluvar, author of the Tirukkural, an ancient Tamil work on secular ethics and morality. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : (26 Mar 2025 - Wednesday) Kanyakumari to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Annai Celestial resorts\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kanyakumari to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Innova\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-03-22','2025-03-26',1,0,0,'2025-01-20 19:15:50','2025-01-21 10:41:23'),(850,1488,15518,2,2,0,82900,18000,'Kerala Diaries','Sugge