les who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timing. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Relax HouseBoat (Meal Plan - APAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (26 Mar 2025 - Wednesday) Alleppey to Kanyakumari\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Relax HouseBoat\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Kanyakumari\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Kanyakumari. On the way Visit Sree Padmanabha Swamy temple. Upon arrival check into the hotel. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Annai Celestial resorts (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (27 Mar 2025 - Thursday) Kanyakumari sightseeing 2\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Annai Celestial resorts\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Kanyakumari sightseeing 2\r\nMorning after breakfast sightseeing of Kanyakumari - Kanyakumari is the southernmost end of Tamil Nadu, the Landâ€™s End of India or the point where the three seas meet - the Bay of Bengal, The Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean. Later visit Kumari amman temple dedicated to the virgin goddess Kanyakumari (Parvati) who stands guard over the country. The temple is built at the spot where the goddess is believed to have waited for her consort Lord Siva. Gandhi Memorial, constructed at the spot where the ashes of Mahatma Gandhi were kept for public view in an urn before a portion was immersed into the three seas. Vivekananda Memorial built on the Vivekananda Rock where the great Philosopher and guide Swami Vivekananda went into meditation that transformed him into one of the most charismatic spiritual leader. The Thiruvalluvar Statue, or the Valluvar Statue, is a 133-feet tall stone sculpture of the Tamil poet and philosopher Valluvar, author of the Tirukkural, an ancient Tamil work on secular ethics and morality. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Annai Celestial resort (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 7 : (28 Mar 2025 - Friday) Kanyakumari to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Annai Celestial resorts\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kanyakumari to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Innova\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-03-22','2025-03-26',1,0,0,'2025-01-21 16:07:59','2025-01-21 16:53:31'),(851,1490,15512,4,0,0,173500,50000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival in Hanoi & Half-Day City Tour (PVT)\r\n- Timing: Arrival, 2:00 PM hotel check-in.  \r\n- Activities: Visit Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum, Ba Dinh Square, Tran Quoc Pagoda, Hoan Kiem Lake, Hanoi Old Quarter.  \r\nOvernight: Hanoi.  \r\n\r\nDay 2: Ninh Binh â€“ Trang An or Tam Coc & Hoa Lu Tour (SIC)\r\n- Timing: Full-day tour (Shared).  \r\n- Activities: Boat trip in Trang An/Tam Coc, explore water caves, visit Hoa Lu Ancient Capital (Dinh, Le, and Ly Dynasty temples).  \r\n- Meals: Breakfast/ Lunch.  \r\n- Overnight: Hanoi.  \r\n\r\nDay 3: Hanoi to Ha Long Bay â€“ Cruise Overnight  \r\n- Timing: Morning transfer to Halong Bay, cruise check-in.  \r\n- Activities: Cruise through limestone islands, swimming, kayaking (weather permitting).  \r\n- Meals: Breakfast, Lunch, Dinner.  \r\n- Overnight: Onboard the cruise.  \r\n\r\nDay 4: Ha Long Bay to Hanoi & Fly to Da Nang  \r\n- Timing: Early morning Tai Chi, cruise activities, disembark by 11:30 AM.  \r\n- Activities: Sunrise Tai Chi, scenic cruising, transfer to Hanoi for flight to Da Nang. \r\n- Reach to Hanoi around 3pm and transfer to airport fly to Da Nang \r\n- Meals: Breakfast /Brunch.  \r\n- Overnight: Da Nang.  \r\n\r\nDay 5: Cam Thanh Coconut Forest & Hoi An Tour (SIC) 12:30 â€“ 18:30\r\n- Timing: 12:30 PM â€“ 6:30 PM (Shared).  \r\n- Activities: Basket boat ride, fishing village exploration, Hoi An walking tour (Market, Museum, Japanese Covered Bridge, Assembly Halls).  \r\n- Meals: Breakfast.  \r\n- Overnight: Da Nang.  \r\n\r\nDay 6: Full-Day Bana Hills & Golden Bridge (SIC)\r\n- Timing: Morning departure (Shared).  \r\n- Activities: Cable car ride, Golden Bridge, Ling Ung Pagoda, Chua Mountain peak, Fantasy Park with free games, waterfalls, and scenic trails.  \r\n- Meals: Breakfast.  \r\n- Overnight: Da Nang.  \r\n\r\nDay 7: Departure from Da Nang (No guide) \r\n- Timing: Free time until airport transfer.  \r\n- Activities: Leisure on your own.  \r\n\r\n','','Economy Class airfare.\r\nAll road transportation in 16-seats Air-conditional vehicle \r\n5 nights hotel accommodation on Twin/double/triple sharing with daily breakfast\r\n1 night on Halong Bay cruise Twin/double/ triple sharing with all meals\r\nCable car to Ba Na Hill\r\nBoat trip in Cam Thanh \r\nSurchage 3 Feb Tet Holiday \r\nAll meals mentioned as per program above\r\nEnglish speaking guide during sightseeing\r\nEntrance fees as per above program\r\nDrinking water on transfer during visit 500ml*2/person/day\r\nGST\r\n','Other meals & Beverages not mentioned above\r\nEarly check-in/ Late check-out\r\nCompulsory tips for guide and driver US$3/client/day\r\nPersonal expense such as laundry, meals or drinks during, etc..,\r\nOther items not mentioned in above\r\nTCS\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2025-02-02','2025-02-08',1,0,0,'2025-01-21 18:58:11','2025-01-21 20:08:05'),(852,1491,15512,4,0,0,219000,50000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01: Arrival in Hanoi\r\n- Arrival in Hanoi.\r\n- Pick-up from the airport and transfer to hotel for check-in  \r\n- Afternoon city tour: Temple of Literature, Hoa Lo Prison Museum  \r\n- Evening: Explore local beer at Ta Hien Streets, bars, or shopping malls  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Hanoi  \r\n\r\nDay 02: Hanoi to Ninh Binh Karst Landscape  \r\n- Morning: Depart for Ninh Binh  \r\n- Visit Hoa Lu Ancient Capital, cycling around the village  \r\n- Afternoon: Boat ride at Tam Coc, buffet lunch  \r\n- Evening: Return to Hanoi  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Hanoi  \r\n\r\nDay 03: Hanoi to Halong Bay Night Cruise \r\n- Morning: Depart for Halong Bay  \r\n- Seafood lunch on board, visit floating fishing villages and limestone caves  \r\n- Afternoon: Surprising Cave, Titop Island  \r\n- Evening: Sunset party, cooking class, and dinner on the sundeck  \r\n- Accommodation: Overnight on cruise  \r\n\r\nDay 04: Halong Bay to Hanoi - Fly to Danang\r\n- Morning: Breakfast on board, kayaking at Luon Cave  \r\n- Return to Hanoi, fly to Danang  \r\n- Evening: Arrival in Danang and transfer to hotel  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Danang  \r\n\r\nDay 05: Danang - Ba Na Hills & Golden Bridge  \r\n- Morning: Cable car to Ba Na Hills, visit Golden Bridge  \r\n- Afternoon: Visit Fantasy Park, enjoy rides and attractions  \r\n- Evening: Return to Danang  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Danang  \r\n\r\nDay 06: Danang - Fly to Ho Chi Minh City \r\n- Morning: Breakfast at hotel, check-out, flight to Ho Chi Minh City  \r\n- Afternoon: Arrive in Ho Chi Minh City, transfer to hotel  \r\n- Evening: Explore the city, Walking Street  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Ho Chi Minh City  \r\n\r\nDay 07: Ho Chi Minh City - Cu Chi Tunnels \r\n- Morning: Visit Cu Chi Tunnels  \r\n- Afternoon: Explore tunnels and learn about war history, tea and cassava served  \r\n- Evening:Return to Ho Chi Minh City  \r\n- Accommodation: Hotel in Ho Chi Minh City  \r\n\r\nDay 08: Departure from Ho Chi Minh City\r\n- Morning: Breakfast at hotel, check-out  \r\n- Flight: Departure  ','','Economy Class airfare.\r\nAccommodation with sharing room\r\nMeals as mentioned in itinerary of daily inclusion term \r\nEnglish speaking guides for tour and excursion except leisure time\r\nTransfers with modern conditioned vehicles\r\nTours and excursion as mentioned in the itinerary\r\nEntrance fees for mentioned visits\r\nLocal travel insurance included in sightseeing tickets\r\nWater 2 bottle 500ml / pax/ day in car\r\nGovernment taxes & Service charge\r\nAll tours & transfers on Pvt basis except Halong bay cruise shuttle transfer.\r\nTravel Insurance\r\nVisa\r\nGST\r\n','Other services and meals than mentioned\r\nEarly check in & late check out\r\nTipping for guide and driver @ USD 5 PP per day\r\n TCS\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2025-02-02','2025-02-09',1,0,0,'2025-01-22 15:01:39','2025-01-22 16:03:45'),(853,1492,15518,2,2,0,105000,22200,'Kerala Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (22 Mar 2025 - Saturday) Cochin Arrival\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin Arrival\r\nArrival at Cochin and transfer to hotel. Check in at Hotel. In Cochin Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Starlit Suites Kochi (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (23 Mar 2025 - Sunday) Cochin to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Starlit Suites Kochi\r\nTransfers - Cochin to Alleppey (House Boat)\r\nMorning after breakfast, check out and proceed to Alleppey (House Boat) Check in 12.00 noon and Enjoy the backwaters, scenery and different places in Kerala Style House boats from 12Noon. Observe the daily life of peoples who lives near the lake/canal while cruising. In the houseboat you will be greeted with welcome drink. Lunch, Dinner and breakfast will be provided as per the timing. Evening Tea/Coffee & snacks will be provided. Overnight stay in the houseboat.\"\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Relax HouseBoat (Meal Plan - APAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (24 Mar 2025 - Monday) Alleppey to Munnar\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Relax HouseBoat\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level.On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Visit Matupetti dam, Echo pint. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Munnar Queen (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (25 Mar 2025 - Tuesday) Munnar to Madhurai\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Munnar Queen\r\nTransfers - Munnar to Madurai\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive to Madurai. Visit Meenakshi Temple, Tirumalai Nayak Palace. Overnight stay at Hotel.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel POPPYS (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (26 Mar 2025 - Wednesday) Madurai To Rameshwaram \r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - POPPYS\r\nTransfers - Madurai To Rameshwaram \r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed towards Rameshwaram. Visit Sri Ramanatha Swamy temple, Dhanushkodi, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman temple, Villoondi Theertham etc. Overnight at the Resort/hotel.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Daiwik Hotel Rameswaram (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (27 Mar 2025 - Thursday) Rameshwaram to Kanyakumari\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Daiwik Hotel Rameswaram\r\nTransfers - Rameshwaram to Kanyakumari\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and proceed to Kanyakumari, Kanyakumari is the southernmost end of Tamil Nadu, the Landâ€™s End of India or the point where the three seas meet - the Bay of Bengal, The Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean. Later visit Kumari amman temple dedicated to the virgin goddess Kanyakumari (Parvati) who stands guard over the country. The temple is built at the spot where the goddess is believed to have waited for her consort Lord Siva. Gandhi Memorial, constructed at the spot where the ashes of Mahatma Gandhi were kept for public view in an urn before a portion was immersed into the three seas. Vivekananda Memorial built on the Vivekananda Rock where the great Philosopher and guide Swami Vivekananda went into meditation that transformed him into one of the most charismatic spiritual leader. The Thiruvalluvar Statue, or the Valluvar Statue, is a 133-feet tall stone sculpture of the Tamil poet and philosopher Valluvar, author of the Tirukkural, an ancient Tamil work on secular ethics and morality. \r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Annai Celestial resorts (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 7 : (28 Mar 2025 - Friday) Kanyakymari to Kovalam\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - Annai Celestial resorts\r\nTransfers - Kanyakymari to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and  transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel.  Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel KTDC Samudra Kovalam (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 8 : (29 Mar 2025 - Saturday) Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - KTDC Samudra Kovalam\r\nDeparture Transfer - Kovalam to Trivandrum Drop\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Trivandrum Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* 7N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Innova\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-03-22','2025-03-29',0,0,0,'2025-01-22 16:25:32','2025-01-22 17:35:50'),(854,1493,17406,6,0,0,150000,30000,'South India Diaries','Suggested Itinerary  \r\n\r\nDay 1: 13 May 2025 - Arrive at Madurai\r\nArrival at Madurai airport/railway station. Transfer to the hotel. Visit the renowned Meenakshi Temple, Thirumalai Nayak Palace, Gandhi Museum, and flower market.  \r\nOvernight Stay: Hotel POPPYS (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 2: 14 May 2025 - Madurai to Rameshwaram \r\nBreakfast at Hotel POPPYS. Transfer to Rameshwaram, home to Ramanathaswamy Temple, one of the 12 Jyotirlingas. Explore the templeâ€™s iconic hallways and carvings.  \r\nOvernight Stay: Daiwik Hotel Rameswaram (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 3: 15 May 2025 - Rameshwaram  \r\nAfter breakfast, visit Ramanathaswamy Temple, Dhanushkodi, Pamban Bridge, Dr. APJ Abdul Kalam Museum, Sri Panchmukhi Hanuman Temple, and Villoondi Theertham.  \r\nOvernight Stay: Daiwik Hotel Rameswaram (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 4: 16 May 2025 - Rameshwaram to Kanyakumari\r\nBreakfast at Daiwik Hotel. Proceed to Kanyakumari. Visit Kumari Amman Temple, Gandhi Memorial, Vivekananda Memorial, and the towering Thiruvalluvar Statue.  \r\nOvernight Stay: Annai Celestial Resorts (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 5: 17 May 2025 - Kanyakumari to Trivandrum \r\nBreakfast at Annai Celestial. En route to Trivandrum, stop at Poovar Island and Kovalam Beach. Explore Trivandrumâ€™s colonial architecture and galleries.  \r\nOvernight Stay: Forte Manor (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 6: 18 May 2025 - Trivandrum  \r\nVisit Sree Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthira Malika Palace, Napier Museum, and Zoo (closed on Mondays).  \r\nOvernight Stay: Forte Manor (CPAI).  \r\n\r\nDay 7: 19 May 2025 - Departure \r\nBreakfast at Forte Manor. Transfer to Trivandrum airport/railway station for onward journey.  \r\n\r\nTour ends with happy memories!','','Economy  class airfare.\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAll Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\nGST\r\n','All those which are not mentioned above\r\nEntry Fees \r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature\r\nAny Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\nAyurveda Charges\r\n\r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2025-05-13','2025-05-19',1,0,0,'2025-01-24 18:04:04','2025-01-24 18:04:04'),(855,1494,195,2,0,0,89400,36000,'Europe Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 : 14 Oct\r\nArrival at the Baku Airport and drive towards the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening proceed for the Night Tour illuminated by Baku Lights (2 hrs)\r\n\r\nDay 02 : 15 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for Gobustan, Mud Volcano, Fire Temple and Burning Mountain (Entrance fee, Lunch and hotel pick and drop included). \r\n\r\nDay 03 : 16 Oct\r\n After breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive towards the Baku Airport for your onward flight towards Istanbul. Arrival at the Airport and drive towards the pre-booked hotel in Istanbul. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening proceed for Turkish Night on the Bosphorus (unlimited soft drinks without any meals included)\r\n\r\nDay 04 : 17 Oct\r\n Have breakfast at the hotel and head for Hagia Sophia, Basilica Cistern, Grand Bazaar Skip the Ticket Line.\r\n\r\nDay 05 : 18 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and drive towards the Istanbul airport for your onward flight towards Budapest. Arrival at the airport and drive towards the pre-booked hotel in Budapest. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 06 : 19 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast proceed for City Sightseeing Budapest Hop-On Hop-Off Bus and Boat Tour (24hr ticket). Boat time till 5 pm. (Approx 1.5 hrs tour)\r\nEvening : Danube Beat Boat Party Cruise Ticket (Standard Entry 21:30), Budapest (Standard without bubbles and drinks)\r\n\r\nDay 07 : 20 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and drive towards the Budapest Airport for your onward journey to Prague. Arrival at the Prague Airport and drive towards the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. \r\n\r\nDay 08 : 21 Oct\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel and proceed for Prague Jewish Quarter Walking Tour with Admission Tickets (Prague Synagogues with tickets 10:00), (Approx 2.5 hrs tour)\r\nCharles Bridge and Prague Castle Walking Tour (Charles Bridge and Prague Castle Walking Tour 14:00), Prague\r\n\r\nDay 09 : 22 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and drive towards the Prague Airport for your onward journey towards Georgia. Arrival at the Georgia Airport and drive towards the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 10 : 23 Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and explore the city at your own-cost after check-out. Around 9pm transfer from Georgia hotel to Airport.\r\n\r\nDay 11 : 24 Oct\r\nEarly morning flight (01:20)\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare \r\n* Internal sector flights included\r\n* 9N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Transfer from Baku Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Baku hotel to Baku Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Istanbul Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Istanbul hotel to Istanbul Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Budapest Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Budapest hotel to Budapest Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Prague Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Prague hotel to Prague Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Georgia Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Georgia hotel to Georgia Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-10-14','2025-10-24',0,0,0,'2025-01-28 18:15:07','2025-02-01 17:42:33'),(856,1498,20507,4,0,0,40000,14000,'Prayagraj Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Feb : At 10 pm, leave from Delhi Airport to Vrindavan. Late night check-in at hotel. \r\n\r\n2nd Feb : Early morning check-out from hotel. And cover Vrindavan and Agra as per time availability. Night stay in Agra. \r\n\r\n3rd Feb : Early Morning check-out from Agra and leave for Lucknow. Local sightseeing in Lucknow. Night stay in Lucknow. \r\n\r\n4th Feb : Early morning leave for Prayagraj. Night stay in Prayagraj at self-booked hotel. \r\n\r\n5th Feb : Early morning leave for Varanasi. After Darshan and local visit drop at Varanasi Airport around 9 pm.\r\n','','* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* 1N accommodation in Varanasi\r\n* 1N accommodation in Agra\r\n* 1N accommodation in Lucknow','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-02-01','2025-02-05',0,0,0,'2025-01-29 13:56:42','2025-01-29 17:46:50'),(857,1499,8,2,0,0,0,0,'Kolkata Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Tuesday 18th February) : Kolkata Airport to Hotel - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour\r\nOn arrival at Airport & transfer to hotel. Check-in to hotel & rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at Kolkata\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Wednesday 19th February) : Gangasagar - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours\r\nAfter early breakfast start for full day excursion to Gangasagar â€“ An island in the confluence of River Ganga & Bay of Bengal & famous for Kapil Muni Ashram which is considered to be a great religious significance. Evening return back to Kolkata. Overnight s