nh City (PVT)\r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh, transfer downtown, and check in at your hotel (14:00). Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, pick upâ€™s airport guide, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (PVT) (B)\r\nDepart at 7:30 AM (time varies by hotel) for a scenic boat ride to a historic floating market on the Tien River. Enjoy fresh fruits, folk music, and visit local businesses crafting coconut candy and rice popcorn. Explore a village by foot and bike, and admire an ancient houseâ€™s traditional architecture. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh City fly to Danang â€“ Hoi An Ancient Town Half Day (B) (PRIVATE)\r\nArrive in Da Nang and transfer to Hoi An, a historic 16th-century trading port. Check in at the hotel (14:00), then explore top attractions, including the Japanese Covered Bridge, Fujian Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Hoi An Market, and enjoy a lantern boat excursion. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, lantern boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (PVT)(B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:00 AM for Ba Na Hills (35km from Da Nang). Take the Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Old Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and Orchid Garden. Experience the hill-climbing train, Le Jardin Dâ€™Amour, and walk across the famous Golden Bridge for panoramic views. Enjoy lunch at your own expense, then explore Fantasy Park with various indoor games. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nEntrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, sharing guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Da Nang â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for a flight to Hanoi. Upon arrival, transfer to the city center and check in at the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (outside), One Pillar Pagoda, and Hanoi Train Street. Explore Hoan Kiem Lake, stroll through the Old Quarterâ€™s \"36 Streets,\" and shop at Dong Xuan Market. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) \r\nDepart at 8:00 AM for Ha Long Bay (4-hour drive). Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and check into your cabin. Enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through the bay. Stop for a swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for a sunset view before a seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nNote: The itinerary may vary by cruise.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits. \r\n\r\nDay 7 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/Brunch)\r\nWake up early to enjoy the stunning sunrise over Ha Long Bay. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a local rowboat ride. Enjoy brunch while cruising back to the pier, then return to Hanoi. Transfer to the airport (without a guide) for your flight home. Goodbye and see you again!\r\nNote: The cruise itinerary may vary.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy class Airfare\r\n* Internal sector flights included\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2025-03-16','2025-03-22',1,0,0,'2025-02-05 13:56:17','2025-02-05 19:41:44'),(863,1506,15494,4,0,0,8700,6168,'Goa Diaries','Day 1: Airport to Hotel Transfer\r\nDay 2: North Goa Tour\r\nDay 3: Day at leisure\r\nDay 4: Hotel to Airport Transfer','Rooms are subject to availability\r\n','Economy Class airfare\r\nDaily Breakfast\r\nAirport Transfers on pvt basis\r\nNorth Goa Tours.\r\nVehicle : Innova Crysta\r\nGST\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense\r\nAnything which is not mentioned in inclusions','Airfare is dynamic.\r\nRooms are subject to availability','2025-02-06','2025-02-09',0,0,0,'2025-02-05 17:24:26','2025-02-05 18:14:59'),(864,1507,15512,5,1,0,319314,61686,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City (PVT)\r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh, transfer downtown, and check in at your hotel (14:00). Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, pick upâ€™s airport guide, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (PVT) (B)\r\nDepart at 7:30 AM (time varies by hotel) for a scenic boat ride to a historic floating market on the Tien River. Enjoy fresh fruits, folk music, and visit local businesses crafting coconut candy and rice popcorn. Explore a village by foot and bike, and admire an ancient houseâ€™s traditional architecture. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh City fly to Danang â€“ Hoi An Ancient Town Half Day (B) (PRIVATE)\r\nArrive in Da Nang and transfer to Hoi An, a historic 16th-century trading port. Check in at the hotel (14:00), then explore top attractions, including the Japanese Covered Bridge, Fujian Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Hoi An Market, and enjoy a lantern boat excursion. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, lantern boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (PVT)(B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:00 AM for Ba Na Hills (35km from Da Nang). Take the Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Old Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and Orchid Garden. Experience the hill-climbing train, Le Jardin Dâ€™Amour, and walk across the famous Golden Bridge for panoramic views. Enjoy lunch at your own expense, then explore Fantasy Park with various indoor games. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nEntrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, sharing guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Da Nang â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for a flight to Hanoi. Upon arrival, transfer to the city center and check in at the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (outside), One Pillar Pagoda, and Hanoi Train Street. Explore Hoan Kiem Lake, stroll through the Old Quarterâ€™s \"36 Streets,\" and shop at Dong Xuan Market. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) \r\nDepart at 8:00 AM for Ha Long Bay (4-hour drive). Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and check into your cabin. Enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through the bay. Stop for a swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for a sunset view before a seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nNote: The itinerary may vary by cruise.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits. \r\n\r\nDay 7 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/Brunch)\r\nWake up early to enjoy the stunning sunrise over Ha Long Bay. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a local rowboat ride. Enjoy brunch while cruising back to the pier, then return to Hanoi. Transfer to the airport (without a guide) for your flight home. Goodbye and see you again!\r\nNote: The cruise itinerary may vary.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat.\r\n\r\n','','* Internal sector flights included\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS \r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n','2025-03-16','2025-03-22',0,0,0,'2025-02-06 13:19:35','2025-02-25 12:39:42'),(865,1509,624,2,0,0,169200,34000,'Arunachal Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Sunday 16th March) : Guwahati Airport to Tezpur - Transfer (Approx Distance 170 km)\r\nMeet and greet on arrival at Guwahati Airport / Railway Station and transfer to Tezpur. On arrival check in to the hotel. Evening is free for leisure. Overnight stay at Tezpur.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Monday 17th March) : Tezpur to Dirang - Transfer and On the way Sightseeing (Approx Distance 200 km)\r\nAfter breakfast, check out and drive to Dirang. En route, visit Tipi Orchidarium with over 500 orchid species and stop at Nag Temple. Enjoy scenic views and waterfalls along the way. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. In the afternoon, visit an Apple orchard, Kiwi Farm (seasonal), Dirang Monastery, and Kalachakra Monastery. Dirang is also famous for its hot water springs. Overnight stay at Dirang.\r\n+ (Contd. 2nd Day) : To enter Arunachal Pradesh, an Inner Line Permit (ILP) is required, issued by the state government.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Tuesday 18th March) : Dirang to Tawang - Transfer and on the way Sightseeing (Approx Distance: 130 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, check out and drive to Tawang, the Land of Hidden Paradise. En route, enjoy the stunning Sela Pass (13,700 ft) and Sela Lake, which remains frozen most of the year. Visit Jaswant Garh War Memorial, dedicated to a brave soldier from the 1962 Indo-China war. Continue to Nuranng Falls, famous for scenes from the movie Koyla. Arrive in Tawang, check in, and enjoy the evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Tawang.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Wednesday 19th March) : Tawang - Local Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast, visit Tawang Monastery, a 17th-century complex with 65 buildings and an 8-meter gilded Buddha statue. Next, explore Urgeling Gompa, the 6th Dalai Lamaâ€™s birthplace, and the War Memorial dedicated to the 1962 Sino-Indian war martyrs. Visit the local craft center for masks, carpets, and mementos. Evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Tawang.\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Thursday 20th March) : Tawang to Bomdila - Transfer and Sightseeing (Approx Distance: 170 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Bomdila (8,200 ft.), known for its Buddhist monasteries and cool climate. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. Visit Gontse Rabgyaling Monastery (Upper Gonpa) and Thub-Chog Gatsel Ling Monastery (Lower Gonpa). Enjoy panoramic views of the Himalayas. In the evening, explore the local market. Overnight stay at Bomdila.\r\n\r\n6th Day - (Friday 21st March) : Bomdila to Kaziranga - Transfer (Approx Distance: 210 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, check out and transfer to Kaziranga. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. Evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Kaziranga.\r\n\r\n7th Day - (Saturday 22nd March) : Kaziranga - National Park Safari \r\nEarly morning, enjoy an elephant ride in Kaziranga National Park to spot rhinos, deer, wild buffalo, and possibly tigers. Return to the resort for breakfast and relax. In the afternoon, take a jeep safari through the park and visit Kaziranga Orchid Park. Return to the hotel for the overnight stay.\r\nNote: Elephant rides and jeep safaris are subject to availability and managed by the Assam Forest Department.\r\n\r\n8th Day - (Sunday 23rd March) : Kaziranga to Shillong - Transfer (Approx Distance: 295 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Shillong (4,900 ft.), known as the \"Scotland of the East.\" En route, visit the serene Umium Lake. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. Evening at leisure. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n9th Day - (Monday 24th March) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion (Approx Distance: 60 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), the wettest place in the world. En route, enjoy views of Mawdok-Dympep Valley and visit Nohkalikai Falls, Seven Sisters Falls, and Mawsmai Caves. In the evening, return to Shillong, stopping at Elephanta Falls. Overnight stay at Shillong. \r\n\r\n10th Day - (Tuesday 25th March) : Shillong to Mawlynnong and Dawki - Excursion (Approx Distance: 120 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Mawlynnong, Asia\'s Cleanest Village, to see the living root bridge and a balancing boulder. Next, visit Dawki near the India-Bangladesh border for stunning views of the Umangot River. In the evening, return to Shillong for an overnight stay. \r\n\r\n11th Day - (Wednesday 26th March) : Shillong to Guwahati - Sightseeing and Transfer (Approx Distance: 100 Km)\r\nAfter breakfast, check out and visit Don Bosco Museum (closed on Sundays) and Ward\'s Lake. Then, drive to Guwahati, check in to your hotel. In the evening, enjoy an optional Golden Sunset Cruise on the Brahmaputra (direct payment). Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\n12th Day - (Thursday 27th March) : Guwahati Hotel to Guwahati Airport - Transfer \r\nAfter breakfast, visit Kamakhya Temple (8:00 AM - 1:00 PM & 3:00 PM until dark). Transfer to Guwahati Airport/Railway Station for your onward journey. Note: Temple visit may be adjusted based on your departure time.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Accommodation on twin Sharing Basis. \r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan (as mentioned above) \r\n* 1-Ertiga / Similar as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive A/c vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (ac will not run in hill area) \r\nâ€¢ All hotel taxes (as per itinerary). \r\nâ€¢ ILP \r\nâ€¢ 01 Jeep safari & 01 Elephant safari Once during the tour \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage. \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary. \r\nâ€¢ Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any. \r\nâ€¢ VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot). \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure. \r\nâ€¢ Insurance. \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nPermit require for Arunachal Pradesh (ILP). It is mandatory that guest should carry 02 copies of passport size photograph, original photo ID proof with photo copy (identity card Voter ID card / Pass-port / Driving License / Aadhar Card) for processing the permit. PAN Card is not acceptable for issuance of the Permit.\r\nPermit also require for traveling to Bumla Pass. Requires 02 more copies of passport size photographs along with original photo ID proof.\r\nSupplement cost (If guest want any add on Service must be Informe at the time of Booking):\r\nBumla pass: Rs.6, 500/- per Sumo car.\r\n\r\n','2025-03-16','2025-03-27',1,0,0,'2025-02-08 17:18:14','2025-02-08 17:55:53'),(866,1510,355,2,0,0,44000,12000,'Varanasi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival at the Airport and transfer to the pre-booked hotel (Pvt). Check-in at the hotel and relax. Visit the Kashi Vishwanath Temple. Head to Dashashwamedh Ghat in the evening for the world-famous Ganga Aarti.  Experience the mesmerizing rituals and the spiritual ambience of the Aarti performed to honor the river Ganges. Have dinner at the hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, proceed for Sarnath (around 20 mins from Varanasi city). Visit significant sites including Dhamek Stupa, Archaeological Museum, Chaukhandi Stupa. Evening at leisure. Have dinner at the hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Depart early in the morning for a boat ride on the Ganges at sunrise. The ride offers serene views of the ghats and temples as the city wakes up. Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out from the hotel. Transfer to the Varanasi Airport (Pvt) for your homebound journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N accommodation with breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nWill drop near places of temple as govt. will allow','2025-02-26','2025-02-28',1,0,0,'2025-02-10 17:09:23','2025-02-10 18:58:50'),(867,1511,3511,22,0,0,0,0,'Gangtok Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 21st February) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours\r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Gangtok (5,500 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Gangtok\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 22nd February) : Gangtok to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\nAfter breakfast, start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft. / 37 Kms. / 02 Hrs. from Gangtok) and further drive to New Baba Mandir (13,200 ft. / 16 Kms. / 01 Hrs. from Tsomgo Lake). Evening back to Gangtok. Overnight stay at Gangtok. Note: In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing. Due to winter season (heavy snow) vehicle will be able to drive till Snow point on the way to Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 23rd February) : Gangtok to Darjeeling - Halfday Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 7 hours\r\nAfter breakfast Check out from Hotel & enjoy a half day city tour visiting Plant Conservatory, Dro-dul Chorten & Gonjang Monastery. Afternoon proceed to Darjeeling. On arrival, check-in to your hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Monday 24th February) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill & Joyride\r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km\r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM for joy ride , Later visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Evening free for shopping or leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nNote: Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n+ (Contd. 4th Day) : Darjeeling Himalayan Railway - Steam Engine - Ticket\r\nThe Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (DHR), a UNESCO World Heritage Site since December 5, 1999, is an iconic narrow-gauge railway in India, cherished for its scenic allure. Established in 1881, it weaves through the breathtaking landscapes of the Indian Himalayas. Affectionately known as the \"Toy Train,\" it offers a captivating journey through verdant tea gardens, quaint villages, and sweeping mountain vistas. The train\'s remarkable route features dramatic loops and steep gradients, highlighting Victorian engineering excellence. Notably, it operates from the Ghum railway station, the highest railway station in India at 7,400 feet. This historic railway delivers a nostalgic experience, immersing travelers in the region\'s natural beauty and rich cultural heritage.\r\n \r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 25th February) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop\r\nApprox Distance: 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : 5-Crysta as per itinerary \r\n* One tour escort\r\n* Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis) \r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges. \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation','2025-02-21','2025-02-25',1,0,0,'2025-02-11 15:56:53','2025-02-11 17:05:53'),(868,1512,3511,8,0,0,0,0,'Gangtok Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 21st February) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours\r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Gangtok (5,500 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Gangtok\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 22nd February) : Gangtok to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\nAfter breakfast, start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft. / 37 Kms. / 02 Hrs. from Gangtok) and further drive to New Baba Mandir (13,200 ft. / 16 Kms. / 01 Hrs. from Tsomgo Lake). Evening back to Gangtok. Overnight stay at Gangtok. Note: In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing. Due to winter season (heavy snow) vehicle will be able to drive till Snow point on the way to Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 23rd February) : Gangtok to Darjeeling - Halfday Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 7 hours\r\nAfter breakfast Check out from Hotel & enjoy a half day city tour visiting Plant Conservatory, Dro-dul Chorten & Gonjang Monastery. Afternoon proceed to Darjeeling. On arrival, check-in to your hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Monday 24th February) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill & Joyride\r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km\r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM for joy ride , Later visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Evening free for shopping or leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nNote: Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n+ (Contd. 4th Day) : Darjeeling Himalayan Railway - Steam Engine - Ticket\r\nThe Darjeeling Himalayan Railway (DHR), a UNESCO World Heritage Site since December 5, 1999, is an iconic narrow-gauge railway in India, cherished for its scenic allure. Established in 1881, it weaves through the breathtaking landscapes of the Indian Himalayas. Affectionately known as the \"Toy Train,\" it offers a captivating journey through verdant tea gardens, quaint villages, and sweeping mountain vistas. The train\'s remarkable route features dramatic loops and steep gradients, highlighting Victorian engineering excellence. Notably, it operates from the Ghum railway station, the highest railway station in India at 7,400 feet. This historic railway delivers a nostalgic experience, immersing travelers in the region\'s natural beauty and rich cultural heritage.\r\n \r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 25th February) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop\r\nApprox Distance: 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : 2-Crysta as per itinerary \r\n* Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis) \r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges. \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation','2025-02-21','2025-02-25',1,0,0,'2025-02-11 17:11:05','2025-02-11 17:45:22'),(871,1515,3511,22,0,0,0,0,'Gangtok Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Friday 21st February) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€