 the time of booking','2025-05-30','2025-06-04',1,0,0,'2025-03-01 16:27:38','2025-03-01 16:27:38'),(898,1549,15512,4,0,0,294800,34000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City (PVT)\r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh, transfer downtown, and check in at your hotel. Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, pick upâ€™s airport guide, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (PVT) (B)\r\nDepart at 7:30 AM (time varies by hotel) for a scenic boat ride to a historic floating market on the Tien River. Enjoy fresh fruits, folk music, and visit local businesses crafting coconut candy and rice popcorn. Explore a village by foot and bike, and admire an ancient houseâ€™s traditional architecture. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh City fly to Danang â€“ Hoi An Ancient Town Half Day (B) (PRIVATE)\r\nArrive in Da Nang and transfer to Hoi An, a historic 16th-century trading port. Check in at the hotel (14:00), then explore top attractions, including the Japanese Covered Bridge, Fujian Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Hoi An Market, and enjoy a lantern boat excursion. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, lantern boat, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (PVT)(B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:00 AM for Ba Na Hills (35km from Da Nang). Take the Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Old Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Nghinh Phong Top, Le Nim Villas, and Orchid Garden. Experience the hill-climbing train, Le Jardin Dâ€™Amour, and walk across the famous Golden Bridge for panoramic views. Enjoy lunch at your own expense, then explore Fantasy Park with various indoor games. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nEntrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, sharing guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Da Nang â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (B)\r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for a flight to Hanoi. Upon arrival, transfer to the city center and check in at the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (outside), One Pillar Pagoda, and Hanoi Train Street. Explore Hoan Kiem Lake, stroll through the Old Quarterâ€™s \"36 Streets,\" and shop at Dong Xuan Market. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) \r\nDepart at 8:00 AM for Ha Long Bay (4-hour drive). Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and check into your cabin. Enjoy a fresh seafood lunch while cruising through the bay. Stop for a swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for a sunset view before a seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nNote: The itinerary may vary by cruise.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits. \r\n\r\nDay 7 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/Brunch)\r\nWake up early to enjoy the stunning sunrise over Ha Long Bay. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a local rowboat ride. Enjoy brunch while cruising back to the pier, then return to Hanoi. Transfer to the airport (without a guide) for your flight home. \r\nNote: The cruise itinerary may vary.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal sector flights included\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance \r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS ','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n','2025-05-30','2025-06-05',1,0,0,'2025-03-03 14:34:22','2025-03-03 16:57:58'),(899,1550,15494,4,0,0,17000,12000,'Goa Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 (28th march)\r\nArrival at the Goa Airport and Transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (29th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North Goa Tour. \r\n\r\nDay 03 (30th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (31st March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the South Goa Hotel. Day at leisure or you can explore nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 05 (1st April)\r\nHave breakfast and check-out from the hotel and proceed for the South Goa Tour and transfer to the Airport for your homebound journey.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation with breakfast + lunch/dinner\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* North Goa tour on PVT\r\n* South Goa tour on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExtra hrs and extra kms charges will be extra','2025-03-28','2025-04-01',1,0,0,'2025-03-03 15:55:44','2025-03-04 15:20:43'),(900,1551,15494,4,0,0,16500,11000,'Goa Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 (28th march)\r\nArrival at the Goa Airport and Transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (29th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, proceed for the North Goa Tour. \r\n\r\nDay 03 (30th March)\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and transfer to the pre-booked South Goa hotel and proceed for the South Goa Tour.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (31st March)\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Airport for your homebound journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation with breakfast + lunch/dinner\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* North Goa tour on PVT\r\n* South Goa tour on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Innova','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExtra hrs and extra kms charges will be extra','2025-03-28','2025-03-31',1,0,0,'2025-03-03 17:19:09','2025-03-03 17:42:09'),(901,1554,419,12,0,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Sat 20th December) : Arrival Srinagar â€“ Sightseeing\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist in transferring you to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will encompass a 35-minute drive, offering an initial glimpse of Srinagar city. En route, you\'ll cross the Abdullah Bridge, connecting the banks of the Jhelum River, and pass by the bustling Dal Lake market, known locally as Dal Gate, leading towards the renowned Dal Lake.After a brief period of relaxation, you\'ll embark on a local sightseeing tour, exploring the famed Mughal gardens of Nishat, Shalimar, and Chashme Shahi. These gardens offer an exquisite experience amidst the natural beauty and captivating views of the valley surrounded by majestic mountains.Following the sightseeing tour, you\'ll be escorted to your hotel or houseboat for an overnight stay, providing a chance to unwind and reflect on the day\'s experiences.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Sun 21st December) : Srinagar to Sonamarg - Day Trip\r\nPost the breakfast, we will depart from our hotel and lead our drive to Sonamarg. Sonamarg (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is situated 90kms north-east of Srinagar. You can hire a ( horse or pony/ Union Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore Baltal Valley or Zero Point. Do not miss to click memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. After the tour to Sonamarg, we will take our way back to Srinagar to the hotel for overnight stay.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Mon 22nd December) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Srinagar.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Tue 23rd December) : Gulmarg â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Hotel.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Wed 24th December) : Gulmarg to Srinagar - Departure\r\nTour concludes:We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the airport/railway/bus station for your onward destination.\r\n\r\nTransportation Used: NAC 1-Tempo - 13 Seater \r\n\r\n1st Day (20 Dec)	Arrival Srinagar - Sightseeing \r\n	-Other Inclusions \r\n	-shikara \r\n2nd Day (21 Dec)	Srinagar to Sonamarg - Day Trip \r\n3rd Day (22 Dec)	Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip \r\n4th Day (23 Dec)	Gulmarg - Sightseeing \r\n	-Other Inclusions \r\n	-Gondola phase 1 & 2- Subject to availability\r\n	-Skiing \r\n	-Snowboarding \r\n5th Day (24 Dec)	Gulmarg to Srinagar - Departure \r\n','','â€¢	Economy class airfare\r\nâ€¢	Accommodation on a twin/double/triple sharing basis (as per the package). \r\nâ€¢	Meals as per the package. \r\nâ€¢	Sightseeing by assigned vehicle (as per the package). \r\nâ€¢	Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\nâ€¢	Driver allowances. \r\nâ€¢	Toll tax & Parking. \r\nâ€¢	Snowboarding, Gondola ride, Skiing \r\nâ€¢	Gondola Ride phase 1 & 2 \r\n','â€¢	Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\nâ€¢	Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\nâ€¢	Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\nâ€¢	Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\nâ€¢	Expenses of personal nature such as laundry, mini bars, etc. \r\nâ€¢	Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc. \r\nâ€¢	The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg and vice versa, or to other destinations like Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Doodhpathri in the event of heavy snow, is not included in your package. \r\nâ€¢	Anything not in inclusions is Excluded \r\n','Airfare is dynamic.','2025-12-20','2025-12-24',1,0,0,'2025-03-06 13:56:36','2025-03-06 13:56:36'),(902,1555,419,12,0,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Sat 20th December) : Arrival Srinagar â€“ Sightseeing\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist in transferring you to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will encompass a 35-minute drive, offering an initial glimpse of Srinagar city. En route, you\'ll cross the Abdullah Bridge, connecting the banks of the Jhelum River, and pass by the bustling Dal Lake market, known locally as Dal Gate, leading towards the renowned Dal Lake.After a brief period of relaxation, you\'ll embark on a local sightseeing tour, exploring the famed Mughal gardens of Nishat, Shalimar, and Chashme Shahi. These gardens offer an exquisite experience amidst the natural beauty and captivating views of the valley surrounded by majestic mountains.Following the sightseeing tour, you\'ll be escorted to your hotel or houseboat for an overnight stay, providing a chance to unwind and reflect on the day\'s experiences.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Sun 21st December) : Srinagar to Sonamarg - Day Trip\r\nPost the breakfast, we will depart from our hotel and lead our