mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-21','2025-03-28',1,0,0,'2025-03-08 16:25:04','2025-03-08 17:46:28'),(907,1564,419,3,1,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Sun 23rd March) : Arrival Srinagar - Drop at Hotel\r\n\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist with your transfer to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will take approximately 35 minutes, offering a scenic drive through the heart of Srinagar, crossing the Abdullah Bridge that spans the picturesque Jhelum River. After check-in, the remainder of the day is yours to relish at your own pace. Whether you prefer to explore or simply relax and unwind, the choice is entirely yours. This marks the beginning of your Srinagar experienceâ€”an opportunity to embrace the charm of this beautiful destination. Enjoy an overnight stay at your selected hotel.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Mon 24th March) : Srinagar to Pahalgam - Day Trip\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, we\'ll embark on our tour to Pahalgam. Along the way, you\'ll have the chance to enjoy sightseeing at Awantipora ruins & Saffron Fields. Once in Pahalgam, you can explore places such as Aru, Betaab Valley, and Chandanwari using Union Cabs at your own expense, each boasting its natural allure. While in Pahalgam, indulge in activities that interest you, including skiing, golfing, visiting the Lidder Amusement Park, trekking, or experiencing thrilling whitewater rafting at your own cost. After the sightseeing tour, we\'ll return to the hotel in Srinagar for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Tue 25th March) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Drop at Hotel\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, we will proceed towards Gulmarg . On the arrival to Gulmarg Check-in to the hotel, day will be free at leisure. Overnight .\r\n\r\n4th Day (Wed 26th March) : Gulmarg - Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Hotel.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Thu 27th March) : Gulmarg to Srinagar - Departure\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel and check-out. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Srinagar with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Gulmarg with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Innova\r\n* Airport transfers and sightseeing on pvt.\r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-23','2025-03-27',1,0,0,'2025-03-11 17:13:46','2025-03-12 10:40:26'),(908,1569,419,3,1,0,0,0,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Sun 23rd March) : Arrival Srinagar - Sightseeing\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist in transferring you to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will encompass a 35-minute drive, offering an initial glimpse of Srinagar city. En route, you\'ll cross the Abdullah Bridge, connecting the banks of the Jhelum River, and pass by the bustling Dal Lake market, known locally as Dal Gate, leading towards the renowned Dal Lake. After a brief period of relaxation, you\'ll embark on a local sightseeing tour, exploring the famed Mughal gardens of Nishat, Shalimar, and Chashme Shahi. These gardens offer an exquisite experience amidst the natural beauty and captivating views of the valley surrounded by majestic mountains. Following the sightseeing tour, you\'ll be escorted to your hotel or houseboat for an overnight stay, providing a chance to unwind and reflect on the day\'s experiences.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Mon 24th March) : Srinagar to Pahalgam - Drop at Hotel\r\nIn the early morning, following breakfast, we\'ll set off on a drive towards Pahalgam. Upon arrival, you\'ll check in to the hotel. The rest of the day is yours to enjoy leisure time or take a pony ride to Baisaran valley at your own expense. Overnight stay in Pahalgam.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Tue 25th March) : Pahalgam - Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast .you can visit places like Aru, Betaab valley and Chandanwari by Union Cabs at your own cost which inhibits natural beauty in itself. You can also partake in the activities of your interest like skiing, golfing, Lidder amusement park, trekking or white river rafting. Post the tour to Pahalgam, we will take our way back to the hotel for overnight stay In Pahalgam.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Wed 26th March) : Pahalgam to Srinagar - Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Srinagar with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Pahalgam with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Non AC\r\n* Airport transfers and sightseeing on pvt.\r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-23','2025-03-26',1,0,0,'2025-03-13 14:20:09','2025-03-13 15:27:35'),(909,1568,2690,3,1,0,52000,20000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (17th Apr):\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET APT - Krabi Hotel (Ao-Anang Area) (1-PRIVATE VAN HKT Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\nDay 2 (18th Apr):\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour By Speed Boat + Picinic Lunch ( Exclude National Park Fee THB 200 ) On PVT \r\n3Ad. + 1Ch. \r\n\r\nDay 3 (19th Apr):\r\nTRANSFERS : EX KRABI HOTEL - Phuket Hotel (Patong Area) (1-PRIVATE VAN KBV Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\nDay 4 (20th Apr):\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour By Speed Boat + Khai Island + Lunch + Transfer ( Excl. National Park Fee) on PVT\r\n3Ad. + 1Ch. \r\n\r\nDay 5 (21st Apr):\r\nTRANSFERS : EX PHUKET HOTEL - Phuket Apt (1-PRIVATE VAN HKT Max 9 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N accommodation in Krabi with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N accommodation in Phuket with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned abovde\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-04-17','2025-04-21',1,0,0,'2025-03-13 17:13:57','2025-03-13 19:06:27'),(911,1570,16002,3,1,0,91100,20000,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay : 01 \r\nArrival at DPS Airport | Pick up & drop to hotel Kuta.\r\n\r\nDay : 02 \r\nFull day Water sports (Banana boat + Jet Ski + parasailing) | Padang Padang beach & Uluwatu temple.\r\n\r\nDay: 03 \r\nFull day Nusa Penida West Tour (Kelingking Beach + Paluang Cliff + Broken Beach + Angel Billabong + Snorkelling from beach at Crystal Bay) with lunch (SIC)\r\n\r\nDay: 04 \r\nFull day Kintamani tour | Mount batur view point | Tegalalang rice terrace | Tegenungan waterfalls | Desa Swing Package 1 (5 swings + 2 nests) | Coffee plantation.\r\n\r\nDay: 05 \r\nFull day Lempuyang temple (Gate of heaven) | Tukad Cepung Falls & Tirta gangga.\r\n\r\nDay: 06 \r\nBreakfast at hotel | Check out & drop to airport | Departure.\r\n\r\n \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation in Kuta with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Ubud with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Return Airport & inter hotel transfer by Pvt Basis\r\n* All entrance tickets included, unless mentioned otherwise\r\n* Vehicle Used : Avanza \r\n* English speaking driver\r\n* Toll and Parking Fee Local Taxes\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2025-04-17','2025-04-22',1,0,0,'2025-03-15 14:00:04','2025-03-17 12:21:06'),(912,1571,419,3,1,0,101500,25600,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n	\r\n1st Day (Sun 23rd March) : Arrival Srinagar to Sonamarg - Drop at Hotel\r\nOn the arrival at Srinagar Airport we will proceed towards Sonamarg, after check-in Day will be free at leisure. Overnight Stay in a Hotel.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Mon 24th March) : Sonamarg â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast, we will proceed to Sonamarg. Sonamarg, (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is 90kms northâ€“east of Srinagar. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore. Hire a ( horse or pony /Union (Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. Do not miss clicking memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. Overnight stay at Hotel .\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Tue 25th March) : Sonamarg to Pahalgam - Sightseeing\r\nAfter early breakfast at the hotel, drive from Sonmarg to Pahalgam (valley of Kashmir). Pahalgam is a famous health Resort of Kashmir. On the way visit Saffron fields, Saffron Market, Apple Valley and Lidder river continue to drive to Pahalgam. After fresh up One can just enjoy the town of Pahalgam trek to some of the most beautiful places on earth by a Horse riding like Kanimarg, Dabiyan, Pahalgam valley and Baisaran own Cost. Overnight at the hotel.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Wed 26th March) : Pahalgam to Srinagar - Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Sonamarg with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Pahalgam with breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Non AC\r\n* Airport transfers and sightseeing on pvt.\r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-23','2025-03-26',1,0,0,'2025-03-15 15:06:46','2025-03-15 17:12:08'),(913,1572,15512,3,1,0,147400,32000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 - 17 Apr: Arrival Hanoi Vietnam â€“ half day tour\r\nOur English-speaking guide will greet you at Noi Bai airport and transfer you to your hotel for check-in (2:00 PM). In the afternoon, explore Dong Xuan Market, the Old Quarter, and Ngoc Son Temple. Enjoy a cyclo ride around Hoan Kiem Lake and the Old Quarter, immersing yourself in Hanoi\'s vibrant culture. The tour ends around 4:30 PM. Dinner is on your own, and you\'ll overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, water, hotel, entrance, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 - 18 Apr: Wonderful Ninh Binh (B)\r\nDepart from your hotel at 8:00 AM for a 2-hour, 100 km transfer to Ninh Binh. Enjoy a 2-hour boat trip through Tam Cocâ€™s karst landscape and caves. After lunch, visit Hoa Lu, Vietnamâ€™s 9th-century ancient capital, for a cultural tour. Return to Hanoi by 6:00 PM. Dinner and overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fees , local rowboat trip, breakfast ,hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - 19 Apr: Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B,L,D)\r\nDeparture to Ha Long Bay is at 8:00 AM in a shared van (4 hours). Arrive at noon, board the cruise, and enjoy a seafood lunch while exploring Bai Tu Long Bay. Swim, visit a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for sunset views and a seafood dinner. Overnight on the cruise.\r\nInclusion : Shared transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits\r\n\r\nDay 4- 20 Apr: Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ flight to HCM city (B,BR)\r\nEarly risers can enjoy the sunrise and stunning Bay views with towering limestone. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a short rowboat ride with locals, having brunch onboard as you cruise back. Travel back to Hanoi, where you\'ll be transferred to the airport for your 6:00 PM flight to HCM City. Upon arrival, our guide will transfer you to your hotel for check-in. Overnight in HCM City.\r\nInclusion : Shared transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5- 21 Apr: Cu chi tunnels - Ho Chi Minh city tour full day (B)\r\nDepart your hotel at 8:30 AM for the Cu Chi countryside to explore the underground tunnels used by guerrilla warriors during the war. Visit a rice paper workshop before heading to HCM City in the afternoon. Tour Cho Lon market, a Chinese pagoda, Notre Dame Cathedral, Central Post Office, and City Hall. Return to your hotel by 5:30 PM. Overnight in HCM.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast and  hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 22 Apr : HCM City departure (B)\r\nFree for shopping. Have lunch on your own and free until late afternoon we head back to Tan Son Nhat airport around for your evening flight back home. Goodbye and hope to see you again soon! \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Domestic Flights (HAN-SGN)\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Hanoi with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Ha Long (Cruise) with all meals\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Ho Chi Minh City with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: 3$ per person/day/mandatory \r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nDaily working hours : We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. Any activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n','2025-04-17','2025-04-22',1,0,0,'2025-03-17 12:36:31','2025-03-17 14:40:35'),(914,1573,419,4,0,0,113300,23000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Thu 17th April) : Arrival Srinagar - Sightseeing\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist in transferring you to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will encompass a 35-minute drive, offering an initial glimpse of Srinagar city. En route, you\'ll cross the Abdullah Bridge, connecting the banks of the Jhelum River, and pass by the bustling Dal Lake market, known locally as Dal Gate, leading towards the renowned Dal Lake. After a brief period of relaxation, you\'ll embark on a local sightseeing tour, exploring the famed Mughal gardens of Nishat, Shalimar, and Chashme Shahi. These gardens offer an exquisite experience amidst the natural beauty and captivating views of the valley surrounded by majestic mountains. Following the sightseeing tour, you\'ll be escorted to your hotel or houseboat for an overnight stay, providing a chance to unwind and reflect on the day\'s experiences.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 18th April) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Srinagar.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 19th April) : Srinagar to Sonamarg - Srinagar - Sonamarg Drop at Hotel\r\nAfter breakfast we will depart from srinagar and start our way to Sonamarg. After reaching hotel, the day will be free at leisure, Overnight in Sonamarg.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sun 20th April) : Sonamarg - Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast, we will proceed to Sonamarg. Sonamarg, (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is 90kms northâ€“east of Srinagar. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore. Hire a ( horse or pony /Union (Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. Do not miss clicking memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. Overnight stay at Hotel .\r\n\r\n5th Day (Mon 21st April) : Sonamarg to Pahalgam - Drop at Hotel\r\nAfter early breakfast at the hotel, drive from Sonmarg to Pahalgam (valley of Kashmir). Pahalgam is a famous health Resort of Kashmir. On the way visit Saffron fields, Saffron Market, Apple Valley and Lidder river continue to drive to Pahalgam. After fresh up One can just enjoy the town of Pahalgam trek to some of the most beautiful places on Earth by a Horse riding like Kanimarg, Dabiyan, Pahalgam valley and Baisaran own Cost. Overnight at the hotel.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Tue 22nd April) : Pahalgam to Srinagar - Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the Airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Non AC Innova\r\n* Sightseeing by assigned vehicle (as per the package). \r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru\r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg and vice versa, or to other destinations like Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Doodhpathri in the event of heavy snow, is not included in your package. \r\n* Anything not in inclusions is Excluded \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-04-17','2025-04-22',1,0,0,'2025-03-17 15:27:18','2025-03-17 16:00:57'),(915,1577,2690,3,1,0,38450,20000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\n1st Day - Thu, 17th Apr\r\n* Phuket Airport to Krabi Hotel - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)\r\n\r\n2nd Day - Fri, 18th Apr\r\n* Krabi 4 Island Tour - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)\r\n* Krabi 4 Island Tour by Longtail boat with lunch box (Excluding Island Fees) - SIC - Tour + Entry Fees (3Ad. + 1Ch.)\r\n\r\n3rd Day - Sat, 19th Apr\r\n* Krabi Hotel to Krabi Airport - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)\r\n* Chiangmai Airport to Chiangmai Hotel - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)\r\n\r\n4th Day - Sun, 20th Apr\r\n* Chiangmai - Blue, White & Black temple - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)\r\n* Chiangmai - Blue temple, White, Black temple (chiang Rai ) - Entry Fees (3Ad. + 1Ch.)\r\n\r\n5th Day - Mon, 21st Apr\r\n* Chiangmai Hotel to Chiangmai Airport - Pvt Transfer (1-Private)','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal flights included (KBV-CNX)\r\n* 2N accommodation in Krabi with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N accommodation in Chiang Mai with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned abovde\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-04-17','2025-04-21',1,0,0,'2025-03-19 15:29:59','2025-03-19 17:56:29'),(916,1579,15611,2,2,0,0,0,'Darjeeling Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Wednesday 26th March) : Bagdogra Airport to Darjeeling - Pickup \r\nApprox Distance : 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Darjeeling (6,950 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Thursday 27th March) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill \r\nApprox Distance : 130 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 8 hours \r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM, visit Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple (Peace Pagoda). Evening free for shopping or leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nNote: Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Friday 28th March) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance : 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Darjeeling with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner.\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Airport transfers and tours on PVT.\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis) \r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges \r\nâ€¢ Insurance \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-03-26','2025-03-28',1,0,0,'2025-03-22 14:03:15','2025-03-22 15:30:00'),(917,1581,1305,2,2,3,66200,15000,'Shillong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Wednesday 26th March) : Guwahati Airport / Rly Station to Shillong - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nOn arrival at Guwahati Airport transfer to Shillong, which is also called the \'Scotland of the East\". On the way visit a majestic placid lake with its surrounding sylvan hills Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which is the biggest local market. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Thursday 27th March) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion \r\nApprox Distance : 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hours \r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), the wettest place in the world. Enroute enjoy view of Mawdok - Dympep Valley View Point. You will see the beautiful waterfall known as Nohkalikai. Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls). You can also explore the caves known as Mawsmai. Evening return to Shillong, enroute visit Elephanta falls. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Friday 28th March) : Shillong to Mawlynnong and Dawki - Excursion \r\nApprox Distance : 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 4 hours \r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Mawlynnong â€“ â€œAsiaâ€™s Cleanest Villageâ€. Mawlynnong offers many interesting sights such as the living root bridge and another strange natural phenomenon of a boulder balancing on another small rock. Later proceed to Dawki, a small town near India Bangladesh border. Enjoy breathtaking view of the Umangot River. Evening drive back to Shillong. Stay overnight at your hotel in Shillong.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Saturday 29th March) : Shillong to Guwahati Airport - Sightseeing and Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Wardâ€™s Lake. Later transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation in Shillong with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner.\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area) \r\nâ€¢ All hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any \r\nâ€¢ VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Insurance \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-03-26','2025-03-29',1,0,0,'2025-03-22 17:23:59','2025-03-22 18:24:47'),(918,1580,349,4,0,0,213500,27000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n* Abu Dhabi Attractions ( 2 Day 2 Park Pass (Yas Water World / Ferrari / Warner Bros/Sea World) ) (Only Ticket)(04-Adults)\r\n* TRIO - Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Half Day City Tour (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Atlantis Attractions ( Aquaventure + Lost Chambers Super pass ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Miracle Garden + Global Village (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n* Burj Khalifa 124th + 125th Floor - Non Prime Hour \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Abu Dhabi with daily breakfast\r\n* 5N Accommodation in Dubai with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers and inter-hotel transfers on pvt basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-11-06','2025-11-13',1,0,0,'2025-03-24 12:30:29','2025-03-24 16:23:11'),(919,1582,195,2,0,0,130100,47000,'Europe Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 01 : 5th Oct\r\nArrival at the Baku Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.  \r\n\r\nDay 02 : 6th Oct\r\nHave breakfast and proceed for Baku Old City UNESCO Heritage Walking Tour (12:00), Baku, Azerbaijan Meeting point - Gosha Gala Square ,47 Kichik Qala, BakÄ±, Azerbaijan  \r\nIn the evening proceed for Baku Lights : the Night Tour illuminated by Baku lights (Group Tour 20:00), Meeting point - Old City tours, 25 Sabir St, Baku 1095, Azerbaijan  \r\n\r\nDay 03 : 7th Oct\r\nAfter breakfast, proceed for Mud Volcanoes and Gobustan Half-Day Tour, Baku, Azerbaijan Shared tour with Gobustan National Park ticket English Start point - Hotel pick-up available.\r\n    \r\nDay 04 : 8th Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to Baku Airport for your onward flight to Istanbul. Transfer from Istanbul Airport to the hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening, proceed for Turkish Night on the Bosphorus 20:30, Istanbul, Meeting Point - SENKRON Tur-SEREMONI Teknesi, Abdulezel pasa Cad. Balat Parki\r\n\r\nDay 05 : 9th Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast proceed for Istanbul City Tour, Bosphorus Cruise and Cable Car in Small-Group (Hotel pick-up 09:00) \r\n\r\nDay 06 : 10th Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Istanbul Airport for your onward journey to Budapest. Transfer from Budapest Airport to the hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. \r\nIn the evening proceed for Evening Cruise on the Danube with Optional Drinks 19:00, Meeting Point - Akademia 2 ponton, Budapest, Id. Antall Jozsef rkp., 1051 Hungary\r\n\r\nDay 07 : 11th Oct\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel and proceed for Half day Budapest city tour by car / minivan, Budapest, Hungary    \r\n\r\nDay 08 : 12th Oct\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Budapest Airport for your homebound journey.  \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare \r\n* Internal sector flights included (Baku-Istanbul, Istanbul-Budapest)\r\n* 7N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Transfer from Baku Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Baku hotel to Baku Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Istanbul Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Istanbul hotel to Istanbul Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Budapest Airport to hotel on PVT basis\r\n* Transfer from Budapest hotel to Budapest Airport on PVT basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary (on SIC basis)\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa fees for 3 countries ( Azerbaijan, Hungary and Turkey) is included','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entrance fees for Budapest Half Day Tour is excluded.\r\n.* City & Government Tax To Be Paid Locally On Spot.\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\nFor the above said tour, there Is no pick up and drop off from the Hotel, so client will have to reach at departure points and back to hotel also at their own arrangement.','2025-10-05','2025-10-12',1,0,0,'2025-03-25 12:27:38','2025-03-26 12:13:43'),(920,1583,419,2,1,0,42000,6000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : ARRIVAL AT SRINAGAR \r\nArrive at Srinagar Sheikh Ul Alam International Airport, known for one of the world\'s most scenic flights. Srinagar, the summer capital of Jammu & Kashmir, is famous for its rich Sufi and Reshi heritage. Youâ€™ll be greeted by our representative and transferred to your hotel. After check-in, visit Shankaracharya Temple, where the philosopher Shankaracharya stayed over a thousand years ago. In the afternoon, explore the Mughal Gardens: Nishat Garden (Garden of Pleasure), Shalimar Garden (Garden of Love), and Chashmashahi (The Royal Spring). Enjoy dinner and an overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDAY 02 : SRINAGAR TO SONAMARG â€“ DAY EXCURSION TO SONAMARG(88 Kms â€“ 03 Hrs One Way)\r\nAfter a leisurely breakfast, we check out from the hotel and transfer to Sonamarg. Known as the \"Meadow of Gold,\" Sonamarg offers stunning views of snowy mountains, dense pine forests, and high peaks. Itâ€™s a great base for trekking, glaciers, and the Amarnath Cave. The river here is rich in Trout and Mahseer. Sonamarg is also the last stop before the Srinagar-Leh route. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDAY 03 : SRINAGAR TO GULMARG (OVERNIGHT STAY TO GULMARG)\r\nCheck out from the hotel early morning and drive to Gulmarg, passing willow trees, streams, and green meadows. Known as the \"meadow of flowers,\" Gulmarg offers stunning views of snow-capped peaks and dense forests. Enjoy a stroll or pony ride (at your own cost) across the meadow to one of the worldâ€™s highest golf courses. Donâ€™t miss the Gondola lift ride (at your own cost). Overnight stay and dinner at Gulmarg Hotel. \r\n\r\nDAY 04 : GULMARG TO PAHALGAM - OVERNIGHT STAY TO PAHALGAM \r\nAfter breakfast, we check out from the hotel and head to Pahalgam, known as the \"Valley of Shepherds.\" Situated at the confluence of streams from Sheshnag Lake and the Lidder River, Pahalgam (2,130 m) was once a shepherd\'s village with stunning views. En route, visit the saffron fields and 19th-century Awantipura Ruins. Upon arrival, check in to the hotel. The rest of the day is free to explore Pahalgam\'s beauty. You can visit Aru Valley (10 km away), known for its scenic meadows, trekking routes, and activities like fishing, hiking, and horse riding. Overnight stay and dinner at the Pahalgam hotel.\r\n\r\nDAY 05 : PAHALGAM SIGHTSEEING\r\nAfter breakfast, we explore Pahalgam\'s sights, starting with Betaab Valley, 15 km away. Named after the film Betaab, the valley is surrounded by lush meadows, snow-capped mountains, and dense vegetation. A popular tourist spot and campsite, itâ€™s also a base for trekking. The crystal-clear stream water is a local favorite. Nearby attractions include Baisaran and Tulian Lake. Dinner and overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDAY 06 : PAHALGAM-DEPART SRINAGAR (FLY OUT) \r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel and transfer to the SXR Airport for your homebound journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Welcome Drink on arrival\r\nâ€¢ Hotel Accommodation mentioned below or Similar as per the itinerary   (01 Room)\r\nâ€¢ Daily Breakfast & Dinner Only (MAP)\r\nâ€¢ Return and round-trip transfers along with all sightseeing tours by Vehicle Etios/Dzire or Similar Sedan as per Itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Drivers allowance, Fuel Charges, Toll and parking charges.\r\nâ€¢ Child Below 05 Years â€“ Complimentary\r\nâ€¢ 01Hr Boat Ride (Shikara) on world famous Dal Lake â€“ Srinagar \r\nâ€¢ All applicable hotel taxes.\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\nâ€¢ Gondola Ride Tickets Phase 1,2\r\nâ€¢ Guide fee, Camera fee & any monument Entrances \r\nâ€¢ Union cab For Pahalgam Sightseeing.\r\nâ€¢ Union Cab For Drung WaterFall.\r\nâ€¢ Union Cab In Sonamarg.\r\nâ€¢ Union Cab In Gulmarg.\r\nâ€¢ Any changes you may choose to make during your tour & additional costs due to flight cancellation, road blocks etc\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-04-10','2025-04-15',1,0,0,'2025-03-26 13:19:39','2025-03-26 16:25:06'),(922,1585,17406,2,0,1,27500,6000,'Rameshwaram Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n Day 1 : Madurai To Rameswaram Arrival\r\nOn arrival at the Madurai Airport, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and proceed to Rameswaram. Enroute visit Madurai Meenakshi temple &  Annai Indira Gandhi Road Bridge Pamban Bridge. Annai Indira Gandhi Street Bridge is one of the longest bridges in southern India. Check into hotel. Visit Arulmigu Ramanathaswamy Temple. Rameswaram is an exquisite temple in southern India dedicated to Lord Shiva. It is one for the 12 jyotirlingas. After return to Hotel for overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Rameswaram Day 02\r\nAfter breakfast sightseeing of Rameswaram. Visit Five Faced Hanuman Temple, Abdul Kalam house. After visit Adam\'s Bridge. This pathway is underwater and has been commonly known as the â€œRam Setuâ€  or â€œAdams bridge â€œ AKA the bridge Ram made to Sri Lanka. After visit Dhanushkodi Beach. Dhanushkodi Beach is a perfect one day  gate-away in Rameswaram to relax and enjoy the abundance of scenic beauty which stretches on the coastline of Rameswaram. Rameswaram is also popularly referred to as the \'Benaras of the south\'. In order to attain Moksha it is believed that the visit to Rameswaram is mandatory. Overnight at the Resort/hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Madurai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Madurai international Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers and sightseeing on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan AC\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n   \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-29','2025-03-31',1,0,0,'2025-03-27 14:31:26','2025-03-27 14:31:26'),(923,1586,507,5,0,1,0,0,'Nepal Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n04 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Pickup from Kathmandu International Airport and drop at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Half day sightseeing in Kathmandu covering Swyambhunath Stupa (Monkey Temple) & Kathmandu Durbar Square.\r\nïƒ¼	Dinner at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n05 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Half day sightseeing in Kathmandu covering Pashupatinath Temple & Bauddhanath Stupa, \r\nïƒ¼	Drive from Kathmandu to Pokhara & drop at hotel.   210 KM  (6-7 Hours)\r\nïƒ¼	Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Dinner at Hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n06 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Full  day sightseeing in Pokhara covering Bindabashini Temple, Gupteshor Cave, Devi;s Fall, Seti River & Peace Pagoda.\r\nïƒ¼	Dinner at Hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Overnight stay at hotel in Pokhara.\r\n\r\n07 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Morning breakfast at hotel\r\nïƒ¼	Drive from Pokhara to Chitwan & drop hotel.     145 KM  (4-5 Hours)\r\nïƒ¼	Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Lunch at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Elephant/Jeep Safari.\r\nïƒ¼	Village Tour & Tharu Culture Dance Program.\r\nïƒ¼	Dinner at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Overnight stay at hotel in Chitwan.\r\n\r\n08 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Bird Watching & Jungle Walk.\r\nïƒ¼	 Drive from Chitwan to Kathmandu via Manakamana Temple darshan (by Cable Car) & drop at hotel.     170 KM  (5-6 Hours)\r\nïƒ¼	Welcome soft drink at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Dinner at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Overnight stay at hotel in Kathmandu.\r\n\r\n09 April 2025:\r\nïƒ¼	Morning breakfast at hotel.\r\nïƒ¼	Drive from hotel to Kathmandu International Airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Welcome soft drink.\r\nâ€¢ Airport pickup & drop with a/c private Scorpio.\r\nâ€¢ 02 nightâ€™s accommodation at respective hotel in Kathmandu with MAP Plan. \r\nâ€¢ 02 nightâ€™s accommodation at respective hotel in Pokhara with MAP Plan. \r\nâ€¢ 01 night accommodation at respective hotel in Chitwan with AP Plan. \r\nâ€¢ Kathmandu two half day sightseeing.\r\nâ€¢ Pokhara full day sightseeing.\r\nâ€¢ All the Jungle activities in Chitwan.( Elephant/Jeep Safari, Village Tour, Tharu Culture Dance Program, Bird Watching & Jungle Walk)\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Monuments and museum entrance fees for above sightseeing places.\r\n* Fewa Lake boating Charge\r\n* Manakamana Cable Car Ticket : INR. 700 Per Person\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-04-04','2025-04-09',1,0,0,'2025-03-27 17:28:45','2025-03-27 18:06:21'),(925,1587,355,2,0,1,32000,7200,'Varanasi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1- Varanasi Arrival \r\nArrival at Varanasi Airport and transfer to hotel. .  Later in evening aarti by boat ride with Guide (charges Included){transfer timing 4 PM}.\" and Stay overnight in Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2- Varanasi Temple tour \r\nBefore breakfast, early in the morning you will be taken on a temple tour to enjoy the morning rituals in famous temples like, Kashi Vishwanath temple, Annapurna temple, .\r\nLater, you will be taken back to the hotel for breakfast and then visit SankatMochan Hanuman temple , ManasMandir BHU and Sarnath . \r\nStay overnight in Hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ Varanasi Drop \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and drop to Airport .\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Transfers & sightseeing by 1 Ac Sedan\r\n(Vehicle Service from 08:00 Am to 08:00 PM after that additional cost will be applicable )\r\n* Toll, Parking, Driver Allowance.\r\n* All Applicable Tax.\r\n* Boat ride for evening Ganga Aarti (90 minutes ) \r\n*  1 Day full Guide services for Varanasi \r\n\r\n','*  Entrances fees\r\n* Expenses of personal nature such as drinks, telephone, and laundry bills etc\r\n* Tips and porter charges\r\n* Any additional expenses incurred due to any flight delay or cancellation, weather conditions, political closures, technical faults etc\r\n* Any other service/s not specified above\r\n \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-03-29','2025-03-31',1,0,0,'2025-03-28 13:35:29','2025-03-28 13:55:53'),(926,1588,15512,8,0,0,416300,80000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City \r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh, meet your driver, and transfer to the city center (30 minutes). Check in at your hotel (check-in at 14:00) and enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (B)\r\nAt 8:30 AM, you\'ll be picked up and travel through miles of rice fields to the Mekong Delta, Vietnam\'s largest rice bowl. In My Tho City, board a motorboat to explore canals and islands. Visit Thoi Son Island for traditional music, then switch to a paddle boat to see coconut candy and rice wine-making. Continue to a bee farm to taste honey tea and fresh fruit. On the return, stop at Vinh Trang Pagoda, a beautiful blend of Vietnamese, Roman, Chinese, and Cambodian architecture. You\'ll head back to Ho Chi Minh by 5:30 PM, with an overnight stay. Note: The driver doesnâ€™t speak English.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, local boat, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh City fly to Danang â€“ Hoi An Ancient Town Half Day (B) (PRIVATE)\r\nUpon arrival, our driver will greet you and transfer you to Da Nang center, then to Hoi An, a former 16th-century trading port. Explore attractions like the Japanese Covered Bridge, Fujian Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, and Hoi An Central Market. Check-in at 14:00. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B)\r\nEnjoy breakfast at your hotel. At 8:00 AM, transfer to Ba Na Hills (35km from Danang). Ride the Sunworld Cable Car, passing through By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet Hill, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Nghinh Phong top, Le Nim Villas, Orchid Garden, and the hill-climbing train. Walk across the Golden Bridge and enjoy panoramic views. After lunch, explore Fantasy Park with games like 4-5D films, skiver, and dinosaur park. Return to your hotel by 5 PM for an overnight stay in Danang. \r\nEntrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Da Nang â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (B) \r\nAfter breakfast and check-out, transfer to the airport for a flight to Hanoi. Upon arrival, our guide and driver will transfer you to the city center and check-in at the hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (from outside), One Pillar Pagoda, and the scenic Hoan Kiem Lake. Then, enjoy a walk around Hanoi\'s Old Quarter, known for its narrow alleys and traditional shops. The rest of the day is for shopping at Dong Xuan Market. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nDepart your hotel around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour private transfer to Ha Long Bay. Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and settle into your cabin. Enjoy a local seafood lunch while cruising the bay, with stops for swimming and exploring a cave. Relax on a secluded beach and return to the boat to watch the sunset. Enjoy a seafood dinner before overnighting on the cruise. Note: Itinerary may vary based on the cruise program.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi Depature (B/Brunch)\r\nEarly risers can enjoy the sunrise and stunning Bay views with towering limestone. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a short rowboat ride with locals and enjoy brunch on the boat as you cruise back to the pier. Then, head back to Hanoi, where you\'ll be transferred to the airport for your flight home.\r\n Inclusion : Private transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal sector flights\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Ho Chi Minh with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Danang with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Hanoi with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Ha Long Cruise with all meals\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\nâ€¢ SIC tours as mentioned\r\nâ€¢ Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n* Insurance\r\n','*Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nâ€¢ Meals on boat are local food.\r\nâ€¢ TOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n','2025-06-16','2025-06-22',1,0,0,'2025-03-28 16:59:34','2025-03-28 17:28:44'),(927,1591,126,3,2,0,30000,5000,'Jaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1: Leave early morning for Jaipur. After reaching, check-in at hotel. Explore the City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and Jantar Mantar as per the respective timings. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, visit Amer Fort and Jaigarh Fort. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Have breakfast and explore Nahargarh Fort and Birla Mandir. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast and relax or explore local market. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : After having breakfast, check-out and drive back to Delhi.','','* 4 Nights accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Toll Tax\r\n* Driver Allowance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-04-07','2025-04-11',1,0,0,'2025-03-31 19:21:54','2025-03-31 19:29:24'),(928,1592,54,1,0,0,141000,18000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 (15th May) - Arrive Kuala Lumpur - KUL night tour with KL Tower ticket(observation deck ticket only)-(D) \r\nArrive in Kuala Lumpur, transfer to hotel (check-in: 1400-1500 hrs). Evening: Kuala Lumpur night tour, including KL Tower observation deck. Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Overnight at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 02 (16th May) - Kuala Lumpur â€“ Malacca City tour with Boat Cruise (B,D)\r\nStart your day with breakfast at the hotel, then embark on a full-day tour of Malacca. Explore the city\'s rich history and vibrant culture, including a walk along Jonker Street and a visit to the three main worship houses on Harmony Street. Enjoy a scenic Malacca River Cruise before heading to an Indian restaurant for dinner. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 03 (17th May) - Kuala Lumpur - Genting Highland visit with Outdoor theme park (B,D)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Pickup from lobby for Genting Highlands day tour, including cable car ride and outdoor theme park, with a 20-minute stop at Batu Caves. Genting Highlands, located 1,800 meters above sea level, is an entertainment city with an outdoor theme park. Return to Kuala Lumpur in the evening for dinner at an Indian restaurant. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 04 (18th May) - Kuala Lumpur - Singapore\r\nSingapore city evening tour+ Visit to Gardens By the Bay (B,D)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel, then check out and transfer to the airport for a flight to Singapore. Arrive in Singapore, known as the Lion City, and transfer to the hotel (check-in between 2:00-3:00 PM). In the evening, enjoy a city tour followed by a visit to Gardens by the Bay, where you can admire beautiful outdoor parks and iconic architectural structures. Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 05 (19th May) - Singapore - Marina Bay Sands Sky Park(observation deck)+ Sentosa Island Tour(B,D)\r\nBreakfast at hotel. 09:30 hrs : Pick up for Marina Bay Sands Sky Park (observation deck) to enjoy panoramic views of Singapore\'s skyline. Next, head to Sentosa Island for a tour with various attractions. Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 06 (20th May) - Singapore â€“ Shopping tour(B,D)\r\nAfter breakfast, pick up from the hotel lobby for a shopping tour in Orchard Road and nearby malls. Enjoy dinner at an Indian restaurant before returning to the hotel for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 07 (21st May) -Singapore Departure-Universal Studio tour(B,D)\r\nBreakfast at hotel, check out, and store luggage. 10:30 AM : Pickup from hotel, head to Universal Studios Singapore, Southeast Asiaâ€™s first movie theme park with exciting attractions. Dinner at an Indian restaurant. Return to hotel, collect luggage, and transfer to the airport for your flight.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Cost of your round trip economy class airfare on Singapore Airlines (Delhi- Singapore-Kuala Lumpur\r\nSingapore-Delhi)\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar.\r\n* 03 Night accommodation in Singapore\r\n* 03 Nights accommodation in Kuala Lumpur\r\n* 06 Breakfast at hotel buffet\r\n* 07 Dinner at indian restaurant\r\n* Airportâ€“ hotel- airport transfers\r\n Singapore\r\n* Evening City tour with Gardens by the bay\r\n* Marina Bay Sands Sky Park-observation deck ticket\r\n* Universal Studio tour\r\n* Sentosa Island tour with Wings of time, 4D adventure, Trick Eye Museum, SEA Aquarium, Cable Car\r\n* Shopping tour\r\n Kuala Lumpur\r\n* KUL night tour with KL Tower ticket (observation deck only)\r\n* Genting Highland visit with cable car ride\r\n* Outdoor Theme Park ticket Genting highland\r\n* Batu caves visit\r\n* Malaccacity tour with river cruise\r\n* All tour and transfer on shared / joint basis\r\n* Airport taxes as per the routing of the tour.\r\n* Singapore Visa Charge','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Lunch\r\n* Malaysia Visa-No Charges for travel upto 31st Dec ( Minimum USD 500 cash in hand or International Debit or\r\n International Credit Card required on arrival at Kuala Lumpur)\r\nIndian travellers must fill up the MDAC Form via online before arrival in Malaysia.\r\n https://imigresen-online.imi.gov.my/mdac/main\r\n* Malaysia Tourism Tax RM 10per room per night to be paid directly at hotel on check-in\r\n* Any increase in the air fare, fuel surcharge and taxes charged by the airlines on your air ticket.\r\n* Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in all land arrangement which may come in to\r\n effect prior to departure.\r\n* High Season Surcharge if applicable.\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n \r\n ','Day 00 - Flight from Delhi , report 04 hours prior to flight departure\r\nNote : Hotel confirmed as per our group will be given, no preference/choice can be taken\r\nNote : flight schedule given is tentative, flight timings subject to change.','2025-05-14','2025-05-20',1,0,0,'2025-04-01 12:15:14','2025-04-04 14:02:01'),(929,1594,126,3,2,0,30000,12900,'Jaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1: Leave early morning for Jaipur. After reaching, check-in at hotel. Explore the City Palace, Hawa Mahal, and Jantar Mantar as per the respective timings. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, visit Amer Fort and Jaigarh Fort. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Have breakfast and explore Nahargarh Fort and Birla Mandir. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast and relax or explore local market. Overnight stay and dinner at hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : After having breakfast, check-out and drive back to Delhi.','','* 4 Nights accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Innova Crysta\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Toll Tax\r\n* Driver Allowance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-04-08','2025-04-12',0,0,0,'2025-04-01 14:56:11','2025-04-01 15:04:05'),(930,1593,349,4,0,0,133800,13000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 :\r\n  Transfer from DXB AIRPORT to Pre booked hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner to Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nDay 2 :\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to Desert Safari With BBQ Dinner [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Desert Safari With BBQ Dinner to Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nDay 3 :\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to Half Day Dubai City Tour [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Half Day Dubai City Tour to Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nDay 4 :\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to Burj Khalifa Tour [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Burj Khalifa Tour to Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nDay 5 :\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to Miracle Garden + Global Village [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Miracle Garden + Global Village to Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nDay 6 :\r\n  Transfer from Booked Hotel to DXB AIRPORT [with Private transport]\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-05-09','2025-05-14',1,0,0,'2025-04-01 15:11:42','2025-04-01 16:30:35'),(931,1597,419,4,0,0,113300,23000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (23rd May) : Arrival Srinagar - Sightseeing\r\nUpon your arrival at Srinagar International Airport, our team will extend a warm welcome and assist in transferring you to your chosen accommodation, whether it\'s a hotel or a houseboat. The journey to your lodging will encompass a 35-minute drive, offering an initial glimpse of Srinagar city. En route, you\'ll cross the Abdullah Bridge, connecting the banks of the Jhelum River, and pass by the bustling Dal Lake market, known locally as Dal Gate, leading towards the renowned Dal Lake. After a brief period of relaxation, you\'ll embark on a local sightseeing tour, exploring the famed Mughal gardens of Nishat, Shalimar, and Chashme Shahi. These gardens offer an exquisite experience amidst the natural beauty and captivating views of the valley surrounded by majestic mountains. Following the sightseeing tour, you\'ll be escorted to your hotel or houseboat for an overnight stay, providing a chance to unwind and reflect on the day\'s experiences.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (24th May) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Srinagar.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (25th May) : Srinagar to Sonamarg\r\nAfter breakfast we will depart from Srinagar and start our way to Sonamarg. After reaching hotel, the day will be free at leisure. Overnight in Sonamarg.\r\n\r\n4th Day (26th May) : Sonamarg - Sightseing\r\nAfter Breakfast, we will proceed to Sonamarg. Sonamarg, (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is 90kms northâ€“east of Srinagar. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore. Hire a ( horse or pony /Union (Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. Do not miss clicking memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. Overnight stay at Hotel .\r\n\r\n5th Day (27th May) : Sonamarg to Pahalgam - Drop at Hotel\r\nAfter early breakfast at the hotel, drive from Sonmarg to Pahalgam (valley of Kashmir). Pahalgam is a famous health Resort of Kashmir. On the way visit Saffron fields, Saffron Market, Apple Valley and Lidder river continue to drive to Pahalgam. After fresh up One can just enjoy the town of Pahalgam trek to some of the most beautiful places on earth by a Horse riding like Kanimarg, Dabiyan, Pahalgam valley and Baisaran own Cost. Overnight at the hotel.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Tue 22nd April) : Pahalgam to Srinagar - Departure\r\nAfter breakfast check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the Airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Srinagar with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Sonmarg with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Pahalgam with breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Non-AC Innova\r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg and vice versa, or to other destinations like Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Doodhpathri in the event of heavy snow, is not included in your package. \r\n* Anything not in inclusions is Excluded \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2025-05-23','2025-05-28',1,0,0,'2025-04-03 16:01:53','2025-04-04 14:09:40'),(932,1596,15512,9,7,0,0,0,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“  26th May : Arrival Ho Chi Minh Vietnam â€“ Leisure Day\r\nWelcome to Ho Chi Minh City! Upon arrival at Tan Son Nhat Airport, our guide will greet you and transfer you to downtown for check-in (from 14:00). Early check-in is not included. Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : private transfer, guide, hotel, water\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 27th May : Highlight city tour full day (B)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Depart at 10:00 AM to visit Saigon Zoo and Botanical Garden, Vietnam\'s largest zoo, established in 1864. Next, see Notre Dame Cathedral, a stunning replica of Paris\' landmark. Visit the War Remnants Museum, then explore the French-colonial Central Post Office. End the day at Ben Thanh Market, the oldest in Saigon, for shopping and sightseeing. Return to the hotel by 5:00 PM. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel, breakfast\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 28th May : Ho Chi Minh â€“ Fly to Da Nang â€“ Coconut Basket Boat â€“ Hoi An old town (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel, then transfer (without guide) to the airport for your flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival, meet the guide and transfer to the hotel for check-in (14:00). In the afternoon, visit the Green Bay Mau water coconut forest, row a basket boat, catch field crabs, and explore a Vietnam War revolutionary base. Then, visit Hoi An Ancient Town, including the Kwan Temple, Phuc Kien Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Japanese Bridge, and Hoi An Market. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel, water\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 29th May : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B) \r\nHave breakfast at your hotel, then at 9:00 AM, transfer to Ba Na Hills (35km from Danang). Ride the Sun world Cable Car to the Ba Na Hills station, stopping at By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas. Continue to the top of Nui Chua Mountain, exploring Nghinh Phong Peak, Le Nim Villas, Orchid Garden, Le Jardin Dâ€™amour, and Linh Ung Pagoda. Walk across the Golden Bridge with panoramic views. Enjoy lunch on your own and free time at Fantasy Park, Vietnamâ€™s third-largest indoor games zone. Overnight in Danang.\r\nPlease note: Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, DW Debay ancient wine cellar, cotton animal game and carnival skill at Fantasy Park is not included in my quotation, joining them will be at your own account.   \r\nInclusion :  Transfer, guide, entrance fee, cable car ticket, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 30th May : Da Nang â€“ fly to Hanoi â€“ city tour half day  (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel, then transfer to the airport (no guide) for your morning flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival, meet our guide and transfer to the hotel for check-in (2:00 PM). In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum and grounds, then the One Pillar Pagoda. Next, explore the Temple of Literature, Vietnamâ€™s first university, followed by a visit to Ngoc Son Temple at Hoan Kiem Lake. The tour ends around 5:30 PM. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, hotel, breakfast, water\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 31st May : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) â€“ private transfer, sharing cruise\r\nDepart your hotel around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour private transfer to Ha Long Bay. Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and head to your cabin. Enjoy a seafood lunch while cruising through Bai Tu Long Bay. Swim, explore a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for sunset views and a seafood dinner. Overnight on board.\r\nInclusion : private Transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\nExclusion : Beverage\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 1st Jun : Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/BR)(SIC)\r\nEarly risers can enjoy the sunrise and the stunning Bay landscape with towering limestone. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a short rowboat ride with locals and enjoy brunch on the boat as you cruise back. Then, weâ€™ll transfer you back to Ha Noi and to the airport for your flight. Trip ends! Thank you, and we hope to see you again soon.\r\nNote : The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruiseâ€™s program.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch\r\nExclusion : Beverage\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights Included (SGN-DAD, DAD-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day)\r\n* Insurance\r\n*Visa\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.)\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNote : Child 2,2,4 & 4 ys are FOC (under 1m talled). Any extra cost for entrance fee, will be pay directly at the spot.\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. Any activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.','2025-05-26','2025-06-01',0,0,0,'2025-04-05 12:39:12','2025-04-05 13:13:00'),(933,1600,419,4,0,0,113300,25000,'Kashmir Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Fri 23rd May) : Arrival Srinagar to Sonamarg - Drop at Hotel\r\nOn the arrival at Srinagar Airport we will proceed towards Sonamarg, after check-in Day will be free at leisure. Overnight Stay in a Hotel.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Sat 24th May) : Sonamarg â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast, we will proceed to Sonamarg. Sonamarg, (meadows of gold) is a hill station in Ganderbal district which is 90kms northâ€“east of Srinagar. A pony ride offers an incredible experience if you want to explore. Hire a ( horse or pony /Union (Cab ) at additional cost to reach Thajiwas Glacier that is carpeted with snow all year round. Indulge in fun activities with your loved ones here. Do not miss clicking memorable photographs capturing the mesmerizing scenery. Overnight stay at Hotel .\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sun 25th May) : Sonamarg to Srinagar â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast you will depart from Sonamarg and proceed our drive towards Srinagar. From Srinagar you will be given a tour of local sightseeing of our famous Mughal gardens of Nishat and Shalimar & Chashmashahi where you can enjoy the natural beauty and the mesmerizing view of the valley amidst the mountains. Post the sightseeing, we will take you to the hotel for the overnight stay.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Mon 26th May) : Srinagar to Gulmarg - Day Trip\r\nAfter Breakfast , we will drive to Gulmarg (Meadow of Flowers ) which will take us 2 hours to reach there. You can also enjoy the attractive sceneries of Khilanmarg via Gondola ride (Phase I & II) at your own cost. The Gulmarg Gondola is the highest and longest cable car rope-way of the world and one of the best experiences in Kashmir. This cable car ride is divided into 2 stages and takes you to and from Kongdoori Mountain, which is close to Apharwat Peak. The views from the top are mesmerizing. There are various other adventure activities awaiting you like rock climbing, skiing and trekking. You can try your hands in golfing at one of the worldâ€™s largest golf courses, The Royal Spring Golf Course with 18 holes. You can partake in the activities of your interest. Return to your hotel by evening and stay overnight in Srinagar.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Tue 27th May) : Srinagar to Pahalgam â€“ Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, we\'ll journey towards Pahalgam. You\'ll have the opportunity to explore breathtaking places such as Aru, Betaab Valley, and Chandanwari, accessible through Union Cabs at your own expense, each encompassing its own unique natural beauty. While in Pahalgam, you can engage in various activities based on your preferences, including skiing, golfing, visiting the Lidder Amusement Park, trekking, or experiencing thrilling whitewater rafting. Following the tour of Pahalgam, we\'ll return to the hotel for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Wed 28th May) : Pahalgam to Srinagar â€“ Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast check-out from the hotel. We ensure a punctual transfer. Our driver will take you to the Airport for your onward destination.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Sonamarg with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Srinagar with daily breakfast\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Pahalgam with breakfast\r\n* Sightseeing by assigned vehicle (as per the package). \r\n* Vehicle : Non-AC Innova\r\n* Complimentary 60-minute Shikara Ride. \r\n* Driver allowances. \r\n* Toll tax & Parking. \r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Cost of any adventure activities like Gondola Ride, Skiing, Motor Bike, River rafting, Pony / Sledge Ride etc. \r\n* Cost of Union Cab services in Pahalgam, Gulmarg and Sonmarg, Doodhpathri, Yusmarg ( If You Have Not Included it ) \r\n* Guest Entry Fee at Gulmarg / Aru. \r\n* Guide fees, Camera fees, shopping & any monument entrances. \r\n* Entrance fee for Mughal Gardens or for any Park/ Museum/Monument. \r\n* Any expense incurred by unforeseen/natural circumstances e.g. flight delays/cancellations, road blockage, vehicle breakdown, strikes, etc. \r\n* The cost of chained vehicles from Tangmarg to Gulmarg and vice versa, or to other destinations like Sonamarg, Pahalgam, and Doodhpathri in the event of heavy snow, is not included in your package. \r\n* Anything not in inclusions is Excluded \r\n* NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2025-05-23','2025-05-28',1,0,0,'2025-04-07 12:20:02','2025-04-07 13:14:50'),(934,1601,15494,2,0,0,9000,2000,'Goa Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival at the Goa Airport and transfer to the pre-booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, proceed for the North Goa Tour.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Have breakfast at the hotel and proceed for the South Goa Tour.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Check-out from the hotel and transfer to the Airport for your onward journey.','','* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan Car\r\n* Airport Transfers and tours on Pvt\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Extra kms and hours will be calculated afterwards (if any)\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-05-07','2025-05-10',0,0,0,'2025-04-07 16:33:42','2025-04-07 16:36:55'),(935,1602,624,3,1,0,183600,30000,'North East Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - Thursday 12th June, 2025\r\nGuwahati Airport to Tezpur - Transfer\r\nMeet and greet on arrival at Guwahati Airport and transfer to Tezpur. On arrival check in to the hotel. Evening is free for leisure. Overnight stay at Tezpur.\r\n- Approx. Distance: 170 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours\r\n\r\n2nd Day - Friday 13th June, 2025\r\nTezpur to Dirang - Transfer & Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and drive to Dirang. En route, visit the Tipi Orchidarium, home to over 500 orchid species, and the Nag Temple. Enjoy scenic views and waterfalls along the way. Upon arrival, check in to your hotel. In the afternoon, visit the Apple Orchard & Kiwi Farm (seasonal), Dirang Monastery, and Kalachakra Monastery. Dirang is also known for its hot water springs. Overnight stay in Dirang.\r\n- Approx. Distance: 200 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours 30 minutes\r\nThe Inner Line Permit (ILP) is issued by the Secretary (Political) of Arunachal Pradesh. It\'s required for travelers entering the state through check gates along the Assam or Nagaland borders.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - Saturday 14th June, 2025\r\nDirang to Tawang - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\nAfter an early breakfast, check out from the hotel and head to Tawang, the Land of Hidden Paradise. On the way, visit Sela Pass (13,700 ft), a border between Tawang and West Kameng, and the frozen Sela Lake. Continue to Jaswant Garh War Memorial, honoring a soldier from the 1962 Indo-China war. Later, stop by Nuranng Falls, featured in the movie Koyla. Arrive in Tawang, check in to the hotel, and enjoy the evening at leisure.\r\nDistance: 130 km, Travel Time: 7 hours\r\n\r\n4th Day - Sunday 15th June, 2025\r\nTawang - Local Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, visit the 17th-century Tawang Monastery, also known as Galden Namgyal Lhatse, perched at 10,000 ft with 65 buildings, ancient scriptures, and an 8-meter-high Buddha statue. Itâ€™s the largest monastery in the Himalayas and the second oldest in Asia. Next, visit Urgeling Gompa, the birthplace of the 6th Dalai Lama, and then the War Memorial, honoring martyrs of the 1962 Sino-Indian war. You can also explore the local craft center for masks, carpets, jewelry, and other souvenirs. Evening at leisure. Overnight in Tawang.\r\n\r\n5th Day - Monday 16th June, 2025\r\nTawang to Bomdila - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Bomdila (8,200 ft.), the headquarters of West Kameng District, known for its Buddhist monasteries and cool climate. Upon arrival, check in to your hotel, then visit Gontse Rabgyaling Monastery (Upper Gonpa) and Thub-Chog Gatsel Ling Monastery (Lower Gonpa). Enjoy panoramic views of the Himalayas and snow-capped peaks. In the evening, explore the local market. Overnight stay in Bomdila.\r\nDistance: 170 km | Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\n\r\n6th Day - Tuesday 17th June, 2025\r\nBomdila to Guwahati - Transfer\r\nAfter Breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Guwahati. On Arrival Check in at your hotel. Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n- Approx. Distance: 270 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\n\r\n7th Day - Wednesday 18th June, 2025\r\nGuwahati - Local Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, visit Kamakhya Temple (8:00 AM - 1:00 PM & 3:00 PM till dark), Tirupati Balaji Temple, Nabagraha Temple, Assam State Museum (closed on Mondays), State Zoo & Botanical Garden (closed on Fridays), Regional Science Centre, and Sukreswar Temple (6th Jyotirlinga). In the evening, enjoy a River Cruise on the Brahmaputra (direct payment). Overnight in Guwahati.\r\n\r\n8th Day - Thursday 19th June, 2025\r\nGuwahati to Shillong - Transfer and Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, check out and transfer to Shillong (4,900 ft.), the \'Scotland of the East.\' Enroute, visit Umium Lake, a serene lake surrounded by hills. Upon arrival, check in at your hotel. In the evening, visit Don Bosco Museum and Wards Lake. Overnight stay in Shillong.\r\nApprox. Distance: 100 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\n\r\n9th Day - Friday 20th June, 2025\r\nShillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion\r\nAfter an early breakfast, drive to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), the wettest place on Earth. Enjoy views of Mawdok-Dympep Valley and visit Nohkalikai Falls, Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), and Mawsmai Caves. In the evening, return to Shillong, stopping at Elephanta Falls. Overnight stay in Shillong. \r\n- Approx. Distance: 60 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hours.\r\n\r\n10th Day - Saturday 21st June, 2025\r\nShillong to Mawlynnong and Dawki - Excursion\r\nAfter an early breakfast, drive to Mawlynnong, Asiaâ€™s Cleanest Village, to see the living root bridge and a balancing boulder. Then, head to Dawki near the India-Bangladesh border for stunning views of the Umangot River. In the evening, drive back to Shillong for an overnight stay.\r\nApprox. Distance: 120 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours.\r\n\r\n11th Day - Sunday 22nd June, 2025\r\nShillong to Guwahati Airport - Transfer\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey.\r\n- Approx. Distance: 100 km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\n\r','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 10N Accommodation with daily breakfast and dinner\r\n* Exclusive A/c vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (ac will not run in hill area) Ertiga\r\n* All hotel taxes (as per itinerary).\r\n* ILP\r\n','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage.\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary.\r\n* Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any.\r\n* VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot).\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure.\r\nNOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-06-12','2025-06-21',1,0,0,'2025-04-08 11:02:51','2025-04-08 12:54:38'),(936,1606,54,8,0,0,153300,23000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the Singapore Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. \r\nNight Safari with Tram Ride (PVT)\r\n\r\nDat 02 : Have breakfast at the hotel.\r\nSIN City Orientation Drive + Afternoon Sentosa (PVT)\r\nSentosa inclusion (Cable Car + Luge & Skyride + Wings of Time) \r\n\r\nDay 03 : Have breakfast at the hotel\r\nUniversal Studio â€“ ( Dynamic price) (PVT)\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Have breakfast at the hotel\r\nGardens by the Bay (Flower Dome + Supertree)  (PVT)\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Have breakfast at the hotel\r\nDay at leisure for self exploration.\r\n\r\nDay 06 : Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out. Transfer from Hotel to airport on PVT.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-06-14','2025-06-19',1,0,0,'2025-04-11 14:15:28','2025-04-11 16:15:23'),(937,1607,1305,2,2,3,48100,14000,'Shillong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (23rd May) : Guwahati Airport to Shillong - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nOn arrival at Guwahati Airport transfer to Shillong, which is also called the \'Scotland of the East\". On the way visit a majestic placid lake with its surrounding sylvan hills Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which is the biggest local market. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (24th May) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion \r\nApprox Distance : 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hours \r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), the wettest place in the world. Enroute enjoy view of Mawdok - Dympep Valley View Point. You will see the beautiful waterfall known as Nohkalikai. Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls). You can also explore the caves known as Mawsmai. Evening return to Shillong, enroute visit Elephanta falls. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (25th May) : Shillong to Mawlynnong and Dawki - Excursion \r\nApprox Distance : 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 4 hours \r\nAfter early breakfast drive to Mawlynnong â€“ â€œAsiaâ€™s Cleanest Villageâ€. Mawlynnong offers many interesting sights such as the living root bridge and another strange natural phenomenon of a boulder balancing on another small rock. Later proceed to Dawki, a small town near India Bangladesh border. Enjoy breathtaking view of the Umangot River. Evening drive back to Shillong. Stay overnight at your hotel in Shillong.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (26th May) : Shillong to Guwahati Airport - Sightseeing and Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time : 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Wardâ€™s Lake. Later transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation in Shillong with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner.\r\n* Vehicle : Dzire\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area) \r\nâ€¢ All hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any \r\nâ€¢ VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Insurance \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-05-23','2025-05-26',1,0,0,'2025-04-14 11:26:40','2025-04-14 16:12:40'),(938,1609,15512,4,0,0,0,0,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“  21st May : Arrival Ho Chi Minh Vietnam â€“ Leisure Day\r\nWelcome to Ho Chi Minh City! Upon arrival at Tan Son Nhat Airport, our guide will greet you and transfer you to downtown for check-in (from 14:00). Early check-in is not included. Enjoy the rest of the day at leisure. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : private transfer, guide, hotel, water\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 22nd May : Highlight city tour full day (B)\r\nBreakfast at the hotel. Depart at 10:00 AM to visit Saigon Zoo and Botanical Garden, Vietnam\'s largest zoo, established in 1864. Next, see Notre Dame Cathedral, a stunning replica of Paris\' landmark. Visit the War Remnants Museum, then explore the French-colonial Central Post Office. End the day at Ben Thanh Market, the oldest in Saigon, for shopping and sightseeing. Return to the hotel by 5:00 PM. Overnight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel, breakfast\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 23rd May : Ho Chi Minh â€“ Fly to Da Nang â€“ Coconut Basket Boat â€“ Hoi An old town (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel, then transfer (without guide) to the airport for your flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival, meet the guide and transfer to the hotel for check-in (14:00). In the afternoon, visit the Green Bay Mau water coconut forest, row a basket boat, catch field crabs, and explore a Vietnam War revolutionary base. Then, visit Hoi An Ancient Town, including the Kwan Temple, Phuc Kien Assembly Hall, Tan Ky Old House, Japanese Bridge, and Hoi An Market. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\nInclusion : transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel, water\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 24th May : Ba Na hill â€“ Golden Bridge full day (B) \r\nHave breakfast at your hotel, then at 9:00 AM, transfer to Ba Na Hills (35km from Danang). Ride the Sun world Cable Car to the Ba Na Hills station, stopping at By Night station to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas. Continue to the top of Nui Chua Mountain, exploring Nghinh Phong Peak, Le Nim Villas, Orchid Garden, Le Jardin Dâ€™amour, and Linh Ung Pagoda. Walk across the Golden Bridge with panoramic views. Enjoy lunch on your own and free time at Fantasy Park, Vietnamâ€™s third-largest indoor games zone. Overnight in Danang.\r\nPlease note: Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, DW Debay ancient wine cellar, cotton animal game and carnival skill at Fantasy Park is not included in my quotation, joining them will be at your own account.   \r\nInclusion :  Transfer, guide, entrance fee, cable car ticket, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 25th May : Da Nang â€“ fly to Hanoi â€“ city tour half day  (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel, then transfer to the airport (no guide) for your morning flight to Da Nang. Upon arrival, meet our guide and transfer to the hotel for check-in (2:00 PM). In the afternoon, visit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum and grounds, then the One Pillar Pagoda. Next, explore the Temple of Literature, Vietnamâ€™s first university, followed by a visit to Ngoc Son Temple at Hoan Kiem Lake. The tour ends around 5:30 PM. Overnight in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide, entrance fee, hotel, breakfast, water\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 26th May : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D) â€“ private transfer, sharing cruise\r\nDepart your hotel around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour private transfer to Ha Long Bay. Arrive at the port by noon, board the cruise, and head to your cabin. Enjoy a seafood lunch while cruising through Bai Tu Long Bay. Swim, explore a cave, and relax on a secluded beach. Return to the boat for sunset views and a seafood dinner. Overnight on board.\r\nInclusion : private Transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\nExclusion : Beverage\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 27nd May : Explore Bai Tu Long Bay â€“ Hanoi Departure (B/BR)(SIC)\r\nEarly risers can enjoy the sunrise and the stunning Bay landscape with towering limestone. After breakfast at 8:00 AM, take a short rowboat ride with locals and enjoy brunch on the boat as you cruise back. Then, weâ€™ll transfer you back to Ha Noi and to the airport for your flight. Trip ends! Thank you, and we hope to see you again soon.\r\nNote : The final cruise itinerary is subject to change based on each cruiseâ€™s program.\r\nInclusion: Transfer, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch\r\nExclusion : Beverage\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights Included (SGN-DAD, DAD-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.)\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNote : Child 2,2,4 & 4 ys are FOC (under 1m talled). Any extra cost for entrance fee, will be pay directly at the spot.\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. Any activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.','2025-05-21','2025-05-27',1,0,0,'2025-04-15 15:45:25','2025-04-15 17:21:18'),(939,1612,33,4,0,0,212000,38000,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (23rd May) : Private Airport to HK Ferry terminal transf