for the homebound journey\r\n\r\n	\r\n\r\n','','* DEL-CMB-DEL Economy class airfare\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on Half Board basis\r\n* Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Vehicle. (Toyota Mini Coaster)\r\n* Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\n* City tours in Kandy, Bentota & Colombo.\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day                            \r\n* Welcome at the airport with Garlands                         \r\n* Express way charges wherever applicable\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n','* Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.                    \r\n* Early check in or late checkout charges.                                                          \r\n* Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs                                         \r\n* Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.       \r\n* Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.       \r\n* Camera or Video permits.                                             \r\n* Expenses of a personal nature.                         \r\n* Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.                     \r\n* Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n ','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability\r\nTurtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride and Gangaramaya Temple tours can be done at supplementary cost. ','2025-06-13','2025-06-21',1,0,0,'2025-04-21 14:28:42','2025-04-24 17:16:16'),(942,1614,3511,5,0,0,0,0,'North East Diaries','1st Day - (Friday 6th June) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours\r\n\r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Gangtok (5,500 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Gangtok\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Saturday 7th June) : Gangtok to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir - Excursion\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft. / 37 Kms. / 02 Hrs. from Gangtok) and further drive to New Baba Mandir (13,200 ft. / 16 Kms. / 01 Hrs. from Tsomgo Lake). Evening back to Gangtok. Overnight stay at Gangtok. Note: In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing. Due to winter season (heavy snow) vehicle will be able to drive till Snow point on the way to Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 8th June) : Gangtok to Pelling - Transfer Via Namchi\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 200 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 9 hours\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, start for Pelling (6,300 Ft. / 120 Kms. / 5 Hrs.) via Namchi to visit Siddheshwar Dham (Chardham) and Sai Temple. On arrival check-in to your hotel. Overnight stay at Pelling.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n4th Day - (Monday 9th June) : Pelling to Darjeeling - Halfday Sightseeing and Transfer\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 7 hours 30 minutes\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel & start for a half-day sightseeing and visit Pemayangtse monastery, Rabdantse ruins (2nd capital of Sikkim), Sang-Ngag Choling (Skywalk). In afternoon, transfer to Darjeeling (6,950 Ft. / 80 Kms. / 4 Hrs.) via Singla Check post. On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 10th June) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 130 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours\r\n\r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM, visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Evening free for shopping or leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n\r\nNote: Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n6th Day - (Wednesday 11th June) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop\r\n\r\nApprox Distance: 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','DEL-IXB-DEL Economy class airfare\r\nAccommodation as mentioned in hotel section\r\nAll the room are base category unless otherwise mentioned\r\nMeal Plan (as per mentioned above)\r\nExclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. \r\nAll permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary)\r\nRates are valid for INDIAN NATIONALS only','Air Fare / Train fare\r\nPersonal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage\r\nAdditional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\nEntrance Fees & Guide charges\r\nAny cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot)\r\nAny increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\nRoom Heater Charges\r\nInsurance\r\nNOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded','Airfare is dynamic. \r\nRoom/s are subject to availability. \r\nPlease note that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis)','2025-06-06','2025-06-11',1,0,0,'2025-04-21 15:05:09','2025-04-21 15:05:09'),(943,1615,267,17,0,0,62000,7000,'Ludhiana-Manali','Day-wise itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (27th April): After Breakfast depart for Ludhiana. Reach ludhiana, check-in at hotel and evening at leisure. \r\n\r\nDay 2 (28th April): Stay at ludhiana\r\n\r\nDay 3 (29th April):  Check-out after breakfast and leave for Manali. Check-in at hotel. In evening, visit local market. \r\n\r\nDay 4 (30th April): After breakfast, proceed for manali local sightseeing.  \r\n\r\nDay 5 (1st Mayl): After breakfast,  Solang valley and rohtang pass. (Need to check for rohtang pass first)\r\n\r\nDat 6 (2nd May): After breakfast check-out from hotel and leave for return journey to Gurugram.','','5 Nights stay in the mentioned hotels\r\nDaily breakfast\r\n17 seater tempo traveler \r\nToll tax and parking\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expense\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in Inclusions\r\n','','2025-04-27','2025-05-02',1,0,0,'2025-04-21 19:16:42','2025-04-21 19:19:48'),(944,1616,355,5,0,0,0,0,'Varanasi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (20th Jun) - Ayodhya Arrival -Varanasi \r\nPickup from Ayodhya Airport  and transfer Ayodhya sightseeing . Enjoy to temple tour - Ramjanambhoomi, Hanumangarhi, kanak Bhawan & Dashrath Mahal .Then drive to Varanasi Overnight stay in hotel . \r\n                                                                                                                      \r\nDay 2 (21st Jun) - Varanasi \r\nBefore breakfast proceed for Kashi Vishwanath temple, After breakfast Annapurna temple Sankat Mochan Hanuman temple , Manas Mandir , BHU and drive to Sarnath.\r\nSarnath is the spot where Lord Buddha delivered his sermon after getting enlightenment. Top attractions visited in Sarnath are an archeological museums, Buddha temples, stupas, and others. etc\r\nLater in the evening Ganga aarti by boat ride with guide (charges Included). Stay overnight in Hotel.         \r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ Varanasi  drop\r\n\"In morning, after breakfast , check out from hotel and drop at Varanasi Airport.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation on the above-mentioned hotels or similar as per itinerary .\r\n* Breakfast at hotel\r\n* Transfers & sightseeing by Ac Crysta\r\n(Vehicle Service from 08:00 Am to 08:00 PM after that additional cost will be applicable )\r\n* Toll, Parking, Driver Allowance.\r\n* All Applicable Tax.\r\n* 1 Boat ride for evening Ganga Aarti  (90 minutes )\r\n* 2 E- Rickshaw + 1 Guide for 1day at Ayodhya Temple tour\r\n* 1 Full day for Varanasi Temple tour\r\n \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entrances fees \r\n* Tips and porter charges\r\n* Any additional expenses incurred due to any flight delay or cancellation, weather conditions, political closures, technical faults etc\r\n* Any other service/s not specified above\r\n \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-06-20','2025-06-22',1,0,0,'2025-04-22 16:11:27','2025-04-22 16:16:42'),(945,1617,26,5,0,0,374300,48000,'London Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n* Arrival transfer from Airport to Hotel\r\n* London Hop-On Hop-Off Open Top Sightseeing Bus Tour, Valid 1 days + Thame River Cruise + London EYE ticket\r\n* SIC Day trip to Windsor Castle, Stonehenge and Bath(all entrance tickets included)\r\n* SIC Oxford and Traditional Cotswolds Villages \r\n* SIC Warner Bros. Studio Tour London - The Making of Harry Potter with shuttle Transport\r\n* One way transfer to LHR Airport\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* City Tax/Tourist Tax (If Applicable)\r\n* Van tours Tips (4-5 EUR per person per day)\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nVisa charges are dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nSIC Tour pick up is not from the hotel , clients has to make their own arrangement for transfers to & for to the pick up point exact pick up point will come to know once booking is confirmed\r\n \r\n','2025-08-26','2025-08-31',1,0,0,'2025-04-23 13:58:00','2025-04-23 18:08:48'),(946,1620,15542,20,0,0,32000,8000,'Rishikesh Adventures','\r\nDay-wise Itinerary:\r\n\r\nDay 1 (13th May): Early morning departure from Gurgaon. Reach Rishikesh and check-in at hotel. Local sightseeing in evening. \r\nDay 2 (14th May): After breakfast, local sightseeing. \r\nDay 3 (15th May): After breakfast, check-out and travel back to Gurgaon.','','2 nights hotel accommodation in the mentioned hotel\r\nDaily breakfast\r\n20-seater Tempo traveler \r\nDriver Charges\r\nToll Tax\r\nParking\r\n\r\n','Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nAny type of personal expenses\r\nVisit to any tourist spot out of Rishikesh\r\nAnything that is not mentioned in inclusions','Rooms are subject to availability. ','2025-05-13','2025-05-15',0,0,0,'2025-04-25 14:12:55','2025-04-25 14:19:08'),(947,1619,50,2,0,0,88400,16500,'Vietnam Diaries','\r\nDay 1 - 20 May: Arrival Ho Chi Minh City â€“ Afternoon city tour\r\nOn arrival, we will pick up and transfer to your hotel to drop your luggages. (Should land at Ho Chi Minh before 12:00)\r\nAt 1:30 pm, letâ€™s see some French colonial structures including Notre Dame Cathedral, the Old Central Post Office.\r\nContinue on to Ben Thanh market, you have time for shopping here until 5:30 pm, and go back to your hotel to check in and take a rest.\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nHotel check in time: 14:00 pm (Early check in is not guaranteed)\r\n\r\nDay 2 - 21 May: Cu Chi tunnel half day tour (SIC) (B)\r\n\r\n8:00 AM: Letâ€™s move to Cu Chi. It will take approximately one and a half hours by bus driving.\r\n\r\nUpon arrival, before exploring the tunnels, you will have some short introduction followed by an introductory video about how the tunnels were constructed and how the people survived in the harsh conditions of the war time. Then, spend your time to explore the remaining area and tunnel systems which included the special constructed living areas with kitchens, bedrooms side by side with other martial facilities like storage, weapons factories, field hospitals, and command centers helping whoever lives inside the tunnels meet their basic needs. Besides, there are also many hidden trap doors and dangerous traps within the maze-like tunnels for security purpose during the war. Afterward, special tea and cassava\r\n\r\n(guerillaâ€™s food during the war) will be served. 14:00 â€“ 14:30 PM, finish the tour and come back to your hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 3 - 22 May: Ho Chi Minh - Flight to Danang, Marble Mountain - Hoi An town Tour(SIC) (B,D)\r\n\r\nDepending on your flight time, pick up at the hotel and transfer (without guide) to the airport for your flight to Danang by our driver.\r\n\r\n(Should land at Danang airport before 14:30) Hotel check in time: 14:00\r\n\r\n\r\nAt 15:30: Letâ€™s start the SIC tour, we first visit Non Nuoc Stone Carving village - Here you can admire the stone sculptures made under the immensely talented hands of the artists.\r\n\r\nAt 16:45: Visit Marble Mountain. You will discover the hidden caves, shrines and pagodas ( Linh Ung pagoda, Tam Thai, XÃ¡ Lá»£i tower, Tang Chon cave, Hoa Nghiem Cave, Huyen Khong cave,..)\r\n\r\nAt 17:30 : Transfer to Hoi an ancient town\r\n\r\nOn the way to Hoi an, stop to have dinner, enjoy Hoi An special foods such as Cao Lau, Chicken Rice,...\r\n\r\nAt 18:00: Have free time to visit Hoi an walking town at night ( old houses, lanterns, architecture, and folk activities,..)\r\n\r\nAt 20:30: Car and guide takes you back to the hotel in Danang. Overnight in Da Nang.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 4 - 23 May: Danang half day tour (SIC) (B,L)\r\n\r\n09:00-09:30 : Our van and guide will pick you up from the hotel in Da nang and transfer to visit Da nang city.\r\n\r\nVisit Non Nuoc Stone Carving village & Marble Mountains.\r\n\r\nVisit Linh Ung pagoda, on Son Tra peninsula\r\n\r\n11:15 : We drive across Thuan Phuoc bridge, one of the longest cable-stayed bridges of Viet Nam. From here, you will have a great view over Han river bridge, Vung Thung and God\'s eye of Indochina before arriving to visit the Museum of Cham Sculpture.\r\n\r\n12:00: Have Lunch at a local restaurant in Da nang.\r\n\r\n13:00: Van takes you to visit Han Market - the most famous market in Da nang. From here, you can buy some souvenirs to your friends and family\r\n\r\n13:30-14:00 : Back to your hotel in Da nang . Finish the trip\r\n\r\nOvernight in Danang\r\n\r\nDay 5 - 24 May: Bana Hills â€“ Golden Bridge (SIC)(B,L).\r\n\r\nAt 8:00 â€“ 8:30 a.m : Our car and Guide will meet you at your hotel in Da Nang and start the trip to Ba Na Hills.\r\n\r\nAt 9:30 a.m : Upon arrival at Ba Na hills, you will get on a Cable Car which gains 4 world scores\r\n\r\nVisit Debay Wine Cellar built in 1923 (entrance fee by yourself), Le Jardin Dâ€™Amour Flower Garden Highlight in this tour is Golden Bridge ( Hands of God). You will have a chance to see and take photos of this beautiful bridge.\r\n\r\nYou continue to visit Linh Ung pagoda where the highest Buddhism statue in the country is located (27 m).\r\n\r\nAt 11: 30 a.m: Have Lunch at a restaurant and take a short rest.\r\nAt 12:30 p.m: Conquer the peak of Chua Mountain at the height of 1487 m, the highest peak in Ba na to visit Linh Chua Linh Tu Temple. You continue to discover the French Square, visit and play some games in Fantasy Park â€“ one of the largest indoor amusement parks in Vietnam with a series of interesting games.\r\n\r\nAt 15:30: Back to the cabin down the mountain.\r\n\r\nBack to the hotel in Da nang/ Hoi an. Arrive in Da nang at about 17:00. Overnight in Da Nang. \r\n\r\nDay 6 - 25 May: Danang Departure (B)\r\n\r\nDepending on your flight you may have some more time for shopping on your own. Then we will transfer you without a guide to Hanoi airport for your flight home. Goodbye, and hope to see you again soon!\r\n\r\n\r\n','','- DEL-SGN and HAN-DEL economy class airfare included\r\n- One internal flight from Ho Chi Minh to Da Nang is included\r\n- Accommodation based on double/twin/triple sharing room \r\n- Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary \r\n- Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary \r\n- Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu) \r\n- SIC tours as mentioned \r\n- Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary \r\n- Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day) \r\n- Travel Insurance\r\n- Visa','- Early check in/Late check out \r\n- Beverages \r\n- Personal expenses \r\n- Tips (Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory))\r\n- Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.) \r\n- Others not mentioned in the written details above. ','Kindly note: Entrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nPlease see inclusive items listed after each day. \r\nAirfare is dynamic\r\nRooms are subject to availability. \r\n','2025-05-20','2025-05-25',1,0,0,'2025-04-25 14:29:33','2025-04-25 15:22:19'),(948,1621,50,4,0,0,177000,33000,'Vietnam Diaries','\r\nDay 1 - 20 May: Arrival Ho Chi Minh City â€“ Afternoon city tour\r\nOn arrival, we will pick up and transfer to your hotel to drop your luggages. (Should land at Ho Chi Minh before 12:00)\r\nAt 1:30 pm, letâ€™s see some French colonial structures including Notre Dame Cathedral, the Old Central Post Office.\r\nContinue on to Ben Thanh market, you have time