r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide pick up, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 25th May : Cu Chi tunnels half day tour (B)\r\nAt 8 AM, weâ€™ll pick you up from your hotel and head to the Cu Chi Tunnels, about a 1.5-hour drive. You\'ll watch an introductory video, then explore the tunnel system, including living areas, kitchens, hospitals, and hidden traps used during the war. Return to your hotel in Ho Chi Minh City by noon and relax for the afternoon. Overnight in HCMC.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, guide, water, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 26th May : : HCMC â€“ Flight to Danang, Coconut forest, Hoi An (B)\r\nIn the morning, our driver will transfer you to the airport for your flight to Danang (arrive before 13:00). Upon arrival, visit Bay Mau coconut forest, enjoy a basket boat ride, catch crabs, and explore a former revolutionary base. Then, tour Hoi An Ancient Town, including the Japanese Bridge and local market. Return to your hotel by 9:00 PM. Overnight in Danang.\r\nInclusions : Private transfer, guide, entrance fees, boat/basket ride, water, and hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 27th May : Bana Hills (B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:30 AM for Ba Na Hills (35 km from Danang). Take the world-renowned Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Le Nim Villas, Orchid Garden, and ride Vietnamâ€™s only funicular. Walk across the iconic Golden Bridge and enjoy the panoramic views. After lunch (on your own), enjoy free time at Fantasy Park with various games and attractions. Return to your hotel around 5 PM. Overnight in Danang.\r\nKindly note : Entrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 28th May :  Danang -  flight to Phu Quoc, free time (B)\r\nIn the morning, pick up and transfer to the airport for your flight to Phu Quoc by our driver. Upon arrival, meet our driver and transfer to your hotel to check in and take a rest.\r\nOvernight in Phu Quoc\r\nInclusion : Private airport transfer, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 29th May : South 4-Islets Discovery by Speed-boat & Sunworld Cable Car (SIC)(B,L)\r\n08:00â€“08:30 Depart from hotel/resort lobby.\r\n08:45 Visit Pearl Farm.\r\n09:45 Arrive at pier, board speedboat.\r\n10:15 Visit Coral Park â€“ optional Sea-Walking.\r\n10:40 Swim at May Rut Islet.\r\n11:10 Snorkeling at Gam Ghi or Buom Islet (weather dependent).\r\n11:50 Transfer to Fingernail Islet.\r\n14:00â€“14:20 Arrive at Hon Thom â€“ enjoy beach, water park, and theme park.\r\n16:45 Take the cable car (worldâ€™s longest sea-crossing).\r\n17:00 Arrive at An Thoi Square.\r\n17:30 Return to hotel/resort. Overnight in Phu Quoc.\r\nInclusion : Shared transfer, guide, entrance fee, speed-boat, cable car ticket, breakfast, lunch, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 30th May : Vin Wonders (B) NO GUIDE\r\nEnjoy free time in the morning. At 1:30 PM, our driver will take you to VinWonders, a themed amusement park inspired by fairy tales and world civilizations, offering diverse attractions and entertainment. Explore until 7:30 PM, then return to your hotel to rest. Overnight in Phu Quoc.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 8 - 31st May : Phu Quoc Departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel. Depending on your flight you may have some more time for shopping on your own. Then we transfer you (without a guide) to the airport for your flight home. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights Included (SGN-DAD, DAD-PQC)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.)\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNote : Child 2,2,4 & 4 ys are FOC (under 1m talled). Any extra cost for entrance fee, will be pay directly at the spot.\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. Any activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.','2025-05-24','2025-05-31',1,0,0,'2025-05-02 11:14:51','2025-05-02 14:03:51'),(954,1627,7,4,0,0,126400,18000,'Shanghai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 (6th Jun) : Arrival at the PVG Airport.\r\nPVG airport pick up and proceed for half day sightseeing if time permits incl Yu Market, City God Temple, Peopleâ€™s Square, Nanjing road \r\n\r\nDay 2 (7th Jun) : Day Tour\r\nHave breakfast at the hotel and proceed for Day tour for Zhujiajiao water town, back to city free shopping at AP plaza, Bund area with outside looking of Pearl Tv Tower\r\n\r\nDay 3 (8th Jun) : Departure\r\nAfter having breakfast check out from the hotel by 12:00 and one way PVG airport drop by driver with placard only\r\nEND\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation with breakfast\r\n* Airport transfers on PVT.\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Pvt. Vehicle service as per mentioned above\r\n* English speaking guide service\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping USD60 total \r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-06-06','2025-06-08',1,0,0,'2025-05-03 13:20:26','2025-05-14 14:53:55'),(955,1628,19541,2,1,1,142100,34000,'Bhutan Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Transfer from Bagdogra (IXB) Airport Phuentsholing - Wagon R / Alto / Etios Similar\r\nMeet & Greet on arrival at IXB Airport and transfer to Phuentsholing - The Gateway of Bhutan by Road from India. It is a thriving commercial center on the northern edge of the Indian Plains. On arrival check in at the hotel. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing hotel.\r\nNotes:\r\nDepending on your arrival time our representative will assist you in procurement of your permit to Bhutan. The permit issuance takes time depending on the rush one has to stand in queue for procurement of permit. In case the permit is not processed on the day of arrival then it can be issued next day before you start for next destination.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Transfer from Phuentsholing to Thimphu\r\nAfter having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to Thimphu.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Full Day Thimphu Sightseeing - MG Hector / Santa Fe / Creta / Similar\r\nAfter breakfast, enjoy a full-day sightseeing tour of Thimphu. Visit the National Memorial Chorten, built in honor of Bhutan\'s third King; Tashichho Dzong, the seat of Bhutanâ€™s government and monastic body; and Buddha Point for panoramic valley views. Explore the ancient Changangkha Lhakhang temple and see Bhutanâ€™s national animal at the Motithang Takin Preserve. Visit Zilukha Nunnery, the Institute for Zorig Chusum (Arts & Crafts School), and the National Textile Museum to learn about Bhutanese traditions. End with a visit to Zangthopelri Lhakhang Monastery before returning to your hotel for the night.\r\nNotes : Charges for all activities and entry to monuments & memorials need to be paid by the customer on direct payment basis.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Transfer from Thimphu to Paro & Paro Sightseeing - MG Hector / Santa Fe / Creta / Similar\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Paro, stopping en route to visit Tamchog Lhakhang, a temple dedicated to 13th-century bridge builder Thangthong Gyalpo, accessed by one of his original iron chain bridges. On arrival in Paro, check into your hotel. In the afternoon, visit Ta Dzong, a former watchtower now serving as Bhutanâ€™s National Museum, and Rinpung Dzong, an impressive 17th-century fortress housing monks and administrative offices. Return to the hotel for an overnight stay.\r\nNotes : Charges for all activities and entry to monuments & memorials need to be paid by the customer on direct payment basis.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Day Excursion to Chele-La-Pass (With Guide) - MG Hector / Santa Fe / Creta / Similar\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Chele-La Pass, the highest motorable road in Bhutan at 3,810m, offering stunning views of Mt. Jumolhari, Jichu Drake, and the Paro and Haa valleys. Enjoy the scenic drive through forests and optional short walks. Return to Paro in the afternoon for leisure and an overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Transfer from Paro to Phuentsholing (With Guide) - MG Hector / Santa Fe / Creta / Similar\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from hotel and transfer to Phuentsholing. On arrival check in at the hotel. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Transfer from Phuentsholing to Bagdogra (IXB) Airport / NJP Railway Station - Wagon R / Alto / Etios Similar\r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and proceed to Bagdogra (IXB) Airport / NJP Railway Station for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on pvt.\r\n* Tours as mentioned\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Passport fees, immunization costs, city taxes at the hotel and local departure taxes (wherever applicable)\r\n* Optional enhancements like room or flight upgrades, or local camera or video fees\r\n* Additional sightseeing, activities and experiences outside of the itinerary\r\n* Early check-in or late check-out from hotels (unless otherwise specified)\r\n* Breakfast, lunches, dinners and drinks (alcoholic and non-alcoholic), unless specified in the itinerary\r\n* Tips for services and experiences\r\n* Any Visa required, unless mentioned as an inclusion\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-05-22','2025-05-28',1,0,0,'2025-05-03 14:09:38','2025-05-04 15:42:33'),(956,1629,15512,4,0,0,231500,43000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nSuggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 â€“  24th May : Arrival Ho Chi Minh City Vietnam â€“ Leisure Day\r\nWe will welcome you at the airport, then transfer to your hotel to drop your luggages, and take a rest in the lobby in the morning.\r\nAround 12:00, our driver will pick up and transfer (without guide) to some local markets in the center (less than 100 km), you will have time for shopping until 4:00 pm and come back to your hotel to check in and take a rest.\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, guide pick up airport, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 2 â€“ 25th May : Cu Chi tunnels half day tour (B)\r\nAt 8:30 am, Saigon Zoo and Botanical Garden is the biggest zoo in Vietnam and one of the oldest zoos in the world. This botanical garden and zoo was established in 1864.\r\nProceed to Notre Dame, an amazing replica of the one in Paris. Admire the gothic-style architecture of the structure that is surrounded by bell towers and parks.\r\nNext, proceed to the War Remnants Museum showcasing evidence of the Indochina wars.\r\nThe next stop will be the Central Post Office. Built by the French in colonial times, its architecture is worth witnessing!\r\nLastly, proceed to Ben Thanh Market, walk along the fascinating streets and spot the Big Ben. Don\'t forget to shop at the oldest market in Saigon!\r\nFinish the tour at 5:30 pm and go back to your hotel.\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel, breakfast\r\n\r\nDay 3 â€“ 26th May : : HCMC â€“ Flight to Danang, Coconut forest, Hoi An (B)\r\nIn the morning, our driver will transfer you to the airport for your flight to Danang (arrive before 13:00). Upon arrival, visit Bay Mau coconut forest, enjoy a basket boat ride, catch crabs, and explore a former revolutionary base. Then, tour Hoi An Ancient Town, including the Japanese Bridge and local market. Return to your hotel by 9:00 PM. Overnight in Danang.\r\nInclusions : Private transfer, guide, entrance fees, boat/basket ride, water, and hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 4 â€“ 27th May : Bana Hills (B)\r\nAfter breakfast, depart at 8:30 AM for Ba Na Hills (35 km from Danang). Take the world-renowned Sunworld Cable Car to visit Vong Nguyet Hills, Linh Ung Pagoda, and French Villas. Continue to Nui Chua Mountain to explore Le Nim Villas, Orchid Garden, and ride Vietnamâ€™s only funicular. Walk across the iconic Golden Bridge and enjoy the panoramic views. After lunch (on your own), enjoy free time at Fantasy Park with various games and attractions. Return to your hotel around 5 PM. Overnight in Danang.\r\nKindly note : Entrance fares exclude WOW Pass, 10D Movie, Alpine Coaster, Wax Museum, Debay Wine Cellar, Teddy bear grips, coin games and Fantasy Park indoor sports.\r\nInclusion :  Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 â€“ 28th May :  Danang -  flight to Phu Quoc, free time (B)\r\nIn the morning, pick up and transfer to the airport for your flight to Phu Quoc by our driver. Upon arrival, meet our driver and transfer to your hotel to check in and take a rest.\r\nOvernight in Phu Quoc\r\nInclusion : Private airport transfer, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ 29th May : South 4-Islets Discovery by Speed-boat & Sunworld Cable Car (SIC)(B,L)\r\n08:00â€“08:30 Depart from hotel/resort lobby.\r\n08:45 Visit Pearl Farm.\r\n09:45 Arrive at pier, board speedboat.\r\n10:15 Visit Coral Park â€“ optional Sea-Walking.\r\n10:40 Swim at May Rut Islet.\r\n11:10 Snorkeling at Gam Ghi or Buom Islet (weather dependent).\r\n11:50 Transfer to Fingernail Islet.\r\n14:00â€“14:20 Arrive at Hon Thom â€“ enjoy beach, water park, and theme park.\r\n16:45 Take the cable car (worldâ€™s longest sea-crossing).\r\n17:00 Arrive at An Thoi Square.\r\n17:30 Return to hotel/resort. Overnight in Phu Quoc.\r\nInclusion : Shared transfer, guide, entrance fee, speed-boat, cable car ticket, breakfast, lunch, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 7 â€“ 30th May : Vin Wonders (B) NO GUIDE\r\nAt 9:00 - 9:30 am, our driver will pick up and start to move to Vin Wonders which promises to be a potential tourist destination with fun activities, entertainment and interesting experiences. These 6 subdivisions are created with 12 themes inspired by fairy tales, anecdotes of the world or famous civilizations, etc. Because of this, it has created a novelty and attraction. tourists with high education, art and entertainment.\r\n\r\nYou have time to explore here until 7:30 pm, finish the tour, and we will transfer you back to your hotel and take a rest.\r\n\r\nOvernight in Phu Quoc\r\n\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, entrance fee, water, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 8 - 31st May : Phu Quoc Departure (B)\r\nBreakfast at your hotel. Depending on your flight you may have some more time for shopping on your own. Then we transfer you (without a guide) to the airport for your flight home. \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights Included (SGN-DAD, DAD-PQC)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double sharing room\r\n* Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\n* Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\n* SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Entrance fee to the mentioned itinerary\r\n* Bottled water for the touring day (500ml/bottle/pax/day)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Surcharge in peak season (Christmas, New Year, Lunar New Year, etc.)\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNote : Child 2,2,4 & 4 ys are FOC (under 1m talled). Any extra cost for entrance fee, will be pay directly at the spot.\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. Any activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\nBaggage is 20Kg per person for DEL-SGN and PQC-DEL flights.','2025-05-24','2025-05-31',1,0,0,'2025-05-04 15:14:58','2025-05-04 15:33:20'),(957,1630,15901,4,0,0,528000,50000,'2 Dham Darshan','Suggested Iinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : On arrival at Dehradun check in at Hotel. \r\nOvernight stay in hotel with Dinner\r\n\r\nDay 2 : 07:45 - 08:30- DDN-Guptkashi\r\nAfter breakfast transfer you by road to Helipad . On arrival at Sahastradhara Helipad, we fly to Guptkashi Helipad then again fly to Kedarnath from same Helipad. Temple is approx. 500 meters away from helipad and will take approx. 15 min to reach. Ground Staff will accompany the group and lead us to the VIP darshan in Kedarnath temple. After darshan and Poojan, the group will fly back to Guptkashi helipad. We will have lunch & Overnight stay at hotel in Guptkashi located at the bank of river Mandakini or Kedarnath dham.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : 08:30-09:00 - Guptkashi-Badrinath\r\nThe group is headed towards the Helipad at Guptkashi Helipad. From the Helipad we proceed to Badrinath. On arrival at Badrinath Helipad,\r\nThe group will be Check-In to the hotel. After Lunch, we will be going to Mana village, the first Village of India after China border for sightseeing. Our ground staff will assist the guests in taking darshan at the temple. Dinner and   stay at Badrinath.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : 7:45-8:45 - Badrinath-Dehradun\r\nAfter the breakfast, while we are heading back to Dehradun, see the beautiful overview of the Region, especially the picturesque view of the confluences, which is an eye-candy for nature lovers. We will fly between the beautiful valleys of thick forest and over five confluences like Vishnu Prayag, Nanda Prayag, Karna Prayag, Rudra Prayag and Dev Prayag. We will come back and drop Guests to Dehradun Airport or Railway Station.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n','','* Exclusive Helicopter services from Dehradun (Sahastradhara Helipad) to the Do Dham shrines & back.\r\n* 2 Night Accommodation at Do Dham\'s on double sharing basis only with all meals.\r\n* 1 Night Accommodation on double sharing basis with breakfast and Dinner at Dehradun.\r\n* VIP Darshans.\r\n* Shri Kedarnath ji helicopter shuttle services: Guptkashiâ€“ Kedar Guptkashi.\r\n* Helicopter handling charges.\r\n* Pick up and drop from Dehradun airport or Railway Station.\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Maha Abhishek Puja at Badrinath Ji / Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath Ji (at an extra cost)\r\n\r\n\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExcess weight (over 75 kg) is charged at INR 1800/kg. Any extra amount will be collected at the hotel or helipad before the flight.\r\nNote : Exact Schedule can be advised before a day of departure. Above mentioned schedule is tentative just for understanding the operational system & timing. Things can be changed last moment due to any operational or weather changes.\r\nBaggage is limited to 3 kg per passenger. Please avoid large suitcases due to limited space in the helicopter. Extra baggage may not be allowed. Duffle bags are provided during the briefing.\r\nThis tour runs on fixed daily departure times. Passengers must follow the scheduled ETDs or risk being marked as NO-SHOW.\r\n','2025-06-16','2025-06-19',1,0,0,'2025-05-05 11:35:59','2025-05-05 12:26:15'),(958,1631,15901,4,0,0,772000,70000,'Char Dham Darshan','Suggested Iinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : Arrival at Dehradun\r\nThe tour begins with pickup from Dehradun airport or railway station a day before the Chardham Yatra, followed by hotel drop. A detailed tour briefing will be held at 20:30 hrs, during which duffle bags (max 5kg per person) will be provided. Dinner and overnight stay in Dehradun are included. Note: Pilgrims\' body weight will be recorded during the briefingâ€”attendance is mandatory.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Yamunotri \r\n06:00 Departure Sahastradhara helipad, Dehradun \r\n06:30 Arrival Kharsali helipad, Yamunotri\r\nThe Chardham Yatra begins from Sahastradhara Helipad, Dehradun. Guests will check out and be transferred to the helipad, where theyâ€™ll receive pre-flight instructions. On arrival at Kharsali, theyâ€™ll proceed to Yamunotri Temple by palki/pony (6 km trek, approx. 5 hours round trip). After darshan, return to Kharsali for an overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Gangotri\r\n06:35 Departure Kharsali helipad, Yamunotri \r\n07:00 Arrival Harsil Helipad\r\nGuests will check out and board the helicopter from Kharsali to Harsil, a scenic valley near Gangotri. Upon arrival, theyâ€™ll drive 22 km (approx. 50 mins) to Gangotri Temple for darshan, assisted by our staff. After returning, guests can enjoy lunch, relax at the resort, join a campfire, or explore the nearby village for local woolen products.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Kedarnath\r\n07:30 Departure Harsil Helipad \r\n08:10 Arrival Kedarnath helipad\r\nGuests will check out and fly from Harsil to Guptkashi, then take a 10-minute helicopter shuttle to Kedarnath. After VIP darshan (approx. 2 hours), theyâ€™ll return to Guptkashi and transfer to their hotel. Overnight stay will be at Guptkashi or Kedarnath.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Badrinath\r\n08:30 Departure Kedarnath / Guptkashi helipad \r\n09:00 Arrival Badrinath helipad\r\nAfter breakfast, guests will check out and fly from Guptkashi to Badrinath. On arrival, theyâ€™ll check in at a nearby hotel and proceed for temple darshan with staff assistance. An evening visit to Mana village, near the China border, is highly recommended.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Return to Dehradun\r\n09:05 Departure Badrinath helipad \r\n10:00 Arrival Sahastradhara helipad, Dehradun\r\nEarly morning, attend the special Abhishek Puja at Badrinath temple (optional, at your own cost) starting at 4:30 AMâ€” a key highlight of the yatra. After darshan, return to the hotel for breakfast and fly to Dehradun. On arrival, transfer to the airport/railway station. Tour ends with cherished memories.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Helicopter Trip from Dehradun to Dehradun\r\n* All meals in hotels at all Dham (Breakfast, Lunch & Dinner).\r\n* Breakfast & Dinner during the stay in Dehradun.\r\n* Palki / Doli Charges service at Yamunotri.\r\n* VIP darshan arrangement at all temples.\r\n* Landing & Parking charges at Sersi /Sitapur/Guptkashi\r\n* helipad.\r\n* Local Transport for darshan and sightseeing at Gangotri, Badrinath and Kedarnath as per itinenary.\r\n* Hotel accommodation in best Hotels for 04 nights at Yamunotri, Gangotri, Kedarnath (Guptkashi) and Badrinath\r\n* 5 Nights stay, 1 Night at each Dham in Luxury Hotels\r\n* Dehradun Airport Pickup & drop Facilities\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Maha Abhishek Puja at Badrinath Ji / Rudra Abhishek Puja at Kedarnath Ji (at an extra cost)\r\n\r\n\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nExcess weight (over 75 kg) is charged at INR 2300/kg. Any extra amount will be collected at the hotel or helipad before the flight.\r\nNote : Exact Schedule can be advised before a day of departure. Above mentioned schedule is tentative just for understanding the operational system & timing. Things can be changed last moment due to any operational or weather changes.\r\nOnly 5 kg of baggage per passenger is allowed due to limited helicopter space. Large suitcases are not permitted. Duffle bags are provided during briefing. If the group\'s total body weight exceeds 450 kg, extra luggage will be sent by road at an additional shared cost.\r\nThis tour runs on fixed daily departure times. Passengers must follow the scheduled ETDs or risk being marked as NO-SHOW.\r\n','2025-06-16','2025-06-21',0,0,0,'2025-05-05 13:01:22','2025-05-05 14:54:46'),(959,1632,54,4,0,0,95600,15800,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1\r\n  Transfer from Changi International Airport to the booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from the booked Hotel to Evening Mandai (Night Safari) [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Evening Mandai to the booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2\r\n  Transfer from the booked Hotel to Half Day City Tour with Guide (3Hrs) [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3\r\n  Transfer from the booked Hotel to Universal Studios [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Universal Studios to the booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4\r\n  Transfer from the booked Hotel to Full Day Sentosa Island Tour [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Full Day Sentosa Island Tour to the booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 5\r\n  Transfer from Self-booked Hotel to Gardens By The Bay [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Gardens By The Bay to the booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 6\r\n  Transfer from Self-booked Hotel to Changi International Airport [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with Daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Half Day City Tour with Guide (Drop off Little India) (3Hrs) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Universal Studios ( Universal Studio ( Monday -Friday ) ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Full Day Sentosa Island Tour ( Cable Car + Wings Of Time 1st Show + Skyhelix ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Gardens By The Bay ( Flower Dome + Jurassic World : The Exhibition at Cloud Forest ( Valid from 29th May) ) (PVT Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-05-28','2025-06-02',1,0,0,'2025-05-05 16:20:41','2025-05-05 17:01:06'),(960,1633,15496,2,0,0,10000,5000,'Manali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival Manali\r\nPick up from the bus stand and drop to the hotel. Check- in at the hotel.\r\nLocal sightseeing, Hadimba devi temple, club house, Tibetan monestry and Mall road visit \r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast proceed for Manali-Khokhsar, on the way visit Solang valley.\r\n\r\nDay 3 :  Have breakfast at the hotel and proceed for Manali -Nagar-Kullu-Manali\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast at the hotel and check-out.\r\nManali to vashisht\r\n3 hours Jogni waterfall treck \r\nDrop to Manali bus stand','','* Volvo Airfare from Delhi to Manali\r\n* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Vehicle : Alto\r\n* Pick and drop from Manali bus stand on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-05-31','2025-06-03',1,0,0,'2025-05-06 15:04:12','2025-05-06 17:52:28'),(961,1637,33,2,1,0,141900,22000,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Airport Bus Transfers from Hong Kong Airport to Macau Port (No Need to cross the HK Immigration) on SIC Basis + Transfers from Macau Port to Macau Hotel Direct Transfers on PVT Basis - Driver\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Dazzling Macau half day morning tour (Private) Pick up- 12 noon from Hotel lobby. Venetian- West Lobby near ATM. Galaxy- Diamond lobby Tour includes: A Ma temple, Ruins of St Paul cathedral, Kun Lam Statue, Lotus Square & Macau Tower photo stop\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Private Macau Ferry Pier to hotel transfer or Vice versa . Service hours 8 am-10 pm. Vehicle capacity upto 9 pax\r\nFerry ticket 1 way, Eco class, Day sailing, Hong Kong to Macau or Macau to Hong Kong. (7:30 AM to 5:00 PM) (Week Days) (Sun- Thu)	\r\nPick up from ferry Pier & Private Classic Hong Kong half day night tour.1 way Peak tram, Victoria peak, Bahunia Sq , Harbour cruise on Star Ferry, Bruce Lee special Avenue of Star, Old Clock tower. Tour finale with Symphony of light laser show . Duration upto 5 hours. Start time 4 pm. Vehicle capasity-6px (Luggage will be inside the vehicle) \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Private Amazing Ocean park tour, standard entry ticket. Pick up: 9:30 am. Return : 7 pm \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Private Magical Disneyland tour with Tier 3 entry ticket. Pick up: 9:30 am Return:9:30 pm \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Private Peaceful Big Buddha tour w 2way Std Cable car tkts & Outlet mall shopping. Pick up-9:30 am. Return 3:30 pm. Vehicle capacity-6px\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Private Airport Transfer, 1 way (8am-9 pm). Vehicle capacity-6px\r\n','','* 2N Accommodation in Macau with daily breakfast\r\n* 4N Accommodation in Hong Kong with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.','2025-06-22','2025-06-28',1,0,0,'2025-05-07 15:42:49','2025-05-07 17:33:26'),(963,1642,15512,2,1,1,14500,2200,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City, City Half Day (PVT)\r\nUpon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and guide.\r\nVisit the city covering:\r\nâ€¢ Notre Dame Cathedral\r\nâ€¢ Central Post Office\r\nâ€¢ War Remnants Museum\r\nâ€¢ Ben Thanh Market\r\nHead to your hotel to check in and spend rest of the day at your own leisure.\r\nNote: Check in time 14:00\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nPlease note that your driver does not speak English.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (B) (PVT)\r\n8:00 AM: Depart from Ho Chi Minh City to My Tho.\r\nVinh Trang Pagoda: Visit this historic Buddhist temple.\r\nTien River Cruis: Embark on a boat trip to explore four beautiful islands: Dragon, Unicorn, Phoenix, and Tortoise. Experience the serene countryside by sampan, passing through small canals shaded by water coconut trees. Enjoy seasonal fruits, honey tea, and traditional Southern Vietnamese folk music performed by locals.\r\nCoconut Candy Workshop: Learn about the local production of coconut candy and sample fresh products.\r\nReturn to Ho Chi Minh City : Conclude the trip and return to the city.\r\nOvernight: Stay in Ho Chi Minh City.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : HCMC â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (PVT) \r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for your flight to Hanoi.\r\nUpon arrival, meet your guide and driver at the airport for a transfer to the city center.\r\nCheck in at your hotel.\r\nAfternoon Sightseeing\r\nVisit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (viewed from outside), the final resting place of Vietnam\'s revolutionary leader.\r\nExplore the One Pillar Pagoda, a historic Buddhist temple.\r\nStroll around HoÃ n Kiáº¿m Lake (Sword Lake), a serene spot in the city\'s heart.\r\nWander through the Old Quarter, known as \"The 36 Streets,\" each named after the traditional goods sold there.\r\nOvernight : Stay in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nDepart from Hanoi around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour shuttle bus ride to Ha Long Bay. Upon arrival at the port around noon, embark on the cruise, check into your cabin, and enjoy a fresh seafood lunch as you begin your journey through the bay. Afternoon activities include swimming, visiting a mysterious cave, and relaxing on a secluded island beach. Conclude the day with a sunset view from the top deck followed by a seafood dinner. Overnight accommodations are provided on the cruise.\r\nNote : The final cruise itinerary may vary based on the specific cruise program.\r\nInclusion : Sharing transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi (B/Brunch)\r\nEarly risers can witness the breathtaking sunrise and tranquil beauty of Halong Bay\'s towering limestone karsts. After a light breakfast around 7:00 AM, embark on a short rowboat ride with local rowers to explore the bay\'s serene waters. Enjoy a leisurely brunch on the boat as you cruise back to the pier, then begin the journey back to Hanoi.\r\nPlease note that the final cruise itinerary may vary depending on each cruise\'s program.\r\nInclusion: Sharing transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi Depature (B)\r\nHave breakfast and check out.\r\nThen we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. \r\nNote: Our driver doesnâ€™t speak English.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights (SGN-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double/triple sharing room\r\nâ€¢ Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\nâ€¢ SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-06-01','2025-06-06',1,0,0,'2025-05-14 12:31:30','2025-05-14 14:18:34'),(964,1643,15512,2,1,1,12040,4660,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrive Ho Chi Minh City, City Half Day (PVT)\r\nUpon arrival Ho Chi Minh, meeting our driver and guide.\r\nVisit the city covering:\r\nâ€¢ Notre Dame Cathedral\r\nâ€¢ Central Post Office\r\nâ€¢ War Remnants Museum\r\nâ€¢ Ben Thanh Market\r\nHead to your hotel to check in and spend rest of the day at your own leisure.\r\nNote: Check in time 14:00\r\nOvernight in Ho Chi Minh.\r\nPlease note that your driver does not speak English.\r\nInclusion : Transfer, guide, entrance fee, water, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : HCMC â€“ Mekong Delta (B) (PVT)\r\n8:00 AM: Depart from Ho Chi Minh City to My Tho.\r\nVinh Trang Pagoda: Visit this historic Buddhist temple.\r\nTien River Cruis: Embark on a boat trip to explore four beautiful islands: Dragon, Unicorn, Phoenix, and Tortoise. Experience the serene countryside by sampan, passing through small canals shaded by water coconut trees. Enjoy seasonal fruits, honey tea, and traditional Southern Vietnamese folk music performed by locals.\r\nCoconut Candy Workshop: Learn about the local production of coconut candy and sample fresh products.\r\nReturn to Ho Chi Minh City : Conclude the trip and return to the city.\r\nOvernight: Stay in Ho Chi Minh City.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer, guide, entrance fee, breakfast, hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : HCMC â€“ Fly to Hanoi Vietnam â€“ City Tour half day (PVT) \r\nAfter breakfast and hotel check-out, transfer to the airport for your flight to Hanoi.\r\nUpon arrival, meet your guide and driver at the airport for a transfer to the city center.\r\nCheck in at your hotel.\r\nAfternoon Sightseeing\r\nVisit the Ho Chi Minh Mausoleum (viewed from outside), the final resting place of Vietnam\'s revolutionary leader.\r\nExplore the One Pillar Pagoda, a historic Buddhist temple.\r\nStroll around HoÃ n Kiáº¿m Lake (Sword Lake), a serene spot in the city\'s heart.\r\nWander through the Old Quarter, known as \"The 36 Streets,\" each named after the traditional goods sold there.\r\nOvernight : Stay in Hanoi.\r\nInclusion: Private transfer, water, guide, breakfast, hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hanoi â€“ Ha Long, welcome on the boat (SIC) (B/L/D)\r\nDepart from Hanoi around 8:00 AM for a 4-hour shuttle bus ride to Ha Long Bay. Upon arrival at the port around noon, embark on the cruise, check into your cabin, and enjoy a fresh seafood lunch as you begin your journey through the bay. Afternoon activities include swimming, visiting a mysterious cave, and relaxing on a secluded island beach. Conclude the day with a sunset view from the top deck followed by a seafood dinner. Overnight accommodations are provided on the cruise.\r\nNote : The final cruise itinerary may vary based on the specific cruise program.\r\nInclusion : Sharing transfer, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, all meals, permits.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Explore Bay â€“ Hanoi (B/Brunch)\r\nEarly risers can witness the breathtaking sunrise and tranquil beauty of Halong Bay\'s towering limestone karsts. After a light breakfast around 7:00 AM, embark on a short rowboat ride with local rowers to explore the bay\'s serene waters. Enjoy a leisurely brunch on the boat as you cruise back to the pier, then begin the journey back to Hanoi.\r\nPlease note that the final cruise itinerary may vary depending on each cruise\'s program.\r\nInclusion: Sharing transfer for the cruise journey, sharing cruise, guide on boat, entrance fee, boat / junk, breakfast, brunch on boat, hotel.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Hanoi Depature (B)\r\nHave breakfast and check out.\r\nThen we transfer you without guide to the airport for your flight home. \r\nNote: Our driver doesnâ€™t speak English.\r\nInclusion : Private transfer\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights (SGN-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation based on twin/double/triple sharing room\r\nâ€¢ Private air-conditioned vehicle with private driver as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Local English speaking guide as mentioned itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Meals as mentioned (B = breakfast; L = lunch with set menu; D = dinner with set menu)\r\nâ€¢ SIC tours as mentioned\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tipping Policy: $US 3/pax/day (Mandatory)\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMeals on boat are local food.\r\nTOUR TIME & ACTIVITIES	(PRIVATE TOUR)\r\nWith half day tour: 4 hours (AM: 8:30 am - 12:30 am or  PM: 1:30 pm - 5:30 pm)\r\nDaily working hours: We work for 8 hours a day starting from 8:30 am to 5:30 pm. \r\nAny activities out of this time frame must be informed to us 1 day before and will occur surcharges.\r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-06-01','2025-06-06',1,0,0,'2025-05-15 19:41:11','2025-05-17 13:41:16'),(965,1644,54,4,0,0,113100,18000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1\r\n  Transfer from KLIA-Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Self Booked Hotel to KUL Half Day City Tour (03 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from KUL Half Day City Tour (03 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2\r\n  Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Genting Day Tour [with SIC transport]\r\n  Transfer from Genting Day Tour to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3\r\n  Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KLIA-Airport [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from SIN Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Evening Mandai [with SIC transport]\r\n  Transfer from Evening Mandai to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4