\n \r\n3rd Day - (Sunday 29th June) : Gangtok to Darjeeling - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance : 110 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Darjeeling (6,950 Ft.). On arrival check-in to hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Monday 30th June) : Darjeeling - Fullday Sightseeing with Tiger Hill \r\nApprox Distance : 130 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hours \r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of token, if not possible at the time of Sunrise, then it will be covered in day time.) and then back to hotel. After breakfast, starting at 8.30 AM, visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Evening free for leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nNote : Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n5th Day - (Tuesday 1st July) : Darjeeling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance : 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hours \r\nAfter breakfast Checkout from hotel and take, the departure transfers to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section \r\nâ€¢ Meal Plan (as per mentioned above) \r\n* 1-Innova / Xylo / Similar as per itinerary & timing only\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please note that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis) \r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary) \r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot) \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure \r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges \r\nâ€¢ Insurance \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n','Airfare Is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n\r\n','2025-06-27','2025-07-01',1,0,0,'2025-06-25 14:41:07','2025-06-26 12:44:39'),(1029,1715,15534,4,0,0,140000,20000,'Ladakh Diaries','Suggested itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : ARRIVE LEH \r\nArrive Leh and transfer to the hotel. Full day for complete rest for acclimatization to the high altitude of Leh. Overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDAY 02 : LEH \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Shyam Valley and you\'ll be awestruck with the sight of the Indus & Zanskar river Sangam, drive along the Indus river visiting Pathar Sahib Gurdwara and Magnetic Hill (where the cars defy gravity) and further on to Leh Hall of Fame (which has a museum of the Kargil War memorabilia). Later overnight stay at the Leh hotel.\r\n \r\nDAY 03 : LEH â€“ NUBRA  \r\nAfter Breakfast drive to Nubra Valley via Khardungla (Highest Motorable road in the World, 18,380 ft). Arrive at Hundar   by afternoon. Rest of the day free to explore Deskit, Hunder Villages and camel Safari in Sand Dunes between Deskit and Hundar Village. One can go for camel rides (own cost). Overnight stay at Nubra Valley.\r\n\r\nDAY 04 : Nubra\r\nDrive 70 Kms one way 3/4 hrs via various villages to Turtuk. It is the last village from Indian side. Have a look forward on Bunkers and last Indian post. Later in afternoon return to Nubra valley. Overnight stay at Nubra Valley\r\n \r\nDAY 05 : NUBRA â€“ PANGONG\r\nHave early breakfast and proceed to Pangong via Shayok, retrace the route down for Pangong Lake through Shayok 17,350 ft., it is the third highest motorable road in the world. Arrive Pangong and enjoy the beauty of the lake on the Banks of Pangong Lake while appreciating the changing Colors and fascinating high altitude of the Lake. Overnight stay at Pangong.\r\n \r\nDAY 06 : PANGONG â€“ LEH \r\nAfter breakfast drive back to Leh via Changla pass. Upon arrival Leh check in hotel. rest of the day visit local market in Leh. Overnight stay at Leh.\r\n \r\nDay 07: DEPART LEH: After breakfast check out from hotel & proceed to airport to board the flight for onward destination.\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N/7D Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast\r\nâ€¢ Transportation of 1 NAC AC INNOVA for arrival / departure and sightseeing as per itinerary on private basis.\r\nâ€¢ Sightseeing as per itinerary.\r\nâ€¢ Green Fees & Environment Fees (Inner Line Permit)\r\nâ€¢ Toll and taxes\r\nâ€¢ Parking Charges\r\nâ€¢ Driver allowances\r\n\r\n\r\n \r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','â€¢ Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nâ€¢ Oxygen Cylinder.\r\nâ€¢ Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porter age\r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees to Monasteries/ Monuments/Parks/etc & Guide charges\r\nâ€¢ Still camera/ video camera charges/Travel insurance\r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc. (to be borne by the client, who is directly payable on the spot)\r\nâ€¢ Any increase in Airlines taxes or fuel price at the time of departure, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\nâ€¢ Anything not mentioned in the inclusions\r\nâ€¢ Any other activities not mentioned in inclusions like horse riding/tips/ extra food ordered / entry fees / liquor etc.\r\n \r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nPlease note: In case of any natural calamity resulting in rerouting transportation charges or any accommodation not mentioned in inclusion will be additional and change in itinerary will be subject to availability.\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','2025-07-16','2025-07-22',1,0,0,'2025-06-30 13:28:44','2025-06-30 17:36:50'),(1030,1720,35,1,0,0,25100,5000,'Kolkata-Chennai','Day 1: (24 Jul 2025 - Thursday) Arrival in Chennai\r\nMeet & Assist on arrival\r\nArrival Transfer - Arrival in Chennai\r\nOn arrival at the Chennai seaport/airport/railway station, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Chennai. Check in at the hotel and the rest of the day is free at leisure. During your free time, you can walk out to explore the surroundings, interact with locals, visit local markets or stay back in hotel to take pleasure of its modern amenities. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Pride (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 2: (25 Jul 2025 - Friday) Chennai sightseeing Day 2\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Pride\r\n\r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Chennai sightseeing Day 2\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to visit Chennai. Chennai, on the Bay of Bengal in eastern India, is the capital of the state of Tamil Nadu. The city is home to Fort St. George, built in 1644 and now a museum showcasing the cityâ€™s roots as a British military garrison and East India Company trading outpost, when it was called Madras. Visit Fort St. George, Kapaleeshwar Temple, Saint Thomas Church, Parthasarathy Temple, Government Museum, Valluvar Kottam, & Marina Beach. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Pride (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 3: (26 Jul 2025 - Saturday) Chennai to Chennai\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Pride\r\n\r\nTransfers - Chennai to Chennai\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel to visit Chennai. Chennai, on the Bay of Bengal in eastern India, is the capital of the state of Tamil Nadu. The city is home to Fort St. George, built in 1644 and now a museum showcasing the cityâ€™s roots as a British military garrison and East India Company trading outpost, when it was called Madras. Visit Fort St. George, Kapaleeshwar Temple, Saint Thomas Church, Parthasarathy Temple, Government Museum, Valluvar Kottam, & Marina Beach. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel The Pride (Option 1) (Meal Plan - CPAI)\r\n\r\nDay 4: (27 Jul 2025 - Sunday) Chennai Departure\r\nBreakfast at the Hotel - The Pride\r\n\r\nDeparture Transfer - Chennai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Chennai international Airport/Railway station for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n','',' CCU-MAA-CCU economy class airfare \r\n4 star accommodation for 3 nights\r\nMeal plans as indicated on the itinerary\r\nAll Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\nAll Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost','All those which are not mentioned above\r\nEntry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\nPorterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc.\r\nAll Items Of Personal Nature\r\nAny Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc.\r\nAny Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\