nd tour a tea factory to learn about Sri Lanka\'s famed tea production. Next, visit Hakgala Botanical\r\nGarden and then enjoy a relaxing boat ride on Gregory Lake. Transfer back to Kandy for overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Kandy to Bentota\r\nStart your day with a visit to the Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic, a UNESCO World Heritage site that houses a\r\nrevered tooth relic of Buddha. After soaking in the spiritual ambiance, transfer to Bentota, a coastal town known for\r\nits stunning beaches. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or\r\nexploring the town on your own. Stay overnight in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Bentota\r\nAfter breakfast, Visit the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery where you can learn about conservation efforts, and a tranquil\r\nMadu River Boat Ride. Next visit Ambalangoda Mask Factory to learn about traditional mask-making. Next visit the\r\nBrief Garden, by Bevis Bawa, which is a beautifully landscaped garden located in the southern part of Sri Lanka. After\r\na day full of adventure and discovery, enjoy a delicious dinner and a relaxing overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Bentota to Colombo\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for\r\na city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face Green. In the evening,\r\nembark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic boutiques. Conclude your day\r\nwith an overnight stay in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Departure from Colombo\r\nSavor your final breakfast before transferring to the airport for your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable\r\nmemories of your Sri Lankan journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands \r\n* Vehicle : Toyota Mini Coaster \r\nâ€¢ Day Excursion to Nuwaraeliya on the 2nd Day in Kandy.\r\nâ€¢ Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Coaster.\r\nâ€¢ Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Kandy, Nuwaraeliya, Bentota & Colombo.\r\nâ€¢ All applicable government taxes.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.\r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.\r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.\r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase\r\nin surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n* Entrance to Turtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride, Temple of the Tooth Relic, Gregory Lake, Hakgala Botanical Garden, Gangaramaya Temple are on supplement cost','2025-07-13','2025-07-18',1,0,0,'2025-07-10 14:45:53','2025-07-10 15:42:33'),(1037,1728,3052,7,1,1,0,0,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival and Exploration// Kandy\r\nUpon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly welcomed by your driver and transferred to the cultural capital, Kandy.\r\nEn route, visit the fascinating Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can witness baby elephants being fed and\r\nbathed. Continue your journey with a stop at the Mawanella spice garden, exploring Sri Lankaâ€™s rich spice heritage.\r\nOnce in Kandy, check into your hotel and unwind. In the evening, visit the Gem Museum to marvel at Sri Lanka\'s\r\nprecious stones and enjoy a vibrant cultural dance performance. Conclude your day with an over