tal, Kandy. En route, visit the fascinating Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can witness baby elephants being fed and bathed. Continue your journey with a stop at the Mawanella spice garden, exploring Sri Lankaâ€™s rich spice heritage. Once in Kandy, check into your hotel and unwind. In the evening, visit the Gem Museum to marvel at Sri Lanka\'s precious stones and enjoy a vibrant cultural dance performance. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Kandy.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Kandy City Tour  \r\nAfter a sumptuous breakfast, embark on a cultural journey with a visit to the Temple of the Tooth Relic, a sacred site that houses a relic of the Buddha. Continue your exploration with a Royal Botanical Gardens, renowned for its diverse plant species and breathtaking landscapes. In the evening, experience the rich cultural heritage of Sri Lanka at the Gem Museum, followed by a captivating Cultural Dance performance. Enjoy dinner and spend another restful night in Kandy. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Kandy //  Nuwara Eliya  \r\nAfter breakfast transfer to the picturesque town of Nuwara Eliya. Along the way, visit the Hanuman Temple, Ramboda falls and tour a Damro Tea factory to learn about Sri Lanka\'s famed tea production. Next, visit Hanuman Temple and then enjoy a relaxing boat ride on Gregory Lake. Then, check-in to your hotel at Hatton. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hatton to Bentota \r\nAfter breakfast, embark on a scenic drive to the coastal town of Bentota. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or exploring the local area. Enjoy an overnight stay in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Bentota \r\nStart your day with a visit to the Kande Viharaya, a historic Buddhist temple. Then, head to the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery to learn about sea turtle conservation. In the evening, enjoy a Madu River Boat Ride, exploring the mangrove forests and small islands. Stay overnight in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Bentota to Colombo \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for a city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face Green. In the evening embark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic boutiques. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Departure from Colombo \r\nSavor your final breakfast before transferring to the airport for your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable memories of your Sri Lankan journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands \r\n* Vehicle : Toyota Mini Coaster \r\nâ€¢ Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Coaster.\r\nâ€¢ Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Kandy, Nuwaraeliya, Bentota & Colombo.\r\nâ€¢ All applicable government taxes.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.\r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.\r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.\r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase\r\nin surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n* Entrance to Turtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride, Temple of the Tooth Relic, Gregory Lake, Hakgala Botanical Garden, Gangaramaya Temple are on supplement cost','2025-07-15','2025-07-21',1,0,0,'2025-07-11 16:51:19','2025-07-11 18:13:20'),(1040,1731,19541,4,1,0,0,0,'Bhutan Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Wednesday 16th July) : IXB Airport to Phuentsholing - Pick up \r\nApprox Distance: 157 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nMeet & Greet on arrival at IXB Airport and transfer to Phuentsholing (961 ft.) - The Gateway of Bhutan by Road from India. It is a thriving commercial centre on the northern edge of the Indian Plains. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Thursday 17th July) : Phuentsholing to Thimphu - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 150 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast, complete the immigration formalities and transfer to Thimphu (7,710 ft.) the capital city of Bhutan. On the way, stop at places to view scenery and for Photography. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or take a leisure walk around the Thimphu City. Overnight stay at Thimphu.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Friday 18th July) : Thimphu - Sightseeing \r\nAfter breakfast visit the Kuenselphodrang (Buddha Dordenma). Located at a short drive from Thimphu City Centre, Kuenselphodrang offers a good overview of the Thimphu valley. The largest statue of Buddha in the country sits here which houses over one hundred thousand smaller Buddha statues. Then visit the National Memorial Chorten built in the memory of the Third King of Bhutan and visit the Folk Heritage Museum. Afternoon visit Sangaygang View Point. The Lookout point offers a stunning panoramic view of the entire Thimphu. On the way back visit the Takin Preserve Centre. Takin is the National animal of Bhutan. Then visit the Changangkha Lhakhang. This is a popular Buddhist temple and is especially visited by parents to receive blessings for their new-born. Its interiors are full of murals that depict different stories. In the evening, visit the Tashichho Dzong, first built in 1216 A.D. by Lama Gyalwa Lhanangpa. The Dzong is the seat of the National Government and the Central Monastic Body, including the summer residence of the Je Khenpo (Chief Abbot of Bhutan). Overnight stay at Thimphu.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Saturday 19th July) : Thimphu to Paro - Transfer then Sightseeing \r\nApprox Distance: 55 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour 30 minutes \r\nAfter breakfast transfer to Paro (7480 ft.). On the way visit the Tamchog Lhakhang. It was built in the 13th century by Thangthong Gyalpo who is also known as the Iron bridge builder. Situated on a hill top, we have to cross an ancient style bridge to reach the temple. On arrival in Paro, check in at the hotel. Afternoon, visit Ta Dzong - National Museum with an excellent collection of arts, relics, religious thangkha, etc. Rinpung Dzong - Meaning \"fortress of the heap of jewels\". The dzong now serves as the administrative and judicial seat of Paro. In the evening, explore the Paro Town and valley. Overnight stay at Paro.\r\n \r\n5th Day - (Sunday 20th July) : Paro - Taktshang Monastery Excursion \r\nApprox Distance: 40 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 1 hour 30 minutes \r\nAfter breakfast, drive to the base of the abode of gods and monks, the Taktshang Monastery. The monastery is a 2 -3 hours hike uphill from here. One feels truly blessed reaching the monastery. The primary Lhakhang was built surrounding Guru Rinpocheâ€™s Meditation cave in 1684 which clings to the edge of a sheer Rock cliff that plunges 900 meters into the valley below. Legend has it that Guru Rinpoche flew here on the back of a tigress which gives its name â€œTaktshangâ€ meaning Tigerâ€™s nest. Afternoon (If time permits), visit the Drukgyel Dzong. Built in 1647, the dzong was destroyed by accidental fire and left in ruins as an evocative reminder of the great victories it was built to commemorate. Explore the ramparts and experience an unforgettable view of Mt. Jhomolhari (7,314 m). On the way back, visit Kichu Lhakhang, one of the oldest Buddhist temples in Bhutan. Overnight stay at Paro.\r\n \r\n6th Day - (Monday 21st July) : Paro to Phuentsholing - Transfer \r\nApprox Distance: 145 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and transfer to Phuentsholing. On arrival check in at the hotel. In the evening, you may choose to relax at the hotel or walk around the Phuentsholing town. Overnight stay at Phuentsholing.\r\n \r\n7th Day - (Tuesday 22nd July) : Phuentsholing to IXB Airport - Drop \r\nApprox Distance: 170 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hours \r\nAfter breakfast check out from the hotel and drive to IXB Airport for your onward journey.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation with breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Extra Bed/Mattress\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive Non-a/c vehicle for all transfers & sightseeing as per itinerary. \r\nâ€¢ SDF & hotel taxes applicable (as per itinerary). \r\nâ€¢ Guide / Escort charges\r\n* 1-Innova / Xylo / Similar as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nIXB Airport to Phuentsholing, \r\nPhuentsholing to IXB Airport \r\n1-Hiace / Hyundai H1 / Similar as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nPhuentsholing to Thimphu, \r\n,Thimphu to Paro, \r\nParo to Phuentsholing \r\n* Insurance\r\n','â€¢ Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone bills, bar bills, tips & gratuity, bottled water and cost for other activities such as rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porterage, etc. \r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary. \r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees for museums and monuments. \r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to unforeseen contingencies such as landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc. Such expenses will have to be paid directly. \r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure. \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation\r\nGenerally, in Bhutan, most of the vehicle we write Non-AC as because of its location & Altitude, AC are not required. In case guest is insisting on AC, Supplement cost as per vehicle selection would be applicable. The AC will be switched on only when the Vehicle is on move. When the car is travelling uphill AC will be switch off. AC Vehicle supplement charges will be applicable.','2025-07-16','2025-07-22',1,0,0,'2025-07-11 19:16:46','2025-07-11 19:24:43'),(1041,1732,3052,7,1,1,0,0,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival and Exploration// Kandy \r\nUpon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly welcomed by your driver and transferred to the cultural capital, Kandy. En route, visit the fascinating Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can witness baby elephants being fed and bathed. Continue your journey with a stop at the Mawanella spice garden, exploring Sri Lankaâ€™s rich spice heritage. Once in Kandy, check into your hotel and unwind. In the evening, visit the Gem Museum to marvel at Sri Lanka\'s precious stones and enjoy a vibrant cultural dance performance. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Kandy.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Kandy City Tour  \r\nAfter a sumptuous breakfast, embark on a cultural journey with a visit to the Temple of the Tooth Relic, a sacred site that houses a relic of the Buddha. Continue your exploration with a Royal Botanical Gardens, renowned for its diverse plant species and breathtaking landscapes. In the evening, experience the rich cultural heritage of Sri Lanka at the Gem Museum, followed by a captivating Cultural Dance performance. Enjoy dinner and spend another restful night in Kandy. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Kandy //  Nuwara Eliya  \r\nAfter breakfast transfer to the picturesque town of Nuwara Eliya. Along the way, visit the Hanuman Temple, Ramboda falls and tour a Damro Tea factory to learn about Sri Lanka\'s famed tea production. Next, visit Hanuman Temple and then enjoy a relaxing boat ride on Gregory Lake. Then, check-in to your hotel at Hatton. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Hatton to Bentota \r\nAfter breakfast, embark on a scenic drive to the coastal town of Bentota. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or exploring the local area. Enjoy an overnight stay in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Bentota \r\nStart your day with a visit to the Kande Viharaya, a historic Buddhist temple. Then, head to the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery to learn about sea turtle conservation. In the evening, enjoy a Madu River Boat Ride, exploring the mangrove forests and small islands. Stay overnight in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Bentota to Colombo \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for a city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face Green. In the evening embark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic boutiques. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Departure from Colombo \r\nSavor your final breakfast before transferring to the airport for your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable memories of your Sri Lankan journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands \r\n* Vehicle : Toyota Mini Coaster \r\nâ€¢ Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Coaster.\r\nâ€¢ Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Kandy, Nuwaraeliya, Bentota & Colombo.\r\nâ€¢ All applicable government taxes.\r\n