e at the airport with Garlands \r\n* Vehicle : Toyota Mini Coaster \r\nâ€¢ Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned Coaster.\r\nâ€¢ Service of an English-speaking National Guide.\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Kandy, Nuwaraeliya, Bentota & Colombo.\r\nâ€¢ All applicable government taxes.\r\n* Insurance\r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.\r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.\r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.\r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.\r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.\r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase\r\nin surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','* Airfare is Dynamic\r\n* Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n* Entrance to Turtle Hatchery, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Madu River Boat Ride, Temple of the Tooth Relic, Gregory Lake, Hakgala Botanical Garden, Gangaramaya Temple are on supplement cost','2025-07-16','2025-07-22',1,0,0,'2025-07-12 13:17:47','2025-07-12 14:25:24'),(1043,1734,15595,2,0,0,88900,15000,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival â€“ Transfer to Dambulla\r\n\r\nUpon arrival in Sri Lanka, you will be warmly welcomed by our representative at the airport. From there, you will be transferred to Dambulla, located in the heart of the Cultural Triangle. En route, visit the serene and historically significant Ridee Viharaya, also known as the Silver Temple, which is nestled among the hills and known for its intricate rock carvings and peaceful atmosphere. After the visit, continue your journey to Sigiriya. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing after your journey. Enjoy dinner and stay overnight in Dambulla.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Dambulla â€“Golden Temple-Minneriya Safari\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, head to the iconic Golden Temple of Dambulla, a UNESCO World Heritage Site known for its spectacular cave temples filled with ancient Buddha statues and colorful murals. Later in the evening, enjoy an adventurous jeep safari at Minneriya National Park, famous for its large elephant gatherings and diverse wildlife. Capture the beauty of nature and watch elephants in their natural habitat. After the safari, return to your hotel. Dinner and overnight stay in Dambulla.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Dambulla to Hatton via Kandy (Leave 9.00 A.M in the Morning)\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and head towards Hatton via Kandy, the cultural capital of Sri Lanka. En route, stop at a Spice Garden in Matale, where you will be introduced to a variety of spices and herbs that are grown locally and used in traditional Ayurvedic practices. On arrival in Kandy, visit a Royal Botanical Garden. After that transfer to Hatton. Dinner and overnight stay in Hatton.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Hatton to Bentota\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, depart from the hills of Hatton and head towards the sunny southern coast of Bentota, a serene beach destination ideal for relaxation. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and enjoy the remainder of the day at leisure, soaking up the coastal atmosphere or enjoying a peaceful walk along the golden beach. Dinner and overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 5: Bentota â€“ City Tour & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, begin a full day of sightseeing in Bentota. Start with a visit to the revered Kande Viharaya Temple, known for its towering seated Buddha statue and peaceful ambiance. Next, proceed to the Turtle Hatchery in Kosgoda, a conservation project dedicated to protecting endangered sea turtles. In the evening, enjoy a scenic boat ride along the Madu River, exploring its rich mangrove ecosystem and local river life. After the tour, return to the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Bentota to Colombo â€“ City Tour\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and transfer to Colombo, the bustling commercial capital of Sri Lanka. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and later proceed for a guided city tour. Visit key landmarks such as Galle Face Green, the iconic Port City, the historic Independence Square, and view the striking Lotus Tower from outside. Enjoy a shopping tour in Colomboâ€™s popular malls or local boutiques for souvenirs and gifts. Return to the hotel for dinner and stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7: Departure\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, depending on your departure flight time, you will be transferred to Bandaranaike International Airport for your onward journey, marking the end of a memorable 6-night holiday in Sri Lanka.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Toyota KDH Flat Roof   \r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands   \r\n* Service of an English-speaking Driver\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day                              \r\nâ€¢ Express way charges wherever applicable  \r\n* Insurance      \r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.                      \r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.                                                            \r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs                                           \r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.         \r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.         \r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.                                               \r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.                           \r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.                       \r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to \r\nincrease in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or \r\nwhile touring \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nSupplement cost for Minneriya Safari, Dambulla Cave Temple, Royal Botanical Garden, Turtle Hatchery, Madu River Boat Ride, Lotus Tower will be applicable.','2025-08-11','2025-08-17',1,0,0,'2025-07-15 18:33:43','2025-07-15 22:16:01'),(1044,1735,16002,4,0,0,133200,23000,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (6 Oct) : Denpasar Airport to Kuta Hotel - Arrival and Transfer 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nWelcome with Garland 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n2nd Day (7 Oct) :	Day Use Vehicle - Full Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nWater Sports At Tanjung Benoa Beach By Indah (Parasailing, Banana Boat & Jet sky) 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nUluwatu tour 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n3rd Day (8 Oct) :	Day Use Vehicle - Full Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nNusa Penida West Trip with Local lunch Without Pick Up & Drop 	PVT 4 Adults \r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n4th Day (9 Oct) :	Day Use Vehicle - Full Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nBedugul Tour (Ulun Danu Temple & Lake) 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nHandara gate 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nTanah Lot Sunset Tour 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n5th Day (10 Oct) : Day Use Vehicle - Full Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nKintamani Volcano View 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nUbud Village 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nTegenunung Waterfall 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nMy Swing (Swing + Nest + Local Lunch) 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n6th Day (11 Oct) :	Day Use Vehicle - Full Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nATV ride Tandem with local lunch by (Fun ATV) 	Ticket 4 Adults \r\nRiver Rafting with Local lunch By Desa 	Ticket 4 Adults\r\nMineral Water Bottle 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n7th Day (12 Oct :)	Day Use Vehicle - Half Day 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\nDinner @Indian Restaurant Veg Meal 	Coupon 4 Adults \r\n\r\n8th Day (13 Oct) : Ubud Hotel to Denpasar Airport - Departure 	1-APV/Avanza/Xenia \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 7N Accommodation with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Arrival & Departure transfer \r\nâ€¢ Basic English Speaking Driver \r\nâ€¢ Daily water bottle during tours and transfers \r\nâ€¢ All tours and transfers as per itinerary on a private basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nâ€¢ Private Guide \r\nâ€¢ Tourist Tax ( I LOVE BALI ) \r\nâ€¢ Gili Harbor Tax ( Guest Pay Directly at Harbor) \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-10-06','2025-10-13',1,0,0,'2025-07-16 12:05:56','2025-07-16 14:44:17'),(1045,1736,1105,2,1,1,10000,5000,'Udaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at Udaipur and transfer to the hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening experience a boat ride on Lake Pichola, enjoying views of the City Palace and surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, visit the City Palace, a grand complex showcasing Rajput architecture. Explore Jagdish Temple, a well-known temple dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Visit Saheliyon-ki-Bari, a beautiful garden with fountains and kiosks. Enjoy a sunset view from Sajjangarh (Monsoon Palace)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : After breakfast, visit Fateh sagar lake enjoying boating and the scenic surroundings. In the afternoon visit Kumbhalgarh Fort a historical fort with stunning views. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast and check-out from the hotel and transfer to UDR Airport.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N accommodation with daily breakfast and lunch/ dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan Car\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-08-14','2025-08-17',1,0,0,'2025-07-16 16:10:34','2025-07-16 16:31:58'),(1046,1737,15595,2,0,0,92400,12000,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival in Sigiriya  \r\nUpon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly greeted and picked up to begin your journey. After enjoying \r\nbreakfast at a restaurant outside the airport, proceed to the Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can \r\nobserve elephants up close as they bathe and feed by the river. Continue your journey to the Dambulla Cave \r\nTemple, a UNESCO World Heritage Site known for its impressive cave shrines, ancient murals, and Buddha statues. \r\nFollowing your visit, stop for lunch at an outside restaurant before heading to Sigiriya. Upon arrival, check in to \r\nyour hotel, relax for the evening, and enjoy a peaceful dinner and overnight stay. \r\n\r\nDay 2 : Sigiriya to Kandy via Hiriwadunna Village \r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel, begin the day by exploring the majestic Sigiriya Rock Fortress, an ancient royal citadel \r\nperched atop a dramatic rock outcrop, offering panoramic views and centuries-old frescoes. After descending, \r\ntake part in the Hiriwadunna Village Tour, where youâ€™ll experience the charm of rural Sri Lankan life through a \r\nbullock cart ride, catamaran journey, and a traditional village lunch (optional). In the afternoon, proceed to Kandy, \r\nthe hill countryâ€™s cultural heart. Upon arrival, check in at the hotel, relax, enjoy dinner, and spend the night in \r\nKandy. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Cultural & Natural Heritage of Kandy  \r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel, begin your exploration of Kandy, Sri Lankaâ€™s cultural capital. Start with a visit to the \r\nsacred Temple of the Tooth Relic, one of the most important religious sites in the country. Then, enjoy a peaceful \r\nnature walk through the Udawattakele Sanctuary, a historic forest reserve located just above the city, known for \r\nits rich biodiversity, walking trails, and spiritual significance. Later, visit a Gem Museum to learn about Sri Lankaâ€™s \r\nrenowned gemstone industry. In the evening, experience the energy and color of a traditional Kandyan Cultural \r\nDance Show. Return to the hotel for dinner and an overnight stay in Kandy.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Kandy to Nuwara Eliya  \r\nAfter breakfast, depart for Nuwara Eliya. En route, take in the panoramic views at the cascading Ramboda Falls, \r\nvisit the historic Hanuman Temple, and tour a Tea Factory to see tea production firsthand. In the evening, , visit the \r\nSita Amman Temple, a significant site from the Ramayana epic, and explore the enchanting Hakgala Botanical \r\nGarden enjoy a serene boat ride on Gregory Lake. Check into your hotel and stay overnight in Nuwara Eliya. \r\n\r\nDay 5 : Nuwara Eliya to Bentota  \r\nAfter breakfast. embark on a scenic drive to the coastal town of Bentota. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and \r\nspend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or exploring the local area. Enjoy an overnight stay in \r\nBentota. \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Exploring Bentota  \r\nBegin your day with a visit to the Kande Viharaya, home to one of the tallest sitting Buddha statues in Sri Lanka. \r\nNext, visit the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery, where you can learn about turtle conservation efforts and see baby turtles. \r\nIn the afternoon, enjoy a scenic boat ride on the Madu River, navigating through mangroves and spotting wildlife. \r\nFor thrill-seekers, optional water sports activities like jet skiing, banana boat rides, and tube rides await. End your \r\nadventurous day with an overnight stay in Bentota. \r\n\r\nDay 7 : Bentota to Colombo  \r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for \r\na city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Gangaramaya Temple, Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face \r\nGreen. In the evening, embark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic \r\nboutiques. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Colombo. \r\n\r\nDay 8 : Departure from Colombo  \r\nIf time permits, enjoy a final shopping spree after breakfast. Afterwards, you will be transferred to the airport to \r\ncatch your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable memories of your Sri Lankan adventure.  \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 7N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan Car\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day. \r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands. \r\nâ€¢ Express way charges wherever applicable. \r\nâ€¢ Free Cultural Show Tickets (Clients should visit a Gem shop which will be direct by us) at Kandy.  \r\nâ€¢ Free Gem Factory visit and explanation about the gem progress at Kandy.  \r\n* Service of an English-speaking Driver\r\nâ€¢ City tours in Sigiriya, Kandy, Nuwara Eliya, Bentota & Colombo. \r\nâ€¢ All applicable Government Taxes.\r\n* Insurance\r\n                            \r\n   \r\n','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.                      \r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.                                                            \r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs                                           \r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.         \r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.         \r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.                                               \r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.                           \r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.                       \r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to \r\nincrease in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or \r\nwhile touring \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nSupplement cost for Sigiriya Lion Rock, Dambulla Cave Temple, Hiriwaduna Village tour, Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, Temple Of the Tooth Relic, Gregory lake, Hakgala Botanical Garden, Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery, Madu River Boat Safari, Colombo Lotus Tower, Gangaramaya temple will be applicable','2025-08-12','2025-08-19',1,0,0,'2025-07-17 11:28:28','2025-07-17 13:27:03'),(1047,1738,1105,2,1,1,10000,4000,'Udaipur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at Udaipur and transfer to the hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. In the evening experience a boat ride on Lake Pichola, enjoying views of the City Palace and surrounding areas.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : After having breakfast, visit the City Palace, a grand complex showcasing Rajput architecture. Explore Jagdish Temple, a well-known temple dedicated to Lord Vishnu. Visit Saheliyon-ki-Bari, a beautiful garden with fountains and kiosks. Enjoy a sunset view from Sajjangarh (Monsoon Palace)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : After breakfast, visit Fateh sagar lake enjoying boating and the scenic surroundings. In the afternoon visit Kumbhalgarh Fort a historical fort with stunning views. \r\n\r\nDay 4 : Have breakfast and check-out from the hotel and transfer to UDR Airport.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N accommodation with daily breakfast and lunch/ dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan Car\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above.\r\n* Anything that is not mentioned in the inclusions','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-08-14','2025-08-17',1,0,0,'2025-07-17 13:32:19','2025-07-17 15:03:11'),(1048,1739,2690,2,0,1,44900,6000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the BKK Airport and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. Day at Leisure for self exploration.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Have breakfast and proceed for BKK city tour with Marbel buddha and Golden buddha private basis\r\n\r\nDay 03 : After having breakfast proceed for Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch (PU/ 08:00AM) Private basis\r\n\r\nDay 04 : After having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the BKK Airport for your onward journey to Phuket (PVT).\r\nArrival at the HKT Airport and transfer to the booked hotel on Private Basis. Evening at leisure for self exploration.\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Have breakfast and proceed for Phi Phi Island Tour by Speed Boat + Khai Island + Lunch + Transfer on private basis ( Excl. Mandatory National Park Fee THB 400 PP) boat will be on sharing basis.\r\n\r\nDay 06 : After having breakfast proceed for Dolphins Show Phuket (Regular Seat ROW E,F,G) private basis\r\n\r\nDay 07 : After having breakfast, check-out from the hotel and transfer to the HKT Airport on pvt. basis for your homebound journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flights (BKK-HKT)\r\n* 3N Accommodation at Bangkok with breakfast\r\n* 3N Accommodation at Phuket with breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','*Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-07-28','2025-08-03',1,0,0,'2025-07-17 17:07:12','2025-07-18 10:48:08'),(1049,1740,329,2,0,0,0,0,'Malaysia Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 - Arrive Kuala Lumpur, meet with our representative and transfer to hotel. \r\nOvernight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 02 - Breakfast  \r\nBreakfast at hotel. Proceed to do a Kuala Lumpur city tour,(approx 03 hours) KL is the capital city of Malaysia, boasting gleaming skyscrapers, colonial architecture, charming locals, and a myriad of natural attractions. Divided into numerous districts, its main hub is called the Golden Triangle which comprises Bukit Bintang, KLCC and Chinatown. KL is widely recognised for numerous landmarks, including Petronas Twin Towers (the worldâ€™s tallest twin skyscrapers- entrance ticket not included, only photostop) \r\nOvernight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 03 - Breakfast  \r\nCheck out from hotel and transfer to Genting Highland. Enroute stopover for approx 20 minutes at Batu Caves \r\nGenting Highlands is a popular resort destination located about an hourâ€™s drive from Kuala Lumpur, Malaysia. Known for its cool climate and entertainment options, it offers a range of attractions, including an outdoor theme park(ticket included) \r\nOvernight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 04- Breakfast  \r\nDay at leisure, to explore Genting Highland your own. \r\nOvernight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 05- Breakfast  \r\nCheck out and transfer to Kualalumpur city. \r\nCheck in to hotel. \r\nDay at leisure, to explore city on your own. \r\nOvernight at hotel. \r\n\r\nDay 06  -Early morning check out & transfer to airport for flight to Delhi. \r\n','','* Economy class airfare Delhi- Kuala Lumpur- Delhi on Air India \r\n* 3N Accommodation at Kuala Lumpur\r\n* 02 nights accommodation at Genting Highland \r\n* 04 Breakfast \r\n* Airport â€“ hotel- airport transfers \r\n* Kuala Lumpur city tour-03 hrs approx \r\n* SkyWorld Outdoor theme park ticket at Genting Highland \r\n* 2 way cable car \r\n* Enroute Batu Caves visit ( 20 minutes stop) \r\n* All transfers & Tours on seat in coach/ sharing basis \r\n* Airport taxes  \r\n* GST \r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Malaysia Visa -No Charges for travel ( Minimum USD 500 cash in hand or International Debit or  International Credit Card required on arrival at Kuala Lumpur). \r\n* Malaysia Tourism Tax RM 10 per room per night to be paid directly at hotel on check-in \r\n* Any increase in the air fare, fuel surcharge and taxes charged by the airlines on your air ticket. \r\n* Any increase in the rate of exchange leading to an increase in all land arrangement which may come in to effect prior to departure. \r\n* Cost of extension of the validity or deviation from route of your air ticket. \r\n* High Season Surcharge if applicable. \r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n\r\n','Note: Above is an indicative itinerary. Day and timings of tour scheduled may change if required by overseas service provider.\r\n-KL night tour +KL Tower entrance (observatory deck only) - Supplement Cost\r\n-Sunway Lagoon tour with 6 theme parks - Supplement Cost','2025-08-19','2025-08-24',1,0,0,'2025-07-17 17:23:33','2025-07-17 18:19:10'),(1050,1741,15512,8,2,0,327300,52000,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Phu Quoc - Grand World Phu Quoc\r\nMorning flight to Phu Quoc, welcome to Pearl island of Vietnam. Our guide and driver will pick up and transfer to hotel for checking in ( check-in time 2pm).\r\nEvening, visit Grand World Phu Quoc\r\nOvernight in Phu Quoc\r\n \r\nDay 2 : Phu Quoc Safari & Vin Wonder (B) (No guide)\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to visit Phu Quoc Safari, Vietnam\'s largest wildlife conservation park, one of the most Safari in Southeast Asia, the park has the area of 500 hectares and is home to around 150 species of rare wild animals (about 3,000 units for all of those species), some of which are white lion, black-and-white ruffed lemur, Bengal tiger, Arabian oryx, and white tiger. More than that, this is also where the largest number of endangered species, like rhinoceros, flamingos, and giraffe are being preserved.\r\nIn the afternoon, enjoy VinWonder â€“ Vietnamâ€™s biggest theme park, the multi-experience playground suitable for all ages. which means you will have plenty of time to indulge yourself in all of the incredible shows and attractions: Fantasy World; Adventure world; Ocean World; Show Onceâ€¦. \r\n \r\nDay 3 : Four islands â€“ Hon Thom waterpark & Cable Car  (B/Basic local Picnic Lunch) (Group tour)\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to An Thoi boat station, get on a speed boat and cruise to 4 islands in Southern of main island. The first place is Buom island, then Gam Ghi island where you can swim and snorkeling at coral reef sites, exploring around the rocks, hidden sea lives, fishes and natural coralsâ€¦ Then next is May Rut island with beautiful natural beach and have a picnic lunch.\r\nAfternoon, go ahead to Hon Thom island, enjoy Water park / Amusement Park on the island (you should bring along swimsuit)â€¦ After few hours enjoying on Hon Thom, we will use cable car to return to main islandâ€¦ The Cable car is recognized by the Guinness world records with the title of â€œThe worldâ€™s longest 3-wire sea cable car with a length of 7899.9mâ€, built with modern and advanced technology from the worldâ€™s leading manufacturers. But perhaps, the most attractive thing for tourists is the unique experience when watching from the ideal height on the cable car to admire the natural masterpiece given to the Southern Phu Quoc island. Transfer to hotel & Overnight in Phu Quoc\r\n Note: Lunch with basic local food followed the program \r\nIf the weather is good, there will be video recording by fly cam on the island of SiC tour\r\n \r\nDay 4 : Phu Quoc â€“ Fly to Ho Chi Minh city â€“ Half day city tour (B)\r\nArrive in Ho Chi Minh city (Saigon), pick up and transfer to the city centre & check in hotel (check in time from 2pm on ward). \r\nToday you will visit half day Saigon city tour, the first place is The Independence Palace symbolizes Vietnam\'s victory, peace, and territorial integrity. This place has a glamorous design, hundreds of rooms equipped with luxurious furnishings and decorations, and an enormous and gorgeous exterior space; next is War Remnants Museum: Formerly known as the Museum of American War Crimes, this is a poignant display of the futility of war, the museum is a call for peace and hopes that history does not repeat itself; continue to Notre Dame Cathedral and Old Post Office: Built between 1877 and 1883 this is one of the best examples of classical French colonial architecture. End of the tour is Ben Thanh Market: This bustling market is very popular with tourists, primarily due to its central location. It has a wide selection of goods ranging from fake Nike shoes to beautiful silk Ao Dais.  Overnight in Ho Chi Minh city. \r\n \r\nDay 5 : Ho Chi Minh city â€“ Mekong Delta â€“ Ho Chi Minh city  (B) \r\nMekong delta is known as The Nine Dragon river delta since it is formed by nine rivers. The background of this area is the largest site of endless paddy fields, coconut farms, tropical gardens. Morning, drive to My Tho, known as the \"rice basket\" in Vietnam. Upon arrival Cruising through Mekong River, passing a fishing villages. Visiting some small islets as Turtle, Dragon, Phoenix Island,.. under a green canopy of water coconut trees. Walking through some villages to a fruit garden. Taste tropical fruits, while having live traditional music. Have honey tea. Short rowing boat ride, enjoy the nice boat ride through natural island and canals in Ben Tre under the shadow of the water coconut trees... Return and Overnight in Ho Chi Minh city.\r\n \r\nDay 6 : Ho Chi Minh - Departure  (B) \r\nAt leisure till transfer to airport for return flight to your sweet home.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flight (PQC-SGN)\r\n* 5N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* All road transportation in  16 Seater Air-conditional vehicle \r\n* Cable car Ba Na Hill and 4 island \r\n* Ticket Vin wonder & Safari\r\n* English speaking guide during sightseeing\r\n* Entrance fees as per above program\r\n* Drinking water on transfer during visit 500ml*2/person/day\r\n* insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Early check-in/ Late check-out\r\n* All flights / airport tax.   \r\n* Compulsory tips for guide and driver US$3/client/day\r\n* Other items not mentioned in above\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-07-28','2025-08-02',1,0,0,'2025-07-21 14:20:20','2025-07-21 15:09:52'),(1051,1743,15540,2,0,0,0,0,'Mauritius Diaries','Tours Offered :\r\n\r\nFull Day South Island Tour on SIC basis.\r\nFull Day North Island Tour on SIC basis.\r\nFull Day Ile Aux cerf tour on SIC basis.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation as mentioned with breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Airport return transfers on SIC\r\n* Tours as mentioned on SIC\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-08-07','2025-08-11',1,0,0,'2025-07-21 15:59:22','2025-07-22 12:38:11'),(1052,1744,54,4,0,0,149000,26000,'Singapore Diaries','Tours Offered: \r\n- Night Safari ** SIC Basis  ** (Complimentary Animal Show + Tram Ride)\r\n- FD Sentosa Saver (luge3+cc+wot) ** SIC Basis  ** (Cable Car (Mount Faber Line) + Luge & Skyline (3 Rides) 11am-03pm + Wings Of Time (07.40 Pm))\r\n- Merlion City Drive with Flyer ** SIC Basis  ** (Time Capsule will be closed for upgrading works from 28-Apr\'25 onwards till further notice + Singapore Flyer)\r\n- Universal Studios ** SIC Basis  ** (Transformers the Ride will be closed for maintenance from 17th May (Saturday) to 29th May (Thursday))\r\n- Gardens By The Ba