Duration upto 5 hours. Start time 4 pm. Vehicle capasity-6px (Luggage will be inside the vehicle) (Kowloon Side Hotels)\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Private Peaceful Big Budha tour w 2way Std Cable car tkts & Outlet mall shopping. Pick up-9 30 am. Return 3:30 pm. Kowloon. Vehicle capacity-6px\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Private Amazing Ocean park tour, standard entry ticket. Pick up: 9:30 am. Return: 7 pm Hotel Located in Kowloon or Hong Kong Island\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Private Magical Disneyland tour with Tier 4 entry ticket. Pick up: 9:30 am, Return: 9:30 pm Location- Kowloon side Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Private Hotel to HK Ferry pier transfer, 1 way. Kowloon or Hong Kong side hotels. Service time: 8 am-10 pm. Vehicle capacity-6px\r\nDay 5 : Ferry ticket 1 way, Eco class, Day sailing, Hong Kong to Macau or Macau to Hong Kong. (7:30 AM to 5:00 PM) (Week Days) (Sun- Thu)\r\nDay 5 : Private Macau Ferry Pier to hotel transfer or Vise versa . Service hours 8 am-10 pm. Vehicle capasity upto 9 pax\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Dazzling Macau half day morning tour (Private) Pick up- 12 noon from Hotel lobby. Venetian- West Lobby near ATM. Galaxy- Diamond lobby Tour includes: A Ma temple, Ruins of St Paul cathedral, Kun Lam Statue, Lotus Square & Macau Tower photo stop\r\n\r\nDay 7 : Private Macau Ferry Pier to hotel transfer or Vise versa . Service hours 8 am-10 pm. Vehicle capasity upto 9 pax\r\nDay 7 : Ferry ticket 1 way, Eco class, Day sailing, Hong Kong to Macau or Macau to Hong Kong. (7:30 AM to 5:00 PM) (Week Days) (Sun- Thu)\r\nDay 7 : Private HK Ferry terminal to Airport transfer( 8am - 10 pm). Vehicle capacity-6px\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation in Hong Kong with daily breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Macau with daily breakfast\r\n* Airport Transfers and tours on PVT (2 Vehicles will be provided)\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-10-01','2025-10-07',1,0,0,'2025-07-24 17:12:11','2025-07-24 17:25:59'),(1055,1747,349,3,0,0,68500,18000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Tours:\r\n\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner (SIC Basis)(03-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Half Day City Tour (SIC Basis)(03-Adults)\r\n* Burj Khalifa 124th-125th Floor, Non-Prime Hours (SIC Basis)\r\nâ€¢ Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) ( Ferrari World ) (SIC Basis)(03-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (SIC Basis)(03-Adults)\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned on SIC basis\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes hotel tax or city tax (If applicable)\r\nâ€¢ Tourism Dirham is not included in above quotation and shall be directly payable by the guest.\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nDubai hotels may collect incidental/security fee will be collected by all hotels in the form of a credit card hold or cash payment ranging from dirham100-dirham 300. This amount will be returned at check-out if there are no missing items, damages or excessive cleaning required.','2025-08-14','2025-08-18',1,0,0,'2025-07-24 18:44:43','2025-07-24 20:47:54'),(1056,1749,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (03 Oct 2025 - Friday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Throughout the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Munnar \r\n\r\nDay 2 : (04 Oct 2025 - Saturday) Munnar Sightseeing \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing \r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (05 Oct 2025 - Sunday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady. Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 : (06 Oct 2025 - Monday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 5 : (07 Oct 2025 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Cochin\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Cochin\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel and Transferred to Cochin. Check in to the hotel. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 6 : (08 Oct 2025 - Wednesday) Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nDeparture Transfer - Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport for departure.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Sedan Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc.\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc.\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNIGHT DRIVE - AFTER 1900 HRS WILL BE CHARGED EXTRA.\r\nTransportation Vehicle KM allowed on the basis of Garage to Garage (Timing 08 AM -07 PM).\r\nIn Hill station & Forest station, room & vehicle will not be air conditioned\r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.\r\n','2025-10-03','2025-10-08',1,0,0,'2025-07-25 15:57:00','2025-07-25 16:16:29'),(1058,1750,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (03 Oct 2025 - Friday) Trivandrum Arrival\r\nArrival at the Trivandrum airport and transfer to hotel. Later proceed for Sightseeing of Trivandrum . Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace, Zoo ( Closed on Mondays ), Napier Museum , Veli Tourist village .Overnight stay at hotel/ Resort\r\n\r\nDay 2 : (04 Oct 2025 - Saturday) Trivandrum TO Kanyakumari\r\nMorning after breakfast drive to Kanyakumari. Upon arrival check into the hotel. Kanyakumari is the southernmost end of Tamil Nadu, the Landâ€™s End of India or the point where the three seas meet - the Bay of Bengal, The Arabian Sea and the Indian Ocean. Later visit Kumari amman temple dedicated to the virgin goddess Kanyakumari (Parvati) who stands guard over the country. The temple is built at the spot where the goddess is believed to have waited for her consort Lord Siva. Gandhi Memorial, constructed at the spot where the ashes of Mahatma Gandhi were kept for public view in an urn before a portion was immersed into the three seas. Vivekananda Memorial built on the Vivekananda Rock where the great Philosopher and guide Swami Vivekananda went into meditation that transformed him into one of the most charismatic spiritual leader. The Thiruvalluvar Statue, or the Valluvar Statue, is a 133-feet tall stone sculpture of the Tamil poet and philosopher Valluvar, author of the Tirukkural, an ancient Tamil work on secular ethics and morality. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (05 Oct 2025 - Sunday) Kanyakymari to Kovalam\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and  transfer to Kovalam. Check in at Hotel.  Kovalam is an evergreen and pleasant climatic beach. Kovalam is a dreamland for tourists all over the world. With high rock promontory and a calm bay of blue waters, this beach paradise creates a unique aquarelle on moonlit nights. Kovalam was brought to the public eye by the Maharaja of Travancore. Over the past three decades, the place has been well developed, and now figures prominently on the world tourism map. Overnight stay at Kovalam.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : (06 Oct 2025 - Monday) Poovar - Kovalam - Poovar\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to Poovar Sightseeing . Poovar is a small rustic town situated 27 kms from Thiruvananthapuram with unspoilt, unexplored golden sand beaches and beautiful backwaters of Kerala. Also known as a fishing village, the tranquil Poovar island lies between the Arabian Sea and the Neyyar River. Hiring a boat, (especially during the sunset)that will take you through the mangrove forest of backwaters is a must-do activity. Overnight stay at Kovalam\r\n\r\nDay 5 : (07 Oct 2025 - Tuesday) Kovalam to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel/resort\"\r\n\r\nDay 6 : (08 Oct 2025 - Wednesday) Alleppey to Munnar\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Munnar. Munnar is 1800 mts above sea level and also the place of South India\'s highest peak (Anamudi - 2695 mts). On the way visit Valara, Cheeyappara waterfalls & Tea Plantations. Check in to Hotel. Afternoon visit Rajamala (Eravikulam National Park - open as per the directions by the forest authorities ), the best place to see Nilgiri Tahr (Hermitragus Hilarious) - the mountain goat of South India & Tea Museum. Evening have a short visit at Munnar town. You can see the beautiful tea estates like a green paradise. Overnight stay at Munnar.\r\n\r\nDay 7 : (09 Oct 2025 - Thursday) Munnar Sightseeing DAY 02\r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\nDay 8 : (10 Oct 2025 - Friday) Munnar to Cochin\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel and Transferred to Cochin. Check in to the hotel. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\n\r\nDay 9 : (11 Oct 2025 - Saturday) Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort, later check out from the hotel and drive to Airport.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 8N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Sedan Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc.\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc.\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNIGHT DRIVE - AFTER 1900 HRS WILL BE CHARGED EXTRA.\r\nTransportation Vehicle KM allowed on the basis of Garage to Garage (Timing 08 AM -07 PM).\r\nIn Hill station & Forest station, room & vehicle will not be air conditioned\r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.\r\n','2025-10-03','2025-10-11',1,0,0,'2025-07-26 16:45:53','2025-07-26 18:41:03'),(1059,1751,329,4,0,0,44500,9000,'Kuala Lumpur Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 \r\n  Transfer from KLIA-Airport to Self-Booked KL Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from the Booked KL Hotel to KUL Half Day City Tour (04 Hours) [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from KUL Half Day City Tour (04 Hours) to the Booked KL Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2\r\n  Transfer from the Booked KL Hotel to Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) [with SIC transport]\r\n  Transfer from Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) to the Booked KL Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3\r\n  Transfer from the Booked KL Hotel to KLIA-Airport [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from LGK Airport to the Booked Langkawi hotel [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from the Booked Langkawi hotel to Half Day Langkawi Island Tour [with Private transport]\r\n  Transfer from Half Day Langkawi Island Tour to the Booked Langkawi hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4\r\n  Transfer from the Booked Langkawi hotel to Island Hopping Tour (Shared Boat) - Ex Beach & City Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n  Transfer from Island Hopping Tour (Shared Boat) - Ex Beach & City Hotel to the Booked Langkawi hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 5\r\n  Transfer from Self-Booked Langkawi hotel to LGK Airport [with Private transport]\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\