f personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes if applicable are to be paid by the guest directly\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n','2025-08-14','2025-08-18',1,0,0,'2025-07-26 21:56:54','2025-07-26 22:29:59'),(1061,1753,15518,1,0,0,31600,4000,'Kerala Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : (03 Oct 2025 - Friday) Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar(Arrival)\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Throughout the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel Munnar \r\n\r\nDay 2 : (04 Oct 2025 - Saturday) Munnar Sightseeing \r\nSightseeing Day 02 - Munnar Sightseeing \r\nMorning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sightseeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel\r\n\r\nDay 3 : (05 Oct 2025 - Sunday) Munnar - Thekkady\r\nTransfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady. Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ). Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 4 : (06 Oct 2025 - Monday) Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nTransfers - Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) Overnight stay at same hotel\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 5 : (07 Oct 2025 - Tuesday) Alleppey to Cochin\r\nTransfers - Alleppey to Cochin\r\nMorning after breakfast Checkout from Hotel and Transferred to Cochin. Check in to the hotel. Proceed for Cochin sightseeing. Visit the Dutch Palace-built by the Portuguese in 1557 and subsequently renovated by the Dutch after 1663. The murals are perhaps the best in India. Jewish Synagogue - built in 1568 and the oldest Synagogue in the Commonwealth are at Mattancherry. St. Francis Church - built in 1510 and the oldest European church in India, Chinese Fishing Nets- introduced by the court of Kublai Khan can be seen in Fort Cochin. Fort Cochin Beach etc. Overnight stay at Cochin\r\nOvernight Stay at Hotel \r\n\r\nDay 6 : (08 Oct 2025 - Wednesday) Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nDeparture Transfer - Cochin to Cochin Departure\r\nMorning have breakfast at resort later check out from the Hotel and drive to Airport for departure.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* All Inclusion and sightseeing By Ac Sedan Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* All Toll, Parking, Driver Bata & Fuel Cost\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Porterage At Hotels And Airports, Tips, Insurance, Laundry, Liquors, Wine, Etc.\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc.\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Ayurveda Charges\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n* Mandatory X- Mas / New Year Eve Supplementary Charges , That Should Be Paid By The Guest Directly To The Hotels Concerned.','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNIGHT DRIVE - AFTER 1900 HRS WILL BE CHARGED EXTRA.\r\nTransportation Vehicle KM allowed on the basis of Garage to Garage (Timing 08 AM -07 PM).\r\nIn Hill station & Forest station, room & vehicle will not be air conditioned\r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.\r\n','2025-10-03','2025-10-08',1,0,0,'2025-07-28 15:36:08','2025-07-29 17:31:56'),(1062,1760,2690,2,0,0,45400,10000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nTransfers from Phuket airport to Krabi hotel PVT basis\r\nTransfers from Krabi hotel to Phuket hotel PVT basis\r\nTransfers from Phuket hotel to Phuket airport PVT basis\r\nKrabi 4 Island Tour by Speed Boat+ Picnic Lunch (Exclude the National Park Admission Fee) SIC basis\r\nPhuket Half Day City Tour on SIC basis (Big Buddha is not operational till further notice)\r\nPhi Phi Island Tour by Speed Boat + Khai Island + Lunch + Transfer on SIC ( Excl.Mandatory National Park Fee THB 400 PP) (PU/07:00)\r\nPhuket Tiger Kingdom on PVT Basis\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* HKT Airport to Krabi Hotel transfers on PVT\r\n* Krabi Hotel to Phuket Hotel transfers on PVT\r\n* Phuket Hotel to Phuket Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-08-02','2025-08-07',1,0,0,'2025-07-30 16:11:39','2025-07-30 17:37:08'),(1063,1761,38,2,0,0,33000,9000,'Thailand Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1st Day (3rd Aug)	\r\nTRANSFERS : EX BKK APT - Pattaya Hotel ( Central Pattaya ) 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n2nd Day (4th Aug) - SIC TOURS - PATTAYA 	Coral Island Tour By Speedboat With Indian Buffet Lunch on SIC \r\n\r\n3rd Day (5th Aug) - SIC TOURS - PATTAYA 	Nong Nooch Garden Admission + Show + Lunch on SIC \r\n\r\n4th Day (6th Aug) - TRANSFERS : EX PTY HOTEL - Bangkok Hotel (Pratunam & Sukhumvit Soi 1-24) 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n5th Day (7th Aug) - SIC TOURS - BANGKOK 	Half Day BKK Temple & Tour (2 Temple ) on SIC \r\n\r\n6th Day (8th Aug) - SIC TOURS - BANGKOK 	Full Day Safari World + Marine Park with Lunch on SIC \r\n\r\n7th Day (9th Aug) - TRANSFERS : EX BKK HTL - Bangkok BKK APT 	1-PRIVATE Seden BKK (Max 3 + Luggage) \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* BKK Airport to Pattaya Hotel transfers on PVT\r\n* Pattaya Hotel to Bangkok Hotel transfers on PVT\r\n* Bangkok Hotel to Bangkok Airport transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-08-03','2025-08-09',1,0,0,'2025-07-30 17:54:47','2025-07-30 19:31:51'),(1065,1768,557,1,0,0,92000,13000,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1: Arrival â€“ Transfer to Dambulla\r\n\r\nUpon arrival in Sri Lanka, you will be warmly welcomed by our representative at the airport. From there, you will be transferred to Dambulla, located in the heart of the Cultural Triangle. En route, visit the serene and historically significant Ridee Viharaya, also known as the Silver Temple, which is nestled among the hills and known for its intricate rock carvings and peaceful atmosphere. After the visit, continue your journey to Sigiriya. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing after your journey. Enjoy dinner and stay overnight in Dambulla.\r\n\r\nDay 2: Dambulla â€“Golden Temple-Minneriya Safari\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, head to the iconic Golden Temple of Dambulla, a UNESCO World Heritage Site known for its spectacular cave temples filled with ancient Buddha statues and colorful murals. Later in the evening, enjoy an adventurous jeep safari at Minneriya National Park, famous for its large elephant gatherings and diverse wildlife. Capture the beauty of nature and watch elephants in their natural habitat. After the safari, return to your hotel. Dinner and overnight stay in Dambulla.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Dambulla to Hatton via Kandy (Leave 9.00 A.M in the Morning)\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and head towards Hatton via Kandy, the cultural capital of Sri Lanka. En route, stop at a Spice Garden in Matale, where you will be introduced to a variety of spices and herbs that are grown locally and used in traditional Ayurvedic practices. On arrival in Kandy, visit a Royal Botanical Garden. After that transfer to Hatton. Dinner and overnight stay in Hatton.\r\n\r\nDay 4: Hatton to Bentota\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, depart from the hills of Hatton and head towards the sunny southern coast of Bentota, a serene beach destination ideal for relaxation. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and enjoy the remainder of the day at leisure, soaking up the coastal atmosphere or enjoying a peaceful walk along the golden beach. Dinner and overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 5: Bentota â€“ City Tour & Sightseeing\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, begin a full day of sightseeing in Bentota. Start with a visit to the revered Kande Viharaya Temple, known for its towering seated Buddha statue and peaceful ambiance. Next, proceed to the Turtle Hatchery in Kosgoda, a conservation project dedicated to protecting endangered sea turtles. In the evening, enjoy a scenic boat ride along the Madu River, exploring its rich mangrove ecosystem and local river life. After the tour, return to the hotel and relax. Dinner and overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Bentota to Colombo â€“ City Tour\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and transfer to Colombo, the bustling commercial capital of Sri Lanka. Upon arrival, check into your hotel and later proceed for a guided city tour. Visit key landmarks such as Galle Face Green, the iconic Port City, the historic Independence Square, and view the striking Lotus Tower from outside. Enjoy a shopping tour in Colomboâ€™s popular malls or local boutiques for souvenirs and gifts. Return to the hotel for dinner and stay overnight in Colombo.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 7: Departure\r\n\r\nAfter breakfast, depending on your departure flight time, you will be transferred to Bandaranaike International Airport for your onward journey, marking the end of a memorable 6-night holiday in Sri Lanka.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast/lunch or dinner\r\n* Vehicle : Toyota KDH Flat Roof   \r\nâ€¢ Welcome at the airport with Garlands   \r\n* Service of an English-speaking Driver\r\n* 02*500ml Bottles per person per Day                              \r\nâ€¢ Express way charges wherever applicable  \r\n* Insurance      ','â€¢ Entrance Fee to any sites which is not mentioned above.                      \r\nâ€¢ Early check in or late checkout charges.                                                            \r\nâ€¢ Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs                                           \r\nâ€¢ Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.         \r\nâ€¢ Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.         \r\nâ€¢ Camera or Video permits.                                               \r\nâ€¢ Expenses of a personal nature.                           \r\nâ€¢ Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.                       \r\nâ€¢ Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to \r\nincrease in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or \r\nwhile touring \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nSupplement cost for Minneriya Safari, Dambulla Cave Temple, Royal Botanical Garden, Turtle Hatchery, Madu River Boat Ride, Lotus Tower will be applicable.\r\nRates are indicative as of now','2025-08-03','2025-08-09',1,0,0,'2025-08-01 12:52:33','2025-08-01 14:15:59'),(1066,1771,349,4,0,0,122350,23000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Marina Dhow Cruise With Dinner (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Half Day City Tour (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Burj Khalifa Tour ( Burj Khalifa 124th + 125th Floor - Non Prime Hour NRF (Child Cost Applicable till 8 Years Only) ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) ( Ferrari World ) (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\nâ€¢ TRIO - Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (SIC Basis)(04-Adults)\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT Basis\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* All Tours will be on Shared Transfers Basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nTourism Dirham is not included in the quote and shall be Directly Payable by the guest ','2025-09-27','2025-10-01',1,0,0,'2025-08-02 17:00:07','2025-08-02 19:04:44'),(10