ival & Departure transfer \r\nâ€¢ Basic English Speaking Driver \r\nâ€¢ Daily water bottle during tours and transfers \r\nâ€¢ All tours and transfers as per itinerary on a private basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nâ€¢ Private Guide \r\nâ€¢ Tourist Tax ( I LOVE BALI ) \r\nâ€¢ Gili Harbor Tax ( Guest Pay Directly at Harbor) \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-10-08','2025-10-15',0,0,0,'2025-08-22 15:21:02','2025-08-22 17:55:30'),(1081,1790,16002,4,0,0,0,0,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - Wednesday 8th October, 2025\r\nDenpasar Airport to Ubud Hotel - Arrival and Transfer\r\n+ Welcome with Garland - Ticket\r\nOn Arrival Welcome\r\n\r\n2nd Day - Thursday 9th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Lempuyang Temple - Ticket\r\nLempuyang Temple sits on the steep slopes of Mount Lempuyang in Bali, with great views of the Mount Agung volcanoin the distance, framed by a famous stone gate (dubbed the â€˜Gates of Heavenâ€™). Sadly, the great view also means it draws crowds of tourists every day.\r\n+ Tirta Gangga - Ticket\r\nTirta Gangga is a former royal palace in eastern Bali, Indonesia. Named after the sacred river Ganges in India, it is noted for the Karangasem royal water palace, bathing pools and its Patirthan temple.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - Friday 10th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Goa Gjah - Ticket\r\nGoa Gajah is locally known as the Elephant Cave because of its close proximity to the Elephant River. A mysterious cave, relics, and ancient bathing pools set amid green rice paddies and a garden lure tourists from nearby Ubud.\r\n+ Sacred Monkey Forest - ticket\r\n+ ubud palace - Ticket\r\n+ Ubud market - ticket\r\n\r\n4th Day - Saturday 11th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day Including Interhotel Transfer\r\n+ Tanah Lot Sunset Tour - Ticket\r\nTanah Lot is one of seven ocean temples in Bali and has been a center of mythology for centuries. This Hindu temple, dedicated to the Gods of the sea and dates back to the 16th century, holds much significance for locals but is now just as well loved by visitors to the island.\r\n\r\n5th Day - Sunday 12th October, 2025\r\nNusa Penida West Trip with Local lunch With Pick Up & Drop - PVT\r\nAngel Bilabong + Kelingking beach + Broken beach + Crytsal Bay\r\n\r\n6th Day - Monday 13th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Half Day (6 hrs)\r\n+ candle light dinner @Jimbaran beach by Flavours of India - Ticket\r\n\r\n7th Day - Tuesday 14th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Gwk ( Garuda Wisnu Kencana ) - Ticket\r\nThe GWK Cultural Park is best known for being home to the enormous Garuda Wisnu Kencana (GWK) statue. Standing 121m tall, including the base, itâ€™s the tallest statue in Indonesia and one of the tallest in the world.\r\n+ Padang 2 Beach - Ticket\r\nPadang Padang Beach is a true hidden gem that has captivated surfers and beachgoers alike. This stunning tropical paradise, known for its dramatic limestone cliffs, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and world-class surf breaks, has become a must-visit destination for those seeking the ultimate Bali beach experience.\r\n+ Uluwatu tour - Ticket\r\nAn Uluwatu tour typically involves visiting Uluwatu Temple, a stunning cliffside temple with panoramic views of the Indian Ocean, watching the Kecak dance performance.\r\n\r\n8th Day - Wednesday 15th October, 2025\r\nKuta Hotel to Denpasar Airport - Departure\r\n\r\n','','* 7N Accommodation \r\n* Arrival & Departure transfer\r\n* Vehicle 1 APV/Avanza/Xenia) \r\nâ€¢ Basic English Speaking Driver \r\nâ€¢ Daily water bottle during tours and transfers \r\nâ€¢ All tours and transfers as per itinerary on a private basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nâ€¢ Private Guide \r\nâ€¢ Tourist Tax ( I LOVE BALI ) \r\nâ€¢ Gili Harbor Tax ( Guest Pay Directly at Harbor) \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n2 PAN Cards will be required','2025-10-08','2025-10-15',0,0,0,'2025-08-23 16:57:09','2025-08-23 19:30:51'),(1082,1791,3511,4,0,0,91200,18000,'Gangtok Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Sunday 5th October) : Bagdogra Airport to Darjeeling - Pickup\r\nApprox Distance: 70 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nMeet and Greet on arrival at Bagdogra International Airport and transfer to Darjeeling (6,950 Ft.). On arrival check-in to the hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n \r\n2nd Day - (Monday 6th October) : Darjeeling to Gangtok - Fullday Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 230 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 10 hrs\r\nEarly morning (4:00 AM) visit Tiger Hill (Subject to availability of Permit / Token) back to hotel. After breakfast at 8:30 AM check out from hotel (with luggage) and visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Ropeway (Note: Closed on 19th of Every Month), Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Japanese Temple(Peace Pagoda). Afternoon proceed to Gangtok (5,500 Ft. / 91 Kms. / 4 Hrs.). On arrival Check-in to your hotel. Overnight stay at Gangtok.\r\nNote: Darjeeling ropeway will be on direct payment basis. It has limited cabins (Approx. 8 and per cabin 4 persons can be accommodated), resulting in long queues due to high tourist volume. Be patient with potential delays. It could also impact your schedule for other sightseeing activities due to time constraints.\r\n \r\n3rd Day - (Tuesday 7th October) : Gangtok to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 120 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 8 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast, start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft. / 37 Kms. / 02 Hrs. from Gangtok) and further drive to New Baba Mandir (13,200 ft. / 16 Kms. / 01 Hrs. from Tsomgo Lake). Evening back to Gangtok. Overnight stay at Gangtok. Note: In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing. Due to winter season (heavy snow) vehicle will be able to drive till Snow point on the way to Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir.\r\n \r\n4th Day - (Wednesday 8th October) : Gangtok to Bagdogra Airport - Drop\r\nApprox Distance: 125 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 5 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast, checkout from the hotel and take departure transfer to Bagdogra International Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\nâ€¢ Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section\r\nâ€¢ Meal plan as mentioned\r\n* 1-Innova / Xylo / Similar as per itinerary & timing only.\r\nâ€¢ Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis)\r\nâ€¢ All permit fees & hotel taxes (as per itinerary)\r\n\r\n','â€¢ Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage\r\nâ€¢ Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\nâ€¢ Entrance Fees & Guide charges\r\nâ€¢ Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot)\r\nâ€¢ Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\nâ€¢ Room Heater Charges\r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation','2025-10-05','2025-10-08',1,0,0,'2025-08-25 11:44:07','2025-08-25 12:40:00'),(1083,1792,1559,4,1,1,0,0,'Gujarat Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n1st Day (Thu 6th November) : AHMEDABAD - Arrival & Stay\r\nUpon arriving at Ahmedabad Airport, you will be picked up and escorted to the hotel by our local tour representative via private transfer. After check-in formalities, evening free for leisure activities. Overnight stay at hotel in Ahmedabad.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 7th November) : Ahmedabad to Bhuj - Arrival and Transfer and Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 350 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 7 hrs\r\nHave breakfast and drive to Bhuj. On arrival visit places like Aina Mahal Museum, Pragmahal Museum, Swaminarayan temple, Bharatiya Sanskriti Darshan Exhibition & Cenotaphs of Royal Family. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 8th November) : Bhuj - Dhordo (White Desert) Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 200 Km\r\nToday after Breakfast get ready to explore the Banni and Pachcham regions and the edge of the Great Rann of Kutch. Visit Dhordo village, Ludiya village and Khavda village. Later visit Kalo Dungar (Black Hill) and Dattatray Temple, which provides the view of the Great Rann & sunset. Later drive to Bhuj and overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sun 9th November) : Bhuj to Dwarka - Transfer & Sightseen Via Jamnagar\r\nApprox Distance: 400 Km\r\nAfter Breakfast proceed to Jamnagar with as per our Gujarat package. After reaching Jamnagar, stop by Lakhota Lake and Lakhota Museum. Seek blessings at Bala Hanuman Temple and proceed to Dwarka by road. After a long drive from Ahmedabad to Dwarka, check into the hotel with family and unwind. If time permits then attend evening Aarti at Dwarkadhish Temple. Return to your hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Mon 10th November) : Dwarka - Fullday Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km\r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel, take a holy dip in the Gomti River and then start temple hopping in Dwarka. Visit Nageshwar Jyotirlinga Temple, Gopi Talav, and Bet Dwarka. On the way back to Dwarka visit Rukmani Temple. Take the afternoon to explore coastal attractions including the lighthouse on the beach. Attend evening aarti at Dwarkadhish Temple and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Tue 11th November) : Dwarka to Somnath - Transfer Via Porbander Sightseeing\r\nApprox Distance: 220 Km\r\nAfter breakfast in Dwarka, check out and drive to Somnath. Stop by Porbandar along the way to visit Kirti Mandir where Mahatma Gandhi was born and visit Sudama Temple. Continue your family holidays in Gujarat by proceeding to Somnath town. After check-in formalities, visit Bhalka Tirth, Triveni Sangam, and Geeta Mandir. Attend evening aarti at Somnath Temple and later enjoy light and sound show in Somnath. Return to your hotel and overnight stay at the Hotel in Somnath.\r\nNOTE: Heavy vehicles are not allowed in Porbandar City.\r\n\r\n7th Day (Wed 12th November) : Somnath to Vadodara - Transfer and Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 400 Km\r\nPost breakfast drive to Vadodara. On arrival at Vadodara check in at the hotel and if time permits visit Laxmi Vilas palace, Sayaji baug Zoo, Kirti Mandir then return back to the hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n8th Day (Thu 13th November) : Vadodara to Ahmedabad - Transfer via Statue of Unity day excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 300 Km\r\nEarly morning drive to Kevadiya to visit â€œStatue of Unityâ€: It is the world\'s tallest statue with a height of 182 meters, Exhibition, Audio Visual Gallery, Valley of Flowers, Sardar Sarovar Dam Viewpoint. Later drive to Ahmedabad and overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n9th Day (Fri 14th November) : AHMEDABAD - Sightseeing and Drop\r\nAfter Breakfast at the hotel visit attractions in Ahmedabad as per Gujarat tour itinerary. Pay a visit to Gandhi Ashram, enjoy boating in Kankaria Lake, and admire the architecture of Siddi Syed Mosque, Adalaj Stepwell, and Akshardham Temple. Later drop at Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Ac accommodation in the above-mentioned hotels\r\n* Meal Plan: As mentioned in column on buffet menu (Pure Veg.)\r\n* Ac Vehicle as per the above-mentioned itinerary\r\n* Driver Allowance, Toll Tax Parking.\r\n* Pick up and drop from Airport\r\n* All applicable luxury taxes of hotels','* Entry fees to monuments and sightseeing places\r\n* Anything not mentioned in the package â€œINCLUDESâ€\r\n* Statue of unity tickets booked directly by guest own on the website: www.soutickets.in (Closed on Monday)\r\n* Gir Jungle safari permit book directly by guest own on the website: www.girlion.gujarat.gov.in (remains closed from 16th June to 15th Oct every year)\r\n* Porter-age charges at hotels and airports, tips, insurance, laundry, liquors, wine, extra room services, phone calls (STD, ISD)\r\n* All items of personal nature\r\nNOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-11-06','2025-11-14',1,0,0,'2025-08-25 18:41:27','2025-08-25 21:39:38'),(1084,1794,16002,4,0,0,156000,15600,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - Wednesday 8th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Welcome with Garland - Ticket\r\nOn Arrival Welcome\r\n+ Tegenungan Waterfall - Ticket\r\nTegenungan waterfall is located in the village of Kemenuh, Gianyar Regency, about a 30-minute drive from Ubud. Itâ€™s easily accessible from other parts of the island as well, such as Kuta, Seminyak, and Sanur.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - Thursday 9th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Lempuyang Temple - Ticket\r\nLempuyang Temple sits on the steep slopes of Mount Lempuyang in Bali, with great views of the Mount Agung volcanoin the distance, framed by a famous stone gate (dubbed the â€˜Gates of Heavenâ€™). Sadly, the great view also means it draws crowds of tourists every day.\r\n+ Tirta Gangga - Ticket\r\nTirta Gangga is a former royal palace in eastern Bali, Indonesia. Named after the sacred river Ganges in India, it is noted for the Karangasem royal water palace, bathing pools and its Patirthan temple.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - Friday 10th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Goa Gjah - Ticket\r\nGoa Gajah is locally known as the Elephant Cave because of its close proximity to the Elephant River. A mysterious cave, relics, and ancient bathing pools set amid green rice paddies and a garden lure tourists from nearby Ubud.\r\n+ Sacred Monkey Forest - ticket\r\n+ ubud palace - Ticket\r\n+ Ubud market - ticket\r\n+ Activitiy package (05 swing + 02 nest + Local lunch) By Desa Swing - Ticket\r\n\r\n4th Day - Saturday 11th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day Including Interhotel Transfer\r\n+ Tanah Lot Sunset Tour - Ticket\r\nTanah Lot is one of seven ocean temples in Bali and has been a center of mythology for centuries. This Hindu temple, dedicated to the Gods of the sea and dates back to the 16th century, holds much significance for locals but is now just as well loved by visitors to the island.\r\n\r\n5th Day - Sunday 12th October, 2025\r\nNusa Penida West Trip with Local lunch With Pick Up & Drop - PVT\r\nAngel Bilabong + Kelingking beach + Broken beach + Crytsal Bay\r\n\r\n6th Day - Monday 13th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Half Day\r\n+ candle light dinner @Jimbaran beach by Flavours of India - Ticket\r\n\r\n7th Day - Tuesday 14th October, 2025\r\nDay Use Vehicle - Full Day\r\n+ Gwk ( Garuda Wisnu Kencana ) - Ticket\r\nThe GWK Cultural Park is best known for being home to the enormous Garuda Wisnu Kencana (GWK) statue. Standing 121m tall, including the base, itâ€™s the tallest statue in Indonesia and one of the tallest in the world.\r\n+ Padang 2 Beach - Ticket\r\nPadang Padang Beach is a true hidden gem that has captivated surfers and beachgoers alike. This stunning tropical paradise, known for its dramatic limestone cliffs, crystal-clear turquoise waters, and world-class surf breaks, has become a must-visit destination for those seeking the ultimate Bali beach experience.\r\n+ Uluwatu tour - Ticket\r\nAn Uluwatu tour typically involves visiting Uluwatu Temple, a stunning cliffside temple with panoramic views of the Indian Ocean, watching the Kecak dance performance. \r\n+ Kecak Dance Tour - Ticket\r\nthe unique Kecak fire dance, performed by a group of men using sound techniques. Follow the story of this historical dance which embodies the romantic story of love between Rama and Sinta, a mythical giant named Ravana, and a Monkey army, all against the backdrop of the Indian Ocean at sunset.\r\n\r\n8th Day - Wednesday 15th October, 2025\r\nKuta Hotel to Denpasar Airport - Departure\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* 7N Accommodation \r\n* Arrival & Departure transfer\r\n* Vehicle 1 APV/Avanza/Xenia) \r\nâ€¢ Basic English Speaking Driver \r\nâ€¢ Daily water bottle during tours and transfers (2 water bottles (500ml) per day per person \r\nâ€¢ All tours and transfers as per itinerary on a private basis \r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\nâ€¢ Private Guide \r\nâ€¢ Tourist Tax ( I LOVE BALI ) \r\nâ€¢ Gili Harbor Tax ( Guest Pay Directly at Harbor) \r\nâ€¢ NOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded \r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n2 PAN Cards will be required','2025-10-08','2025-10-15',0,0,0,'2025-08-27 12:59:18','2025-08-27 14:04:29'),(1085,1798,1559,4,1,1,0,0,'Gujarat Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n1st Day (Thu 6th November) : AHMEDABAD - Arrival & Stay\r\nUpon arriving at Ahmedabad Airport, you will be picked up and escorted to the hotel by our local tour representative via private transfer. After check-in formalities, evening free for leisure activities. Overnight stay at hotel in Ahmedabad.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 7th November) : Ahmedabad to Bhuj - Arrival and Transfer and Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 350 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 7 hrs\r\nHave breakfast and drive to Bhuj. On arrival visit places like Aina Mahal Museum, Pragmahal Museum, Swaminarayan temple, Bharatiya Sanskriti Darshan Exhibition & Cenotaphs of Royal Family. Overnight stay at the hotel.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 8th November) : Bhuj - Dhordo (White Desert) Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 200 Km\r\nToday after Breakfast get ready to explore the Banni and Pachcham regions and the edge of the Great Rann of Kutch. Visit Dhordo village, Ludiya village and Khavda village. Later visit Kalo Dungar (Black Hill) and Dattatray Temple, which provides the view of the Great Rann & sunset. Later drive to Bhuj and overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sun 9th November) : Bhuj to Dwarka - Transfer & Sightseen Via Jamnagar\r\nApprox Distance: 400 Km\r\nAfter Breakfast proceed to Jamnagar with as per our Gujarat package. After reaching Jamnagar, stop by Lakhota Lake and Lakhota Museum. Seek blessings at Bala Hanuman Temple and proceed to Dwarka by road. After a long drive from Ahmedabad to Dwarka, check into the hotel with family and unwind. If time permits then attend evening Aarti at Dwarkadhish Temple. Return to your hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n5th Day (Mon 10th November) : Dwarka - Fullday Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km\r\nAfter breakfast at the hotel, take a holy dip in the Gomti River and then start temple hopping in Dwarka. Visit Nageshwar Jyotirlinga Temple, Gopi Talav, and Bet Dwarka. On the way back to Dwarka visit Rukmani Temple. Take the afternoon to explore coastal attractions including the lighthouse on the beach. Attend evening aarti at Dwarkadhish Temple and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n6th Day (Tue 11th November) : Dwarka to Somnath - Transfer Via Porbander Sightseeing\r\nApprox Distance: 220 Km\r\nAfter breakfast in Dwarka, check out and drive to Somnath. Stop by Porbandar along the way to visit Kirti Mandir where Mahatma Gandhi was born and visit Sudama Temple. Continue your family holidays in Gujarat by proceeding to Somnath town. After check-in formalities, visit Bhalka Tirth, Triveni Sangam, and Geeta Mandir. Attend evening aarti at Somnath Temple and later enjoy light and sound show in Somnath. Return to your hotel and overnight stay at the Hotel in Somnath.\r\nNOTE: Heavy vehicles are not allowed in Porbandar City.\r\n\r\n7th Day (Wed 12th November) : Somnath to Vadodara - Transfer and Sightseen\r\nApprox Distance: 400 Km\r\nPost breakfast drive to Vadodara. On arrival at Vadodara check in at the hotel and if time permits visit Laxmi Vilas palace, Sayaji baug Zoo, Kirti Mandir then return back to the hotel and overnight stay.\r\n\r\n8th Day (Thu 13th November) : Vadodara to Ahmedabad - Transfer via Statue of Unity day excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 300 Km\r\nEarly morning drive to Kevadiya to visit â€œStatue of Unityâ€: It is the world\'s tallest statue with a height of 182 meters, Exhibition, Audio Visual Gallery, Valley of Flowers, Sardar Sarovar Dam Viewpoint. Later drive to Ahmedabad and overnight stay at hotel.\r\n\r\n9th Day (Fri 14th November) : AHMEDABAD - Sightseeing and Drop\r\nAfter Breakfast at the hotel visit attractions in Ahmedabad as per Gujarat tour itinerary. Pay a visit to Gandhi Ashram, enjoy boating in Kankaria Lake, and admire the architecture of Siddi Syed Mosque, Adalaj Stepwell, and Akshardham Temple. Later drop at Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Ac accommodation in the above-mentioned hotels\r\n* Meal Plan: As mentioned in column on buffet menu (Pure Veg.)\r\n* Ac Vehicle as per the above-mentioned itinerary\r\n* Driver Allowance, Toll Tax Parking.\r\n* Pick up and drop from Airport\r\n* All applicable luxury taxes of hotels','* Entry fees to monuments and sightseeing places\r\n* Anything not mentioned in the package â€œINCLUDESâ€\r\n* Statue of unity tickets booked directly by guest own on the website: www.soutickets.in (Closed on Monday)\r\n* Gir Jungle safari permit book directly by guest own on the website: www.girlion.gujarat.gov.in (remains closed from 16th June to 15th Oct every year)\r\n* Porter-age charges at hotels and airports, tips, insurance, laundry, liquors, wine, extra room services, phone calls (STD, ISD)\r\n* All items of personal nature\r\nNOTE: Anything not in inclusions is excluded\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-11-06','2025-11-14',0,0,0,'2025-08-28 11:43:31','2025-08-28 11:58:33'),(1086,1799,15542,2,0,0,0,0,'Wellness Diaries','*  Wellness drinks on Arrival\r\n*   Room as per chosen category\r\n*   Doctor Consultation with our Ayurveda /Naturopathy Doctors\r\n*   All meals- Pure vegetarian\r\n*   Yoga consultations with group yoga and Pranayam session for wellbeing\r\n*   Daily group Meditation session\r\n*   Ayurveda therapy per day per person basis as recommended by our in-house doctor. \r\n*    Body composition analysis\r\n*    Fitness consultation & session with our fitness expert \r\n\r\nMeal Timings : \r\nBreakfast- 7: 30 AM to 9:30 AM\r\nLunch â€“ 1 pm to 3 pm\r\nDinner- 7:30 PM to 9: 30 Pm\r\n\r\nArrival- Departure time is:- \r\nArrival 01:00 PM\r\nDeparture: 11:00 AM\r\n\r\nLate Departure - policy:- \r\nDeparture between: - 12 to 1 pm â€“ 20% of the total charges \r\nDeparture between: - 2 pm to 4 pm- 30% of the total charges \r\nDeparture between: - 4 pm to 6 pm- 50 % of the total charges \r\nDeparture between: - will be applicable of full day charge\r\n\r\n\r\n','','','* Any type of personal expense\r\n\r\n','Important notice- Clothes are washed in the room & drying in the balcony is strictly prohibited in our property. We have laundry services on the property which is on a chargeable basis. \r\n\r\nKindly please be noted MODI YOGA RETREAT is not a hotel, this is purely a wellness treatment center. Smoking, alcohol & non-vegetarian foods are strictly prohibited in our wellness center.\r\n\r\n*Your treatment days might get increased, depending on the person\'s body constitution & doctor 