n/day\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Other meals & Beverages not mentioned above\r\n* Airport tax\r\n* Compulsory tips for guide and driver US$3/client/day\r\n* Personal expense such as laundry, meals or drinks during, etc..,\r\n* Other items not mentioned in above\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2025-10-28','2025-11-03',1,0,0,'2025-10-07 12:19:36','2025-10-07 12:46:17'),(1122,1832,15512,4,0,0,0,0,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 1 : HANOI ARRIVAL â€“ CITY TOUR\r\n\r\nDAY 2 : HANOI - HA LONG DAILY CRUISE â€“ SIC TOUR (B, L)\r\n\r\nDAY 3 : HANOI -  FLY TO DANANG (B)\r\n\r\nDAY 4 : BANA HILLS â€“ GOLDEN BRIDGE â€“ SIC TOUR (B)\r\n\r\nDAY 5 : DANANG â€“ FLIGHT TO HO CHI MINH (B)\r\n\r\nDAY 6 : HO CHI MINH- CU CHI TUNNELS â€“ CITY TOUR (B, L)\r\n\r\nDAY 7 : HO CHI MINH â€“ DEPARTURE (B)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare (DEL-HAN, SGN-DEL)\r\n* Internal flight (HAN-DAD, DAD-SGN)\r\n*Accommodation in a twin or double/triple  sharing room with daily breakfast\r\n* Air-conditioned vehicle with experienced drivers\r\n* Experienced local English speaking guides\r\n* Lunch or Dinner as specified in the itinerary\r\n* Daily shared Halong cruise with Vietnamese food\r\n* Entrance fees for all visits as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* 01 bottle of mineral water per person per day tour\r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Personal expenses, such as laundry, telephone, drinks, etc.\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned\r\n* All other services not specified in the itinerary\r\n* USD 2/pax/day for Guide & USD 1/pax/day for Driver (mandatory)\r\n* Tips for boat man, cruse staff,â€¦\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nConfirmation of the above-mentioned hotels are subject to availability only otherwise we will confirm similar category hotel.\r\n*** Please note: Standard check in time is 14.00 hrs, check out time is 12:00 noon.','2025-10-28','2025-11-03',1,0,0,'2025-10-07 14:49:33','2025-10-07 16:16:31'),(1123,1834,439,6,1,1,0,0,'Armenia Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival\r\nArrival at Zvartnots International Airport. Meet and greet transfer to the hotel. Overnight in Yerevan\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Yerevan City tour/Vernissage\r\nStart exploring Yerevan which is also named â€œPink Cityâ€ for buildings with pink color which gives the stone\r\nâ€œtufaâ€. Itâ€™s an old and ancient city therewith considered also a modern and splendid city. Start your tour from\r\nRepublic Square which was build 1950s by the project of Tamanian 20 years of after his death. Walking\r\nthrough the Northern Avenue, which is the modern part of the capital and considers to be the heart of\r\nYerevan. Afterwards we are next to Opera House and Swan Lake where we can have photo stop. Continue to\r\nCascade monument which is an open-air museum. Climbing up the stairs you will enjoy the fascinating view\r\nof Yerevan. Walking through memorial park and stop by the Mother Armenia Monument. Visit Ararat Brandy\r\nmuseum Overnight in Yerevan.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Yerevan-Khor Virap-Areni-Noravank- Yerevan\r\nToday we are going to learn more about the historical treasures of Armenia by driving to Ararat Valley to\r\nvisit Khor Virap Monastery. The monastery of Khor Virap (3rd â€“ 17th cc.) is located in the place of an\r\nancient capital of Armenia â€“Artashat. The significance of the church is relatively connected with Grigor\r\nIlluminator who was spreading Christianity in Armenia\r\nContinue our trip to one of the most important agricultural regions of Armenia â€“ to Vayots Dzor region.\r\nAfterwards, visit one of the local wineries in Areni village for homemade wine degustation.\r\nTodayâ€™s cultural discovery will be Noravank Monastery - a spectacular monastic complex, surrounded with\r\nmountains, richly covered by red stones which give one the harmony of culture and nature. Return to\r\nYerevan. Overnight at the hotel in Yerevan\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Yerevan-Tsaxkadzor-Sevan Lake-Yerevan\r\nDeparture to the resort town of Tsakhkadzor (Gorge of Flowers) â€“ town of forested mountains. Walking tour\r\naround the city. Opportunity to ride up the ropeway which will take you to the peak of mount Teghenis from\r\nwhere opens breathtaking view to the forested town. The most popular season to visit Tsaghkadzor is winter\r\nbecause of the famous ski resort which is the biggest in Armenia and attracts tourists and professional\r\nathletes from all around the world for skiing and snowboarding. The road will take you today to Lake Sevan\r\nwhich is going to be one of the highlights if your trip. Climb the stairs up on the peninsula from where opens a\r\nfascinating view to the â€œblue-eyedâ€ lake. Sightseeing tour on the peninsula. Lake Sevan is considered to be one\r\nof the largest sweet lakes in the world at an altitude of 1897 meters above sea level. Back to Yerevan.\r\n\r\nDay 5:Yerevan / Garni / Geghard /Yerevan\r\nAfter breakfast departure to Geghard Monastery (13th c.) â€“ a monastery which is hewn out from a cave. The\r\nmonastery had been originally named Ayrivank meaning \"the Monastery of the Cave\". The name commonly\r\nused for the monastery today, Geghard, or more fully Geghardavank meaning \"the Monastery of the Spear\".\r\nThe monastery is also included in the UNESCO World Heritage list.\r\nContinue our journey to Garni Pagan Temple from 1st c. The temple was built by Armenian King Tiridates and\r\nwas dedicated to the God of Sun Mithra. Garni is the only Hellenistic temple existing nowadays in Armenia.\r\nThe stairs of the temple are made huge and high which means that every human being climbing up the stairs\r\nis condescending to God of Sun\r\nBack to capital. Overnight in Yerevan\r\n\r\nDay6: Departure\r\nTransfer to the airport. Departure home!\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation with Daily breakfast\r\n* Individual airport/hotel/airport transfer\r\n* Transportation for sightseeing tours on private bases\r\n*  English speaking Guide\r\n*  Entrance fee to sightseeing places\r\n* 1x ropeway ticket in Tsaghkadzor\r\n* 1 x wine degustation\r\n* 2 bottle water per day per person\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Travel Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n* Alcoholic Beverages\r\n* Tips and portage\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nDepending on the weather conditions travel routes can be changed','2025-10-14','2025-10-19',1,0,0,'2025-10-09 17:27:45','2025-10-09 20:13:17'),(1124,1835,15595,4,0,0,0,0,'Sri Lanka Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival in Sri Lanka - Kandy\r\nUpon arrival at the airport, you will be warmly welcomed by your driver and transferred to the cultural capital,\r\nKandy. En route, visit the fascinating Pinnawala Elephant Orphanage, where you can witness baby elephants being\r\nfed and bathed. Continue your journey with a stop at the Mawanella spice garden, exploring Sri Lankaâ€™s rich spice\r\nheritage. Once in Kandy, check into your hotel and unwind. In the evening, visit the Gem Museum to marvel at Sri\r\nLanka\'s precious stones and enjoy a vibrant cultural dance performance. Conclude your day with an overnight stay\r\nin Kandy.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Kandy to Nuwara Eliya\r\nStart your day with a visit to the Temple of the Sacred Tooth Relic, a UNESCO World Heritage site that houses a\r\nrevered tooth relic of Buddha. After soaking in the spiritual ambiance, transfer to the picturesque town of Nuwara\r\nEliya. Along the way, visit the Hanuman Temple, and tour a tea factory to learn about Sri Lanka\'s famed tea\r\nproduction. In the evening, enjoy a relaxing boat ride on Gregory Lake before checking into your hotel for an\r\novernight stay in Nuwara Eliya.\r\n\r\nDay 3: Nuwara Eliya to Bentota\r\nAfter breakfast, visit the Sita Amman Temple, a significant site from the Ramayana epic, and explore the\r\nenchanting Hakgala Botanical Garden. Later, embark on a scenic drive to the coastal town of Bentota. Upon arrival,\r\ncheck into your hotel and spend the rest of the day at leisure, relaxing by the beach or exploring the local area.\r\nEnjoy an overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Exploring Bentota\r\nBegin your day with a visit to the Kande Viharaya, home to one of the tallest sitting Buddha statues in Sri Lanka.\r\nNext, visit the Kosgoda Turtle Hatchery, where you can learn about turtle conservation efforts and see baby turtles.\r\nIn the afternoon, enjoy a scenic boat ride on the Madu River, navigating through mangroves and spotting wildlife.\r\nFor thrill-seekers, optional water sports activities like jet skiing, banana boat rides, and tube rides await. End your\r\nadventurous day with an overnight stay in Bentota.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Bentota to Colombo\r\nAfter breakfast, transfer to Colombo, Sri Lanka\'s bustling commercial capital. Check into your hotel and set out for\r\na city tour, visiting landmarks such as the Gangaramaya Temple, Independence Square, Port City, and Galle Face\r\nGreen. In the evening, embark on a guided shopping tour to explore Colomboâ€™s vibrant markets and chic\r\nboutiques. Conclude your day with an overnight stay in Colombo.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Departure from Colombo\r\nIf time permits, enjoy a final shopping spree after breakfast. Afterwards, you will be transferred to the airport to\r\ncatch your departure flight, taking with you unforgettable memories of your Sri Lankan adventure.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation at the hotels mentioned or similar on HB.\r\n* Express way charges wherever applicable\r\n* Transportation in a Pvt Air-conditioned vehicle.\r\n* Service of an English-speaking driver\r\n* City tours in Kandy, Nuwara Eliya, Bentota & Colombo\r\n* All applicable Government Taxes\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\nValue Additions :\r\nFree Cultural Show Tickets (Clients should visit a Gem shop which will be direct by us) at Kandy.\r\n02*500ml Bottles per person per Day\r\nWelcome at the airport with Garlands\r\nFree Gem Factory visit and explanation about the gem progress at Kandy.\r\n \r\n','* Entrance Fee to any sites.\r\n* Visa is available free on arrival and through the online application system. To apply for online please visit - https://eta.gov.lk  \r\n* Tips to Guides / Chauffeurs\r\n* Any fluctuations in the dollar component will affect the costing.\r\n* Lunch or any extra meal not mentioned on the above program during the tour.\r\n* Camera or Video permits.\r\n* Expenses of a personal nature.\r\n* Any service not specifically mentioned in the inclusion.\r\n* Any increase of cost due to political disturbance / bandh or increase in tax or fuel cost, leading to increase in surface transportation and land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure or while touring\r\n* Visa\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nPinnawala elephant orphanage, Temple of the tooth relic, Gregory Lake, Turtle hatchery, Madu river boat ride, Haggala botanical garden, Gangaramaya temple and Lotus tower on supplement cost\r\n','2025-12-26','2025-12-31',1,0,0,'2025-10-09 17:55:38','2025-10-09 18:33:36'),(1126,1833,15512,2,1,0,0,0,'Vietnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Ho Chi Minh Arrival \r\n\r\nDay 2 : HO CHI MINH â€“ HALF DAY CITY TOUR - CU CHI TUNNELS SIC TOUR (B/L)\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Ho Chi Minh - Danang \r\n\r\nDay 4 : DA NANG - BA NA HILLS â€“ GOLDEN BIRDGE â€“ SIC TOUR (B)\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Danang - Flight to Hanoi \r\n\r\nDay 6 : Day 6 : HANOI- HALONG DAILY CRUISE â€“ SIC TOUR ( B/L)\r\n\r\nDay 7 : HANOI HALF DAY CITY SIC TOUR (B,L) - Fly to Hometown (B/L)\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare (DEL-SGN, HAN-DEL)\r\n* Internal Flights (SGN-DAD, DAD-HAN)\r\n* Accommodation in Twin/Double sharing with daily breakfast (Standard check in time: 14.00 & check out time 12.00)\r\n* Private airport transfer two ways\r\n* Half day Hanoi city SIC tour with Vietnamese lunch\r\n* Day trip Halong Bay SIC tour with Vietnamese lunch\r\n* Day trip Ba Na SIC tour\r\n* Day trip Cu Chi Tunnels and Ho Chi Minh city tour SIC tour with Vietnamese lunch\r\n* Experienced local English speaking guides\r\n* Entrance fees for all visits as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* 01 bottle of mineral water per person per day tour\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Personal expenses, such as laundry, telephone, drinks, etc.\r\n* All other services not specified in the itinerary\r\n* Compulsory Tips Policy (for Guide & Driver) : USD 2/pax/day for Guide & USD 1/pax/day for Driver\r\n* TCS\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-01-07','2026-01-13',0,0,0,'2025-10-10 13:04:03','2025-10-10 13:32:28'),(1127,1836,33,4,0,0,316500,65000,'Hong Kong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Private Airport to Hotel Transfer â€“ Kowloon Side (One-Way) â€“ Available from 8:00 AM to 9:00 PM; vehicle capacity up to 6 passengers.\r\nDay 1 : Shared Classic Hong Kong Half-Day Night Tour (Kowloon Hotels) â€“ Includes one-way Peak Tram, Victoria Peak, Golden Bauhinia Square, Star Ferry Harbour Cruise, Bruce Lee Tribute at Avenue of Stars, Old Clock Tower, and Symphony of Lights show; starts 4:00 PM, duration up to 5 hours;\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Shared Magical Disneyland Tour â€“ Tier 4 Entry Ticket â€“ Includes (Tier 4) Disneyland admission; pickup at 9:30 AM and return by 9:30 PM from Kowloon Hotels (HP8, Regal Kowloon, HP Metropolis, Royal Garden, InterContinental Grand Stanford).\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Shared Amazing Ocean Park Tour â€“ Standard Entry â€“ Includes park admission; pickup at 9:30 AM and return by 7:00 PM from Kowloon Hotels (HP8D, Regal Kowloon, HP Metropolis, Royal Garden, InterContinental Grand Stanford)\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Shared Hotel to Ferry Pier Transfer (One-Way) â€“ From Kowloon Hotels (HP8, Regal Kowloon, HP Metropolis, Royal Garden, InterContinental Grand Stanford) at 12:45 pm for 2:30 pm Ferry.\r\nDay 4 : One-Way Ferry Ticket â€“ Economy Class (Day Sailing) â€“ Hong Kong to Macau or Macau to Hong Kong, 7:30 AM to 5:00 PM, Weekdays (Sunday to Thursday).\r\nDay 4 : Private Transfer â€“ Macau Ferry Pier â†” Hotel or Macau Hotel to ferry pier or Macau Port to Hotel  or Macau Hotel to port â€“ One-way private transfer; service available from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM; vehicle capacity up to 6 passengers.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Shared Dazzling Macau Morning Tour (SIC) â€“ Includes A-Ma Temple, Ruins of St. Paulâ€™s, Kun Iam Statue, Lotus Square & Macau Tower photo stop; pickup between 10:00â€“11:00 AM from hotel lobby.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Private Transfer â€“ Macau Ferry Pier â†” Hotel or Macau Hotel to ferry pier or Macau Port to Hotel  or Macau Hotel to port â€“ One-way private transfer; service available from 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM; vehicle capacity up to 6 passengers.\r\nDay 6 : One-Way Ferry Ticket â€“ Economy Class (Day Sailing) â€“ Hong Kong to Macau or Macau to Hong Kong, 7:30 AM to 5:00 PM, Weekdays (Sunday to Thursday).\r\nDay 6 : Private Ferry Pier to Airport Transfer (One-Way), service available 8:00 AM to 10:00 PM; vehicle capacity up to 6 passengers.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Ferry tickets \r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Early morning surcharge not included\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\n-Pre-Arrival Registration for Hong Kong is compulsory for all the passengers holding Indian Passport. We will require a copy of the PAR before booking any hotel.','2025-12-27','2026-01-01',1,0,0,'2025-10-10 16:45:36','2025-10-11 13:25:56'),(1128,1837,297,4,2,0,135000,30000,'Visakhapatnam Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 1 : VIZ