ai with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT for Dubai\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nBaggage per flight mentioned below:\r\nYYZ-DXB Check-in Baggage : 2pc, Cabin : 1pc\r\nDXB-DEL Check-in Baggage : 30kg, Cabin : 7kg\r\nDEL-YYZ Check-in Baggage : 23kg, Cabin : 7 kg \r\n\r\n\r\n','2026-03-02','2026-03-05',0,0,0,'2026-01-13 13:40:02','2026-01-13 14:46:58'),(1161,1882,16002,4,0,0,0,0,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay : 01 Airport â€“ Hotel Transfers\r\n\r\nDay : 02 Benoa Water sports ( Parasailing , Banana Boat , Jet ski ) + Ulubatu Temple Tour ( B )\r\n\r\nDay : 03 West Nusa Penida tour  \r\n4 beaches - Kelingking Beach, Angel Billabong, Broken Beach, Crystal bay + Lunch Indonesia Set Menu - Back to Hotel ( B )\r\n\r\nDay : 04 Ulandanu + Handara gate + Tanaa lot Temple Visit with Entrance Tickets ( B )\r\n\r\nDay : 05 Inter  Hotel Transfers + Kintamani Volcano tour + Bali swing package +  Rice  Terrace + Coffee Plantation (B) \r\n\r\nDay : 06  ATV Ride on couple sharing basis  ( B )\r\n\r\nDay : 07 Hotel â€“ airport Departure Transfers ( B )\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation in Kuta with breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Ubud with breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the Itinerary\r\n* All the tours and transfers on Pvt\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tourism Tax\r\n* Visa\r\n* Anything not mentioned in the inclusions\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-03-15','2026-03-21',1,0,0,'2026-01-13 19:06:34','2026-01-14 11:58:30'),(1162,1883,349,3,0,0,61800,22000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the DXB Airport and transfer (Pvt) to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Have breakfast at the hotel.\r\nHalf-Day Dubai City Tour (SIC) Duration : 5 Hours Approx\r\nBurj Khalifa 124th+125th Floor-Non Prime Hour (Duration 1 to 2 hrs) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Have Breakfast at the hotel.\r\nPremium Desert Safari with BBQ Dinner (Duration 6 Hrs) SIC\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Have Breakfast at the hotel and relax (or explore nearby places on your own).\r\nEvening Tour Dubai Marina Luxury Dhow Dinner Cruise (Duration 2 hrs) SIC\r\n \r\nDay 05 : After having breakfast check-out from the hotel and Transfer to the DXB Airport (PVT) for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation in Dubai with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT for Dubai\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meals other than the mentioned\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nBaggage per flight mentioned below:\r\nDTW-DXB Check-in Baggage : 2pc, Cabin : 1pc\r\nDXB-DEL Check-in Baggage : 30kg, Cabin : 7kg\r\nDEL-YYZ Check-in Baggage : 23kg, Cabin : 7 kg \r\n\r\n\r\n','2026-03-02','2026-03-05',1,0,0,'2026-01-14 14:13:48','2026-01-14 17:51:59'),(1164,1885,624,4,0,0,0,0,'Guwahati Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n1st Day - (Thursday 22nd January) : Guwahati Airport to Shillong - Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nOn arrival at Guwahati Airport & transfer to Shillong, which is also called the \'Scotland of the East\". On the way visit a majestic placid lake with its surrounding sylvan hills Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which is the biggest local market. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Friday 23rd January) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hrs\r\nAfter an early breakfast, proceed for a full-day excursion to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), renowned as one of the wettest places on earth. En route, stop to admire the cascading Elephanta Falls, soak in the breathtaking vistas from Mawdokâ€“Dympep Valley Viewpoint, and explore the unique Garden of Caves. On arrival, witness some of Cherrapunjeeâ€™s most spectacular natural wonders including the majestic Nohkalikai Falls (the tallest plunge waterfall in India), the enchanting Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), and the fascinating limestone formations inside the Mawsmai Caves. In the evening, drive back to Shillong for an overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Saturday 24th January) : Shillong to Guwahati - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Wardâ€™s Lake. After that drive to Guwahati. Arrive and check in at your hotel. In evening we suggest an optional tour of Golden sunset cruise on the Brahmaputra (Direct Payment by own). Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Sunday 25th January) : Guwahati - Hajo & Sualkuchi Day Excursion\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to visit Hajo for famous Shiv temple & Sualkuchi famous for handloom and traditional silk textile in Assam. Back to hotel. Overnight Stay in Guwahati.\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Monday 26th January) : Guwahati Hotel to Guwahati Airport - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel, proceed to visit Kamakhya Temple (Notes -Timing 08:00 A.M till 01:00 P.M & 3:00 P.M till its gets dark), Tirupati Balaji Temple, Nabagraha Temple, State Zoo cum Botanical Garden (Closed on Friday), Regional Science Centre and Sukreswar Temple (The 6th Jyotirlinga of Shiva). Later drop at Guwahati Airport for onwards Journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section\r\n* Meal Plan (as mentioned above)\r\n* Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area)\r\n* Vehicle : 1-Ertiga as per itinerary & timing only.\r\n* All hotel taxes (as per itinerary)','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any\r\n* VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot)\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\n* NOTE: Anything not mentioned in the inclusions is excluded.','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n','2026-01-22','2026-01-26',1,0,0,'2026-01-16 15:11:39','2026-01-16 15:59:39'),(1165,1884,435,2,2,0,208100,77000,'Switzerland Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Arrival at the ZRH Airport. Transfer from Zurich Airport to Lucerne Hotel with Swiss Pass.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Visit Lake Lucerne and enjoy boat cruise, Chapel Bridge, Lion Monument Tour - Sharing with Swiss Pass\r\nMount Titlis with Ice Flyer Tour - Sharing with Swiss Pass\r\n\r\nDay 03 : Transfer from Lucerne Hotel to Interlaken Hotel with Swiss Pass\r\nEnjoy scenic Lake Thun and Lake Brienz with the Swiss Travel Pass\r\n\r\nDay 04 : Mount Jungfrau - Top of Europe Tour - Sharing with Swiss Pass\r\n\r\nDay 05 : Transfer from Interlaken Hotel to Zurich Hotel with Swiss Pass\r\nRhine Waterfalls Tour - Sharing with Swiss Pass ( No boat ride)\r\n\r\nDay 06 : Lindt Chocolate factory Tour - Sharing with swiss pass\r\n\r\nDay 07 : Zurich Hotel to Zurich Airport Transfer on Pvt. Basis\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare (CCU-DEL, DEL-ZRH, ZRH-DEL, DEL-CCU)\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Lucerne with breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Interlaken with breakfast\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Zurich with breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC\r\n* Swiss Travel Pass - 06 Days Continuous - 2nd Class\r\n* Zurich Hotel to Zurich Airport PVT\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n*  Hotel City Tax is not included and is payable directly to the hotel.\r\n* Tourist/local/city taxes, if applicable, are to be paid directly to the hotel by the client.\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAmenities such as Wi-Fi, tea/coffee facilities, and others are subject to availability and not guaranteed in all hotels/rooms. Supplements may apply.\r\nAll tours are on SIC (Seat-In-Coach) basis unless specified otherwise, and clients are responsible for reaching the designated starting points.\r\nCertain sightseeing activities may be subject to cancellation due to weather conditions, security alerts, or public holidays.\r\n','2026-05-18','2026-05-24',1,0,0,'2026-01-16 16:24:19','2026-01-17 22:24:17'),(1166,1886,624,2,0,0,0,0,'Guwahati Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n1st Day - (Thursday 22nd January) : Guwahati Airport - Transfer\r\nMeet and greet on arrival at Guwahati Airport and transfer to Hotel. On arrival check in to hotel. Overnight stay at Guwahati.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Friday 23rd January) : Guwahati - Hajo & Sualkuchi Day Excursion\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to visit Hajo for famous Shiv temple & Sualkuchi famous for handloom and traditional silk textile in Assam. Back to hotel. Ovewrnight Stay in Guwahati.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Saturday 24th January) : Guwahati to Shillong - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Kamakhya Temple, Tirupati Balaji Temple, Nabagraha Temple. After that transfer to Shillong (4,900 ft.), called \'Scotland of the East\". Enroute visit Umium Lake, a majestic placid lake with its surrounding sylvan hills. On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Sunday 25th January) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hrs\r\nAfter an early breakfast, proceed for a full-day excursion to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), renowned as one of the wettest places on earth. En route, stop to admire the cascading Elephanta Falls, soak in the breathtaking vistas from Mawdokâ€“Dympep Valley Viewpoint, and explore the unique Garden of Caves. On arrival, witness some of Cherrapunjeeâ€™s most spectacular natural wonders including the majestic Nohkalikai Falls (the tallest plunge waterfall in India), the enchanting Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), and the fascinating limestone formations inside the Mawsmai Caves. In the evening, drive back to Shillong for an overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Monday 26th January) : Shillong to Guwahati Airport - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Wardâ€™s Lake. Later transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Accommodation as mentioned in hotel section\r\n* Meal Plan (as mentioned above)\r\n* Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area)\r\n* Vehicle : 1 Dzire as per itinerary & timing only.\r\n* All hotel taxes (as per itinerary)','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any\r\n* VIP Darshan in Kamakhya Temple\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot)\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\n* NOTE: Anything not mentioned in the inclusions is excluded.','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\n','2026-01-22','2026-01-26',0,0,0,'2026-01-16 18:57:55','2026-01-17 13:31:22'),(1167,1887,19,4,0,0,98000,18000,'Istanbul Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 01 : Istanbul - Arrival \r\nWelcome to Istanbul! Meet our team at the airport and transfer to your hotel. Check in and have a leisure day.\r\n\r\nDay 02 : Dinner Cruise on Bosphorus, SIC Basis\r\nEvening transfer to cruise port for Night Show on Bosphorus. Set Menu dinner + soft drinks.\r\n\r\nDay 03 : SIC Istanbul City Tour with Lunch\r\nHead back in time and discover the old world of the Sultanahmet area during this full-day small-group guided walking tour in Istanbul. This tour explores the amazing UNESCO World Heritage-listed Blue Mosque which exemplifies why Istanbul is the city where east meets west. Enjoy a walk through the famous Topkapi Palace where Sultan\'s roamed and harems flourished. Plus, spend time observing Hagia Ireneâ€™s Byzantine architecture and stroll through the Grand Bazaar to witness handicrafts created by local artists.\r\n\r\nTopkapi Palace closed on Tuesdays / Grand Bazaar closed on Sundays / Blue Mosque outside visit on Fridays!\r\n\r\nDay 04: SIC Princess Island Tour with Lunch\r\nIt is one of the most popular sightseeing spots in Istanbul. It is an island that attracts a lot of attention from domestic and foreign tourists. Enjoy the idyllic, car-free environment as you travel by Electric Car wagon. You will start this tour with a ferry trip. Then there is a lunch full of fresh, seasonal specialties. You will also enjoy free time on the island to swim and shop for souvenirs or admire the Ottoman mansions. You can admire the most popular places of Istanbul such as Topkapi Palace and Maiden\'s Tower with a boat trip from Istanbul to Buyukada.\r\n\r\nDay 05: Istanbul - Day at leisure\r\n\r\nDay 06:   Departure        \r\nAccording to your flight time transfer to Airport. End of our service.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation in Istanbul\r\n* Return Airport transfers in Istanbul, PVT Basis\r\n* Dinner Cruise on Bosphorus, SIC Basis\r\n* Istanbul City Tour with Lunch, SIC Basis\r\n* Istanbul Princess Island Tour with Lunch, SIC Basis\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Tips to the local guide and driver (Suggested tipping: 3 US$/pp per day to guide, 2 US$/pp per day to driver).\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nCity tax is directly payable by client to the Hotel. \r\nSIC pick up and drop will not be from the Hotel. SIC tour will start and end from specific city centre location and clients need to reach that location on own and come back from that location on own\r\nSIC Tours are operated on Sharing basis in Coaches. Pick up and drop time is fixed and the coach will not wait for more than 5 min. \r\nClients need to call the supplier 01 day prior to recheck meeting point and time, failure of call may result in missing of service with no refund.\r\nAs per standard norms, 01 Medium Suitcase + 01 Cabin luggage is allowed per pax in vehicles for private transfers. If there is extra luggage please book a bigger vehicle at extra cost.\r\n','2026-06-11','2026-06-16',1,0,0,'2026-01-17 15:05:28','2026-01-17 22:32:53'),(1169,1888,195,4,0,0,89600,17000,'Baku Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDAY 01 : BAKU ARRIVAL\r\nâ— Arrival: Touchdown at Hyder Aliyev International Airport. Transfer to your cozy hotel. Freshen up and relax.\r\nâ— Stay: Overnight in Baku.\r\n\r\nDAY 02 : ABSHERON TOUR + PANORAMIC TOUR \r\nâ— Absheron Excursion: Venture into the Absheron Area to explore the Fire Temple, The Ateshgah Fire Temple, also known as the Fire Temple of Baku, is a historic religious site located in Surakhani, a suburb of Baku\r\nFire Mountain â€“ Yanardag, and capture stunning photos at the iconic HEYDER ALIYEV CENTER.\r\nâ— Evening Delight: Get enchanted with the Baku Night City Tour â€“ Highland Park,\r\nFunicular Ride, Martyr Alleys, Flame Tower, Little Venice, Baku Boulevard, Carpet Museum, Deniz Mall, and the vibrant Nizami Street.\r\nâ— Stay: Overnight in Baku.\r\n\r\nDAY 03 : QOBUSTAN TOUR   \r\nâ— Qobustan Area Exploration-Mud Volcano, & Gobustan : Embark on an adventure to the Qobustan Area,\r\ndiscovering the Mud Volcano, Gobustan State Preserve\'s archaeological treasures, and the striking Bibi Heybat Mosque. The State Preserve is full of archaeological monuments. Largest known concentrations of petroglyphs in the world | Later on, Visit 28 Mall, named after the nearby  metro station â€œ28 Mayâ€ and located in one of the most vibrant districts of Baku. Find a good mix of international and local brands and visit some of the mall\'s 16 coffee shops and restaurants. \r\nâ— Stay: Another captivating night in Baku.\r\n\r\nDAY 04 : SHAHDAG WITH CANDY CANE MOUNTAIN\r\nâ— Embark on a trip to witness the splendor of Azerbaijan\'s mountainous greater caucasus region. Prepare for a spectacular mountain expedition through Azerbaijan\'s most awe-inspiring landscapes. Be awed by the vivid red and white rock formations of the range which create a surreal, dreamlike setting. Visit Candy Canes Mountains, pink beauty of the Nature, Complete your trip with a visit to the Shahdag Mountain Resort. Enjoy exhilarating roller coaster rides or take in the incredible landscapes from cable cars. Transfer back to your Hotel. On the way, you will also be able to see the Red Village, a 100% Jewish settlement, the biggest outside Israel, and the USA. After the village, we will head to our Hotel in Baku\r\nRelaxation: Overnight in the heart of bustling Baku.\r\n\r\nDAY 05 : OLD BAKU CITY TOUR\r\nVISIT Charm of Baku\r\nâ— Old City Gems: Discover the historical wonders of Baku Old City, including Icharishahar, Maiden Tower, Palace of Shirvanshah, and the charming Museum of Miniature Books.\r\nâ—  Retail Therapy: Head to Deniz Mall, Azerbaijanâ€™s largest shopping center. Admire the dramatic architecture of a retail and leisure complex arranged around a four-story central atrium which floods all areas of the mall with daylight.  \r\nâ— Stay: Another captivating night in Baku.\r\n\r\nDAY 06 : BAKU DEPARTURE\r\nâ— Farewell: Transfer to Baku Airport. Bid adieu to Baku, carrying cherished memories of an unforgettable journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation in Baku with daily breakfast\r\n* All tours and transfers on Pvt\r\n* Transportation in Air Conditioned Vehicle with professional driver \r\n* Panoramic City Tour with Photo Stop (Flame Tower, Boulevard Park, Nizami street, Crystal Hall, Carpet Museum, Little Venice, Hyder Aliyev)\r\n* Old City Tour (Ichari Seher, Maiden Tower, Shirvanshah Palace)\r\n* Qobustan Tour (Mud Volcano, Rock Petro Glyph)\r\n* Ateshgah Tour (Fire Temple, Fire Mountain)\r\n* Shahdag Day Tour with Candy Mountain, Red Village & Cable Car.\r\n. Entrances Included: Funicula Ride, Fire Temple & Fire Mountain, Cable car at Shahdag, Rock Museum & Mud Volcano safari by Lada Car \r\n* Insurance\r\n* Visa\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Tips to Driver/Guide\r\n* Additional hours for transportation\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-06-11','2026-06-16',1,0,0,'2026-01-19 18:19:59','2026-01-20 16:40:45'),(1170,1889,54,8,4,0,260700,50000,'Singapore Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Transfer from Changi International Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Evening Mandai [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Evening Mandai to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to City Orientation Drive - Drop off Little India (3Hrs) [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Day at Leisure (You can explore nearby places on your own)\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Universal Studios Tour [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from Universal Studios Tour to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Changi International Airport [with Private transport]','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation in Singapore with daily breakfast\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on Pvt\r\n* Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (PVT Basis)(08-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* City Orientation Drive - Drop off Little India (3Hrs) (PVT Basis)(08-Adults, 04-Child)\r\n* Afternoon Sentosa Island Tour