alk +  Saraswati temple + Ubud palace \r\nDay 2 : Trita Empul + Gunung Kawi Temple Valley + Tegalalang Rice Terrace + Coffee plantation Bali Swing  Entrance ticket with transfers \r\nDay 3 â€“ Inter Hotel transfers Ubud to Nusa Dua + Goa Gajah (Elephant Cave) + Uluwatu Temple cliff views + Kacak dance Entrance ticket with transfers \r\nDay 4 â€“ Leisure day \r\nDay 5 â€“Leiure day \r\nDay 6 â€“ Ulan Danu Bartan temple + Jatiluwih Rice Terraces + Tanha lot temple Entrance ticket with transfers \r\nDay 7 â€“ Departure \r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n,','','* 2N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tourism Levy IDR 150.000/ pax\r\n* Any other taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-06-14','2026-06-20',0,0,0,'2026-02-14 14:55:28','2026-02-17 10:57:57'),(1193,1912,17600,2,0,0,29800,10000,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay 1 - Arrival at the DPS Airport and transfer to Ubud + Campuhan ridge walk +  Saraswati temple + Ubud palace  ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 2 â€“ Trita Empul + Gunung Kawi Temple Valley + Tegalalang Rice Terrace + Coffee plantation Bali Swing  Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 3 â€“ Inter Hotel transfers Ubud to Nusa Dua + Goa Gajah (Elephant Cave) + Uluwatu Temple cliff views + Kacak dance Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 4 â€“ Leisure day \r\nDay 5 â€“ Leisure day \r\nDay 6 â€“ Ulan Danu Bartan temple + Jatiluwih Rice Terraces + Tanha lot temple Entrance ticket with transfers ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\nDay 7 â€“Malestic beach  +Departure ( Full day Car on disposal 10 hrs )\r\n\r\n','','* 3N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Tourism Levy IDR 150.000/ pax\r\n* Any other taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n* TCS\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-06-14','2026-06-20',1,0,0,'2026-02-17 11:06:03','2026-02-17 15:30:28'),(1195,1913,1305,4,0,0,0,0,'Shillong Diaries','Suggested Itinerary:-\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Sunday 8th March) : Guwahati Airport to Shillong - Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nOn arrival at Guwahati Airport & transfer to Shillong, which is also called the \'Scotland of the East\". On the way visit a majestic placid lake with its surrounding sylvan hills Umium Lake (Barapani). You may do the water sports here (Optional). On arrival at Shillong, check in at your hotel. Evening you can visit Police Bazaar which is the biggest local market. Overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Monday 9th March) : Shillong to Laitlum Canyons - Krang Suri Falls - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 115 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 4 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast proceed to Laitlum Canyons for some breathtaking views. Then visit Krang Suri Falls. It is one of the best waterfalls in Meghalaya. You can also swim in a naturally formed pool here. You can also go behind the waterfall and see the water falling in front of you. After Lunch (Own cost) return back to Shillong. Overnight at Shillong.\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Tuesday 10th March) : Shillong to Cherrapunjee - Excursion\r\nApprox Distance: 60 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 2 hrs\r\n\r\nAfter an early breakfast, proceed for a full-day excursion to Cherrapunjee (4,400 ft.), renowned as one of the wettest places on earth. En route, stop to admire the cascading Elephanta Falls, soak in the breathtaking vistas from Mawdokâ€“Dympep Valley Viewpoint, and explore the unique Garden of Caves. On arrival, witness some of Cherrapunjeeâ€™s most spectacular natural wonders including the majestic Nohkalikai Falls (the tallest plunge waterfall in India), the enchanting Nohsngithiang Falls (Seven Sisters Falls), and the fascinating limestone formations inside the Mawsmai Caves. In the evening, drive back to Shillong for an overnight stay at Shillong.\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Wednesday 11th March) : Shillong to Guwahati Airport - Sightseeing and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 100 Km â€¢ Est. Travel Time: 3 hrs\r\nAfter breakfast check out from hotel and visit Don Bosco Museum (Sunday Closed) & Wardâ€™s Lake. Later transfer to Guwahati Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* 1-Ertiga as per itinerary & timing only.\r\n* Exclusive AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. (AC will not run in hill area)\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* All hotel taxes (as per itinerary)\r\n\r\n','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, porterage\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Guide charges, Entry Fees & Camera Charges if any\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like cyclone, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client and directly payable on the spot)\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\nNOTE: Anything not mentioned in the inclusions is excluded.\r\n','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.','2026-03-08','2026-03-11',0,0,0,'2026-02-17 16:44:13','2026-02-17 17:09:54'),(1197,1919,17600,2,0,0,29800,10000,'Bali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\nDay 1 - Arrival at the DPS Airport and transfer to Ubud