4N Accommodation in Singapore with Daily Breakfast\r\n* KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) ( KL Tower Observation Deck ) (PVT Basis)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) ( Cable Car 2 Way + Enroute Batu Caves (30 mins photostop) ) (PVT Basis)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Sunway Lagoon Tour ( Sunway Lagoon 6 Park ) (PVT Basis)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Airport Transfers on PVT Singapore and Malaysia\r\n* Evening Mandai ( Night Safari ) (Only Ticket)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* City Orientation Drive - Drop off Little India (3Hrs) (Only Ticket)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* MBS Skypark Non Peak Hours + Gardens By The Bay ( MBS Non Peak (Before 4 PM) + Gardens by the Bay: Flower Dome & Cloud Forest featuring Jurassic World: The Experience ) (Only Ticket)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Full Day Sentosa Island Tour ( Cable Car + Madame Tussauds 4in1 + Wings Of Time 1st Show ) (Only Ticket)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Universal Studios Tour ( Universal Studio Ticket ) (Only Ticket)(02-Adults, 01-Child)\r\n* Visa for Singapore\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any Taxes (If Applicable)\r\n* Visa for Malaysia\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nMid-night Surcharge applicable from 11pm - 07am on Private Transfers.','2026-06-05','2026-06-13',1,0,0,'2026-04-08 17:30:35','2026-04-08 18:24:59'),(1222,1959,355,2,0,0,13200,2700,'Varanasi Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :-\r\n\r\nDay 1 : April 25 - Arrival and Evening Aarti (Check-in 2:00 PM)\r\nArrival at the Train Station. Pick up and private transfer to the hotel. Check-in and relax after the journey.\r\nEvening: Walk through the narrow lanes of old Varanasi to Dashashwamedh Ghat to witness the spectacular evening Ganga Aarti.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : April 26 - Culture, Sarnath, and Alaknanda Cruise\r\nMorning (Early): Sunrise boat ride (at your own cost) to witness the daily rituals at the Ghats.\r\nMid-Morning: Visit the main Kashi Vishwanath Temple, Annapurna Temple, and Vishalakshi Temple.\r\nAfternoon : Excursion to Sarnath, the place where Lord Buddha preached his first sermon. Visit Dhamek Stupa, Chaukhandi Stupa, and the Sarnath Museum.\r\nEvening (Pre-booked): Alaknanda Cruise experience on the Ganga River.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : April 27 - Hidden Gems and Spiritual Exploration\r\nMorning : Visit the Monkey Temple (Durga Temple), Tulsi Manas Mandir, and Sankat Mochan Temple.\r\nAfternoon : Free time for local shopping at Godowlia Market for Banarasi sarees and handicrafts.\r\nEvening: Attend the Aarti at Assi Ghat for a more intimate experience.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : April 28 - Departure (Check-out 11:00 AM)\r\nMorning : Early breakfast. Check out of the hotel.\r\n 11:30 AM: Transfer to the railway station to catch the 1:30 PM train \r\n','','* 3N Accommodation in Varanasi with Daily Breakfast.\r\n* Tours and transfers as mentioned in the itinerary on PVT\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan\r\n ','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n\r\n\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-04-25','2026-04-28',0,0,0,'2026-04-14 16:28:58','2026-04-15 18:13:08'),(1223,1960,435,3,1,0,584400,60000,'Switzerland Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n* Excursion to Rhine falls with Swiss pass.\r\n\r\n* Lindt chocolate factory tour\r\n\r\n* Excursion to Mt. Jungfraujoch with Swiss pass\r\n\r\n* Excursion to Mt. Pilatus with Swiss Pass','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 2N Accommodation in Lucerne with Breakfast \r\n* 2N Accommodation in Interlaken with Breakfast \r\n* 1N Accommodation in Zurich with Breakfast \r\n* 06 Days Swiss pass-2nd class\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Transfers to be managed on your own using Swiss Pass\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* TCS\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nAll tours and transfers are based on SIC ( starting from a meeting point)\r\n','2026-06-04','2026-06-09',1,0,0,'2026-04-15 14:39:58','2026-04-15 16:37:33'),(1225,1961,15518,2,0,0,0,0,'Kerala Dairies','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 1 (14th May) :\r\nArrival Transfer - Cochin - Munnar\r\nOn arrival at the Cochin airport meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and afterwards to transfer you to your already booked hotel in Munnar Proceed to Munnar. Visit Cheeyapara and Valara water falls on the way to Munnar. Through out the journey enjoy beautiful streams small waterfalls, Rubber, Pepper cardamom and Tea plantations and thick forests; God has blessed his own country with incomparable beauty on arrival at Munnar check in to Hotel. At leisure. Overnight stay in Hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n* Day 2 (15th May) : Munnar Sightseeing\r\n Morning after breakfast proceed to enjoy full day sight seeing tour of Munnar. Rose Garden, Tea Garden, Photo Point, Mattupetty Dam/Lake, Echo Point & Kundala Dam/Lake. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n* Day 3 (16th  May) :  Transfers - Munnar - Thekkady\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the hotel and transfer to Thekkady . Thekkady is a world famous wildlife sanctuary and it is also called as Periyar. On arrival check in at Hotel. Afternoon visit wildlife sanctuary & enjoy the boating ( tickets charges are extra and subject to availability ) . Visit spice plantations. Apart from being enjoyable these plantation tours gives tourists an insight into the growing, harvesting and processing of spices. Evening will be free for Cultural show ( Kathakali & Kalaripayattu on direct payment ) & local shopping. Overnight stay at Thekkady.\r\n\r\n\r\n* Day 4 (17th  May ) : Transfers -Thekkady to Alleppey\r\nMorning after breakfast leave for Alleppey, Allappuza famous for its backwaters. Visit Alleppey beach, sunset and enjoy shopping if staying in Alleppey. Visit Alleppey Beach and Backwaters. Enjoy all the amenities of this hotel/resort for a day which includes fishing in the backwaters (depends on the hotel/resort selected) . Overnight Stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n* Day 5 (18th May ) : Transfers - Alleppey to Trivandrum\r\nBreakfast at Residing Hotel and transfer to your already booked hotel in Trivandrum. Visit Padmanabha Swami Temple, Kuthiramalika Palace Museum, Zoo, NapierÂ  Museum & Veli Tourist Village. Overnight stay at hotel/resort.\r\n\r\n* Day 6 (19th May )\r\nDeparture Transfer - Trivandrum Dep\r\nMorning after breakfast check out from the Hotel and transferred to Trivandrum Airport for your onward journey. \r\n\r\n','','* 2N Accommodation in Munnar with Daily Breakfast.\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Thekkady with Breakfast.\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Alleppey with Breakfast.\r\n* 1N Accommodation in Trivandrum with Breakfast. \r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* Vehicle- Sedan ','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces \r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Only Non Ac Rooms Are Provided In Munnar And Thekkady As They Are Hill Stations\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking \r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.','2026-05-14','2026-05-19',1,0,0,'2026-04-17 18:00:23','2026-04-18 13:37:31'),(1226,1962,15496,2,0,0,18000,3000,'Manali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\'\r\nDay 1 : Chandigarh to Manali\r\nPick up from Chandigarh and drive to Manali. \r\nOn arrival, check in at the hotel and relax. Overnight stay in Manali.\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Manali Local Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, proceed for local sightseeing in Manali. Visit the serene Hadimba Devi Temple, set amidst dense cedar forests. Explore the peaceful Buddhist Monastery Manali.\r\nLater, visit Vashisht Village, known for its natural hot water springs and ancient temples. Return to the hotel. Overnight stay in Manali.\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Solang Valley + Atal Tunnel + Sissu Excursion\r\nAfter breakfast, head towards Solang Valley, famous for thrilling adventure activities like paragliding, zorbing, ATV rides, and more (at own cost).\r\nLater, drive through the iconic Atal Tunnel to reach Sissu, known for its stunning landscapes and waterfalls. Return to Manali by evening. Overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Naggar & Kullu Excursion\r\nAfter breakfast, drive to Naggar, a charming village. Visit the historic Naggar Castle and the renowned Nicholas Roerich Art Gallery.\r\nLater, enjoy a short hike to Jana Waterfall.\r\nYou can also opt for adventure activities like river rafting or paragliding in Kullu Valley (at own cost). Return to Manali. Overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Manali â€“ Kasol â€“ Manikaran Excursion\r\nAfter breakfast, proceed towards Kasol. En route, visit Manikaran Sahib, a famous pilgrimage site with a revered Gurudwara and hot springs.\r\nExplore the vibrant Kasol Market and riverside cafÃ©s. Return to Manali by evening. Overnight stay.\r\n\r\nDay 6: Manali to Chandigarh Departure\r\nAfter breakfast, check out from the hotel and drive back to Chandigarh with unforgettable memories of your Himachal trip.','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 5N Accommodation as mentioned with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Sedan\r\n* Pick up and drop off as per the itinerary from the respective Airport and on a point to point basis as per the itinerary.\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Heater Charges @ Extra Directly payable at property\r\n* Rohtang Pass( As per local cab union rates only)\r\n* Monument Entrance Fee / Camera Fees.\r\n* Any expenses caused by reasons beyond our control such as roadblocks due to natural climates and accidents. Etc\r\n* Cost of 4*4 and cost of Chained Vehicles in case of Heavy Snowfall\r\n* Night Charges for cab will apply after 9 pm.\r\n* AC will not work in Hilly areas but in Plains as per NGT Guidelines.\r\n\r\n\r\n','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-06-03','2026-06-08',1,0,0,'2026-04-22 11:56:20','2026-04-22 12:13:03'),(1227,1963,15531,10,0,0,169800,20000,'Kanatal Dairies ','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 1st  (Sun 31st May) : Gurgaon to Kanatal - Transfer\r\nPick up from Gurgaon and proceed towards Kanatal via a comfortable road transfer, enjoying a scenic drive through the changing landscapes from city plains to the serene hills of Uttarakhand. Upon arrival in Kanatal, check in to your hotel and relax amidst the à¤¶à¤¾à¤‚à¤¤ and refreshing environment of this peaceful hill station.\r\n\r\n* Day 2nd  (Mon 1st June) : Kanatal - Day Trip Mussoorie\r\nAfter breakfast, proceed for a scenic day excursion from Kanatal to Mussoorie, popularly known as the â€œQueen of Hills.â€ Enjoy a beautiful drive through the hills as you reach Mussoorie and begin your sightseeing with a visit to the famous Kempty Falls, where you can relax and enjoy the natural surroundings. Later, explore the bustling Mall Road, perfect for shopping, cafÃ©s, and local experiences. You can also visit Gun Hill for panoramic views of the Himalayan ranges at your own cost . After enjoying the day in Mussoorie, return back to Kanatal by evening for a comfortable overnight stay.\r\n\r\n* Day 3rd (Tue 2nd June) : Kanatal - Day Visit Tehri\r\nTake a early Breakfast, proceed to Tehri Sightseeing Tehri lake provides a hundred opportunities to the adventure lovers who throw caution to the winds by engaging in activities like Scuba Diving, Angling, Canoeing, Rowing , Boating, Water scooter, speed Boating, Rafting, Kayaking, House Boat, Cruise boating at your own cost and later in evening back to Kanatal .\r\n\r\n* Day 4th (Wed 3rd June) : Kanatal - Fullday Sightseeing\r\nAfter breakfast, Proceed for a full-day sightseeing tour of Kanatal. Visit Surkanda Devi Temple, enjoy panoramic views from various viewpoints, and explore the scenic Kaudia Forest. You can also engage in adventure activities like zip-lining and trekking. Later, visit the local eco parks and enjoy leisure time amidst nature. Return to your hotel by evening. Overnight stay in Kanatal.\r\n\r\n* Day 5th (Thu 4th June) : Drop To - Gurgaon\r\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel . Drop to Gurgaon.','','* 4N Accommodation in Kanatal with Daily Breakfast.\r\n* All transfers and sightseeing as per the itinerary.\r\n* Vehicle will be provided from 8:00 am to 8:00pm\r\n* Vehicle : 12 seater Tempo Traveller\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* A/C room will not be provided in hill area.\r\n* A/C will not work on hills.\r\n* Entry fee for any monument will be paid directly by the client\r\n* Vehicle is as per itinerary and not on disposal. Additional sightseeing or transfer which are not mentioned in itinerary is payable to the driver directly.','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking. \r\nIn Mussoorie , Vehicle will not go to Landour due to government restrictions. It will only go up to Landour Parking or can be parked in Mussoorie. Guests will need to proceed to Landour by a local union vehicle on a direct basis.\r\n\r\n','2026-05-31','2026-06-04',0,0,0,'2026-04-22 14:13:55','2026-04-22 16:01:55'),(1228,1964,126,2,0,0,14200,1500,'Rajasthan Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival & Jaipur Heritage\r\nFocus on the iconic landmarks of the Pink City.\r\nMorning Arrival : Check in to your hotel and start at the Hawa Mahal, known for its intricate honeycomb windows.\r\nCity Center Sightseeing: Visit the City Palace complex to see royal courtyards and museums. Nearby, explore the Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO-listed astronomical observatory.\r\nEvening: Enjoy a scenic photo stop at Jal Mahal (Water Palace) during sunset.\r\nOvernight: Jaipur. \r\n\r\nDay 2: Forts & Local Culture\r\nExplore the hilltop fortifications and vibrant markets.\r\nAmer Fort : Spend the morning at Amer Fort. You can opt for an elephant ride or jeep to the entrance.\r\nNahargarh & Jaigarh Forts : Visit Nahargarh Fort for panoramic views of the city and Jaigarh Fort to see the world\'s largest cannon on wheels.\r\nShopping : Head to Bapu Bazaar for textiles, mojari footwear, and traditional jewelry.\r\nOvernight: Jaipur. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Jaipur to Ranthambore \r\nTransition from heritage to wildlife.\r\nMorning (9:00 AM) : Depart for Ranthambore National Park .\r\nAfternoon Arrival: Check in to a jungle resort such as Maa Ashapura Farm or similar.\r\nAfternoon Safari: Join your first jungle safari (2:30 PM â€“ 6:00 PM) in a Jeep or Canter to spot Bengal tigers, leopards, and deer.\r\nOvernight: Ranthambore Wildlife Resort. \r\n\r\nDay 4: Return to Jaipur \r\nMorning After Breakfast Depature to Jaipur\r\n','','* 2N stay in Jaipur with breakfast\r\n* 1N stay in Ranthambore with breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary \r\n* Vehicle : Sedan','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Safari\r\n* Activities','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-04-30','2026-05-03',1,0,0,'2026-04-22 17:40:49','2026-04-22 17:50:10'),(1229,1965,126,2,0,0,0,0,'Rajasthan Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Arrival & Jaipur Heritage\r\nFocus on the iconic landmarks of the Pink City.\r\nMorning Arrival : Check in to your hotel and start at the Hawa Mahal, known for its intricate honeycomb windows.\r\nCity Center Sightseeing: Visit the City Palace complex to see royal courtyards and museums. Nearby, explore the Jantar Mantar, a UNESCO-listed astronomical observatory.\r\nEvening: Enjoy a scenic photo stop at Jal Mahal (Water Palace) during sunset.\r\nOvernight: Jaipur. \r\n\r\nDay 2: Forts & Local Culture\r\nExplore the hilltop fortifications and vibrant markets.\r\nAmer Fort : Spend the morning at Amer Fort. You can opt for an elephant ride or jeep to the entrance.\r\nNahargarh & Jaigarh Forts : Visit Nahargarh Fort for panoramic views of the city and Jaigarh Fort to see the world\'s largest cannon on wheels.\r\nShopping : Head to Bapu Bazaar for textiles, mojari footwear, and traditional jewelry.\r\nOvernight: Jaipur. \r\n\r\nDay 3 : Jaipur to Ranthambore \r\nTransition from heritage to wildlife.\r\nMorning (9:00 AM) : Depart for Ranthambore National Park .\r\nAfternoon Arrival: Check in to a jungle resort such as Maa Ashapura Farm or similar.\r\nAfternoon Safari: Join your first jungle safari (2:30 PM â€“ 6:00 PM) in a Jeep or Canter to spot Bengal tigers, leopards, and deer.\r\nOvernight: Ranthambore Wildlife Resort. \r\n\r\nDay 4: Return to Jaipur \r\nMorning After Breakfast Depature to Jaipur\r\n','','* 2N stay in Jaipur with breakfast\r\n* 1N stay in Ranthambore with breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary \r\n* Vehicle : Sedan','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Safari\r\n* Activities','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-04-30','2026-05-03',0,0,0,'2026-04-22 18:15:30','2026-04-22 18:16:42'),(1230,1966,419,4,0,0,0,0,'Amarnath Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 01: \r\nArrival Srinagar Airport & Srinagar local sightseeing.\r\n\r\n* Day 02: \r\nSrinagar to Balthal & Night stay in camp.\r\n\r\n* Day 03: \r\nEarly morning proceeds for Amarnath Darshan by Pony & return to Balthal and overnight stay in Camp.\r\n\r\n* Day 04: \r\nBalthal to Srinagar via Sri Kheer Bhawani Durga Temple.\r\n\r\n* Day 05: \r\nSrinagar Airport drop','','* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Balthal Camp sharing basis (Langar)\r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Srinagar hotel with Breakfast and Dinner.\r\n* 1 Hours Shikara ride.\r\n* Pony from Baltal to Holicave & Holicave to Baltal.\r\n* All Tour by AC Cab\r\n* Vehicle - Sedan ','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n\r\n','Airfare are  dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-07-22','2026-07-26',0,0,0,'2026-04-22 18:35:22','2026-04-23 13:55:17'),(1231,1967,126,2,0,0,0,0,'Rajasthan Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day (Thu 30th April) : Jaipur to Ranthambhore - Arrival and Transfer\r\nApprox Distance: 200 Km\r\nUpon arrival, meet our representative and take a transfer to Ranthambore. Arrival, Check-In to the Hotel. Evening is free for leisure. You can spend it as per your own liking on your own. Overnight stay at Ranthambore.\r\n\r\n2nd Day (Fri 1st May) : Ranthambhore to Jaipur - Safari and Transfer\r\nEarly morning National Park Safari (safari charges extra), After safari back to hotel had your breakfast and check out from hotel drive to Jaipur and check in to hotel . Overnight in Jaipur.\r\n\r\n3rd Day (Sat 2nd May) : Jaipur - Sightseeing\r\nEarly Morning After breakfast, head out for the Amber Fort. Also, visit the Jai Garh, Jal Mahal, Sheesh Mahal & Jantar Mantar. Drive past the Hawa Mahal. While in Jaipur also visit Maharajaâ€™s City Palace and Ram Niwas Gardens. Overnight at Jaipur Hotel.\r\n\r\n4th Day (Sun 3rd May) : Jaipur - Shopping and Departure\r\nApprox Distance: 50 Km\r\nMorning After breakfast, check out from the Hotel. Half day is free for Shopping Activity. Visit the famous shopping places like World Trade Park, GT, Johari Bazar, Ajmeri Gate etc. Afternoon you will be heading to the Jaipur Train Station/bus stop.\r\n\r\n','','* 2N stay in Jaipur with breakfast\r\n* 1N stay in Ranthambore with breakfast\r\n* Tours 