ur (SIC)\r\nEnjoy a full day tour along the spectacular Great Ocean Road, one of the worldâ€™s most scenic coastal drives.\r\n\r\n\r\nDay 6 â€“ Departure from Melbourne\r\nPrivate transfer from hotel to Melbourne Airport for your onward journey.\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* Internal Flight (SYD-MEL)\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary on SIC\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance\r\n\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes (If applicable)\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-05-28','2026-06-02',1,0,0,'2026-05-02 14:26:04','2026-05-02 15:05:44'),(1246,1982,3511,11,5,0,0,0,'Gangtok Dairies','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 01 (22nd June) :  NJP Rly Station - Gangtok (120 kms / 5 hrs)\r\nMeet & Greet on arrival at NJP Railway Station & Transfer to Gangtok. On arrival Check-in to hotel & rest of the day at leisure. Overnight stay at Gangtok.\r\n\r\n* Day 02 (23rd June) : Gangtok Local Sightseeing\r\nStart for a Full day city tour covering Tashi view point, Ganesh Tok, Hanuman Tok,  Cottage Industry and Handicraft Centre, Institute of Tibetology, Dro-dul Chorten, Enchey Monastery & Banjakhri Falls (maximum 6 hours). Overnight stay at Gangtok.\r\n\r\n* Day 03 ( 24th June ) : Gangtok to Phodong Excursion.\r\nAfter breakfast start for an excursion to Phodong. Visit Phodong Monastary , Sevensister falls Phodong market Back to Gangtok and Overnight Stay.\r\n\r\n* Day 04 (25th June)  : Excursion to Tsomgo Lake & Baba Mandir\r\nAfter breakfast start for an excursion to Tsomgo Lake (12,400 ft.) & Baba Mandir (13,200 ft.) which is 55 kms one way from Gangtok city. Overnight stay at Gangtok.\r\n(In case of Land slide or any other reason Tsomgo Lake is closed we will provided alternate sightseeing.)\r\nSupplement Cost for Nathula Pass @ Rs. 5000+ 5% GST per car will be charged extra (Monday closed).\r\n\r\n* Day 05 (26th June)  :  Gangtokâ€“ Darjeeling (100 kms / 4 hrs)\r\nThis morning start for drive to Darjeeling (6,950 ft.). On arrival check-in to your hotel. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\n\r\n* Day 06 (27th June) : Darjeeling Sightseeing\r\nEarly Morning (at 04:00 am) drive to Tiger hill (8,400 ft.) to watch the spectacular sunrise over Mt. Khangchendzongha (28,208 ft. Worlds 3rd highest peak), on your way back visit Ghoom Monastery and Batasia Loop. After breakfast visit Himalayan Mountaineering Institute, P.N. Zoological Park (Thursday closed), Tenzing Rock, Tibetan Refugee self-help Centre (Sunday closed), Tea Garden (outer view), Ropeway and Japanese Temple. Evening free for shopping or leisure. Overnight stay at Darjeeling.\r\nSupplement Cost for Toy train and steam Engine @ Rs 1900 + 5% GST per person (including vehicle halting)\r\n\r\n* Day 07 (28th June)  : Darjeeling â€“ Kalimpong (57 kms / 2 Â½ hrs) Sightseeing\r\nAfter Breakfast transfer to Kalimpong (3,950 ft.). On arrival check-in to your hotel. Afternoon enjoy half day tour of Kalimpong Visiting Mangal Dham, Deolo Hill, Dr. Grahamâ€™s Home, Golf Garden, Durpin Dara Hills & Pine View Nursery. Overnight stay at Kalimpong.\r\n\r\n* Day 08 (29th June) : Kalimpong â€“ NJP Rly Station  (75 kms / 3 hrs)\r\nAfter breakfast Check-out from hotel on time and take the departure transfer to NJP Railway Station. ','','* 4 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Gangtok hotel with Breakfast and Dinner. \r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Darjeeling hotel with Breakfast and Dinner.\r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Kalimpong hotel with Breakfast and Dinner.\r\n* Exclusive Non-AC vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis)\r\n* Vehicle: 03 Innova /Xylo/ Scorpio/ Similar','* Airfare /Train fare \r\n* Entrance Fees & Guide charges\r\n* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot)\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\n* Room Heater Charges\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nA/C will not work during uphill journey\r\nAll transfers from Gangtok / Pelling / Darjeeling to onward destinations will be provided either in morning from 07:00 a.m. to 08:00 a.m. or in afternoon from 01:00 p.m. to 02:00 p.m.\r\nPermit require for Tsomgo Lake/ New Baba Mandir. It is mandatory that guest should carry 02 copies of passport size photograph, original photo ID proof with photo copy (identity card â€“ Voter ID card / Pass-port / Driving License) for processing the permit. Aadhar Card / PAN Card - not acceptable for issuance of the Permit.\r\nAs Innova is low chassis car and not ideal to travel Tsomgo Lake â€“ Baba Mandir. Alternative in Luxury vehicle like Scorpio / Xylo will be provided.','2026-06-22','2026-06-29',1,0,0,'2026-05-02 17:15:08','2026-05-02 18:01:51'),(1247,1985,329,4,0,0,75600,16000,'Malaysia Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from KLIA-Airport to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n* Evening at Leisure or you can explore nearby places on your own\r\n\r\nDay 2\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from the Booked Hotel to KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) [with Private transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from KL By Night tour with KL Tower (4 Hrs) to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\n\r\nDay 3\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) [with SIC transport]\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from Genting Day Tour (8 Hours) to the Booked Hotel [with SIC transport]\r\n\r\nDay 4\r\nâ€¢ Transfer from the Booked 