nating high altitude of the Lake. Overnight stay at Pangong.\r\n\r\nDay 4 :   After breakfast drive back to Leh via Changla pass and visit Thiksey Monastery. Later in the evening guest can walk to Local Bazaar . Overnight stay at Leh.  Overnight stay at the hotel in Leh.\r\n\r\n Day 5 : Depart Leh: After breakfast, transfer to Domestic Airport to catch the flight for your onward Destination.\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\n ','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 4N Accommodation as mentioned with Daily breakfast\r\n* Transportation in 01 Nac Innova \r\n* Inner line permit','* Personal expenses such as laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, porter age\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Entrance Fees to Monasteries/ Monuments/Parks/etc & Guide charges\r\n* Still camera/ video camera charges\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc. (to be borne by the client, who is directly payable on the spot)\r\n\r\n \r\n\r\nÂ· \r\n ','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking','2026-05-25','2026-05-29',0,0,0,'2026-05-12 14:19:41','2026-05-12 15:00:13'),(1262,2001,260,5,0,0,0,0,'Coimbatore Diaries ','Suggested Itinerary : \r\n\r\n* Day 1 ( 16th June) : Arrive at Coimbatore\r\nOn arrival at the Coimbatore airport, meet our representative who will be there for your warm welcome and proceed to hotel. Check into hotel. Visit Gedee Car Museum, Adiyogi shiva statue and local shopping. Overnight stay at hotel\r\n\r\n* Day 2 (17th June ) : Coimbatore to Ooty\r\nAfter morning breakfast checkout and proceed to Ooty, on arrival check in to hotel. After fresh up visit Nilgiri Mountain Railway, Rose Garden, Ooty Lake. Overnight Stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n* Day 3 (18th June) : Ooty to Coonoor sight seeing\r\nA small town up in the hills, Coonoor has a wealth of scenic sights and pleasant urban places of interest. Explore the numerous day-trip ideas around Coonoor: Visit Simâ€™s Park, Dolphinâ€™s nose, Lambâ€™s Rock, Doddabetta Peak and The Tea Factory and the Tea Museum. Overnight Stay at Hotel.\r\n\r\n* Day 4 (19th June) : Ooty to Kodaikanal\r\nAfter breakfast checkout from hotel and proceed to Kodaikanal. Check into hotel. Free day to leisure. Overnight at Hotel\r\n\r\n* Day 5 (20th June ) : Kodaikanal \r\nAfter munching some healthy breakfast in the morning, step out for a sightseeing tour of Kodaikanal. Spend the day amid the beauty and tranquillity of the place. Visit attractions like Pillar Rocks and Bear-Shola falls which are known to offer breath-taking sights to the visitors. Later, you can visit places like Bryant Park and Kodai Lake. While the Bryant Park is  visited for its beautiful greenery, the Kodai Lake is known for its serenity and boat rides. After this long sightseeing tour, return back to the hotel for dinner. Enjoy a comfortable stay at night in the hotel.\r\n\r\n* Day 6 (21st June) : Madurai Departure\r\nMorning after breakfast check out the Hotel and drive towards the Madurai international Airport for your onward journey. Tour ends with happy memories.\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 1 Night\'s accommodation in Coimbatore with Breakfast \r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Ooty with Breakfast \r\n* 2 Nightâ€™s accommodation in Kodaikanal with Breakfast .\r\n* All Inclusion and sight seeing By Ac Vehicle as per the itinerary from 8.00 AM to 7.00 PM\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : INNOVA 6+1 \r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Entry Fees To Monuments And Palaces\r\n* Any Cost Arising Due To Natural Calamities Like Landslides, Roadblocks, Etc\r\n* Any Increase In Taxes Or Fuel Leading To An Increase In Surface Transport\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions','Airfare is dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNon A/c rooms Are only provided in Munnar, Thekkady, Ooty, Kodaikanal & Coorg as these are hill stations and temperature will be Less.\r\nEntry fees, boat rides are chargeable and to be paid directly by the guest. Few monuments and sightseeing points are closed on every Monday and on national holidays. Itinerary can be revised without any prior notice. Sightseeing points may be excluded due to closer of the place or due to weather/travelling conditions.Â \r\nTransportation Vehicle KM allowed on the basis of Garage to Garage (Timing 08 AM -07 PM).\r\nIn Hill station & Forest station, room & vehicle will not be air conditioned.','2026-06-16','2026-06-21',0,0,0,'2026-05-12 14:37:28','2026-05-12 15:18:29'),(1263,2002,15496,5,1,0,9500,4000,'Manali Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n16th May : Arrival at Manali and pick up from bus stop and transfer to the booked hotel. Check-in at the hotel and relax. Evening Manali Tour.\r\n\r\n17th May : After having breakfast, proceed for Solang Valley, Atal Tunnel, Sissu and Gramphu\r\n\r\n18th May : After having breakfast, proceed for Manikaran \r\n\r\n19th May : Check-out from the hotel and manage the transfer on your own ','','* 3N Accommodation with daily breakfast\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Vehicle : Ertiga/Sumo\r\n* Vehicle will be on point to point basis\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n','Hotel/s are subject to availability at the time of booking.\r\n','2026-05-16','2026-05-19',0,0,0,'2026-05-12 19:13:09','2026-05-13 11:24:58'),(1264,2003,349,3,0,0,85000,17000,'Dubai Diaries','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\nDay 1 : Transfer from DXB AIRPORT to the Booked Hotel [with Private transport]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Catamaran Cruise at Marina [SIC]\r\nTransfer from Catamaran Cruise at Marina to the Booked Hotel [SIC]\r\n\r\nDay 2 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Half Day Dubai City Tour [SIC]\r\nTransfer from Half Day Dubai City Tour to the Booked Hotel [SIC]\r\nTransfer from the Booked Hotel to Burj Khalifa Tour [SIC]\r\nTransfer from Burj Khalifa Tour to the Booked Hotel [SIC]\r\n\r\nDay 3 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Desert Safari With BBQ Dinner [SIC]\r\nTransfer from Desert Safari With BBQ Dinner to the Booked Hotel [ SIC}\r\n\r\nDay 4 : Transfer from the Booked Hotel to Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) [ PVT ]\r\nTransfer from Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) to the Booked Hotel [PVT]\r\n\r\nDay 5 : Day at Leisure. You can explore the nearby places on your own.\r\n\r\nDay 6 : Transfer to DXB Airport from the Booked Hotel [ PVT]\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 6N Accommodation with Daily Breakfast\r\n* Catamaran Cruise at Marina (SIC) (03-Adults)\r\n* Half Day Dubai City Tour (SIC) (03-Adults)\r\n* Burj Khalifa Tour ( Burj Khalifa 124th + 125th Floor - Non Prime Hour NRF (SIC) (03-Adults)\r\n* Safari With BBQ Dinner PVT ( Standard Camp ) (SIC) (03-Adults)\r\n* Abu Dhabi Tour + Attraction ( Ex Dubai) ( Ferrari World + Grand Mosque Visit + Enroute Baps Temple (PVT)\r\n* Return Airport Transfers on PVT\r\n* Visa\r\n* Insurance','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* Any taxes (if applicable)\r\n* Anything not mentioned in inclusions\r\n* TCS','Airfare is Dynamic\r\nRoom/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nRates are subject to change at the time of booking','2026-10-01','2026-10-07',0,0,0,'2026-05-14 12:20:28','2026-05-14 12:50:03'),(1265,2006,3511,11,5,0,401000,32000,'Gangtok Dairies','Suggested Itinerary :\r\n\r\n1st Day - (Monday 22nd June) : Bagdogra Airport to Gangtok - Pickup\r\n\r\n2nd Day - (Tuesday 23rd June) : Gangtok to Lachung - Drive with on the way Sightseeing\r\n\r\n3rd Day - (Wednesday 24th June) : Lachung - Yumthang Valley Excursion\r\n\r\n4th Day - (Thursday 25th June) : Lachung to Gangtok - Transfer\r\n\r\n5th Day - (Friday 26th June) : Gangtok to Nathula, Tsomgo Lake & New Baba Mandir - Excursion\r\n\r\n6th Day - (Saturday 27th June) : Gangtok to Pelling - Transfer Via Namchi and Ravangla\r\n\r\n7th Day - (Sunday 28th June) : Pelling - Fullday Sightseeing with sky walk\r\n\r\n8th Day - (Monday 29th June) : Pelling to Bagdogra Airport - Drop\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','','* 7N Accommodation with Breakfast and Dinner\r\n* Tours as mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Exclusive vehicle for transfers & sightseeing. Please brief to guest that vehicle will not be at disposal it will be available to guest as per itinerary only (point to point basis)\r\n* Vehicle : 3 Innova/ Xylo/ Similar as per Itinerary & timing only','* Personal Expenses such as Laundry, telephone calls, tips & gratuity, mineral water, soft & hard drinks, rafting, rock climbing, paragliding, joy ride (Toy Train), porterage\r\n* Additional sightseeing or extra usage of vehicle, other than mentioned in the itinerary\r\n* Entrance Fees & Guide charges\r\n* Any cost arising due to natural calamities like, landslides, road blockage, political disturbances (strikes), etc (to be borne by the client, should be is directly payable on the spot)\r\n* Any increase in taxes or fuel price, leading to increase in cost on surface transportation & land arrangements, which may come into effect prior to departure\r\n* Room Heater Charges\r\n* Sikkim Tourism Sustainability Development Fees.\r\n\r\nNOTE: Anything not mentioned in the inclusions is excluded.','Room/s are subject to availability at the time of booking\r\nNOTE: AC will not work in Hill Area and Vehicles will be on Point-to-Point basis in Mountain, Some hotels may be little far from the Parking or Drop place, that will be on your own by walk or local transportation.\r\nPermit is required for visiting Tsomgo Lake and New Baba Mandir. It is mandatory for all guests to carry an original valid Government-issued photo ID proof (such as Voter ID, Passport, or Driving License) for processing the permit. Please note that Aadhar Card and PAN Card are not accepted for issuance of the permit. \r\nPermit also require for traveling to North Sikkim (Lachung & Lachen). We request you to send us a scanned copy of the original valid photo ID proof that each guest will be carrying during the trip. This documentation is essential to initiate the permit process and ensure a hassle-free experience for the guests.\r\nAs Innova is low chassis car and not ideal to travel Tsomgo Lake - Baba Mandir / Lachen & Lachung . Alternative in Luxury vehicle like Scorpio / Xylo will be provided\r\nTransfer from Bagdogra/NJP railway station will be provided from 06:00 hrs. To 17:00 hrs.\r\nAll transfers from Gangtok / Pelling to onward destinations will be provided either in morning from 07:00 a.m. to 08:00 a.m. or in afternoon from 02:00 p.m. to 03:00 p.m.\r\n\r\nSupplement cost\r\n(If guest want any add on Service must be Informed at the time of Booking)\r\nNathula pass (Monday closed) - Rs.6000.00 per car It can be done on the same day with Tsomgo Lake - Baba Mandir Excursion.\r\nZero Point : Rs. 4,200.00 + 5% GST per car on the day of Excursion to Yamthang Valley , Lachung.\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n\r\n','2026-06-22','2026-06-29',0,0,0,'2026-05-16 18:26:44','2026-05-18 10:47:44'),(1267,2004,15611,2,1,0,0,0,'Darjeeling Dairies','','','* Economy Class Airfare\r\n* 3N Accommodation with breakfast\r\n* All transfers as per the itinerary by Non AC Private vehicle and AC will be provided in plain area with extra payment basis.\r\n* Non-ac Wagon R/similar\r\n* Vehicle will be point to point basis not in disposal\r\n','* Any type of personal expense\r\n* Any meal other than the mentioned above\r\n* All entry fees\r\n* Room heater or blower in room [ If hotel provide on complimentary basis then it included]\r\n* Nathula Permit not included ( Tour cost INR 6200/- approx /per vehicle) - If you want to visit nathula please inform us or driver.\r\n* Pelling Skywalk (INR 1200/- approx / per vehicle) + Entry Fee INR 100 per pe